notes={{t="Hold Walk on Air for now. Falling With Style needs it soon, and it takes a minute and a half to come back.",tp=1},{t="Blademaster Ren stands inside the watchtower.",w=1},{t="Halaan Hawk-Eye waits atop the watchtower. Take the spiral stairs up.",w=1},{t="Halaan's gift shows you the distant pylon. Move or press Escape to end the view.",tp=1},{t="Myriaal Mistwake stands on the watchtower's top floor, by its ledge.",w=1},{t="A hop on flat ground counts as well, so there's no need to drop from the tower.",tp=1},{t="Xyton Silverwind is in the great tree behind Rorian, at ground level.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blademaster Ren stands inside the watchtower.",w=1},{t="Akeri Duskblade stands inside the watchtower.",w=1},{t="Cirrusfly Soldiers swarm around the queen. Clear the nearest ones before you pull her.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Read Leyline is your racial. Cast it at the standing stones the arrow points to (2 sec cast).",tp=1},{t="Next to a leyline, Read Leyline doubles your health and mana regeneration for 15 minutes. Anywhere else it lasts 30 seconds.",tp=1},{t="There are leylines all over the island. Recast Read Leyline whenever you pass one.",tp=1},{t="The leyline shows as a blue rift on the ground by the standing stones.",w=1},{t="One Raw Windstone can give several clusters. The 15 usually take about 10 stones, 15 at most.",tp=1},{t="With other players farming stones, camp one spawn or circle a few close ones instead of roaming.",tp=1},{t="You pick Herbalism, Mining or Skinning here. A later quest wants 20 skill, so gather as you travel.",tp=1},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blademaster Ren stands inside the watchtower.",w=1},{t="Xyton Silverwind is in the great tree behind Rorian, at ground level.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Urs'anah is inside the ursera cave west of Thendal Grove.",w=1},{t="Ursera Scavengers roam the cave around Urs'anah, who is level 5. Pull them away from her one by one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Equip the weapon Valreaa gave you for Aggressive Encroachment before you fight the thugs.",tp=1},{t="Malduko Cloudcrush is upstairs, on the temple's top floor.",w=1},{t="A leyline runs beside the thugs. Recast Read Leyline there when it runs out.",tp=1},{t="Keep Small Eggs and Strider Meat. Restocking the Larders wants 3 eggs and 8 Strider Meat.",tp=1},{t="Rathiril Sunlance is in the main lodge, around the corner from Aonda.",w=1},{t="Coriella Calmbreeze runs the village inn.",w=1},{t="Elayaa Easewind trains hunters inside a house.",w=1},{t="Naeluna Swiftmend is inside a house.",w=1},{t="Mages: Enchanting makes Novice's Practice Wand at skill 1, and a Stamina enchant for the bracers you wear.",tp=1},{t="Take this one by clicking the bounty notice on the village's west side.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="'Badwind' Bennic is deep in the bandits' cave. Its mouth hides behind a waterfall.",w=1},{t="Bennic and his bandits are level 7. Fight them one at a time in the cave.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Elayaa Easewind trains hunters inside a house.",w=1},{t="Naeluna Swiftmend is inside a house.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="No credit after sitting? Abandon the quest, take it again from Raan and sit back down.",tp=1},{t="Sit for about a minute until Boosted Rest shows. Cooking or bandaging meanwhile won't reset the wait.",tp=1},{t="Cook Charred Wolf Meat while you wait. It raises Cooking and leaves your Small Eggs alone.",tp=1},{t="If Boosted Rest still hasn't come after a few minutes, relog and sit by the fire again.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Windshaper Novice Seers gather at a leyline in the forest south-west of the village.",w=1},{t="Recast Read Leyline on the Seers' leyline before you fight them.",tp=1},{t="There's a single Hippogryph Matriarch. Kill her whenever you see her up.",tp=1},{t="The down feathers lie on the ground around the hippogryph nests.",w=1},{t="Vulgara the Insatiable is a level 8 elite. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Vulgara keeps to a hilltop just south-west of Shen'dar Village.",w=1},{t="She respawns slowly. If another group just killed her, expect a long wait.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Most well-fed foods also give 5% more kill XP for 15 minutes.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Naeluna Swiftmend is inside a house.",w=1},{t="Elayaa Easewind trains hunters inside a house.",w=1},{t="If the Mark of Akir is gone from your buffs, Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village gives it back.",tp=1},{t="Take the stairs inside the house. The Wardrobe stands one floor up.",w=1},{t="Then walk back toward town. A short scene on the way finishes the quest, even if someone else clicked first.",tp=1},{t="Equip the reward you picked from Among the Faithful: the Stained Ritual Dagger, Curved Scimitar or Windswept Shortbow.",tp=1},{t="Peacekeeper Vaaniel is the body lying by the road, northeast of the tower.",w=1},{t="Keep a bag slot free. This quest puts items in your bags.",tp=1},{t="Skypriest Aanders waits on the watchtower's roof, up the spiral stairs inside.",w=1},{t="Walk back down the stairs afterwards, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supply Caches, the small bags on the ground in Falaath, hold the supplies too.",tp=1},{t="Touch a drifting tornado for 40% run speed over 5 minutes. Dealing damage ends it.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hungry Bandits (8 to 9) hide in stealth among Windfield Orchard's trees by the road. Keep to the road and don't stop.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nyalah Brightfire stands inside a house.",w=1},{t="Alvarion Windfield is upstairs, one floor up inside the house.",w=1},{t="Valennia Stormfist stands on the tower's top floor. Take the winding stairs up.",w=1},{t="Walk back down the tower's stairs, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Fillion Flamebreeze lies inside the Shriekling Den.",w=1},{t="The den's birds only notice you when you're close.",tp=1},{t="Lose any bird on you before you click Fillion. Clicking him in combat puts you outside the den.",tp=1},{t="Aamelia Windfield walks between two spots in Windfield Orchard, so she may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Hunters: tab to the Hungry Bandits early and Hunter's Mark them, then back off and shoot.",tp=1},{t="Hungry Bandits hide in stealth among the apple trees and open on you up close.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct drifts a short way east and west, so it may sit off the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Mages: Polymorph a Flutterfly and swat it, then repeat on the same bug for more dust.",tp=1},{t="A Flutterfly that stays put after a swat wasn't caught. Swat it again.",tp=1},{t="Use the Flutterfly Swatter on a Flutterfly, then click the dust it leaves.",u=253666},{t="If you cross the orchard on the way up, stealthed bandits hide among its trees. Expect one to open on you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Flutterfly Swatter is an uncommon weapon. Equip it if you have it.",tp=1},{t="The Bandit Highwaymen are up on the mountain northwest of the orchard.",w=1},{t="Go down the way you came up. The ridge drops off sharply toward the orchard.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="When Aamelia stops during the scene, there's time to light a campfire and cook.",tp=1},{t="Alvarion Windfield is upstairs, one floor up inside the house.",w=1},{t="Belann Windwood is inside a house.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Rogues: you can wield the Trusty Wrench and the Flutterfly Swatter together.",tp=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Use the Index Esoteria beside each Windstone Formation, the large crystals at the stones.",u=254584},{t="The stones' east side is a long drop to the river. Leave by the south-west slope you came up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Taming Rod at its longest range, so the tame ends before the crawler gets to you.",u=267272},{t="Windsong Crawlers know Claw (Rank 2). Fight alongside your tamed one to learn it.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Use the Taming Rod while still at max range, so the tame ends before it reaches you.",u=267298},{t="Dismiss the last beast you tamed first, or the Taming Rod won't take a new one.",tp=1},{t="Use the Taming Rod while still at max range, so the tame ends before it reaches you.",u=264163},{t="Quel'dora is the pet trainer. Teach your pet Great Stamina and Natural Armor while you're here.",tp=1},{t="Valennia Stormfist stands on the tower's top floor. Take the winding stairs up.",w=1},{t="Hunters: equip the Bow of Hours here if you have it. It's an uncommon bow.",tp=1},{t="Walk back down the tower's stairs, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A leyline crosses the trail just north of Valanaar. Recast Read Leyline as you pass.",tp=1},{t="Commander Belguilos is indoors, one floor up in a house.",w=1},{t="Valennia Stormfist is up the tower stairs, beside Talaanis Shadowsong.",w=1},{t="Walk back down the tower's stairs, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Walk on Air glides you from the lower peak down to Urs'endris. Only step off with it ready.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Abandoned Belongings are crates lying round the ruins.",tp=1},{t="Vayn Moongaze stands in the cave mouth northeast of Elegael Thornpaw.",w=1},{t="Shadowgale Acorns are small seeds on the ground, mostly at the foot of trees.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Look for Lady's Tear Moss on the trees.",tp=1},{t="Vayn Moongaze stands in the cave mouth northeast of Elegael Thornpaw.",w=1},{t="Stand still until each heal finishes. If you move, the druid may not count.",tp=1},{t="Nyalah Brightfire stands inside a house.",w=1},{t="Talaanis Shadowsong is up the tower stairs, beside Valennia Stormfist.",w=1},{t="Walk down the tower stairs, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Valennia Stormfist is up the tower stairs, beside Talaanis Shadowsong.",w=1},{t="Walk down the tower stairs, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hyusaa Quickbreeze is up the steps of the Shrine of Akir.",w=1},{t="Valennia Stormfist is in the inner sanctum, up the spiral staircase.",w=1},{t="Baron Anvillaxx, level 13, and level 12 Malevolent Storms attack once Elaadrin starts the scene.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Talaanis Shadowsong is up the tower stairs, beside Valennia Stormfist.",w=1},{t="The skycutter runs on a 6-minute cycle, so expect up to a 6-minute wait at the dock.",tp=1},{t="Stay aboard until the skycutter docks. Stepping off early can knock you off Dalaran's landing platform.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Leave Dalaran only by the portal. The land round the city is level 30 and up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Bartleby gives up at 1% health, so the fight ends there.",tp=1},{t="Baros Alexston is inside the building at the edge of Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="Salma is inside the farmhouse.",w=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Don't vendor the eyes, snouts, vulture meat or livers. Salma takes all of them.",tp=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="At the Molsen Farm well, take a sample with the kit from your bags.",u=254545},{t="Defias respawn faster while you keep killing here. Stay in one spot and watch for new ones spawning beside you.",tp=1},{t="Defias Trappers root you with Net for 9 seconds and backstab. Fight them one at a time and face them.",tp=1},{t="You can loot the wardrobe from outside the house with the right camera angle.",tp=1},{t="Furlbrow's Wardrobe stands inside the farmhouse at the pumpkin farm.",w=1},{t="Benny Blaanco (level 15) is around the pumpkin farm and hits unusually hard. Fight him alone, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep three Murloc Eyes from these murlocs for Salma's Westfall Stew.",tp=1},{t="Look for the oat sacks along the farm fences and next to the buildings.",tp=1},{t="Each sack takes 5 seconds to open. Clear mobs close by first so nothing hits you mid-cast.",tp=1},{t="At the Jansen Stead well, west of the Furlbrows, take a sample with the kit.",u=254545},{t="Loot every Harvest Watcher. They drop Salma's Okra and the 5 Flasks of Oil Captain Grayson wants later.",tp=1},{t="Isosprings and Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. Look on the Auction House, or hand it in later if you find them.",tp=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ozwin Ironsprocket hides in the barn at Saldean's Farm.",w=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Innkeeper Heather sells Longjaw Mud Snapper, good food to eat between pulls.",tp=1},{t="Bind your hearth here. Sentinel Hill is your base until Redridge.",tp=1},{t="Monty stands on the middle platform of the tram's Ironforge station, where the tram from Stormwind stops.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Use the Rat Catcher's Flute beside each Deeprun Rat along the tracks. Lead all five back to Monty.",u=17117},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Nipsy waits on the platform at the Stormwind end of the tram.",w=1},{t="Baros Alexston is inside the building at the edge of Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="Christopher Hewen at Sentinel Hill sells both too.",tp=1},{t="Take the Gatehouse Shipment up to the second floor of Trias' shop and use it at the door.",u=277198},{t="Elaine Trias waits in the shop below the door.",w=1},{t="The Miners' Union Cards drop from level 18 elite undead in the mine before the Deadmines portal. Take a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wilder Thistlenettle is inside a building in the Dwarven District.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Donyal Tovald is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Murloc Warriors and Hunters (15-17) spawn on this beach. Clear the way to the footlocker one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Foe Reaper 4000, a level 20 rare, walks the fields around this barrel. Spot it before you click.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About 40 Defias Pillagers and Looters (levels 13 to 15) fill Moonbrook. Clear around each crate before you open it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="For Alchemists. It asks for Silverleaf and Peacebloom: an Herbalist picks them on the way; anyone else buys them at the Auction House."},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Foe Reaper 4000, a level 20 rare, roams the fields round these golems. Watch for it between pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Murlocs on the southern coast drop the eyes.",tp=1},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Captain Sanders' chest sits on the small island off the coast. Swim out to it.",w=1},{t="Defias Highwaymen (17-18) backstab for double damage. Keep them in front of you and pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is upstairs in the Cenarion Enclave.",w=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="The Shrine Bauble lasts 5 minutes once looted: swim west and go straight to the Shrine of Remulos."},{t="The bauble's container sits on the lake floor in one of a few spots. Find it from the surface, then dive straight down.",tp=1},{t="With the Shrine Bauble in your bags, go to the Shrine of Remulos tree and use it there.",u=15877},{t="The Bauble Container sits on the lake bed, 35 to 65 yards down. Spot it from the surface, then dive.",w=1},{t="Stand in the water at the cave mouth and use the sampler from your bags.",u=15844},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Renzik is upstairs in the SI:7 building in Old Town.",w=1},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It sends you back to Alba Fairmoon in Westfall, on your way to the Deadmines.",tp=1},{t="It follows Sprite Jumpsprocket's dynamite errand, which needs Rough Dynamite.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Rift Spawns are inside the Blue Recluse, the tavern in the Mage Quarter.",w=1},{t="Read the Cantation of Manifestation inside the tavern to make the Rift Spawns show.",u=7308},{t="When a Rift Spawn falls stunned, use the Chest of Containment Coffers on it.",u=7247},{t="Sneed and his Shredder, a level 20 elite, are inside the Deadmines. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Guard Parker stands by the traders' camp where the road from Elwynn enters Redridge.",w=1},{t="The Wanted Poster is just outside the Lakeshire Town Hall's door.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Darcy walks about inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Wiley is upstairs in the inn.",w=1},{t="Chef Breanna is inside the house just west of the inn.",w=1},{t="The Glinting Mud has several spawn spots in the lake. If it isn't at one, try the next.",tp=1},{t="The Glinting Mud lies on the lake bed, underwater.",w=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="The Defias Messenger sets off from Moonbrook and walks the road north past Jangolode Mine.",tp=1},{t="He respawns 4 to 5 minutes after a kill. If the road is empty, wait at Moonbrook.",tp=1},{t="Guard Parker stands by the traders' camp where the road from Elwynn enters Redridge.",w=1},{t="A Lake Thresher, a level 25 elite, swims through the lake and kills you in a few hits at this level. Dive for the toolbox only while it's on the far side.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Oslow's toolbox is in a Sunken Chest on the lake bed, underwater.",w=1},{t="Opening the chest takes 5 seconds, so mind your breath.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Bailiff Conacher is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Chef Breanna is inside the house just west of the inn.",w=1},{t="Darcy walks about inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Timed: 60 minutes. Go straight to the first fork in the Rethban Caverns and back. Dying and releasing fails it."},{t="Yorus Barleybrew is inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Redridge Bashers (19-20) and Drudgers (20-21) crowd the caverns' mouth. Clear a way you can run back along.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Old Murk-Eye walks the whole Longshore. If he isn't out, he respawns at the southernmost murloc camp.",tp=1},{t="Old Murk-Eye is level 20 and walks among Tidehunters of 18 to 19. Pull him alone, clear of their camps.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="If the Defias Traitor isn't beside Sentinel Hill, wait for him to respawn.",tp=1},{t="Defias in Moonbrook rush the Traitor when he arrives. Stay at his side the whole way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Edwin VanCleef (level 21 elite) is the Deadmines' last boss. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Scout Riell stands with Gryan at the top of the Sentinel Hill tower.",w=1},{t="Outside the dungeon, bandanas drop from Diggers and Workers in the mine under Moonbrook, among a few elites.",tp=1},{t="It follows Sprite Jumpsprocket's dynamite errand, which needs Rough Dynamite.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Deadmines, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can only do it after planting the explosives inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can only do it after planting the explosives inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wilder Thistlenettle is inside a building in the Dwarven District.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Deadmines, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Milton Sheaf is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="This chain ends in Poisons training.",tp=1},{t="This chain puts Touch of Zanzil on you. Anti-Venom cures it, and so can a Paladin or Druid.",tp=1},{t="Anti-Venom needs First Aid 80 and one Small Venom Sac, from Duskwood's Venom Web and Pygmy Venom Web Spiders.",tp=1},{t="Pick Pocket the Malformed Defias Drone for the key. It starts at the door, then walks laps round the tower.",tp=1},{t="The Malformed Defias Drone hits very hard. If your Stealth breaks next to it, Sprint away.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="With a dagger, open on each Sentry or Patroller with Ambush. Clearing them is slower than sneaking, and safer.",tp=1},{t="The chest is one floor below the top, on a bookshelf. Climb the chair, then the lamp. Drop Stealth to open it.",tp=1},{t="Clear the Sentries on the chest's floor first. After you loot the journal you can't Stealth for a while.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mobs on the floor above can hit you through the floor. Check what's overhead before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Drones, the Malformed one too, can be waiting at the door on your way out. Keep Sprint ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="Brother Paxton is inside Northshire Abbey.",w=1},{t="Theocritus waits on the Tower of Azora's highest level. Climb all the way up.",w=1},{t="Dawn Brightstar keeps only a few scrolls and potions, so check what she has left.",tp=1},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is upstairs in the Cenarion Enclave.",w=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="Restless Spirits of 23 guard the relics and attack on sight. The statue's stealth wears off, so don't linger.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Each relic is a small orb beside a cat statue in a wall alcove. The Relic of the Claw is deepest, past a bridge.",w=1},{t="Cast Teleport: Moonglade for the way back to Dendrite. It lands you much closer than the walk north.",tp=1},{t="Chatter, a level 23 rare spider, roams Alther's Mill among the Greater Tarantulas.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The quest also wants 6 Tarantula Eggs. Click them where they lie on the ground at the mill.",tp=1},{t="Raise Lockpicking to 80 on the Practice Lockboxes around the mill first. The Poisons chain needs it later.",tp=1},{t="Murlocs on this shore respawn very fast. Move away from the water before you rest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The same murlocs drop the fins and Selling Fish's Spotted Sunfish.",tp=1},{t="Grunts and Outrunners (19-21) stand close together here, with a few Summoners (22-23). Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supplies come from Grain Sacks, Meat Haunches and Water Barrels; weapons from Weapon Racks and loose Stolen Weapons.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Incinerator Gar'im is inside a cave in Render's Valley, southeast Redridge.",w=1},{t="Gar'im (level 23) fights beside his Shadowcasters. Bring a group of four, or leave this one out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The road north passes right by the Dragonmaw orcs of Angerfang Encampment (28 to 29), with Highland Spiders (28) just west of it. Stay on the road and keep moving.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Samor Festivus is on an upper floor, up the stairs.",w=1},{t="Samor Festivus sells a few Healing Potions, and so does Dewin Shimmerdawn near James Halloran.",tp=1},{t="Gobbler wanders a short way around the marsh. If he isn't on his spot, look nearby.",tp=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kixxle sells Healing Potions in short supply. Buy what you can afford before the gnoll camps.",tp=1},{t="About 35 stalkers of 21 to 22 fill the tunnels, and the rare Leech Widow, level 24, roams them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The gnolls here drop a lot of Wool Cloth. Keep it for First Aid bandages.",tp=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Opening the Sealed Barrel takes 5 seconds. Clear the murlocs around it first.",tp=1},{t="Merrin Rockweaver is inside the small cave at the dig site.",w=1},{t="The piles lie on the harbor floor, 10 to 20 yards down in the bay west of the docks. Surface for air between them.",w=1},{t="Young crocolisks (21-22) swim the channel east of town, and Bluegill Raiders (28-29) hold the south shore. Stay in the west bay.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Stoutfist is on the top floor of Menethil Keep, up the stairs.",w=1},{t="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is inside Stormwind Keep, in the throne room.",w=1},{t="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker stands inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors. Go into the building the arrow points at.",w=1},{t="Chef Grual only offers this at Cooking 50.",tp=1},{t="Chef Grual works in the inn's kitchen.",w=1},{t="If Stitches gets into Darkshire, Althea can be dead or stuck fighting him. Wait for her respawn.",tp=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Elaine Carevin is indoors.",w=1},{t="Take this before you meet Sven: Elaine Carevin stops offering it once Sven's Revenge is in your log.",tp=1},{t="Herble sells the Bronze Tube in small numbers. Buy one if he has it; Viktori asks for it later.",tp=1},{t="Herble Baubbletump, next to Viktori, sells the Bronze Tube but keeps only two. If he is out, Billibub Cogspinner in Stormwind's Dwarven District stocks more."},{t="Blind Mary is indoors.",w=1},{t="Skeletal Mages cast Frostbolt, and their Frost Armor slows you as you hit them. Don't count on running.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Warriors Hamstring you as well, so pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Insane Ghoul haunts the chapel. If he isn't inside, check around its walls.",w=1},{t="An Old History Book can drop from almost any Duskwood mob. Use it from your bags to start this.",u=2794},{t="The dagger drops from the Lost Stalker, a ghost found a little north of Darkshire or north of the Raven Hill road.",tp=1},{t="Use Ira's Dagger from your bags to start this.",u=281143},{t="Stitches, a level 35 elite, walks this road to Darkshire once someone ends Abercrombie's chain. Keep well clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="If Watcher Dodds is missing, Stitches may have killed him. Wait for his respawn.",tp=1},{t="The Memory of Valor is inside the small house at Raven Hill.",w=1},{t="Bliztik is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Bliztik sells Healing Potions in small numbers. Buy any he has.",tp=1},{t="Abercrombie's shack stands north of Raven Hill Cemetery.",w=1},{t="Cooks: the dire wolves here drop Lean Wolf Flanks for Seasoned Wolf Kabobs. Keep them.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: keep a Small Venom Sac. With First Aid 80 it makes Anti-Venom for Touch of Zanzil.",tp=1},{t="Keep 6 Gooey Spider Legs from these spiders. Chef Grual asks for them later.",tp=1},{t="The Old Footlocker is on the floor inside the Moonbrook Schoolhouse.",w=1},{t="The note is in a heap of Burned-Out Remains north-west of Moonbrook. Click the heap.",w=1},{t="You hand it in at other Burned-Out Remains, in the southern Barrens, when your road passes there in your 30s.",tp=1},{t="The Strange Lockbox with the Aquatic Endurance half lies deep under the sea here. Watch your breath bar.",tp=1},{t="Chef Grual works in the inn's kitchen.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Targorr the Dread is an elite inside the Stormwind Stockade dungeon. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You finish it inside Stormwind Stockades, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Drudgers and Bashers share spawn points. If Drudgers run short, kill Bashers to bring more.",tp=1},{t="Miners: Copper and Tin Veins in the cave can give Rethban Ore as well.",tp=1},{t="Stonewatch Keep's orcs are elites. Take your axes from Grunts and Outrunners outside its walls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Blackrock Outrunners cast Net, which roots you. Running from a bad pull is harder here.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blind Mary is indoors.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Black Ravagers roam the road from Darkshire to Raven Hill and the woods toward the Yorgen Farmstead.",tp=1},{t="The Mound of loose dirt is behind the old stump on Sven's farm.",w=1},{t="Stealthed Defias prowl the farm and slow you, and fights near the barn pull mobs through its wall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bliztik is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Abercrombie's shack stands north of Raven Hill Cemetery.",w=1},{t="Starving Dire Wolves notice you from farther away than most wolves. Give them extra room as you pass.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Rabies, from the Rabid Dire Wolves, halves your health regen for 10 minutes. Expect longer rests.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Farley is inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",w=1},{t="The Storage Chest is upstairs in the Lion's Pride Inn.",w=1},{t="Brother Paxton is in Northshire Abbey's library, on the ground floor.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Brother Kristoff stands outside the Cathedral of Light, in Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="Milton Sheaf is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Tavernkeep Smitts is inside the inn.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mor'Ladim, a level 35 elite, roams Raven Hill Cemetery. Look for him before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ghouls here run 24 to 29. Take Flesh Eaters and Rotted Ones; Plague Spreaders and Brain Eaters are higher.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mor'Ladim, a level 35 elite, walks a loop round the cemetery. Look around before every pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Warders are down in the Dawning Wood Catacombs. Raiders and Healers walk the graves above.",w=1},{t="These skeletons run 26 to 29, above your level here. Pair up if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mages: Skeletal Warders can shield themselves from Fire and Frost, and Counterspell won't stop it.",tp=1},{t="Tavernkeep Smitts is inside the inn.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Stormwind Stockades, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Stormwind Stockades, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bellygrub (level 24) has far more health than a boar should, and uses Charge and Tremor, an area hit.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lead him into Lakeshire for the guards' help, but deal most of the damage yourself or he drops no tusk.",tp=1},{t="Pull Yowler, then back off until the gnolls with him lose interest and go back.",tp=1},{t="Lieutenant Fangore fights with 2 more gnolls at his side. Treat it as a group fight, or leave it out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Morganth, a level 26 elite, holds the Tower of Ilgalar with his Servants. Keep clear of the tower.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Lion Statue stands among Shadowhide gnolls of 23 to 26, beside Morganth's Tower of Ilgalar.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23, fill the tower. Bring a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Empty Jar sits on a barrel on the watch tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You'll find Gath'Ilzogg inside Stonewatch Keep.",w=1},{t="Gath'Ilzogg, a level 26 elite, stands among elite guards. Bring a group of five.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tharil'zun, a level 24 elite, is a very hard fight. Bring help.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hunters: send the pet up to pull Tharil'zun and wait on the ground below him.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Shadowcaster here is an elite, level 22 to 23. Bring a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Render's Camp mixes Champions (24-25) with Summoners, Trackers and the rare Kazon (27). Pull from the edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Corporal Keeshan waits at the far end of the Render's Rock cave.",w=1},{t="Corporal Keeshan not here? Another player has taken this quest. Corporal Keeshan is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Out of the cave, Keeshan's path runs close to many mobs. Rest to full before you start, and expect extra pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bailiff Conacher is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mosshide Trappers net you in place, and Brutes (25), Mystics (26) and the Alpha (27) share their camps.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sida's Bag is a rare drop. Kill every ooze you pass; most of them gather round Ironbeard's Tomb.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Perfect Razormaw Eggs lie on the ground across Raptor Ridge, among the Razormaws.",w=1},{t="Raptor Ridge's Razormaws are 27 to 29, and the Razormaw Matriarch (31) is a rare there. Pull one at a time; they hit hard for their level.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Giant Wetlands Crocolisks cast Tendon Rip, a long slow. You can't outrun one once it lands.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The key pieces drop from crawlers, murlocs and striders of level 18-21. Below 20, bring two more players.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Raging Reef Crawlers (20-21) Thrash for two extra swings at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The sunken ship breaks line of sight with Greymist Oracles and stops their Lightning Bolts.",tp=1},{t="Greymist Oracles cast a heavy Lightning Bolt and heal themselves. Burst them down first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Greymist Tidehunters' melee poison ticks for 30 seconds. Let it wear off before the next pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="At 28 the Threshwackonator 4100, a level 20 elite, is a fight you can take alone.",tp=1},{t="It turns on you once you reach Gelkak, so start the walk back at full health.",tp=1},{t="Druids: Entangling Roots holds it in place once it turns, so you can back off and cast.",tp=1},{t="The Threshwackonator 4100 waits on the beach south of Gelkak. Talk to it to start.",w=1},{t="This quest gives you a Draught of Water Breathing. Hold on to it: quests under water come later.",tp=1},{t="Gyromast's Key has no use after this. Destroy it to free the slot.",tp=1},{t="A Strange Lockbox in the water off this coast holds the Aquatic Agility half. Swim out to it.",tp=1},{t="With both halves in your bags, join them at the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade.",u=15883},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is on the upper floor of the Cenarion Enclave.",w=1},{t="Dal Bloodclaw is 25 and the village's furbolgs 23 to 24. Clear his path before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dal Bloodclaw patrols Thistlefur Village. Look along his path if he isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Saltspittle Oracles heal and hit you with an instant shock every few seconds. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ancient Statuette is small and lies on the ground at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Talen talks for about 20 seconds after the hand-in before he offers Ruuzel.",tp=1},{t="Ruuzel walks with a Wrathtail Myrmidon and a Wrathtail Sea Witch, and they fight together.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill one escort, run out until the others reset, then pull again.",tp=1},{t="Lady Vespia, a rare in the same area, can drop the Ring of Zoram too.",tp=1},{t="A thrown bomb or grenade pulls Ruuzel on her own, away from her escorts.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Plant Bundles are small, brown and half sunk in the ground, easy to walk past.",tp=1},{t="Herbalists: Find Herbs shows the Plant Bundles on the minimap.",tp=1},{t="Pelturas talks for about 25 seconds after the hand-in. Wait for him to offer Elune's Tear.",tp=1},{t="Elune's Tear is a small blue stone lying on the lake's central island.",w=1},{t="Pelturas talks for a few seconds before he offers The Ruins of Stardust.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Kimlya stands in the raised room off the inn's north side. Take the left ramp from mid-hall.",w=1},{t="Stardust Covered Bushes are spread over the whole island. Work your way around it.",tp=1},{t="Kaela Shadowspear stands on the rise above the valley into Windshear Crag.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks stands by a goblin hut a short way north of Gaxim.",w=1},{t="Piznik is inside the Windshear Mine, west of its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine holds about 60 kobolds of 20 to 23, Geomancers among them. Clear a path in and out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds come at Piznik in waves while he mines, casters among them. Eat and drink between waves.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sorrow Wing, a level 27 rare elite wyvern, can spawn by the lake in the middle of the Pridewing hills. Keep clear of it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Worn Chest sits in a small glade west of the road to Felwood.",w=1},{t="Terrowulf worgen of 28 to 29 from the Howling Vale stand a short way west of the chest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About a dozen Terrowulf worgen of 28 to 30 and the rare Packlord (32) crowd round the tome.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Tome of Mel'Thandris lies on a table at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Anilia stands in the middle of Xavian's satyrs, 28 to 30. Clear your way to her one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Search Satyrnaar, the Bleakheart satyrs' ruins just west of Forest Song, for the Vine-Wrapped Scroll.",w=1},{t="Tell us where you found the Vine-Wrapped Scroll in Satyrnaar.",a=1},{t="Geltharis is level 32 but casts nothing. Clear the Xavian satyrs round him first and start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Bottle of Disease sits on a table in the Forsaken camp.",w=1},{t="About seven Forsaken of 28 to 30 hold the camp, and some of them hide in stealth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The slimes roam all round the Forsaken camp. Its Forsaken are 28 to 30, and some lurk in stealth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Hidden Shrine sits on a hilltop. The path up starts on its south-east side. Click the shrine to hand in.",w=1},{t="Their Frost Nova roots you in place, so running won't save you. Pull the elementals one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Some of the elementals are underwater, and your breath runs down while you fight them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Once you hold 5 Intact Elemental Bracers, use the Divining Scroll.",u=5456},{t="If you carry an Elixir of Water Breathing, drink it before you dive.",u=5996},{t="Foulweald Ursas Thrash for three hits at once. Fight them at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Totemics share spawn points with Warriors. If Totemics run short, kill Warriors to free the spots.",tp=1},{t="Every Foulweald here is 23 to 25. Pull single furbolgs from the camp's edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shadethicket Oracle is a hard fight alone. Bring a partner if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards hold the Barrens' north gate, just west of the way in. Keep to the arrow.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards hold the Barrens' north gate, just west of the way in. Keep to the arrow.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Satyrnaar's Bleakheart satyrs are 26 to 28. Prince Raze, a level 32 rare, can spawn among them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krolg stands at his hut on the south side of Mystral Lake.",w=1},{t="Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation near Krolg. He only talks to you in furbolg form.",u=5462},{t="Ran Bloodtooth, level 30, stands with five of his guards (levels 27 to 28) close round him. Thin them out before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Loot Ran Bloodtooth's Skull from him. The next step of the chain asks you to bring it to Raene.",tp=1},{t="Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation again before you talk to Krolg. The furbolg form lasts 3 minutes.",u=5462},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Velinde's Locker is past the overhead bridge, up in the Sentinels' bunkhouse.",w=1},{t="Marshal McBride is inside the abbey.",w=1},{t="Once you have the book, use your Hearthstone inside the tent. You land at the abbey without a fight.",u=6948},{t="The Stolen Books lie inside the Defias tent in the Northshire Vineyards.",w=1},{t="The Thugs can't reach you inside the tent.",tp=1},{t="Defias Thugs at the camp are level 3 and 4. Slip between them to the tent.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Llane Beshere is on the abbey's ground floor.",w=1},{t="Eagan Peltskinner stands outdoors, beside the abbey.",w=1},{t="Kobold Vermin at the camp drop the Nibbled-On Book.",tp=1},{t="Brother Paxton is indoors, in the abbey's library.",w=1},{t="Brother Paxton is indoors, in the abbey.",w=1},{t="Marshal McBride is inside the abbey.",w=1},{t="Sell your gray items here and buy a stack of water.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Marshal McBride is inside the abbey.",w=1},{t="Brother Paxton is indoors, in the abbey's library.",w=1},{t="You pick Herbalism, Mining or Skinning here. A later quest wants 20 skill, so gather as you travel.",tp=1},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Khelden Bremen is upstairs in the abbey.",w=1},{t="Priestess Anetta is downstairs in the abbey, at street level.",w=1},{t="Llane Beshere is on the abbey's ground floor.",w=1},{t="Brother Sammuel is on the abbey's ground floor, next to Llane Beshere.",w=1},{t="Tordrin Sternblade stands outside, by the stable behind the abbey.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Kobold Laborers work inside Echo Ridge Mine, past its mouth.",w=1},{t="Shinyfinder Narf roams inside Echo Ridge Mine.",w=1},{t="Priestess Anetta is downstairs in the abbey, at street level.",w=1},{t="Jorik Kerridan is in the stable behind the abbey.",w=1},{t="Marshal McBride is inside the abbey.",w=1},{t="Brother Neals is on the abbey's upper floor.",w=1},{t="Use the Kobold Tracking Kit. The tracks then show on your minimap.",u=247970},{t="Helene Peltskinner is inside the house northeast of Goldshire.",w=1},{t="About a minute of sitting by the fire gives Boosted Rest and completes it.",tp=1},{t="No credit after sitting? Abandon the quest, take it again from Sam and sit back down.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="William Pestle is inside Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="Priestess Josetta is upstairs in Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tomas charges 1 silver to teach Cooking.",tp=1},{t="Stonetusk Boars around Goldshire drop Chunks of Boar Meat, your first Cooking material.",tp=1},{t="Brog also sells the Small Brown Pouch if you need bag space.",tp=1},{t="Maximillian Crowe is in the inn's basement.",w=1},{t="Cylina Darkheart is on the inn's lower floor.",w=1},{t="Her grimoires teach your imp Blood Pact and Firebolt (Rank 2).",tp=1},{t="Zaldimar Wefhellt is upstairs in Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Buff Guard Roberts with Power Word: Fortitude and heal him with the Rank 2 Lesser Heal.",tp=1},{t="Maybell Maclure is inside the small house at the Maclure Vineyards.",w=1},{t="Gramma Stonefield is inside the farmhouse.",w=1},{t="A Kobold Miner stands next to Goldtooth and usually joins the fight. Expect two at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Narg the Taskmaster, a level 10 rare, sometimes spawns near Goldtooth. Leave him alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nimsy, inside Fargodeep Mine, calls a Rumbler into the fight. Bring a group if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds in Fargodeep Mine respawn quickly. Rest outside the mine.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nimsy is inside Fargodeep Mine.",w=1},{t="Any of the larger rooms inside Fargodeep Mine gives the credit.",w=1},{t="Blacksmiths: keep any Rough Stone you find in the mines. It makes sharpening stones and weightstones.",tp=1},{t="Keep the Bag of Marbles. It cuts a target's chance to hit by 25% for 10 sec, ten throws in all.",tp=1},{t="William Pestle is inside Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="Priestess Josetta is upstairs in Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="Priestess Josetta is upstairs in Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="Michelle Belle is upstairs in Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Maximillian Crowe is in the inn's basement.",w=1},{t="Zaldimar Wefhellt is upstairs in Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="The junk piles sit among packed murlocs. Clear around one before you loot it, or leave it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Helene Peltskinner is inside the house northeast of Goldshire.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Fishing Nets sit in the water and are easy to miss.",tp=1},{t="Murloc Streamrunners move faster than you, so you can't run from them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Junk Piles sit among packed murlocs. Clear around one before you loot it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The junk piles sit among packed murlocs. Clear around one before you loot it, or leave it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The junk piles sit among packed murlocs. Clear around one before you loot it, or leave it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Turn back as soon as the exploration credit shows, and the rest of the mine's kobolds stay out of it.",tp=1},{t="The credit comes partway down Jasperlode Mine's middle tunnel.",w=1},{t="Geosculptor Yip summons three Rumblers. Start that fight at full health and mana.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mother Fang uses a net and poison. Once netted you can't run, so pull her at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Brother Paxton is indoors, in the abbey's library.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Two murlocs stand by the huts next to Rolf's corpse. The Foragers drink potions that heal 61-68.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pull the pair away from the huts, kill one, then back off until the other gives up and walks home.",tp=1},{t="Warriors: Charge one murloc, Hamstring the other when it arrives, kill the first, then walk away from the slowed one until it gives up.",tp=1},{t="Priests: start with Power Word: Shield, Renew and full mana. Kill one, back off, then take the second.",tp=1},{t="Mages: Polymorph one, kill the other, then deal with the sheep.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: save Evasion for when both are on you, and leave once the first one dies.",tp=1},{t="Warlocks: Fear one, put your damage-over-time spells on both, then finish them off one at a time.",tp=1},{t="Paladins: kill one murloc first and save Divine Protection for when both are on you. You can't attack while it's up.",tp=1},{t="Throw the Bag of Marbles at the murloc you're fighting, if you still have it.",u=1191},{t="Young Forest Bears come first. Pick up Prowlers between them.",tp=1},{t="Lead a bear to Guard Thomas and the guards help. It counts if you did more than half its damage.",tp=1},{t="The Bundles of Wood lie at the foot of the trees north of the logging camp.",w=1},{t="Croaky, a level 11 elite murloc, swims by the Waterlogged Toolbox. Look for him before you loot it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Croaky is a level 11 elite. Ask around for a partner before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Croaky drops his head, and it starts this quest.",tp=1},{t="Croaky swims in the river south of Guard Thomas's bridge, near the Duskwood border.",w=1},{t="Its drop starts a quest. Pick it up if you come across it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Princess brings her two Porcine Entourage boars, and her Rushing Charge hits hard.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bring a healing potion. This fight often ends up needing one.",tp=1},{t="Warriors: Charge Princess, keep Rend on her and use Thunder Clap when her boars arrive.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: have Evasion off cooldown before you pull.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: with a thrown weapon, stand behind the fence near her. She and her boars lose time walking round it.",tp=1},{t="Defias Bandits drop the deed only rarely. If it never shows, carry on without it.",tp=1},{t="Keep out of the farmhouse. Morgan the Collector, Surena Caledon and Erlan Drudgemoor stand together inside.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Elmpaw, level 12, roams north of Stone Cairn Lake. His head starts this quest.",tp=1},{t="William brews the liquor for a few seconds after you hand over the kelp. The Escape shows once he's done.",tp=1},{t="Helene Peltskinner is inside the house northeast of Goldshire.",w=1},{t="Target a Rockhide Boar, then use the Taming Rod from your bags.",u=266158},{t="Dismiss the boar, then target a Gray Forest Wolf and use the second Taming Rod.",u=266253},{t="Dismiss the wolf, then target a Young Forest Bear and use the third Taming Rod.",u=266254},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Maximillian Crowe is in the inn's basement.",w=1},{t="Remen Marcot is in the inn's basement, beside Maximillian Crowe.",w=1},{t="Priestess Josetta is upstairs in Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="Zaldimar Wefhellt is upstairs in Goldshire's inn.",w=1},{t="Maybell Maclure is inside the house at the Maclure Vineyards.",w=1},{t="Riverpaw gnolls rarely drop the schedule, but the rare Gruff Swiftbite always carries it.",tp=1},{t="Hogger has several spawn points, so he may not be where the arrow ends.",tp=1},{t="Pull Hogger toward the guard tower and the guards join in. It counts if you did at least half his damage.",tp=1},{t="Warlocks: keep Hogger feared and let your damage-over-time spells kill him.",tp=1},{t="Hogger is a hard fight alone at this level. Find a group if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Zaldimar Wefhellt is upstairs in the inn.",w=1},{t="Priestess Josetta is upstairs in the inn.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Salma is inside the farmhouse.",w=1},{t="Quartermaster Lewis is inside the Sentinel Hill tower.",w=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Take Thor's gryphon to Stormwind. Humans know that flight path from the start.",tp=1},{t="Explosive Rockets, one of the reward picks, do good damage and can pull one mob away from its pack.",tp=1},{t="Morgan Pestle is inside his shop in the Trade District.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gakin the Darkbinder is downstairs in The Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Morgan the Collector is inside the farmhouse at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch.",w=1},{t="Surena Caledon and Erlan Drudgemoor stand with Morgan, so expect all three at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep Morgan feared and kill Surena first.",tp=1},{t="Surena Caledon is inside the farmhouse at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch.",w=1},{t="Morgan the Collector and Erlan Drudgemoor stand with Surena, so expect all three at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gakin the Darkbinder is downstairs in The Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Use the Bloodstone Choker in the bottom room of The Slaughtered Lamb.",u=6928},{t="Osric Strang is inside Limited Immunity, his shop in Old Town.",w=1},{t="Harry Burlguard is inside the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town.",w=1},{t="Bartleby gives up at 1% health, so he won't fight to the death.",tp=1},{t="High Priestess Laurena is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Only if you carry the Package for Stormpike. It's a delivery to Algaz Station.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Monty stands on the middle platform of the tram's Ironforge station, where the tram from Stormwind stops.",w=1},{t="Use the Rat Catcher's Flute beside each Deeprun Rat along the tracks. Lead all five back to Monty.",u=17117},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Old Icebeard is a level 11 elite, and the Meat Locker sits in his cave.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Old Icebeard walks out on patrol now and then. Loot the locker while he's away.",tp=1},{t="Mages and Warlocks: Polymorph or Fear him long enough to loot the locker.",tp=1},{t="The Meat Locker lies deep inside Old Icebeard's cave, near its far end.",w=1},{t="The Headhunters are inside the cave. The exploration credit is deep in, down the left-hand passages.",w=1},{t="Dropping into the hold from the slope above lands you among the trolls. Clear your way in on foot.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Vagash is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Vagash is a level 11 elite. Fight him down at the ranch with its defenders, not up on the hill.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Vagash is up the dirt path on the hill north of Amberstill Ranch.",tp=1},{t="Drag him downhill to Rudra Amberstill and the guard posted at the ranch's south end. With their help you can kill him alone.",tp=1},{t="The kill counts if you do more than half his damage.",tp=1},{t="Glacial Roar stuns everyone near Vagash for 3 seconds. Fight him beside the guards, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Vagash is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Coldridge Hammer is a two-handed mace. Paladins can use it now; Warriors and Shamans may need to train the skill.",tp=1},{t="Vagash is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Pick Farsen's farsight option first. Press Escape once the objective updates, then hand it in.",tp=1},{t="Rockjaw Ambushers drop the Empty Powder Keg, but rarely.",tp=1},{t="Skullthumpers fill the quarry pit and the mine; the Bonesnappers are mostly inside the mine.",w=1},{t="The Rockjaw Bonesnappers are inside the quarry mine.",w=1},{t="Dark Iron Spies drop the Dark Iron Map. Use it to start this quest.",u=274268},{t="Pilot Hammerfoot is through the tunnel north-east of the quarry, at the end of the eastern road.",w=1},{t="Free a bag slot before you click the corpse. A Pilot's Revenge gives you Hildelve's Journal.",tp=1},{t="Mangeclaw comes down to the corpse once you've taken this quest.",tp=1},{t="The Craftsman's Dagger (6.8 DPS, +1 Agility, no level requirement) holds up well past this zone.",tp=1},{t="Keryn Sylvius is upstairs in the inn.",w=1},{t="Hamish Bergwort is in the Tower of Azora.",w=1},{t="Elder Finseer, a level 11 rare murloc, walks Stone Cairn Lake's shore among the huts. Croaky, an 11 elite, stays in the river south of the bridge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Mining Tools lie inside Jasperlode Mine.",w=1},{t="The Kobold Geomancers are inside Jasperlode Mine.",w=1},{t="Disenchant the Crude Wax Effigies the Kobold Geomancers drop to get Luminous Residue.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Shaw is on the upper floor of the SI:7 building in Old Town.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Duthorian Rall is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Thor's gryphon from Stormwind's Trade District takes you there. You learned the flight on your first walk to Sentinel Hill.",tp=1},{t="Ozwin Ironsprocket hides in the barn at Saldean's Farm.",w=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Don't vendor the eyes, snouts, vulture meat or livers. Salma takes all of them.",tp=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Quartermaster Lewis is inside the Sentinel Hill tower.",w=1},{t="At the Molsen Farm well, take a sample with the kit from your bags.",u=254545},{t="Defias respawn faster while you keep killing here. Stay in one spot and watch for new ones spawning beside you.",tp=1},{t="Defias Trappers root you with Net for 9 seconds and backstab. Fight them one at a time and face them.",tp=1},{t="You can loot the wardrobe from outside the house with the right camera angle.",tp=1},{t="Benny Blaanco (level 15) is around the pumpkin farm and hits unusually hard. Fight him alone, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Furlbrow's Wardrobe stands inside the farmhouse at the pumpkin farm.",w=1},{t="Keep three Murloc Eyes from these murlocs for Salma's Westfall Stew.",tp=1},{t="Look for the oat sacks along the farm fences and next to the buildings.",tp=1},{t="Each sack takes 5 seconds to open. Clear mobs close by first so nothing hits you mid-cast.",tp=1},{t="At the Jansen Stead well, west of the Furlbrows, take a sample with the kit.",u=254545},{t="Loot every Harvest Watcher. They drop Salma's Okra and the 5 Flasks of Oil Captain Grayson wants later.",tp=1},{t="Isosprings and Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. Look on the Auction House, or hand it in later if you find them.",tp=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ozwin Ironsprocket hides in the barn at Saldean's Farm.",w=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Innkeeper Heather sells Longjaw Mud Snapper, good food to eat between pulls.",tp=1},{t="Christopher Hewen at Sentinel Hill sells both too.",tp=1},{t="Baros Alexston is inside the building at the edge of Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="The Miners' Union Cards drop from level 18 elite undead in the mine before the Deadmines portal. Take a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Donyal Tovald is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Take the Gatehouse Shipment up to the second floor of Trias' shop and use it at the door.",u=277198},{t="Elaine Trias waits in the shop below the door.",w=1},{t="Murloc Warriors and Hunters (15-17) spawn on this beach. Clear the way to the footlocker one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Foe Reaper 4000, a level 20 rare, walks the fields around this barrel. Spot it before you click.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About 40 Defias Pillagers and Looters (levels 13 to 15) fill Moonbrook. Clear around each crate before you open it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="For Alchemists. It asks for Silverleaf and Peacebloom: an Herbalist picks them on the way; anyone else buys them at the Auction House."},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Foe Reaper 4000, a level 20 rare, roams the fields round these golems. Watch for it between pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skeletal Miner is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Murlocs on the southern coast drop the eyes.",tp=1},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Alchemy.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Captain Sanders' chest sits on the small island off the coast. Swim out to it.",w=1},{t="Defias Highwaymen (17-18) backstab for double damage. Keep them in front of you and pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Baros Alexston is inside the building at the edge of Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="Renzik is upstairs in the SI:7 building in Old Town.",w=1},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It sends you back to Alba Fairmoon in Westfall, on your way to the Deadmines.",tp=1},{t="It follows Sprite Jumpsprocket's dynamite errand, which needs Rough Dynamite.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Rift Spawns are inside the Blue Recluse, the tavern in the Mage Quarter.",w=1},{t="Read the Cantation of Manifestation inside the tavern to make the Rift Spawns show.",u=7308},{t="When a Rift Spawn falls stunned, use the Chest of Containment Coffers on it.",u=7247},{t="Sneed and his Shredder, a level 20 elite, are inside the Deadmines. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ursula Deline is downstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Use the Tome of Divinity from your bags to start this.",u=6775},{t="Duthorian Rall is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Bring 10 Linen Cloth, from humanoids such as the Defias, and you hand this in on the spot.",tp=1},{t="Target Henze Faulk, then use the Symbol of Life from your bags to bring him back.",u=6866},{t="Guard Parker stands by the traders' camp where the road from Elwynn enters Redridge.",w=1},{t="The Wanted Poster is just outside the Lakeshire Town Hall's door.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Darcy walks about inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Wiley is upstairs in the inn.",w=1},{t="Chef Breanna is inside the house just west of the inn.",w=1},{t="The Glinting Mud has several spawn spots in the lake. If it isn't at one, try the next.",tp=1},{t="The Glinting Mud lies on the lake bed, underwater.",w=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="The Defias Messenger sets off from Moonbrook and walks the road north past Jangolode Mine.",tp=1},{t="He respawns 4 to 5 minutes after a kill. If the road is empty, wait at Moonbrook.",tp=1},{t="Guard Parker stands by the traders' camp where the road from Elwynn enters Redridge.",w=1},{t="A Lake Thresher, a level 25 elite, swims through the lake and kills you in a few hits at this level. Dive for the toolbox only while it's on the far side.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Oslow's toolbox is in a Sunken Chest on the lake bed, underwater.",w=1},{t="Opening the chest takes 5 seconds, so mind your breath.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Chef Breanna is inside the house just west of the inn.",w=1},{t="Darcy walks about inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Timed: 60 minutes. Go straight to the first fork in the Rethban Caverns and back. Dying and releasing fails it."},{t="Yorus Barleybrew is inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Bailiff Conacher is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Redridge Bashers (19-20) and Drudgers (20-21) crowd the caverns' mouth. Clear a way you can run back along.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Old Murk-Eye walks the whole Longshore. If he isn't out, he respawns at the southernmost murloc camp.",tp=1},{t="Old Murk-Eye is level 20 and walks among Tidehunters of 18 to 19. Pull him alone, clear of their camps.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="If the Defias Traitor isn't beside Sentinel Hill, wait for him to respawn.",tp=1},{t="Defias in Moonbrook rush the Traitor when he arrives. Stay at his side the whole way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Edwin VanCleef (level 21 elite) is the Deadmines' last boss. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Scout Riell stands with Gryan at the top of the Sentinel Hill tower.",w=1},{t="Outside the dungeon, bandanas drop from Diggers and Workers in the mine under Moonbrook, among a few elites.",tp=1},{t="It follows Sprite Jumpsprocket's dynamite errand, which needs Rough Dynamite.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Deadmines, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can only do it after planting the explosives inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can only do it after planting the explosives inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wilder Thistlenettle is inside a building in the Dwarven District.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Deadmines, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ursula Deline is downstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Gakin the Darkbinder is downstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Spackle also sells the Succubus's grimoires. Buy them, and the Voidwalker's if you have gold to spare.",tp=1},{t="Duthorian Rall is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="If Duthorian offers nothing, use the Tome of Valor he gave you from your bags.",u=6776},{t="Milton Sheaf is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="This chain is how a Rogue learns Poisons. Don't skip it.",tp=1},{t="This chain puts Touch of Zanzil on you. Anti-Venom cures it, and so can a Paladin or Druid.",tp=1},{t="Anti-Venom needs First Aid 80 and one Small Venom Sac, from Duskwood's Venom Web and Pygmy Venom Web Spiders.",tp=1},{t="Pick Pocket the Malformed Defias Drone for the key. It starts at the door, then walks laps round the tower.",tp=1},{t="The Malformed Defias Drone hits very hard. If your Stealth breaks next to it, Sprint away.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="With a dagger, open on each Sentry or Patroller with Ambush. Clearing them is slower than sneaking, and safer.",tp=1},{t="The chest is one floor below the top, on a bookshelf. Climb the chair, then the lamp. Drop Stealth to open it.",tp=1},{t="Clear the Sentries on the chest's floor first. After you loot the journal you can't Stealth for a while.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mobs on the floor above can hit you through the floor. Check what's overhead before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Drones, the Malformed one too, can be waiting at the door on your way out. Keep Sprint ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="Brother Paxton is inside Northshire Abbey.",w=1},{t="Theocritus waits on the Tower of Azora's highest level. Climb all the way up.",w=1},{t="Dawn Brightstar keeps only a few scrolls and potions, so check what she has left.",tp=1},{t="Raise Lockpicking to 80 on the Practice Lockboxes around the mill first. The Poisons chain needs it later.",tp=1},{t="Chatter, a level 23 rare spider, roams Alther's Mill among the Greater Tarantulas.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The quest also wants 6 Tarantula Eggs. Click them where they lie on the ground at the mill.",tp=1},{t="Murlocs on this shore respawn very fast. Move away from the water before you rest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Grunts and Outrunners (19-21) stand close together here, with a few Summoners (22-23). Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supplies come from Grain Sacks, Meat Haunches and Water Barrels; weapons from Weapon Racks and loose Stolen Weapons.",tp=1},{t="Incinerator Gar'im is inside a cave in Render's Valley, southeast Redridge.",w=1},{t="Gar'im (level 23) fights beside his Shadowcasters. Bring a group of four, or leave this one out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mountaineer Stormpike is upstairs in the Algaz Station bunker.",w=1},{t="Only if you carry the Package for Stormpike. It's a delivery to Algaz Station.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The road north passes right by the Dragonmaw orcs of Angerfang Encampment (28 to 29), with Highland Spiders (28) just west of it. Stay on the road and keep moving.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Samor Festivus is on an upper floor, up the stairs.",w=1},{t="Samor Festivus sells a few Healing Potions, and so does Dewin Shimmerdawn near James Halloran.",tp=1},{t="Gobbler wanders a short way around the marsh. If he isn't on his spot, look nearby.",tp=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kixxle sells Healing Potions in short supply. Buy what you can afford before the gnoll camps.",tp=1},{t="About 35 stalkers of 21 to 22 fill the tunnels, and the rare Leech Widow, level 24, roams them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The gnolls here drop a lot of Wool Cloth. Keep it for First Aid bandages.",tp=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Opening the Sealed Barrel takes 5 seconds. Clear the murlocs around it first.",tp=1},{t="Merrin Rockweaver is inside the small cave at the dig site.",w=1},{t="The piles lie on the harbor floor, 10 to 20 yards down in the bay west of the docks. Surface for air between them.",w=1},{t="Young crocolisks (21-22) swim the channel east of town, and Bluegill Raiders (28-29) hold the south shore. Stay in the west bay.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Stoutfist is on the top floor of Menethil Keep, up the stairs.",w=1},{t="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is inside Stormwind Keep, in the throne room.",w=1},{t="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker stands inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="High Priestess Laurena is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Ursula Deline is downstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Level 40 Horde guards stand on the Gold Road north of the Crossroads. Keep east of the road, out of their sight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Takar the Seer is in Horde land. Keep well away from Horde guards and towns on the way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards stand on the Gold Road north of the Crossroads. Keep east of the road, out of their sight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Unlit Torch lies on a table beside the Archaeologist's Cart, outside the house.",w=1},{t="Light a campfire and use the Unlit Torch from your bags beside it to get a Burning Torch.",u=190307},{t="Set the Archaeologist's Cart alight with the Burning Torch from your bags.",u=190308},{t="The Wooden Figurine sits on a table upstairs in the house.",w=1},{t="No Cooking means no campfire of your own. The fire at Talen's camp, west of here, works too.",tp=1},{t="The Heartswood is the giant tree in the Ruins of Ordil'Aran.",w=1},{t="Gakin the Darkbinder is downstairs in The Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Spackle also sells the Succubus's grimoires. Buy them, and the Voidwalker's if you have gold to spare.",tp=1},{t="Use the Heartswood Core at the summoning circle, then kill the Succubus it calls.",u=6913},{t="The summoning circle is in the Slaughtered Lamb's lowest room, down every flight of stairs.",w=1},{t="Use the Wooden Figurine at the same circle, then kill the Incubus it calls.",u=190186},{t="The Succubus hits much harder, but the Voidwalker keeps you alive longer. Use it on risky pulls.",tp=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors. Go into the building the arrow points at.",w=1},{t="Chef Grual only offers this at Cooking 50.",tp=1},{t="Chef Grual works in the inn's kitchen.",w=1},{t="If Stitches gets into Darkshire, Althea can be dead or stuck fighting him. Wait for her respawn.",tp=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Elaine Carevin is indoors.",w=1},{t="Take this before you meet Sven: Elaine Carevin stops offering it once Sven's Revenge is in your log.",tp=1},{t="Herble sells the Bronze Tube in small numbers. Buy one if he has it; Viktori asks for it later.",tp=1},{t="Herble Baubbletump, next to Viktori, sells the Bronze Tube but keeps only two. If he is out, Billibub Cogspinner in Stormwind's Dwarven District stocks more."},{t="Blind Mary is indoors.",w=1},{t="Skeletal Mages cast Frostbolt, and their Frost Armor slows you as you hit them. Don't count on running.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Warriors Hamstring you as well, so pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Insane Ghoul haunts the chapel. If he isn't inside, check around its walls.",w=1},{t="An Old History Book can drop from almost any Duskwood mob. Use it from your bags to start this.",u=2794},{t="The dagger drops from the Lost Stalker, a ghost found a little north of Darkshire or north of the Raven Hill road.",tp=1},{t="Use Ira's Dagger from your bags to start this.",u=281143},{t="Stitches, a level 35 elite, walks this road to Darkshire once someone ends Abercrombie's chain. Keep well clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="If Watcher Dodds is missing, Stitches may have killed him. Wait for his respawn.",tp=1},{t="The Memory of Valor is inside the small house at Raven Hill.",w=1},{t="Bliztik is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Bliztik sells Healing Potions in small numbers. Buy any he has.",tp=1},{t="Abercrombie's shack stands north of Raven Hill Cemetery.",w=1},{t="Cooks: the dire wolves here drop Lean Wolf Flanks for Seasoned Wolf Kabobs. Keep them.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: keep a Small Venom Sac. With First Aid 80 it makes Anti-Venom for Touch of Zanzil.",tp=1},{t="Keep 6 Gooey Spider Legs from these spiders. Chef Grual asks for them later.",tp=1},{t="The Old Footlocker is on the floor inside the Moonbrook Schoolhouse.",w=1},{t="Daphne Stilwell paces her field. Look round it if she isn't at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Daphne Stilwell wanders around her field, so she may be a few steps from the arrow.",w=1},{t="Daphne Stilwell not here? Another player has taken this quest. Daphne Stilwell is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Defias Raiders (17-18) attack Daphne in three waves of 3, 4 and 5. If she or you die, the quest fails.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The note is in a heap of Burned-Out Remains north-west of Moonbrook. Click the heap.",w=1},{t="You hand it in at other Burned-Out Remains, in the southern Barrens, when your road passes there in your 30s.",tp=1},{t="Chef Grual works in the inn's kitchen.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Targorr the Dread is an elite inside the Stormwind Stockade dungeon. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You finish it inside Stormwind Stockades, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Drudgers and Bashers share spawn points. If Drudgers run short, kill Bashers to bring more.",tp=1},{t="Miners: Copper and Tin Veins in the cave can give Rethban Ore as well.",tp=1},{t="Blackrock Outrunners cast Net, which roots you. Running from a bad pull is harder here.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blind Mary is indoors.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Black Ravagers roam the road from Darkshire to Raven Hill and the woods toward the Yorgen Farmstead.",tp=1},{t="The Mound of loose dirt is behind the old stump on Sven's farm.",w=1},{t="Stealthed Defias prowl the farm and slow you, and fights near the barn pull mobs through its wall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bliztik is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Abercrombie's shack stands north of Raven Hill Cemetery.",w=1},{t="Starving Dire Wolves notice you from farther away than most wolves. Give them extra room as you pass.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Rabies, from the Rabid Dire Wolves, halves your health regen for 10 minutes. Expect longer rests.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Farley is inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",w=1},{t="The Storage Chest is upstairs in the Lion's Pride Inn.",w=1},{t="Brother Paxton is in Northshire Abbey's library, on the ground floor.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ursula Deline is downstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Brother Kristoff stands outside the Cathedral of Light, in Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="Duthorian Rall is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Milton Sheaf is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Tavernkeep Smitts is inside the inn.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mor'Ladim, a level 35 elite, roams Raven Hill Cemetery. Look for him before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mor'Ladim, a level 35 elite, walks a loop round the cemetery. Look around before every pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Warders are down in the Dawning Wood Catacombs. Raiders and Healers walk the graves above.",w=1},{t="These skeletons run 26 to 29, above your level here. Pair up if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mages: Skeletal Warders can shield themselves from Fire and Frost, and Counterspell won't stop it.",tp=1},{t="Tavernkeep Smitts is inside the inn.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Bellygrub (level 24) has far more health than a boar should, and uses Charge and Tremor, an area hit.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lead him into Lakeshire for the guards' help, but deal most of the damage yourself or he drops no tusk.",tp=1},{t="Pull Yowler, then back off until the gnolls with him lose interest and go back.",tp=1},{t="Lieutenant Fangore fights with 2 more gnolls at his side. Treat it as a group fight, or leave it out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Priests and Warlocks: Fangore takes no Shadow damage. Solo, skip him and drop the quest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Morganth, a level 26 elite, holds the Tower of Ilgalar with his Servants. Keep clear of the tower.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Lion Statue stands among Shadowhide gnolls of 23 to 26, beside Morganth's Tower of Ilgalar.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Empty Jar sits on a barrel on the tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23, fill the tower. Bring a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You'll find Gath'Ilzogg inside Stonewatch Keep.",w=1},{t="Gath'Ilzogg, a level 26 elite, stands among elite guards. Bring a group of five.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tharil'zun, a level 24 elite, is a very hard fight. Bring help.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hunters and Warlocks: send the pet up to pull Tharil'zun and wait on the ground below him.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Shadowcaster here is an elite, level 22 to 23. Bring a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Render's Camp mixes Champions (24-25) with Summoners, Trackers and the rare Kazon (27). Pull from the edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Corporal Keeshan waits at the far end of the Render's Rock cave.",w=1},{t="Corporal Keeshan not here? Another player has taken this quest. Corporal Keeshan is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Out of the cave, Keeshan's path runs close to many mobs. Rest to full before you start, and expect extra pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Stormwind Stockades, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Stormwind Stockades, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bailiff Conacher is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Giant Wetlands Crocolisks cast Tendon Rip, a long slow. You can't outrun one once it lands.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mosshide Trappers net you in place, and Brutes (25), Mystics (26) and the Alpha (27) share their camps.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sida's Bag is a rare drop. Kill every ooze you pass; most of them gather round Ironbeard's Tomb.",tp=1},{t="Perfect Razormaw Eggs lie on the ground across Raptor Ridge, among the Razormaws.",w=1},{t="Raptor Ridge's Razormaws are 27 to 29, and the Razormaw Matriarch (31) is a rare there. Pull one at a time; they hit hard for their level.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dal Bloodclaw is 25 and the village's furbolgs 23 to 24. Clear his path before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dal Bloodclaw patrols Thistlefur Village. Look along his path if he isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Plant Bundles are small, brown and half sunk in the ground, easy to walk past.",tp=1},{t="Herbalists: Find Herbs shows the Plant Bundles on the minimap.",tp=1},{t="The Ancient Statuette is small and lies on the ground at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Talen talks for about 20 seconds after the hand-in before he offers Ruuzel.",tp=1},{t="Ruuzel walks with a Wrathtail Myrmidon and a Wrathtail Sea Witch, and they fight together.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill one escort, run out until the others reset, then pull again.",tp=1},{t="Lady Vespia, a rare in the same area, can drop the Ring of Zoram too.",tp=1},{t="A thrown bomb or grenade pulls Ruuzel on her own, away from her escorts.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Saltspittle Oracles heal and hit you with an instant shock every few seconds. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pelturas talks for about 25 seconds after the hand-in. Wait for him to offer Elune's Tear.",tp=1},{t="Elune's Tear is a small blue stone lying on the lake's central island.",w=1},{t="The Worn Chest sits in a small glade west of the road to Felwood.",w=1},{t="Terrowulf worgen of 28 to 29 from the Howling Vale stand a short way west of the chest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About a dozen Terrowulf worgen of 28 to 30 and the rare Packlord (32) crowd round the tome.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Tome of Mel'Thandris lies on a table at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Anilia stands in the middle of Xavian's satyrs, 28 to 30. Clear your way to her one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Search Satyrnaar, the Bleakheart satyrs' ruins just west of Forest Song, for the Vine-Wrapped Scroll.",w=1},{t="Tell us where you found the Vine-Wrapped Scroll in Satyrnaar.",a=1},{t="Geltharis is level 32 but casts nothing. Clear the Xavian satyrs round him first and start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Bottle of Disease sits on a table in the Forsaken camp.",w=1},{t="About seven Forsaken of 28 to 30 hold the camp, and some of them hide in stealth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The slimes roam all round the Forsaken camp. Its Forsaken are 28 to 30, and some lurk in stealth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Hidden Shrine sits on a hilltop. The path up starts on its south-east side. Click the shrine to hand in.",w=1},{t="Pelturas talks for a few seconds before he offers The Ruins of Stardust.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Kimlya stands in the raised room off the inn's north side. Take the left ramp from mid-hall.",w=1},{t="Stardust Covered Bushes are spread over the whole island. Work your way around it.",tp=1},{t="Kaela Shadowspear stands on the rise above the valley into Windshear Crag.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks stands by a goblin hut a short way north of Gaxim.",w=1},{t="Piznik is inside the Windshear Mine, west of its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine holds about 60 kobolds of 20 to 23, Geomancers among them. Clear a path in and out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds come at Piznik in waves while he mines, casters among them. Eat and drink between waves.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sorrow Wing, a level 27 rare elite wyvern, can spawn by the lake in the middle of the Pridewing hills. Keep clear of it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Collin Mauren in Stormwind takes the crystals. Hand them in on your next visit there.",tp=1},{t="Their Frost Nova roots you in place, so running won't save you. Pull the elementals one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Some of the elementals are underwater, and your breath runs down while you fight them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Once you hold 5 Intact Elemental Bracers, use the Divining Scroll.",u=5456},{t="No vendor sells water breathing. The Auction House has Draughts of Water Breathing (30 minutes each); Warlocks can cast Unending Breath instead.",tp=1},{t="If you carry an Elixir of Water Breathing, drink it before you dive.",u=5996},{t="Foulweald Ursas Thrash for three hits at once. Fight them at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Totemics share spawn points with Warriors. If Totemics run short, kill Warriors to free the spots.",tp=1},{t="Every Foulweald here is 23 to 25. Pull single furbolgs from the camp's edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shadethicket Oracle is a hard fight alone. Bring a partner if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards hold the Barrens' north gate, just west of the way in. Keep to the arrow.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards hold the Barrens' north gate, just west of the way in. Keep to the arrow.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Satyrnaar's Bleakheart satyrs are 26 to 28. Prince Raze, a level 32 rare, can spawn among them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krolg stands at his hut on the south side of Mystral Lake.",w=1},{t="Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation near Krolg. He only talks to you in furbolg form.",u=5462},{t="Ran Bloodtooth, level 30, stands with five of his guards (levels 27 to 28) close round him. Thin them out before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Loot Ran Bloodtooth's Skull from him. The next step of the chain asks you to bring it to Raene.",tp=1},{t="Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation again before you talk to Krolg. The furbolg form lasts 3 minutes.",u=5462},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Velinde's Locker is past the overhead bridge, up in the Sentinels' bunkhouse.",w=1},{t="The key pieces drop from crawlers, murlocs and striders of level 18-21. Below 20, bring two more players.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Raging Reef Crawlers (20-21) Thrash for two extra swings at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The sunken ship breaks line of sight with Greymist Oracles and stops their Lightning Bolts.",tp=1},{t="Greymist Oracles cast a heavy Lightning Bolt and heal themselves. Burst them down first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Greymist Tidehunters' melee poison ticks for 30 seconds. Let it wear off before the next pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Threshwackonator 4100 is a level 20 elite that turns on you at Gelkak. At 28 you can kill it alone; start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="It turns on you once you reach Gelkak, so start the walk back at full health.",tp=1},{t="Druids: Entangling Roots holds it in place once it turns, so you can back off and cast.",tp=1},{t="The Threshwackonator 4100 waits on the beach south of Gelkak. Talk to it to start.",w=1},{t="This quest gives you a Draught of Water Breathing. Hold on to it: quests under water come later.",tp=1},{t="Gyromast's Key has no use after this. Destroy it to free the slot.",tp=1},{t="Grundel Harkin stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Thran Khorman stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Durnan Furcutter stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Alamar Grimm is on Anvilmar's upper floor.",w=1},{t="Teo Hammerstorm stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Warriors, Shamans and Warlocks: sell the wolves' gray drops. Your first trainer spell costs about 10 copper.",tp=1},{t="Wear any cloth armor the wolves drop for a slot you have empty. Sell the rest.",tp=1},{t="If you can't afford the 15 waters, sell the gray drops from a few more Ragged Young Wolves.",tp=1},{t="The Frostmane Novices are deep inside the troll cave.",w=1},{t="Alamar Grimm is on Anvilmar's upper floor.",w=1},{t="Timed: 5 minutes. Walk straight into Anvilmar to Durnan Furcutter."},{t="The 5-minute timer keeps running if you log out. If it fails, Nori Pridedrift gives the quest again.",tp=1},{t="Durnan Furcutter stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Teo Hammerstorm stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Thorgas Grimson stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Bromos Grummner stands just inside Anvilmar's door.",w=1},{t="Marryk Nurribit stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Alamar Grimm is on Anvilmar's upper floor.",w=1},{t="Felix Whindlebolt stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Frostmane whelps and Novices, levels 3 and 4, crowd the cave all the way to Grik'nir.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Grik'nir the Cold waits at the far east end of the troll cave.",w=1},{t="Grik'nir the Cold is level 5, and his Frost Shock halves your speed for 8 seconds. You can't outrun him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Timed: 5 minutes. Walk straight into Anvilmar to Durnan Furcutter."},{t="The 5-minute timer keeps running if you log out. If it fails, Nori Pridedrift gives the quest again.",tp=1},{t="Branstock Khalder stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Teo Hammerstorm stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Durnan Furcutter stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Solm Hargrin stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Thran Khorman stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Felix Whindlebolt stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Branstock Khalder stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Grund Drokda stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Use the Earth Sapta beside the Spirit Stone to call the Minor Manifestation of Earth.",u=6635},{t="The Spirit Stone stands in the hills north-west of Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Grund Drokda stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Felix Whindlebolt stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Teo Hammerstorm stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Branstock Khalder stands inside Anvilmar.",w=1},{t="Boosted Rest shows up after about a minute of sitting by Eric's fire.",tp=1},{t="No credit after sitting? Abandon the quest, take it again from Eric and sit back down.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tannok Frosthammer is inside the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Maxan Anvol is inside the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Maxan Anvol is inside the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Innkeeper Belm is inside the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Gremlock Pilsnor is inside the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Gremlock charges 1 silver to teach Cooking.",tp=1},{t="Every kind of Crag Boar drops Chunk of Boar Meat. Keep 4 for Stocking Jetsteam and cook the rest.",tp=1},{t="Seasoned Wolf Kabobs in Darkshire, later in the guide, needs Cooking 50. Cook as you level.",tp=1},{t="Buy the Balanced Throwing Dagger here. It does three times the damage of your Small Throwing Knife.",tp=1},{t="Hogral Bakkan is in the distillery's back room.",w=1},{t="Magis Sparkmantle is upstairs in the distillery.",w=1},{t="Azar Stronghammer is upstairs in the distillery.",w=1},{t="Mountaineer Dolf stands outdoors in Kharanos, south-west of the distillery.",w=1},{t="Ingrid Dunwald is upstairs in the distillery.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Belm keeps the inn inside the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Granis Swiftaxe is indoors at the distillery.",w=1},{t="Blacksmithing lets you make Rough Sharpening Stones (blades) and Weightstones (blunt), +2 damage for 30 minutes.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Young Black Bears drop Thick Bear Fur only while this quest is in your log. Kill the ones you pass from now on.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Yarr Hammerstone is on the lower floor. Loslor Rudge at the depot sells the Mining Pick you'll need.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Miners: the Copper Veins round the Grizzled Den give Rough Stone for sharpening stones and weightstones.",tp=1},{t="The den is crowded with wendigos up to level 8, Wendigo Shamans among them. Frosthowl (9) holds its west end.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Old Icebeard, a level 11 elite, has his own cave south-west of the den. Don't follow wendigos in there.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Flintfire's Shipments are crates on the floor of the Grizzled Den, from its mouth to the back.",w=1},{t="Cornelius is dead. Look for his body inside the den.",w=1},{t="Deeper in, the Young Wendigos (5-6) give way to Wendigos (6-7).",tp=1},{t="Hunters: Hegnar Rumbleshot sells the Ornate Blunderbuss, 3.0 DPS at level 4, twice your starting gun.",tp=1},{t="Pilot Stonegear stands at Steelgrill's Depot, east of Kharanos.",w=1},{t="Hogral Bakkan is in the distillery's back room.",w=1},{t="Azar Stronghammer is upstairs in the distillery.",w=1},{t="Granis Swiftaxe is indoors at the distillery.",w=1},{t="Buy a Thunder Ale from Innkeeper Belm first. Giving it to Jarven distracts him.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Belm is inside the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Jarven Thunderbrew is downstairs, in the distillery's cellar.",w=1},{t="The barrel is in the distillery's cellar, next to Jarven Thunderbrew.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hogral Bakkan is in the distillery's back room.",w=1},{t="Azar Stronghammer is upstairs in the distillery.",w=1},{t="Granis Swiftaxe is indoors at the distillery.",w=1},{t="Magis Sparkmantle is upstairs in the distillery.",w=1},{t="Razzle Sprysprocket is inside a house in Kharanos.",w=1},{t="Shimmerweed Baskets on the ground hold Shimmerweed too.",tp=1},{t="Frostmane Seers are level 9 and cast Lightning Bolt from range. Pull them out of the huts one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The den is crowded with wendigos up to level 8, Wendigo Shamans among them. Frosthowl (9) holds its west end.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Old Icebeard is a level 11 elite, too strong to fight alone, and the Meat Locker sits in his cave. Wait outside until he walks out on his patrol, then slip in behind him, loot the locker and leave. Or bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mages and Warlocks: Polymorph or Fear him long enough to loot the locker.",tp=1},{t="The Meat Locker lies deep inside Old Icebeard's cave, near its far end.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gibblewilt, a level 11 rare gnome, can turn up among the Leper Gnomes. Pull him on his own.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Headhunters are inside the cave. The exploration credit is deep in, down the left-hand passages.",w=1},{t="Dropping into the hold from the slope above lands you among the trolls. Clear your way in on foot.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Great Father Arctikus, a level 11 rare, can wander into the nook. Let him walk off before you go down.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hogral Bakkan is in a back room of the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Maxan Anvol is inside the Thunderbrew Distillery.",w=1},{t="Magis Sparkmantle is upstairs in the distillery.",w=1},{t="Razzle Sprysprocket is inside a house in Kharanos.",w=1},{t="Target a Large Crag Boar, then use the Taming Rod from your bags. It reaches 30 yards.",u=15911},{t="Target a Snow Leopard, then use the second Taming Rod from your bags.",u=15913},{t="Target an Ice Claw Bear, then use the third Taming Rod from your bags.",u=15908},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Belia Thundergranite is in the Hall of Arms, in the Military Ward.",w=1},{t="The Fallen Logs lie on the ground across the slopes south and west of the Misty Pine Refuge.",w=1},{t="Vagash is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Vagash is a level 11 elite. Fight him down at the ranch with its defenders, not up on the hill.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Vagash is up the dirt path on the hill north of Amberstill Ranch.",tp=1},{t="Drag him downhill to Rudra Amberstill and the guard posted at the ranch's south end. With their help you can kill him alone.",tp=1},{t="The kill counts if you do more than half his damage.",tp=1},{t="Glacial Roar stuns everyone near Vagash for 3 seconds. Fight him beside the guards, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Vagash is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Coldridge Hammer is a two-handed mace. Paladins can use it now; Warriors and Shamans may need to train the skill.",tp=1},{t="Vagash is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Pick Farsen's farsight option first. Press Escape once the objective updates, then hand it in.",tp=1},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Skullthumpers fill the quarry pit and the mine; the Bonesnappers are mostly inside the mine.",w=1},{t="The Rockjaw Bonesnappers are inside the quarry mine.",w=1},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Rockjaw Ambushers drop the Empty Powder Keg, but rarely.",tp=1},{t="Dark Iron Spies drop the Dark Iron Map. Use it to start this quest.",u=274268},{t="Pilot Hammerfoot is through the tunnel north-east of the quarry, at the end of the eastern road.",w=1},{t="Free a bag slot before you click the corpse. A Pilot's Revenge gives you Hildelve's Journal.",tp=1},{t="Mangeclaw comes down to the corpse once you've taken this quest.",tp=1},{t="The Craftsman's Dagger (6.8 DPS, +1 Agility, no level requirement) holds up well past this zone.",tp=1},{t="Mountaineer Barleybrew guards the South Gate, the pass into Loch Modan. Leave the pilot's pass the way you came in, then go up the next pass to the south.",w=1},{t="Brock Stoneseeker is usually downstairs inside his building, though he sometimes stands outside it.",w=1},{t="Mountaineer Kadrell walks up and down Thelsamar's road. Look along it if he isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Yanni Stoutheart sells the Simple Wood and the Flint and Tinder a Basic Campfire needs.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Golnir Bouldertoe is inside his shop on the north side of the Great Forge.",w=1},{t="Hulfdan Blackbeard is downstairs.",w=1},{t="Senator Barin Redstone is in the High Seat, Ironforge's throne room.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Monty stands on the middle platform of the Deeprun Tram. The way in is in Tinker Town.",w=1},{t="Use the Rat Catcher's Flute beside each Deeprun Rat along the tracks. Lead all five back to Monty.",u=17117},{t="Nipsy waits on the platform at the Stormwind end of the tram.",w=1},{t="Grimand Elmore is in the Dwarven District, a short walk west of the tram.",w=1},{t="High Priestess Laurena is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Ursula Deline is downstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Ilsa Corbin is upstairs in the Command Center in Old Town.",w=1},{t="Harry Burlguard is inside the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town.",w=1},{t="Bartleby yields at 1% health. Stop attacking and talk to him.",tp=1},{t="Fear Morgan and keep him feared while you kill Surena.",tp=1},{t="Surena Caledon is inside the farmhouse at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch.",w=1},{t="Morgan the Collector and Erlan Drudgemoor stand with Surena, so expect all three at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gakin the Darkbinder is downstairs in The Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Use the Bloodstone Choker in The Slaughtered Lamb's lowest room.",u=6928},{t="Bruegs Kindleborn is in a cave near the top of the mountain by South Gate Pass. A trail climbs to it.",w=1},{t="The way down from Bruegs's cave is steep. Walk it; a careless jump means fall damage.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Tiza Battleforge is upstairs. Take the staircase that starts beneath her ledge.",w=1},{t="Tiza Battleforge is upstairs.",w=1},{t="John Turner walks a stretch of the outer ring by the Auction House. Look along it if he isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Carry 10 Linen Cloth here and this hands in on the spot. Troggs and other humanoids drop it.",tp=1},{t="Tiza Battleforge is upstairs. Take the staircase that starts beneath her ledge.",w=1},{t="Muiredon Battleforge is upstairs too, close to Tiza.",w=1},{t="Braldir Ashmantle is up a mountain trail south-west of Thelsamar.",tp=1},{t="Mountaineer Kadrell patrols Thelsamar's road, so he may have walked off from the arrow.",tp=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Yanni Stoutheart sells the Simple Wood and the Flint and Tinder a Basic Campfire needs.",tp=1},{t="Vidra Hearthstove is inside the Stoutlager Inn.",w=1},{t="The Mountain Boars drop Chunk of Boar Meat too. Keep it for Cooking.",tp=1},{t="Mountain Boars open with a Charge from range that hits for 40 to 100.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Rugelfuss is upstairs, at the very top of the southern guard tower.",w=1},{t="Use the Ceramic Jar on the snow where South Gate Pass opens into Loch Modan.",u=279380},{t="The Jar of Snow expires after 10 minutes. Head for Norric Lochthane as soon as it's full.",tp=1},{t="Stonesplinter Shamans and Bonesnappers of 15-16 stand round the Blastencapper at the camp's east end.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nillen Andemar sells the Heavy Spiked Mace (level 14, +6 Strength) in limited stock. Buy it while he has one.",tp=1},{t="Mountaineer Stormpike is upstairs in the Algaz Station bunker.",w=1},{t="The mine is packed with Tunnel Rat kobolds up to level 14. Geomancers cast Fire Blast from range.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Miners' League Crates stand all along Silver Stream Mine's tunnels, down to its south end.",w=1},{t="Mages: Tunnel Rat Geomancers ward themselves from fire, so use Frostbolt on them.",tp=1},{t="Fire Tar comes from Tunnel Rat Geomancers, who are only inside Silver Stream Mine, a short way in.",w=1},{t="Geomancers cast Fire Blast for 20 to 30 and ward themselves from fire. Earth Shock still lands.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gothor Brumn repairs gear as well.",tp=1},{t="Troggs and Scouts respawn quickly near 26.7, 56.9, enough to finish both quests there. Rest away from that spot.",tp=1},{t="Stonesplinter Scouts Shoot from range for 14-20 a hit. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Fire Sapta beside the rock statue near Braldir Ashmantle. That calls the Minor Manifestation of Fire.",u=6636},{t="The brazier for the Ember stands right beside the rock statue, a little up the trail from Braldir.",w=1},{t="Bruegs's cave sits high above the pass. Take the trail down; jumping off the ledge means fall damage.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bruegs Kindleborn is in a cave high on the mountain above the South Gate Pass.",w=1},{t="Muiredon Battleforge is upstairs, near Tiza Battleforge.",w=1},{t="Jern Hornhelm walks in and out of this house.",w=1},{t="Stonesplinter Geomancers and Diggers of 17-19 work the dig just east of here. Keep to its west edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jern Hornhelm walks in and out of this house.",w=1},{t="Prospector Stormpike is in the Hall of Explorers.",w=1},{t="Jubahl Corpseseeker sells the Grimoires that teach your demons their new ranks.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Jern Hornhelm walks in and out of this house.",w=1},{t="Miran not here? Another player has taken this quest. Miran is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Stay beside Miran all the way to the dig. Dark Iron Ambushers, level 10, attack the shipment.",tp=1},{t="Gradok, Thragomm and Haren Swifthoof, elites of level 19-21, patrol the loch's east shore. Stay off their path.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The 15 minutes include the walk back to Daryl. If they run out, abandon the quest and take it again.",tp=1},{t="Loch Crocolisks crowd the island at the centre of the loch.",w=1},{t="Young Threshadons of 19-20 swim south and west of the island. Swim over from the east shore, level with it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A rare Large Loch Crocolisk, level 22, can lie on the east shore facing the island.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Daggerfang roams the east shore of the loch, so it may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Mountaineer Ylva lies dead in Stonesplinter Valley. Her body carries the banner.",w=1},{t="Use the Banner of Ironforge by Ylva's body. That calls Headsplitter out to fight.",u=253247},{t="Grawmug (17) never leaves Gnasher and Brawler (16), so all three fight you at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Rugelfuss is upstairs, at the very top of the southern guard tower.",w=1},{t="Grawmug (17) never leaves Gnasher and Brawler (16), so all three fight you at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It starts from an item you find in the Hall of Thanes, so only after a run there.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Hall of Thanes, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Afadra is up the switchback ramp from Thom Filch.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Hall of Thanes, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="King Magni is in the throne room, back up the winding passage you came down.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Hall of Thanes, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It starts from an item you find in the Hall of Thanes, so only after a run there.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Mo'grosh ogre is an elite of level 18-20. Take this only with a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bingles' tools lie on the ground in the Stonesplinter trogg camp south-east of the dam.",w=1},{t="Stonesplinter Shamans and Bonesnappers of 15-16 stand round the Blastencapper at the camp's east end.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Young Threshadons of 19-20 swim south and west of the island. Swim over from the east shore, level with it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A rare Large Loch Crocolisk, level 22, can lie on the east shore facing the island.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Abandon and retake the quest if its 12 minutes run out before you're back.",tp=1},{t="Ol' Sooty is an elite of level 20. Take this only with a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Young Threshadons of 19-20 swim south and west of the island. Swim over from the east shore, level with it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A rare Large Loch Crocolisk, level 22, can lie on the east shore facing the island.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The dig's troggs are level 17 to 20: Geomancers, Diggers and Berserk Troggs. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mo'grosh Brutes live only in the caves. Hunt them in the two small caves and stay out of the north-east one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The starter turns up at one of several spots in the loch. Look for the quest marker on your minimap.",tp=1},{t="Young Threshadons in the loch are level 19-20. Give them a wide berth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Discarded Fishing Toolbox lies on the lake bed, underwater.",w=1},{t="Two Dark Iron Sappers, level 17, stand at the barrel. Dark Iron Insurgents of 18-19 camp just east.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hulfdan Blackbeard is downstairs.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ol' Sooty, a level 20 elite, often walks the trail below his cave. Watch the trail ahead as you climb.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only if you killed Ol' Sooty in Loch Modan and have his head.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only if you killed Ol' Sooty in Loch Modan and have his head.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Sneed and his Shredder, a level 20 elite, are inside the Deadmines. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wilder Thistlenettle is inside a building in the Dwarven District.",w=1},{t="The Miners' Union Cards drop from level 18 elite undead in the mine before the Deadmines portal. Take a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Collecting Memories and Oh Brother are both finished in the mine before the Deadmines portal.",tp=1},{t="Foreman Thistlenettle is a level 20 elite in that same mine. Take a group for him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Rift Spawns are inside the Blue Recluse, the tavern in the Mage Quarter.",w=1},{t="Read the Cantation of Manifestation inside the tavern to make the Rift Spawns show.",u=7308},{t="When a Rift Spawn falls stunned, use the Chest of Containment Coffers on it.",u=7247},{t="Take the Gatehouse Shipment up to the second floor of Trias' shop and use it at the door.",u=277198},{t="Elaine Trias waits in the shop below the door.",w=1},{t="Guard Parker stands by the traders' camp where the road from Elwynn enters Redridge.",w=1},{t="Only for Blacksmithing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Darcy walks about inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="The Wanted Poster is just outside the Lakeshire Town Hall's door.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Chef Breanna is inside the house just west of the inn.",w=1},{t="The Glinting Mud has several spawn spots in the lake. If it isn't at one, try the next.",tp=1},{t="The Glinting Mud lies on the lake bed, underwater.",w=1},{t="Timed: 60 minutes. Go straight to the first fork in the Rethban Caverns and back. Dying and releasing fails it."},{t="Yorus Barleybrew is inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Redridge Bashers (19-20) and Drudgers (20-21) crowd the caverns' mouth. Clear a way you can run back along.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Wiley is upstairs in the inn.",w=1},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Look for the oat sacks along the farm fences and next to the buildings.",tp=1},{t="Each sack takes 5 seconds to open. Clear mobs close by first so nothing hits you mid-cast.",tp=1},{t="At the Jansen Stead well, west of the Furlbrows, take a sample with the kit.",u=254545},{t="Renzik is upstairs in the SI:7 building in Old Town.",w=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="The Defias Messenger sets off from Moonbrook and walks the road north past Jangolode Mine.",tp=1},{t="He respawns 4 to 5 minutes after a kill. If the road is empty, wait at Moonbrook.",tp=1},{t="Twenty-eight murlocs along Westfall's southern beaches, with Old Murk-Eye walking there. Good XP, but slow and risky alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tidehunters and Oracles (16-19) hold the southern beaches, and Old Murk-Eye (20) walks there. Pull singles.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Twenty-eight murlocs along Westfall's southern beaches, with Old Murk-Eye walking there. Good XP, but slow and risky alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Twenty-eight murlocs along Westfall's southern beaches, with Old Murk-Eye walking there. Good XP, but slow and risky alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Old Murk-Eye walks the whole Longshore. If he isn't out, he respawns at the southernmost murloc camp.",tp=1},{t="Old Murk-Eye is level 20 and walks among Tidehunters of 18 to 19. Pull him alone, clear of their camps.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Defias respawn faster while you keep killing here. Stay in one spot and watch for new ones spawning beside you.",tp=1},{t="Defias Trappers root you with Net for 9 seconds and backstab. Fight them one at a time and face them.",tp=1},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="If the Defias Traitor isn't beside Sentinel Hill, wait for him to respawn.",tp=1},{t="Defias in Moonbrook rush the Traitor when he arrives. Stay at his side the whole way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Murloc Warriors and Hunters (15-17) spawn on this beach. Clear the way to the footlocker one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Twenty-eight murlocs along Westfall's southern beaches, with Old Murk-Eye walking there. Good XP, but slow and risky alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Foe Reaper 4000, a level 20 rare, walks the fields around this barrel. Spot it before you click.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="At the Molsen Farm well, take a sample with the kit from your bags.",u=254545},{t="Captain Sanders' chest sits on the small island off the coast. Swim out to it.",w=1},{t="Twenty-eight murlocs along Westfall's southern beaches, with Old Murk-Eye walking there. Good XP, but slow and risky alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Twenty-eight murlocs along Westfall's southern beaches, with Old Murk-Eye walking there. Good XP, but slow and risky alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Guard Parker stands by the traders' camp where the road from Elwynn enters Redridge.",w=1},{t="Murlocs on this shore respawn very fast. Move away from the water before you rest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The same murlocs drop the fins and Selling Fish's Spotted Sunfish.",tp=1},{t="Incinerator Gar'im is inside a cave in Render's Valley, southeast Redridge.",w=1},{t="Gar'im (level 23) fights beside his Shadowcasters. Bring a group of four, or leave this one out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Grunts and Outrunners (19-21) stand close together here, with a few Summoners (22-23). Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supplies come from Grain Sacks, Meat Haunches and Water Barrels; weapons from Weapon Racks and loose Stolen Weapons.",tp=1},{t="An elite Lake Thresher swims a patrol over the Lost Tools. Wait for it to pass before you dive.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Oslow's toolbox is in a Sunken Chest on the lake bed, underwater.",w=1},{t="Opening the chest takes 5 seconds, so mind your breath.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Chef Breanna is inside the house just west of the inn.",w=1},{t="Darcy walks about inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gakin the Darkbinder is downstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Spackle also sells the Succubus's grimoires. Buy them, and the Voidwalker's if you have gold to spare.",tp=1},{t="Baros Alexston is inside the building at the edge of Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="Duthorian Rall is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="If Duthorian offers nothing, use the Tome of Valor he gave you from your bags.",u=6776},{t="Milton Sheaf is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Donyal Tovald is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Brother Paxton is inside Northshire Abbey.",w=1},{t="Theocritus waits on the Tower of Azora's highest level. Climb all the way up.",w=1},{t="Check Dawn Brightstar's limited stock of scrolls and potions while you're here.",tp=1},{t="Raise Lockpicking to 80 on the Practice Lockboxes around the mill first. The Poisons chain needs it later.",tp=1},{t="This chain is how you learn Poisons.",tp=1},{t="The Malformed Defias Drone hits far too hard to fight. Pick Pocket the key from Stealth; if Stealth breaks, Sprint.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Drone starts at the tower door, then walks laps round the building.",tp=1},{t="With a dagger, open on each Sentry or Patroller with Ambush. Clearing them is slower than sneaking, and safer.",tp=1},{t="Mobs on the floor above can hit you through the floor. Check what's overhead before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Duskwood Chest is on a bookshelf one floor below the top. Climb onto a chair, then a lamp, then the shelf.",tp=1},{t="Looting the journal blocks Stealth for a while, and Sentries left on that floor wait for you to climb down.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Drones, the Malformed one too, can be waiting at the door on your way out. Keep Sprint ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dwarves: Stoneform clears Touch of Zanzil.",tp=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="Gnomes: Doc Mixilpixil's quests end in a cure for Touch of Zanzil. Anti-Venom, a Paladin or a Druid works too.",tp=1},{t="The start of a Stormwind errand whose last step needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Doc Mixilpixil is in the cellar below SI:7. Take the stairs down.",w=1},{t="The start of a Stormwind errand whose last step needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Part of a Stormwind errand whose last step needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Part of a Stormwind errand whose last step needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Part of a Stormwind errand whose last step needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The spool of thread lies in the shop by the bridge from Cathedral Square to the park.",w=1},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Billibub Cogspinner in the Dwarven District sells Bronze Tubes. If he has none, try the Auction House.",tp=1},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Use the Eau de Mixilpixil the Doc gives you. It clears Touch of Zanzil.",u=8432},{t="It needs a Bronze Tube and silk thread from Stormwind's shops or the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Edwin VanCleef (level 21 elite) is the Deadmines' last boss. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Scout Riell stands with Gryan at the top of the Sentinel Hill tower.",w=1},{t="Outside the dungeon, bandanas drop from Diggers and Workers in the mine under Moonbrook, among a few elites.",tp=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Keep the Flasks of Oil the Harvest Watchers drop. Captain Grayson at the lighthouse asks for five.",tp=1},{t="Foe Reaper 4000, a level 20 rare, roams the fields round these golems. Watch for it between pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Isosprings and Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. Look on the Auction House, or hand it in later if you find them.",tp=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ozwin Ironsprocket hides in the barn at Saldean's Farm.",w=1},{t="Golem Isosprings and Harvester Gyrostabilizers drop rarely. The Auction House often has them.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Twenty-eight murlocs along Westfall's southern beaches, with Old Murk-Eye walking there. Good XP, but slow and risky alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Defias Highwaymen (17-18) backstab for double damage. Keep them in front of you and pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle is up the stairs, on the Sentinel Hill tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="About 40 Defias Pillagers and Looters (levels 13 to 15) fill Moonbrook. Clear around each crate before you open it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Baros Alexston is inside the building at the edge of Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wilder Thistlenettle is inside a building in the Dwarven District.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Deadmines, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hervdana is inside a cave, up a ramp.",w=1},{t="Use the Unfilled Brown Waterskin from your bags at the foot of the waterfall.",u=265732},{t="Hervdana is back up the ramp, inside the cave above the falls.",w=1},{t="The road north passes right by the Dragonmaw orcs of Angerfang Encampment (28 to 29), with Highland Spiders (28) just west of it. Stay on the road and keep moving.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dewin Shimmerdawn sells a few Healing Potions. Buy what you can afford.",tp=1},{t="Gobbler wanders a short way around the marsh. If he isn't on his spot, look nearby.",tp=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kixxle sells Healing Potions in short supply. Buy what you can afford before the gnoll camps.",tp=1},{t="About 35 stalkers of 21 to 22 fill the tunnels, and the rare Leech Widow, level 24, roams them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The gnolls here drop a lot of Wool Cloth. Keep it for First Aid bandages.",tp=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jubahl Corpseseeker sells the Grimoires that teach your demons their new ranks.",tp=1},{t="High Priestess Mims stands with the priest trainers in the Mystic Ward.",w=1},{t="Not confirmed in Forever yet. If High Priestess Mims doesn't offer it, carry on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Not confirmed in Forever yet. If High Priestess Mims doesn't offer it, carry on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="High Priest Rohan stands with the priest trainers in the Mystic Ward.",w=1},{t="Opening the Sealed Barrel takes 5 seconds. Clear the murlocs around it first.",tp=1},{t="Merrin Rockweaver is inside the small cave at the dig site.",w=1},{t="The piles lie on the harbor floor, 10 to 20 yards down in the bay west of the docks. Surface for air between them.",w=1},{t="Young crocolisks (21-22) swim the channel east of town, and Bluegill Raiders (28-29) hold the south shore. Stay in the west bay.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Stoutfist is on the top floor of Menethil Keep, up the stairs.",w=1},{t="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is inside Stormwind Keep, in the throne room.",w=1},{t="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker stands inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Level 40 Horde guards stand on the Gold Road north of the Crossroads. Keep east of the road, out of their sight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Takar the Seer is in Horde land. Keep well away from Horde guards and towns on the way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards stand on the Gold Road north of the Crossroads. Keep east of the road, out of their sight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Unlit Torch lies on a table beside the Archaeologist's Cart, outside the house.",w=1},{t="Light a campfire and use the Unlit Torch from your bags beside it to get a Burning Torch.",u=190307},{t="Set the Archaeologist's Cart alight with the Burning Torch from your bags.",u=190308},{t="The Wooden Figurine sits on a table upstairs in the house.",w=1},{t="No Cooking means no campfire of your own. The fire at Talen's camp, west of here, works too.",tp=1},{t="The Heartswood is the giant tree in the Ruins of Ordil'Aran.",w=1},{t="Gakin the Darkbinder is downstairs in The Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Spackle also sells the Succubus's grimoires. Buy them, and the Voidwalker's if you have gold to spare.",tp=1},{t="Use the Heartswood Core at the summoning circle, then kill the Succubus it calls.",u=6913},{t="The summoning circle is in the Slaughtered Lamb's lowest room, down every flight of stairs.",w=1},{t="Use the Wooden Figurine at the same circle, then kill the Incubus it calls.",u=190186},{t="The Succubus hits much harder, but the Voidwalker keeps you alive longer. Use it on risky pulls.",tp=1},{t="Lord Ello Ebonlocke is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="If Stitches gets into Darkshire, Althea can be dead or stuck fighting him. Wait for her respawn.",tp=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors. Go into the building the arrow points at.",w=1},{t="Chef Grual only offers this at Cooking 50.",tp=1},{t="Chef Grual works in the inn's kitchen.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Elaine Carevin is indoors.",w=1},{t="Take this before you meet Sven: Elaine Carevin stops offering it once Sven's Revenge is in your log.",tp=1},{t="Herble sells the Bronze Tube in small numbers. Buy one if he has it; Viktori asks for it later.",tp=1},{t="Herble Baubbletump, next to Viktori, sells the Bronze Tube but keeps only two. If he is out, Billibub Cogspinner in Stormwind's Dwarven District stocks more."},{t="Blind Mary is indoors.",w=1},{t="Skeletal Mages cast Frostbolt, and their Frost Armor slows you as you hit them. Don't count on running.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Warriors Hamstring you as well, so pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Insane Ghoul haunts the chapel. If he isn't inside, check around its walls.",w=1},{t="An Old History Book can drop from almost any Duskwood mob. Use it from your bags to start this.",u=2794},{t="The dagger drops from the Lost Stalker, a ghost found a little north of Darkshire or north of the Raven Hill road.",tp=1},{t="Use Ira's Dagger from your bags to start this.",u=281143},{t="Stitches, a level 35 elite, walks this road to Darkshire once someone ends Abercrombie's chain. Keep well clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="If Watcher Dodds is missing, Stitches may have killed him. Wait for his respawn.",tp=1},{t="The Memory of Valor is inside the small house at Raven Hill.",w=1},{t="Bliztik is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Bliztik sells Healing Potions in small numbers. Buy any he has.",tp=1},{t="Abercrombie's shack stands north of Raven Hill Cemetery.",w=1},{t="Cooks: the dire wolves here drop Lean Wolf Flanks for Seasoned Wolf Kabobs. Keep them.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: keep a Small Venom Sac. With First Aid 80 it makes Anti-Venom for Touch of Zanzil.",tp=1},{t="Keep 6 Gooey Spider Legs from these spiders. Chef Grual asks for them later.",tp=1},{t="The Old Footlocker is on the floor inside the Moonbrook Schoolhouse.",w=1},{t="Daphne Stilwell paces her field. Look round it if she isn't at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Daphne Stilwell wanders around her field, so she may be a few steps from the arrow.",w=1},{t="Daphne Stilwell not here? Another player has taken this quest. Daphne Stilwell is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Defias Raiders (17-18) attack Daphne in three waves of 3, 4 and 5. If she or you die, the quest fails.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The note is in a heap of Burned-Out Remains north-west of Moonbrook. Click the heap.",w=1},{t="You hand it in at other Burned-Out Remains, in the southern Barrens, when your road passes there in your 30s.",tp=1},{t="Chef Grual works in the inn's kitchen.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bailiff Conacher is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Targorr the Dread is an elite inside the Stormwind Stockade dungeon. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You finish it inside Stormwind Stockades, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Drudgers and Bashers share spawn points. If Drudgers run short, kill Bashers to bring more.",tp=1},{t="Miners: Copper and Tin Veins in the cave can give Rethban Ore as well.",tp=1},{t="Stonewatch Keep's orcs are elites. Take your axes from Grunts and Outrunners outside its walls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Blackrock Outrunners cast Net, which roots you. Running from a bad pull is harder here.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Chatter, a level 23 rare spider, roams Alther's Mill among the Greater Tarantulas.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The quest also wants 6 Tarantula Eggs. Click them where they lie on the ground at the mill.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blind Mary is indoors.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Black Ravagers roam the road from Darkshire to Raven Hill and the woods toward the Yorgen Farmstead.",tp=1},{t="The Mound of loose dirt is behind the old stump on Sven's farm.",w=1},{t="Stealthed Defias prowl the farm and slow you, and fights near the barn pull mobs through its wall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bliztik is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Abercrombie's shack stands north of Raven Hill Cemetery.",w=1},{t="Starving Dire Wolves notice you from farther away than most wolves. Give them extra room as you pass.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Rabies, from the Rabid Dire Wolves, halves your health regen for 10 minutes. Expect longer rests.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Farley is inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",w=1},{t="The Storage Chest is upstairs in the Lion's Pride Inn.",w=1},{t="Brother Paxton is in Northshire Abbey's library, on the ground floor.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ursula Deline is downstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb.",w=1},{t="Brother Kristoff stands outside the Cathedral of Light, in Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="Duthorian Rall is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Milton Sheaf is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Tavernkeep Smitts is inside the inn.",w=1},{t="Mor'Ladim, a level 35 elite, roams Raven Hill Cemetery. Look for him before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ghouls here run 24 to 29. Take Flesh Eaters and Rotted Ones; Plague Spreaders and Brain Eaters are higher.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mor'Ladim, a level 35 elite, walks a loop round the cemetery. Look around before every pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Warders are down in the Dawning Wood Catacombs. Raiders and Healers walk the graves above.",w=1},{t="These skeletons run 26 to 29, above your level here. Pair up if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mages: Skeletal Warders can shield themselves from Fire and Frost, and Counterspell won't stop it.",tp=1},{t="Tavernkeep Smitts is inside the inn.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Bellygrub (level 24) has far more health than a boar should, and uses Charge and Tremor, an area hit.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lead him into Lakeshire for the guards' help, but deal most of the damage yourself or he drops no tusk.",tp=1},{t="Pull Yowler, then back off until the gnolls with him lose interest and go back.",tp=1},{t="Lieutenant Fangore fights with 2 more gnolls at his side. Treat it as a group fight, or leave it out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Priests and Warlocks: Fangore takes no Shadow damage. Solo, skip him and drop the quest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Morganth, a level 26 elite, holds the Tower of Ilgalar with his Servants. Keep clear of the tower.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Unfilled Red Waterskin from your bags in the water at Stonewatch Falls.",u=265747},{t="Elite Blackrock orcs of 21 to 25 camp a short way north-west of the falls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Lion Statue stands among Shadowhide gnolls of 23 to 26, beside Morganth's Tower of Ilgalar.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Empty Jar sits on a barrel on the tower's top floor.",w=1},{t="Elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23, fill the tower. Bring a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The watch tower is full of elite Blackrock orcs, levels 20 to 23. Bring a group of three.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You'll find Gath'Ilzogg inside Stonewatch Keep.",w=1},{t="Gath'Ilzogg, a level 26 elite, stands among elite guards. Bring a group of five.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tharil'zun, a level 24 elite, is a very hard fight. Bring help.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hunters and Warlocks: send the pet up to pull Tharil'zun and wait on the ground below him.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Shadowcaster here is an elite, level 22 to 23. Bring a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Render's Camp mixes Champions (24-25) with Summoners, Trackers and the rare Kazon (27). Pull from the edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Corporal Keeshan waits at the far end of the Render's Rock cave.",w=1},{t="Corporal Keeshan not here? Another player has taken this quest. Corporal Keeshan is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Out of the cave, Keeshan's path runs close to many mobs. Rest to full before you start, and expect extra pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Stormwind Stockades, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Stormwind Stockades, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bailiff Conacher is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Hervdana is back up the ramp, inside the cave above the falls.",w=1},{t="The road north passes right by the Dragonmaw orcs of Angerfang Encampment (28 to 29), with Highland Spiders (28) just west of it. Stay on the road and keep moving.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mosshide Trappers net you in place, and Brutes (25), Mystics (26) and the Alpha (27) share their camps.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Sida's Bag is a rare drop. Kill every ooze you pass; most of them gather round Ironbeard's Tomb.",tp=1},{t="Ashlan stands at the south edge of Dun Modr. The Dark Iron dwarves a few steps north are elites of 27 to 31. Come in from the south, hand in and leave the same way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Perfect Razormaw Eggs lie on the ground across Raptor Ridge, among the Razormaws.",w=1},{t="Raptor Ridge's Razormaws are 27 to 29, and the Razormaw Matriarch (31) is a rare there. Pull one at a time; they hit hard for their level.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Giant Wetlands Crocolisks cast Tendon Rip, a long slow. You can't outrun one once it lands.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Stand in Astranaar's lake and use the Unfilled Blue Waterskin from your bags.",u=265772},{t="Keep the filled waterskin. You hand it in back in the Wetlands, where the road goes next at 30.",tp=1},{t="Dal Bloodclaw is 25 and the village's furbolgs 23 to 24. Clear his path before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dal Bloodclaw patrols Thistlefur Village. Look along his path if he isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Plant Bundles are small, brown and half sunk in the ground, easy to walk past.",tp=1},{t="Herbalists: Find Herbs shows the Plant Bundles on the minimap.",tp=1},{t="The Ancient Statuette is small and lies on the ground at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Talen talks for about 20 seconds after the hand-in before he offers Ruuzel.",tp=1},{t="Ruuzel walks with a Wrathtail Myrmidon and a Wrathtail Sea Witch, and they fight together.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill one escort, run out until the others reset, then pull again.",tp=1},{t="Lady Vespia, a rare in the same area, can drop the Ring of Zoram too.",tp=1},{t="A thrown bomb or grenade pulls Ruuzel on her own, away from her escorts.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Saltspittle Oracles heal and hit you with an instant shock every few seconds. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pelturas talks for about 25 seconds after the hand-in. Wait for him to offer Elune's Tear.",tp=1},{t="Elune's Tear is a small blue stone lying on the lake's central island.",w=1},{t="The Worn Chest sits in a small glade west of the road to Felwood.",w=1},{t="Terrowulf worgen of 28 to 29 from the Howling Vale stand a short way west of the chest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About a dozen Terrowulf worgen of 28 to 30 and the rare Packlord (32) crowd round the tome.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Tome of Mel'Thandris lies on a table at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Anilia stands in the middle of Xavian's satyrs, 28 to 30. Clear your way to her one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Search Satyrnaar, the Bleakheart satyrs' ruins just west of Forest Song, for the Vine-Wrapped Scroll.",w=1},{t="Tell us where you found the Vine-Wrapped Scroll in Satyrnaar.",a=1},{t="Geltharis is level 32 but casts nothing. Clear the Xavian satyrs round him first and start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Bottle of Disease sits on a table in the Forsaken camp.",w=1},{t="About seven Forsaken of 28 to 30 hold the camp, and some of them hide in stealth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The slimes roam all round the Forsaken camp. Its Forsaken are 28 to 30, and some lurk in stealth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Hidden Shrine sits on a hilltop. The path up starts on its south-east side. Click the shrine to hand in.",w=1},{t="Pelturas talks for a few seconds before he offers The Ruins of Stardust.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Kimlya stands in the raised room off the inn's north side. Take the left ramp from mid-hall.",w=1},{t="Stardust Covered Bushes are spread over the whole island. Work your way around it.",tp=1},{t="Kaela Shadowspear stands on the rise above the valley into Windshear Crag.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks stands by a goblin hut a short way north of Gaxim.",w=1},{t="Piznik is inside the Windshear Mine, west of its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine holds about 60 kobolds of 20 to 23, Geomancers among them. Clear a path in and out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds come at Piznik in waves while he mines, casters among them. Eat and drink between waves.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sorrow Wing, a level 27 rare elite wyvern, can spawn by the lake in the middle of the Pridewing hills. Keep clear of it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Collin Mauren in Stormwind takes the crystals. Hand them in on your next visit there.",tp=1},{t="Their Frost Nova roots you in place, so running won't save you. Pull the elementals one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Some of the elementals are underwater, and your breath runs down while you fight them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Once you hold 5 Intact Elemental Bracers, use the Divining Scroll.",u=5456},{t="No vendor sells water breathing. The Auction House has Draughts of Water Breathing (30 minutes each); Warlocks can cast Unending Breath instead.",tp=1},{t="If you carry an Elixir of Water Breathing, drink it before you dive.",u=5996},{t="Foulweald Ursas Thrash for three hits at once. Fight them at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Totemics share spawn points with Warriors. If Totemics run short, kill Warriors to free the spots.",tp=1},{t="Every Foulweald here is 23 to 25. Pull single furbolgs from the camp's edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shadethicket Oracle is a hard fight alone. Bring a partner if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards hold the Barrens' north gate, just west of the way in. Keep to the arrow.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards hold the Barrens' north gate, just west of the way in. Keep to the arrow.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Satyrnaar's Bleakheart satyrs are 26 to 28. Prince Raze, a level 32 rare, can spawn among them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krolg stands at his hut on the south side of Mystral Lake.",w=1},{t="Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation near Krolg. He only talks to you in furbolg form.",u=5462},{t="Ran Bloodtooth, level 30, stands with five of his guards (levels 27 to 28) close round him. Thin them out before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Loot Ran Bloodtooth's Skull from him. The next step of the chain asks you to bring it to Raene.",tp=1},{t="Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation again before you talk to Krolg. The furbolg form lasts 3 minutes.",u=5462},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Velinde's Locker is past the overhead bridge, up in the Sentinels' bunkhouse.",w=1},{t="The key pieces drop from crawlers, murlocs and striders of level 18-21. Below 20, bring two more players.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Raging Reef Crawlers (20-21) Thrash for two extra swings at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The sunken ship breaks line of sight with Greymist Oracles and stops their Lightning Bolts.",tp=1},{t="Greymist Oracles cast a heavy Lightning Bolt and heal themselves. Burst them down first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Greymist Tidehunters' melee poison ticks for 30 seconds. Let it wear off before the next pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Threshwackonator 4100 is a level 20 elite that turns on you at Gelkak. At 28 you can kill it alone; start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="It turns on you once you reach Gelkak, so start the walk back at full health.",tp=1},{t="Druids: Entangling Roots holds it in place once it turns, so you can back off and cast.",tp=1},{t="The Threshwackonator 4100 waits on the beach south of Gelkak. Talk to it to start.",w=1},{t="This quest gives you a Draught of Water Breathing. Hold on to it: quests under water come later.",tp=1},{t="Gyromast's Key has no use after this. Destroy it to free the slot.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: if Ilthalaine has no Encrypted Sigil for you, carry on. It isn't confirmed in Forever yet.",tp=1},{t="Not seen in Forever yet. If Ilthalaine has no Encrypted Sigil for you, carry on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Shanda is on an upper level of Aldrassil.",w=1},{t="Mardant Strongoak is in a small room off the ramp that winds up Aldrassil.",w=1},{t="Keina is inside the base of Aldrassil.",w=1},{t="Alyissia is inside Aldrassil's base, up the ramp past the vendors.",w=1},{t="Frahun Shadewhisper is inside Aldrassil's base, up the ramp past the vendors.",w=1},{t="Not seen in Forever yet. If Ilthalaine has no Encrypted Sigil for you, carry on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ayanna Everstride is in a small room off the ramp that winds up Aldrassil.",w=1},{t="Druids: from here, melee plus Moonfire beats Wrath. Cast Moonfire right after a swing lands.",tp=1},{t="Druids: cast Wrath while your mana lasts, then melee until it refills.",tp=1},{t="Timed: 5 minutes. Take the antidote straight to Iverron by Shadowthread Cave."},{t="Keina is inside the base of Aldrassil.",w=1},{t="Janna Brightmoon is on an upper level of Aldrassil.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Webwood Egg sits at the far end of Shadowthread Cave, near Githyiss the Vile.",w=1},{t="Githyiss the Vile is level 5. Clear the spiders close to him before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill Githyiss for the Fang of Githyiss. It starts a quest you hand to Gilshalan.",tp=1},{t="Githyiss the Vile drops the fang about one time in ten.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Githyiss the Vile drops the fang about one time in ten.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tenaron Stormgrip is at the very top of Aldrassil, where the ramp round the tree ends.",w=1},{t="The Crystal Phial fills at the moonwell north of Aldrassil. Use it from your bags there.",u=5185},{t="The Lost Journal lies at the top of Aldrassil, next to Tenaron Stormgrip.",w=1},{t="Shanda is on an upper level of Aldrassil.",w=1},{t="No credit after sitting? Abandon the quest, take it again from Lyreena and sit back down.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The quest puts the Rare Earth in your bags, so keep a slot free.",tp=1},{t="Tallonkai Swiftroot is up in Dolanaar's tree, on its top level. Climb up to him.",w=1},{t="Aldia is on an upper floor in Dolanaar.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If money is short, buy Thorns before the new rank of Wrath.",tp=1},{t="Cooks: Small Spider Legs make Kaldorei Spider Kabobs and Small Eggs make Herb Baked Eggs, both early skill-ups.",tp=1},{t="Oakenscowl, a level 9 elite, stands south-west of the lake. Keep to the shore, where Timberlings are 5 to 6.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Tallonkai's Dresser stands inside a house in Starbreeze Village.",w=1},{t="Gaerolas Talvethren is on an upper floor in Starbreeze Village.",w=1},{t="The Jade Phial fills at the moonwell in Starbreeze Village. Use it from your bags there.",u=5619},{t="Owls and Nightsabers are faster than you, so running rarely works. Passing other owls mid-fight pulls them in.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Tallonkai Swiftroot is up in Dolanaar's tree, on its top level. Climb up to him.",w=1},{t="When Gnarlpine Mystics run short, kill Warriors. More Mystics come in.",tp=1},{t="Ferocitas uses Thrash, two extra swings at once. Pull him at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ferocitas drops the Gnarlpine Necklace. Use it from your bags to get the jewel.",u=8049},{t="Fel Cones sit at the foot of trees, small ones as well as big ones.",tp=1},{t="Three Fel Cones spawn just west of Zenn Foulhoof, beside the trees there. Check those first.",tp=1},{t="Fel Rock holds about 40 sprites and Vicious Grells, up to level 7. Lord Melenas is 8; clear a path to him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lord Melenas has three spawn points in Fel Rock, so he may not be where the arrow ends.",tp=1},{t="Target Lord Melenas and use the Severed Voodoo Claw: his damage drops for 2 minutes.",u=5457},{t="Use the Tourmaline Phial from your bags at the moonwell in the Pools of Arlithrien.",u=5621},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Druids: pick 5 Earthroot and keep them for Gathering the Cure, a level 14 quest in Auberdine.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tallonkai Swiftroot is up in Dolanaar's tree, on its top level. Climb up to him.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Aldia is on an upper floor in Dolanaar.",w=1},{t="Amara walks the road west out of Dolanaar. If furbolgs ambush her, talk to her once the fight ends.",tp=1},{t="Use the Amethyst Phial from your bags at the Oracle Glade's moonwell.",u=18152},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 10 minutes. Mist follows you; go straight to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak."},{t="Mist is sometimes away from her spot. Wait for her to come back.",tp=1},{t="Mist waits among Bloodfeather harpies of 8 to 11. At level 7, clear a path to her first and take her at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blackmoss the Fetid is a rare level 13 Mire Beast and isn't always up. His Moss-twined Heart starts this quest. Skip him if he's too strong for you."},{t="Its drop starts a quest. Pick it up if you come across it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blackmoss the Fetid is a rare and isn't always up. His heart starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Amara paces the road out of Dolanaar to the west. Look along it if she isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Narret Shadowgrove sells the Empty Vial and Innkeeper Keldamyr the Refreshing Spring Water, both in Dolanaar.",tp=1},{t="Use the Lunar Pendant at the Darnassus bank.",u=279378},{t="Use the Lunar Pendant at the entrance to the Cenarion Hold depths.",u=279378},{t="Use the Lunar Pendant at the inn on the Craftsmen's Terrace.",u=279378},{t="Use the Lunar Pendant at the city gate.",u=279378},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Priestess A'moora is on the upper floor of Darnassus's moon temple.",w=1},{t="Priestess A'moora is on the upper floor of the Temple of the Moon.",w=1},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is halfway up the Cenarion Enclave's tree house, a level below Fandral.",w=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is on an upper floor in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="Once the spirit is done, cast Teleport: Moonglade again. It's the quick way back to Nighthaven.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Target a Webwood Lurker and use the Taming Rod from your bags.",u=15921},{t="Blackmoss the Fetid is a rare and isn't always up. His heart starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Denalan plays a short scene first. Boglings (level 5) show up during it and drop Bogling Roots.",tp=1},{t="Keep the Sprouted Frond. Its heal has its own 2-minute cooldown, apart from potions.",tp=1},{t="Dismiss your pet, then target a Nightsaber Stalker and use the Taming Rod.",u=15922},{t="Dismiss the Nightsaber Stalker, then target a Strigid Screecher and use the Taming Rod.",u=15923},{t="Syurna is inside a tree house in Darnassus.",w=1},{t="Lady Sathrah spawns in a few different spots. Look around if she isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Sethir walks the big tree branch. Stealth, let him pass, then Pick Pocket the journal from behind.",tp=1},{t="Sethir the Ancient is level 12. Don't fight him; Pick Pocket is all the quest needs.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bloodfeather Matriarchs heal with Healing Wave and hit hard with Lightning Bolt. Kill them fast or leave them be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bloodfeather Harpies along the Darnassus road drop the belts too, away from the Matriarchs.",tp=1},{t="Witchmother Arysa casts a hard Lightning Bolt and heals herself with Healing Wave. Pull her at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Oracle Tree Bark is a short walk west of Sentinel Arynia. Click it to hand in.",w=1},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is halfway up the Cenarion Enclave's tree house, a level below Fandral.",w=1},{t="Fandral Staghelm is on the tree house's top level in the Cenarion Enclave. Climb all the way up.",w=1},{t="Syurna is inside a tree house in Darnassus.",w=1},{t="Priestess A'moora is on the upper floor of the Temple of the Moon.",w=1},{t="Priestess Alathea is on the temple's upper floor.",w=1},{t="Use Sathrah's Sacrifice from your bags at the fountain inside the temple.",u=8155},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The portal in Rut'theran Village takes you back up to Darnassus.",tp=1},{t="Oakenscowl is a level 9 elite with nearly three times a normal mob's health. Clear the Timberlings round him first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The way to Vorlus Vilehoof starts east of him. Go round by the arrow, not straight at him.",w=1},{t="The den is packed with about 70 furbolgs of 7 to 9, close together. Pull one at a time and don't run deeper while you fight; Rageclaw and Greenpaw are 10.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Oben Rageclaw sleeps deeper in the den, across a bridge on its upper floor.",w=1},{t="Cross the right-hand bridge where the tunnel opens. The chest is in the small room at its end.",w=1},{t="Go back over the bridge and take the other one. The Nesting chest waits in the room beyond.",w=1},{t="Follow the long ramp down past the bridges to the deepest room. Greenpaw guards the Sky chest there.",w=1},{t="Take the tunnel east into the round hall, climb its ramp and loop east onto the terrace.",w=1},{t="Rageclaw (level 10) walks the round hall's floor under the ramp.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gnarlpine Shamans inside the den drop the Shaman Voodoo Charm, so there's no need to go back out.",tp=1},{t="Kill Rageclaw, then use the Voodoo Charm on his corpse.",u=8149},{t="Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom is held in the den's big central room.",w=1},{t="Lynessa's escort leads back through the den's furbolgs. Take it last, at full health and mana.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom not here? Another player has taken this quest. Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom is back a few minutes after they finish, so wait nearby.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Ursal (12) stands in Gnarlpine Hold among about 20 furbolgs of levels 9 to 11. Clear a path and pull him alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Moonkin Stone is inside a cave. Lunaclaw shows up at the cave mouth, so face that way.",w=1},{t="At the Moonkin Stone in the cave, use the Cenarion Moondust. Defeat Lunaclaw, then speak to his spirit.",u=15208},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is halfway up the Cenarion Enclave's tree house, a level below Fandral.",w=1},{t="Wizbang Cranktoggle is on the inn's upper floor, up the ramps.",w=1},{t="Warriors, Rogues: Laird sells Longjaw Mud Snapper. Stock up on food here, about 40.",tp=1},{t="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde stands up on the platform, next to the flight master.",w=1},{t="The WANTED poster hangs outside the inn.",w=1},{t="Terenthis is indoors, in the building at Auberdine's east end.",w=1},{t="Needs Cooking 10. Herb Baked Eggs get you there and keep giving skill-ups toward 50.",tp=1},{t="Herb Baked Egg is a Small Egg plus Mild Spices from Gorbold Steelhand. Auberdine's campfire cooks it.",tp=1},{t="Warriors, Rogues: Delfrum Flintbeard teaches Blacksmithing here too. Rough Sharpening Stones add 2 blade damage.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Innkeeper Shaussiy is on the inn's ground floor.",w=1},{t="Dalmond is indoors. He also sells Sharp Arrows, Heavy Shots and 6-slot Small Brown Pouches.",w=1},{t="Fish the sea for Gaffer Jacks: off Auberdine's dock or anywhere along Darkshore's coast.",w=1},{t="Fish the sea for Darkshore Grouper: off Auberdine's dock or anywhere along Darkshore's coast.",w=1},{t="Foreststrider Fledglings flee below 30% health. Keep a ranged attack or a snare to finish them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Giant Foreststriders (17-19) and the Strider Clutchmother (20) roam the south. Take the meat from Fledglings.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Greymist Coastrunners by the bones run faster than you. Clear them before the 5-second loot.",tp=1},{t="Reaching the outer edge of the furbolg camp is enough. No need to fight your way in.",tp=1},{t="Target a Rabid Thistle Bear, then use Tharnariun's Hope. It reaches about 50 yards.",u=7586},{t="Wasted the trap on no bear? Tharnariun in Auberdine hands out another.",tp=1},{t="Some Pygmy Tide Crawlers wade offshore. Check the water if the beach is picked clean.",tp=1},{t="Buzzbox 827 sits on the ground, just south of the flight platform.",w=1},{t="Electropellers live in fresh water, not the sea: the Cliffspring River north of Auberdine, the Wildbend River, or the pond in the Grove of the Ancients.",w=1},{t="The Skeletal Sea Turtle lies underwater. Dive down to it when the arrow lands.",w=1},{t="Rabid Thistle Bears can give you Rabies, which halves health regen for 10 minutes. Keep fights short.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Both tablets lie flat on the ground among the ruins.",w=1},{t="Opening a tablet counts it. You don't need to page through.",tp=1},{t="Jai'vhanel is a black owl at the foot of the hills, north of Ameth'Aran.",w=1},{t="Cerellean Whiteclaw stands out on the dock.",w=1},{t="If Cerellean is in the middle of a scene, wait for it to end.",tp=1},{t="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is on an upper floor in Auberdine.",w=1},{t="Thundris Windweaver is in the town hall building at Auberdine's north end.",w=1},{t="The WANTED poster hangs outside the inn.",w=1},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is upstairs in the Cenarion Enclave.",w=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is on an upper floor in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="The Shrine Bauble lasts 5 minutes once looted: swim west and go straight to the Shrine of Remulos."},{t="The bauble's container sits on the lake floor in one of a few spots. Find it from the surface, then dive straight down.",tp=1},{t="With the Shrine Bauble in your bags, go to the Shrine of Remulos tree and use it there.",u=15877},{t="The Bauble Container sits on the lake bed, 35 to 65 yards down. Spot it from the surface, then dive.",w=1},{t="Each lockbox is on its wreck's lowest deck, deep enough to run out of breath. Watch the breath bar.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You can loot each lockbox through the hull from just behind the wreck's stern with Interact with Target.",tp=1},{t="Surface and let your breath refill before each dive.",tp=1},{t="Swim in through the hole in each wreck's hull. The lockbox is at the back of the bottom deck.",w=1},{t="Threshers also swim in the sea past the far end of the Auberdine dock.",tp=1},{t="Elder Darkshore Threshers (16-18) swim among the 12-14 ones. Pull the smaller ones.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Buzzbox 411 sits on the ground. Look down when the arrow lands.",w=1},{t="Greymist murlocs (14-16) crowd the turtle. Pull them off one at a time before you loot it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Reef Crawlers go up to level 17 and hit hard with an instant Muscle Tear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="At the pool below the waterfall, use the Empty Sampling Tube from your bags.",u=12350},{t="The pool below the falls is fresh water. Fish it for the Electropellers.",w=1},{t="Leave the Wild Grells and Vile Sprites alone on the way. Asterion's next quest wants their earrings.",tp=1},{t="Leave the Deth'ryll Satyrs for now. The next quest needs them, and they respawn slowly.",tp=1},{t="Raging Moonkins stand in linked pairs on the crystal's west side. Come at it from the east.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The red crystal stands up on the slope of the eastern mountains.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Ancient Flame is the green-burning torch under the gazebo in Ameth'Aran.",w=1},{t="Anaya Dawnrunner walks a patrol through Ameth'Aran and respawns slowly. Check back if she's gone.",tp=1},{t="Pathfinders get two extra swings with Thrash. Windtalkers' Gust of Wind stuns everyone in melee.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Rabid Thistle Bears can give you Rabies, which halves health regen for 10 minutes. Keep fights short.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="At Auberdine's moonwell, use the Empty Water Tube from your bags.",u=14338},{t="Fill your Empty Cleansing Bowl at this moonwell too. The Blackwood Corrupted needs it.",u=12346},{t="The Thistle Cubs around the Den Mother stun with Ravage too. Clear them before you pull her.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Den Mother is level 18-19. Below 19, bring a partner or come back later.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Looting each Blackwood sample sends furbolgs running at you. Loot at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Xabraxxis takes a few seconds to arrive. He drops a Demon Bag on the ground, and the Talisman is inside.",tp=1},{t="If you hear Xabraxxis yell, another player summoned him. Help kill him and you can open his bag too.",tp=1},{t="With all three samples, use the Filled Cleansing Bowl beside the camp's north bonfire.",u=12347},{t="The Grain, Nut and Fruit Stores run west to east through the camp. The bonfire is between Nut and Fruit.",w=1},{t="Xabraxxis is level 19. Rest to full before you use the bowl.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The cave is full of Stormscale naga, levels 15 to 17. Bring a partner, above all on a Hardcore character.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="One Death Cap grows at the far end of the cave's upper level, another in the south room below.",tp=1},{t="Stormscale Wave Riders' Aqua Jet knocks you back and can throw you off the upper level. Fight away from the edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep to the upper path. Drop to the lower level only if the upper Death Cap is taken.",w=1},{t="Stand in the water at the cave mouth and use the sampler from your bags.",u=15844},{t="Buzzbox 323 sits at the top of a ramp.",w=1},{t="Reef Crawlers go up to level 17 and hit hard with an instant Muscle Tear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Encrusted Tide Crawlers drop the chunks too, but Reef Crawlers are the easier kill.",tp=1},{t="The linked Raging Moonkin pairs still stand west of the crystal. Come in from the east again.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Rogues: take the Curvewood Dagger and keep it. A later poisons quest wants a dagger.",tp=1},{t="The three Blackwood samples have no use after this. Free the bag space.",tp=1},{t="Dalmond is indoors. He also sells Sharp Arrows, Heavy Shots and 6-slot Small Brown Pouches.",w=1},{t="Dark Strand Voidcallers of 28 to 29 stand inside the tower itself. Keep to the Fanatics outside it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dark Strand Voidcallers of 28 to 29 stand inside the tower itself. Keep to the Fanatics outside it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Moonstalker Matriarchs always bring a Runt, so each pull is two animals.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Moonstalker Sires' Exploit Weakness only lands from behind. Keep them in front of you.",tp=1},{t="Moonstalker Matriarchs are level 19-20. Below 19, take only the Sires (17-18).",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You can wear the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak, but Volcor takes it at the turn-in. Keep your old cloak.",tp=1},{t="Dalmond is indoors. He also sells Sharp Arrows, Heavy Shots and 6-slot Small Brown Pouches.",w=1},{t="Earthroot takes Herbalism 15. Without it, look in Battered Chests or the Auction House.",tp=1},{t="Lunar Fungal Blooms grow inside the moonkin caves east of Auberdine. Loot the Lunar Fungus from them.",w=1},{t="Use the Phial of Scrying at the Glaive. Onu talks to you through the Scrying Bowl that appears.",u=5251},{t="The Phial of Scrying has no more use. Free its bag slot.",tp=1},{t="The Twilight Tome is the book on the north pedestal in the Glaive camp.",w=1},{t="Kill Twilight Disciples first. They heal with Renew and a slow Heal you can interrupt.",tp=1},{t="Warriors, Rogues: Twilight Thugs Disarm you for a few seconds. Fight them one at a time.",tp=1},{t="The book drops from Twilight Disciples and Twilight Thugs at the Master's Glaive.",tp=1},{t="If Therylune isn't there, someone is escorting her or she's respawning. Give it a few minutes.",tp=1},{t="Therylune stands at the south end of the Twilight camp at the Master's Glaive.",w=1},{t="Keep Therylune close. The escort fails if she gets too far from you.",tp=1},{t="Prospector Remtravel may be out on another player's escort or respawning. Wait for him.",tp=1},{t="Target a Sickly Deer, then use your Curative Animal Salve. Ten cured deer finish it.",u=15826},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is upstairs in the Cenarion Enclave.",w=1},{t="Volcor waits inside the cave.",w=1},{t="Blackwood Ursas (18-19) and Shamans (19-20) hold Volcor's cave. Clear the ones by the mouth first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Volcor not here? Another player has taken this quest. Volcor is back about 7 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="No fight here. Volcor sneaks out alone; wait about 20 seconds by the cave mouth.",tp=1},{t="Blackwood Trackers (14-15) and Marosh the Devious (16) attack Aynasha in waves. Keep them off her.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Taking this starts the escort on the spot. Only take it when you can walk with Remtravel.",tp=1},{t="Prospector Remtravel not here? Another player has taken this quest. Prospector Remtravel is back about 7 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="This is a level 20 escort and very hard alone. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gravelflint troggs up to level 21 ambush the escort. The Geomancer casts Fireball at Remtravel; stop it first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Murkdeep may already be in the shallows after someone's failed try. Check before you walk in.",tp=1},{t="Standing by the central bonfire starts it. Coastrunners (12-13) come first, then Warriors (15-16), then Murkdeep.",tp=1},{t="The last wave is Murkdeep (19) and a Greymist Hunter at once. Bring a partner if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Step away from the bonfire to rest between waves. The next one won't come at you there.",tp=1},{t="Clear the murlocs around the camp first, staying well away from the bonfire.",tp=1},{t="Murkdeep throws a net that holds you in place. Don't plan on running once he's on you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Grizzled Thistle Bears use Ravage, an instant hard hit that stuns you for a moment.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Grizzled Thistle Bears roam the hills around Buzzbox 525 and the Grove of the Ancients.",tp=1},{t="Onu speaks for about 12 seconds after Return to Onu before he offers this one.",tp=1},{t="The turtle's shell blocks line of sight. Fight Greymist Oracles behind it to stop their Lightning Bolts.",tp=1},{t="Greymist Tidehunters poison you in melee, and it keeps ticking after the hit. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Beached Sea Creature lies among packed Greymist murlocs. Pull one at a time from the edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Greymist Oracles hit hard with Lightning Bolt and heal with Healing Wave. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Click the Beached Sea Creature at its neck end.",w=1},{t="It gives money and Darnassus reputation, but no XP when we last checked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It gives money and Darnassus reputation, but no XP when we last checked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Stormscale Beastmistress swims underwater round the rock spire off the north shore. Watch your breath.",w=1},{t="It gives money and Darnassus reputation, but no XP when we last checked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Strange Lockbox in the water off this coast holds the Aquatic Agility half. Swim out to it.",tp=1},{t="Stormscale naga of 18 to 21 hold the ruins, Warriors the highest. Take the relics on the edges first and pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The key pieces drop from crawlers, murlocs and striders of level 18-21. Below 20, bring two more players.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Raging Reef Crawlers (20-21) Thrash for two extra swings at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The sunken ship breaks line of sight with Greymist Oracles and stops their Lightning Bolts.",tp=1},{t="Greymist Oracles cast a heavy Lightning Bolt and heal themselves. Burst them down first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Greymist Tidehunters' melee poison ticks for 30 seconds. Let it wear off before the next pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Threshwackonator 4100 is a level 20 elite that turns on you at Gelkak. Bring two more players.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="It turns on you once you reach Gelkak, so start the walk back at full health.",tp=1},{t="Druids: Entangling Roots holds it in place once it turns, so you can back off and cast.",tp=1},{t="The Threshwackonator 4100 waits on the beach south of Gelkak. Talk to it to start.",w=1},{t="This quest gives you a Draught of Water Breathing. Hold on to it: quests under water come later.",tp=1},{t="Gyromast's Key has no use after this. Destroy it to free the slot.",tp=1},{t="It gives money and Darnassus reputation, but no XP when we last checked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It gives money and Darnassus reputation, but no XP when we last checked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Priestess Alathea is on the temple's upper floor.",w=1},{t="Timed: 20 minutes. Kerlonian walks south down the road with you to his bag, near the Ashenvale border."},{t="Kerlonian can take a long time to respawn. If he's gone, carry on and check back later.",tp=1},{t="The escort is timed. Start it when you can walk straight south with him.",tp=1},{t="Kerlonian dozes off and stops. Stand next to him and use the Horn of Awakening.",u=13536},{t="Ambushes only come while you're on the main road. Walk beside it instead.",tp=1},{t="Kerlonian's Chest sits on the ground next to him. The Horn of Awakening is inside.",w=1},{t="The Glowing Soul Gem is a rare drop, so this can take a while.",tp=1},{t="Plant Bundles are small, brown and half sunk in the ground, easy to walk past.",tp=1},{t="Herbalists: Find Herbs shows the Plant Bundles on the minimap.",tp=1},{t="A ramp on the north-west side takes you up and out of the shrine.",tp=1},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is upstairs in the Cenarion Enclave.",w=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="Restless Spirits of 23 guard the relics and attack on sight. The statue's stealth wears off, so don't linger.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Each relic is a small orb beside a cat statue in a wall alcove. The Relic of the Claw is deepest, past a bridge.",w=1},{t="Pelturas talks for about 25 seconds after the hand-in. Wait for him to offer Elune's Tear.",tp=1},{t="Saltspittle Oracles heal and hit you with an instant shock every few seconds. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ancient Statuette is small and lies on the ground at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Talen talks for about 20 seconds after the hand-in before he offers Ruuzel.",tp=1},{t="Ruuzel walks with a Wrathtail Myrmidon and a Wrathtail Sea Witch, and they fight together.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill one escort, run out until the others reset, then pull again.",tp=1},{t="Lady Vespia, a rare in the same area, can drop the Ring of Zoram too.",tp=1},{t="A thrown bomb or grenade pulls Ruuzel on her own, away from her escorts.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Kimlya stands in the raised room off the inn's north side. Take the left ramp from mid-hall.",w=1},{t="Elune's Tear is a small blue stone lying on the lake's central island.",w=1},{t="Shadethicket Moss Eaters, 21 to 23, roam the island around it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pelturas talks for a few seconds before he offers The Ruins of Stardust.",tp=1},{t="Stardust Covered Bushes are spread over the whole island. Work your way around it.",tp=1},{t="Shadethicket Raincallers (22-23) and Wood Shapers (23-24) cover the island. Clear around each bush.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kaela Shadowspear stands on the rise above the valley into Windshear Crag.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks stands by a goblin hut a short way north of Gaxim.",w=1},{t="Piznik is inside the Windshear Mine, west of its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine holds about 60 kobolds of 20 to 23, Geomancers among them. Clear a path in and out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds come at Piznik in waves while he mines, casters among them. Eat and drink between waves.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sorrow Wing, a level 27 rare elite wyvern, can spawn by the lake in the middle of the Pridewing hills. Keep clear of it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Archaeologist Flagongut is upstairs in the Deepwater Tavern, Menethil's inn.",w=1},{t="Samor Festivus is on an upper floor, up the stairs.",w=1},{t="Gobbler wanders a short way around the marsh. If he isn't on his spot, look nearby.",tp=1},{t="Keep the Murloc Fins these murlocs drop. Murloc Poachers in Lakeshire asks for 8 later on.",tp=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kixxle sells Healing Potions in short supply. Buy what you can afford before the gnoll camps.",tp=1},{t="About 35 stalkers of 21 to 22 fill the tunnels, and the rare Leech Widow, level 24, roams them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The gnolls here drop a lot of Wool Cloth. Keep it for First Aid bandages.",tp=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The piles lie on the harbor floor, 10 to 20 yards down in the bay west of the docks. Surface for air between them.",w=1},{t="Young crocolisks (21-22) swim the channel east of town, and Bluegill Raiders (28-29) hold the south shore. Stay in the west bay.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Opening the Sealed Barrel takes 5 seconds. Clear the murlocs around it first.",tp=1},{t="Merrin Rockweaver is inside the small cave at the dig site.",w=1},{t="Flagongut's Fossil lies on the ground in the cave at Whelgar's Excavation Site, by Prospector Whelgar.",w=1},{t="The Stone of Relu is a rare drop from any Mottled raptor. Kill them as you cross the marsh.",tp=1},{t="Captain Stoutfist is on the top floor of Menethil Keep, up the stairs.",w=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The road north passes right by the Dragonmaw orcs of Angerfang Encampment (28 to 29), with Highland Spiders (28) just west of it. Stay on the road and keep moving.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gerrig Bonegrip is inside a house in the Forlorn Cavern. Its door is on the south side.",w=1},{t="Make the mana potions and fortitude elixirs with Alchemy, or buy them at the Auction House.",tp=1},{t="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is inside Stormwind Keep, in the throne room.",w=1},{t="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker stands inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="Elaine Carevin is indoors.",w=1},{t="Take this before you meet Sven: Elaine Carevin stops offering it once Sven's Revenge is in your log.",tp=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors. Go into the building the arrow points at.",w=1},{t="Chef Grual only offers this at Cooking 50.",tp=1},{t="Chef Grual works in the inn's kitchen.",w=1},{t="If Stitches gets into Darkshire, Althea can be dead or stuck fighting him. Wait for her respawn.",tp=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Herble sells the Bronze Tube in small numbers. Buy one if he has it; Viktori asks for it later.",tp=1},{t="Herble Baubbletump, next to Viktori, sells the Bronze Tube but keeps only two. If he is out, Billibub Cogspinner in Stormwind's Dwarven District stocks more."},{t="Blind Mary is indoors.",w=1},{t="Skeletal Mages cast Frostbolt, and their Frost Armor slows you as you hit them. Don't count on running.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Warriors Hamstring you as well, so pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Insane Ghoul haunts the chapel. If he isn't inside, check around its walls.",w=1},{t="An Old History Book can drop from almost any Duskwood mob. Use it from your bags to start this.",u=2794},{t="The dagger drops from the Lost Stalker, a ghost found a little north of Darkshire or north of the Raven Hill road.",tp=1},{t="Use Ira's Dagger from your bags to start this.",u=281143},{t="Stitches, a level 35 elite, walks this road to Darkshire once someone ends Abercrombie's chain. Keep well clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="If Watcher Dodds is missing, Stitches may have killed him. Wait for his respawn.",tp=1},{t="The Memory of Valor is inside the small house at Raven Hill.",w=1},{t="Bliztik is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Bliztik sells Healing Potions in small numbers. Buy any he has.",tp=1},{t="Abercrombie's shack stands north of Raven Hill Cemetery.",w=1},{t="Starving Dire Wolves notice you from farther away than most wolves. Give them extra room as you pass.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Rabies, from the Rabid Dire Wolves, halves your health regen for 10 minutes. Expect longer rests.",tp=1},{t="Cooks: these wolves drop Lean Wolf Flanks for Seasoned Wolf Kabobs. Keep them.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: keep a Small Venom Sac. With First Aid 80 it makes Anti-Venom for Touch of Zanzil.",tp=1},{t="Keep 6 Gooey Spider Legs from these spiders. Chef Grual asks for them later.",tp=1},{t="This chain ends in Poisons training.",tp=1},{t="Pick Pocket the Malformed Defias Drone for the key. It starts at the door, then walks laps round the tower.",tp=1},{t="The Malformed Defias Drone hits very hard and can be at the door when you leave. Sprint if Stealth breaks.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ambush with a dagger (the Curvewood Dagger works) opens hard on each tower guard. Slower than sneaking, far safer.",tp=1},{t="The chest is on a bookshelf one floor below the top. Climb chair, lamp, shelf, and leave Stealth to open it.",tp=1},{t="Looting the journal locks Stealth for a while, and sentries left alive on that floor wait below the shelf.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mobs on the floor above can hit you through the floor. Check what's overhead before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dust Devils wander all over Westfall. Take each one you pass.",tp=1},{t="Hunters: Eagle Eye helps you spot Dust Devils from afar.",tp=1},{t="The Old Footlocker is on the floor inside the Moonbrook Schoolhouse.",w=1},{t="The note is in a heap of Burned-Out Remains north-west of Moonbrook. Click the heap.",w=1},{t="You hand it in at other Burned-Out Remains, in the southern Barrens, when your road passes there in your 30s.",tp=1},{t="Learn the flight here on your way to Duskwood.",tp=1},{t="The Strange Lockbox with the Aquatic Endurance half lies deep under the sea here. Watch your breath bar.",tp=1},{t="With both halves in your bags, join them at the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade.",u=15883},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is on the upper floor of the Cenarion Enclave.",w=1},{t="Touch of Zanzil, from this chain, is cleared by Anti-Venom or by a Druid or Paladin.",tp=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 building.",w=1},{t="Chef Grual works in the inn's kitchen.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Wanted Poster is just outside the Lakeshire Town Hall's door.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bailiff Conacher is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Targorr the Dread is an elite inside the Stormwind Stockade dungeon. Take this only for a group run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You finish it inside Stormwind Stockades, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 60 minutes. Go straight to the first fork in the Rethban Caverns and back. Dying and releasing fails it."},{t="Yorus Barleybrew is inside the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Redridge Bashers (19-20) and Drudgers (20-21) crowd the caverns' mouth. Clear a way you can run back along.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Blackrock Outrunners throw Net and root you in place. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stonewatch Keep's orcs are elites. Take your axes from Grunts and Outrunners outside its walls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The same murlocs drop the fins and Selling Fish's Spotted Sunfish.",tp=1},{t="These murlocs respawn very fast. Fight at a camp's edge and rest well away from the water.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The toolbox lies on the lake bed, underwater.",tp=1},{t="A Lake Thresher, a level 25 elite, swims a patrol through this part of the lake. Let it pass before you dive.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Murlocs on this shore respawn fast. Rest well away from the water.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Blind Mary is indoors.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Black Ravagers roam the road from Darkshire to Raven Hill and the woods toward the Yorgen Farmstead.",tp=1},{t="The Mound of loose dirt is behind the old stump on Sven's farm.",w=1},{t="Stealthed Defias prowl the farm and slow you, and fights near the barn pull mobs through its wall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bliztik is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Abercrombie's shack stands north of Raven Hill Cemetery.",w=1},{t="Innkeeper Farley is inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",w=1},{t="The Storage Chest is upstairs in the Lion's Pride Inn.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Milton Sheaf is in the library inside Stormwind Keep.",w=1},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="Clerk Daltry is inside the Darkshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Tavernkeep Smitts is inside the inn.",w=1},{t="Mor'Ladim, a level 35 elite, roams Raven Hill Cemetery. Look for him before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ghouls here run 24 to 29. Take Flesh Eaters and Rotted Ones; Plague Spreaders and Brain Eaters are higher.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mor'Ladim, a level 35 elite, walks a loop round the cemetery. Look around before every pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skeletal Warders are down in the Dawning Wood Catacombs. Raiders and Healers walk the graves above.",w=1},{t="These skeletons run 26 to 29, above your level here. Pair up if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Tavernkeep Smitts is inside the inn.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Madame Eva is indoors.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Stormwind Stockades, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="If you skipped Stormwind Stockades, drop its quests here to free your quest log.",tp=1},{t="Only if you won't finish it: dropping it frees a slot in your quest log.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bellygrub has far more health than a normal boar. A very hard fight alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bellygrub can be led back to Lakeshire, where the guards help. Do most of the damage yourself so the tusk drops.",tp=1},{t="Grunts and Outrunners (19-21) stand close together here, with a few Summoners (22-23). Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supplies come from Grain Sacks, Meat Haunches and Water Barrels; weapons from Weapon Racks and loose Stolen Weapons.",tp=1},{t="Incinerator Gar'im is inside a cave in Render's Valley, southeast Redridge.",w=1},{t="Gar'im (level 23) fights beside his Shadowcasters. Bring a group of four, or leave this one out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Chatter, a level 23 rare spider, roams Alther's Mill among the Greater Tarantulas.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The quest also wants 6 Tarantula Eggs. Click them where they lie on the ground at the mill.",tp=1},{t="Lieutenant Fangore fights with 2 more gnolls at his side. Treat it as a group fight, or leave it out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Priests: Fangore takes no Shadow damage.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Morganth, a level 26 elite, holds the Tower of Ilgalar with his Servants. Keep clear of the tower.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You'll find Gath'Ilzogg inside Stonewatch Keep.",w=1},{t="Gath'Ilzogg, a level 26 elite, stands among elite guards. Bring a group of five.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tharil'zun, a level 24 elite, is a very hard fight. Bring help.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hunters: send the pet up to pull Tharil'zun and wait on the ground below him.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Shadowcaster here is an elite, level 22 to 23. Bring a group of three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Render's Camp mixes Champions (24-25) with Summoners, Trackers and the rare Kazon (27). Pull from the edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Corporal Keeshan waits at the far end of the Render's Rock cave.",w=1},{t="Corporal Keeshan not here? Another player has taken this quest. Corporal Keeshan is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Out of the cave, Keeshan's path runs close to many mobs. Rest to full before you start, and expect extra pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Solomon is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bailiff Conacher is inside the Lakeshire Town Hall.",w=1},{t="Giant Wetlands Crocolisks cast Tendon Rip, a long slow. You can't outrun one once it lands.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Stone of Relu is a rare drop from any Mottled raptor. Kill them as you cross the marsh.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Flagongut's Fossil lies on the ground in the cave at Whelgar's Excavation Site, by Prospector Whelgar.",w=1},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Trappers net you in place, and Brutes (25), Mystics (26) and the Alpha (27) camp east of here.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sida's Bag is a rare drop. Kill every ooze you pass; most of them gather round Ironbeard's Tomb.",tp=1},{t="Perfect Razormaw Eggs lie on the ground across Raptor Ridge, among the Razormaws.",w=1},{t="Raptor Ridge's Razormaws are 27 to 29, and the Razormaw Matriarch (31) is a rare there. Pull one at a time; they hit hard for their level.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nightveiled Rotheaps, level 31 to 32, roam the Wetlands road. Watch the road ahead, step well off it while one passes, and never fight one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Giant Wetlands Crocolisks cast Tendon Rip, a long slow. You can't outrun one once it lands.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Archaeologist Flagongut is upstairs in the Deepwater Tavern, Menethil's inn.",w=1},{t="Dal Bloodclaw is 25 and the village's furbolgs 23 to 24. Clear his path before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dal Bloodclaw patrols Thistlefur Village. Look along his path if he isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Lesser Felguards of 23 to 24 and Felslayers of 22 to 23 fill the shrine around Ilkrud.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ilkrud Magthrull (24) fights with a Succubus, and his 5-second cast summons two Voidwalkers. Interrupt it if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Clear a way out first. Running out resets the Voidwalkers and the Succubus.",tp=1},{t="Right of the shrine's mouth, a hill by a large tree skirts its mobs. Hop the root and keep right.",tp=1},{t="Lady Vespia, a rare in the same area, can drop the Ring of Zoram too.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="About a dozen Terrowulf worgen of 28 to 30 and the rare Packlord (32) crowd round the tome.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Tome of Mel'Thandris lies on a table at the arrow.",w=1},{t="The Worn Chest sits in a small glade west of the road to Felwood.",w=1},{t="Terrowulf worgen of 28 to 29 from the Howling Vale stand a short way west of the chest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Anilia stands in the middle of Xavian's satyrs, 28 to 30. Clear your way to her one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Search Satyrnaar, the Bleakheart satyrs' ruins just west of Forest Song, for the Vine-Wrapped Scroll.",w=1},{t="Tell us where you found the Vine-Wrapped Scroll in Satyrnaar.",a=1},{t="Geltharis is level 32 but casts nothing. Clear the Xavian satyrs round him first and start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Bottle of Disease sits on a table in the Forsaken camp.",w=1},{t="About seven Forsaken of 28 to 30 hold the camp, and some of them hide in stealth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The slimes roam all round the Forsaken camp. Its Forsaken are 28 to 30, and some lurk in stealth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Hidden Shrine sits on a hilltop. The path up starts on its south-east side. Click the shrine to hand in.",w=1},{t="Krolg stands at his hut on the south side of Mystral Lake.",w=1},{t="Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation near Krolg. He only talks to you in furbolg form.",u=5462},{t="Ran Bloodtooth, level 30, stands with five of his guards (levels 27 to 28) close round him. Thin them out before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Loot Ran Bloodtooth's Skull from him. The next step of the chain asks you to bring it to Raene.",tp=1},{t="Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation again before you talk to Krolg. The furbolg form lasts 3 minutes.",u=5462},{t="Once you hold 5 Intact Elemental Bracers, use the Divining Scroll.",u=5456},{t="If you still have the Draught of Water Breathing that Gyromast's Revenge gave you, drink it before you dive.",u=5996},{t="Their Frost Nova roots you in place, so running won't save you. Pull the elementals one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Some of the elementals are underwater, and your breath runs down while you fight them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Foulweald Ursas Thrash for three hits at once. Fight them at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Totemics share spawn points with Warriors. If Totemics run short, kill Warriors to free the spots.",tp=1},{t="Every Foulweald here is 23 to 25. Pull single furbolgs from the camp's edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shadethicket Oracle is a hard fight alone. Bring a partner if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards hold the Barrens' north gate, just west of the way in. Keep to the arrow.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Level 40 Horde guards hold the Barrens' north gate, just west of the way in. Keep to the arrow.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Satyrnaar's Bleakheart satyrs are 26 to 28. Prince Raze, a level 32 rare, can spawn among them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Velinde's Locker is past the overhead bridge, up in the Sentinels' bunkhouse.",w=1},{t="Collin Mauren in Stormwind takes the crystals. Hand them in on your next visit there.",tp=1},{t="Dark Iron Spies drop the Dark Iron Map. Right-click it to start this quest.",tp=1},{t="Afadra Dunwall stands at the bottom of Old Ironforge, up the stairs by the portal.",w=1},{t="From the throne room, take the left door and follow the cobwebbed passage down into Old Ironforge.",tp=1},{t="Thom Filch waits by the bridge into the Hall, near the portal.",w=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker (either one counts).",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Players report the way in starts at Ironforge's throne room: the left door leads down into Old Ironforge, with the portal at the bottom.",s="reported"},{t="The way down to the portal runs on ledges above lava. Falling in kills you, so walk, don't jump.",s="reported"},{t="Campfires can't be lit in Ironforge or below it. Get your camp buffs outside the city before you go.",s="reported"},{t="The bosses are level 16. At 13 the second half is orange to red, so bring crowd control.",s="reported"},{t="A short dungeon on one path. Ghosts come first, then Dark Iron dwarves.",s="reported"},{t="The ghosts at the start can't be bled or polymorphed.",s="reported"},{t="Bloodhound Runts leave a disease that makes the tank take more damage. Cure it between pulls.",s="reported"},{t="Yellow Seaforium barrels explode for about 50 fire damage on everyone within 8 yards.",s="reported"},{t="Kill Dark Iron Looters first. Engineers throw bombs at a spot on the ground, so step off it.",s="reported"},{t="Patrols drift through the halls, so one pack can turn into two. Check for one before you pull.",s="reported"},{t="Killing Faldrim Anvilmar, the first boss, opens the gates further in.",s="reported"},{t="Stone Golems guard the bridge to the last room. They see you from far off and run faster than you, so you can't outrun them.",s="reported"},{t="The Ghostly Attendant waits in the second room, just past the first corridor.",w=1},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="He patrols the middle of his room, so it's easy to pull him along with trash.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="His curse slows the tank's attacks and spells by 20% for 10 minutes.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear one side of the room, let his patrol bring him close, then pull him alone.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Interrupt his Mind Blast. It hits the tank hard.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Finish both ghost counts now. The Enraged Apparitions and Tormented Souls haunt the halls up to Faldrim's room, and past here you may meet no more.",tp=1},{t="Go back to the Ghostly Attendant in the second room, or hand it in on your way out.",tp=1},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="A Dark Iron Summoner at his side calls fire elementals.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Fire bursts off him on a timer, and Combust burns one player for 12 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill the Summoner first and interrupt its summon. Tank the boss away from the group.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Melee step back when fire bursts off him. Fire spells don't hurt him.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Combust is magic, so it can be dispelled.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Past him, four dwarves stand by two kegs. Shoot the kegs from range first, then crowd-control a Looter.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="He patrols the hall, charges, and knocks people away, into other packs if any are near.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="The knockback drops the tank's threat.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Players report his charge stuns, and slows don't work on him.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear a corner, pull him there and keep your backs to the wall.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Tanks take him back right after each knockback.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Two Stone Golems fight with him and hit hard. Looters stand around the room's edges.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Near half health he fears everyone close. A feared player can run into the Looters.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He Rends the tank, a bleed that hits hard.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="The last pack before him has a golem, a Looter and a Summoner. Polymorph or hold the Summoner first.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill the Looters around the room first, then the golems one at a time.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Shamans: drop Tremor Totem before he reaches half health. Golems you kill stay dead if the group wipes.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="When he dies, finish everything else in the room before you relax.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Open the vault doors round Durgen's room. One holds a stone tablet that starts this quest.",tp=1},{t="Afadra is up the switchback ramp from Thom Filch.",w=1},{t="King Magni is in the throne room, back up the winding passage you came down.",w=1},{t="The Barrens is Horde land. The Crossroads guards attack Alliance players on sight, so keep well clear of the town on every leg here. Ratchet is neutral.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Nalpak is in a hidden cave above the cave mouth. The path up starts at the meeting stone and is easy to miss.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws Thrash about every 10 seconds, two extra swings at once. Don't take one on at low health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ebru stands next to Nalpak in the hidden cave above the cave mouth. Take the path up from the meeting stone.",tp=1},{t="Mad Magglish is in the open caves outside the portal, at one of a few spots. He's slow to respawn.",tp=1},{t="He's stealthed and stands in the narrow spots, so look closely.",tp=1},{t="The portal lies at the back of the open caves behind the cave mouth. The way through runs north, then east and back south to it.",w=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="The cave mouth is under the rock face shaped like a skull, south-west of the Crossroads.",s="classic"},{t="Elites patrol the open caves before the portal. Fight there as carefully as inside.",s="reported"},{t="Some ledges inside are high, and a missed jump can kill.",s="reported"},{t="Deviate Guardians call for help when they're low. Kill them fast.",s="reported"},{t="A rare Deviate Faerie Dragon may wander the caves.",s="reported"},{t="Deviates in the outer caves drop hides too. One run has enough for about three players, so top up outside.",tp=1},{t="She can stand at one of several spots. Look before you pull: at one, a Guardian and a Ravager stand with her.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Interrupt her Healing Touch and her Sleep. Clear the mobs around her before you pull.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Her Thorns Aura hurts anyone who hits her in melee. Use ranged attacks and wands where you can.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He puts a random player to sleep. Don't start a long heal while he can cast.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Three pythons stand with him, and he heals them. Kill them first.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="When he gets low he turns into a big snake and hits harder, but he can't cast in that form. Heal up then.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Optional. He swims the river near the start. Kill him when he comes by, early in the run.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hardest of the four Fang leaders, and two elites fight with him. Crowd-control them or kill them first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="If he puts the tank to sleep, he turns on the next player for a few seconds. Healers, watch for it.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Optional. His Chained Bolt jumps between players. Spread out and interrupt it.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Nature spells do nothing to him. Turn him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Clear the mobs around him first. Interrupt his Healing Touch, which heals him for a lot.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He puts players to sleep. Interrupt it if you can; Priests can dispel it.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He hits very hard. His Grasping Vines knock down and root everyone near him for 10 seconds.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Optional: he sits by the waterfall past Serpentis, and Naralex doesn't need him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Healers and ranged stand well back, so the vines catch only the tank.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Two waves of oozes and snakes attack on the way, then Mutanus rises from the pool. Keep them off the Disciple.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="His Thundercrack stuns everyone close to him for a few seconds. Healers and ranged stand back.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Tank him away from the Disciple of Naralex.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Warlocks and Shadow priests: Shadow spells do nothing to him. Use Fire, Holy or your wand.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Starts from an item Mutanus the Devourer drops.",s="questie"},{t="Back up the slope beside the meeting stone to the hidden cave where Ebru and Nalpak stand.",w=1},{t="Show the shard to Sputtervalve in Ratchet. He sends you on to Falla Sagewind.",tp=1},{t="Falla Sagewind's hut sits high on the mountain over the caverns.",w=1},{t="Falla's hill is about 400 yards west of the Crossroads. Climb it from the south as the arrow leads, and keep off the road into the town.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Go past the Hillsbrad fields, up the west side of Alterac into Tirisfal, round the outside of the ruins to their gate, and in to the courtyard.",w=1},{t="Bears, lions, murlocs and spiders above your level live along this walk. Keep to the arrow and pull nothing you can walk past.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="This is the Horde capital. Reaching Undercity flags you for PvP, and any Horde player can attack you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Players report the entrance is in the Lordaeron courtyard above Undercity. Alliance get there through Horde land.",s="reported"},{t="If you die inside, you come back as a ghost in the courtyard.",s="reported"},{t="Open ruins with no set path. Bosses go in any order, and packs patrol the streets.",s="reported"},{t="Flesh Golems knock you back. Fight them with your back to a wall, away from other packs.",s="reported"},{t="Two hidden bosses come after waves of undead, at a statue and at a chimney fire.",s="reported"},{t="Fog and drifting shadows hide enemies. Pull packs back to lit, open ground before you fight.",s="reported"},{t="Gargoyles on the walls turn to stone and heal, and then take no physical damage. Use spells on them.",s="reported"},{t="Cure Ghoul Plague at once: it lasts 30 minutes.",s="reported"},{t="Ghoul packs stand close together. Pull one, and kill the Ragged Ghoul first.",s="reported"},{t="Captain Truman stands where you zone in, in the north-east corner.",w=1},{t="The crest hangs on a wall at one of several spots: behind a door near the Baron, along Bjork's path, or on a tower top. Everyone clicks their own.",tp=1},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Witherfang walks the whole alley with two spiders. Don't let another pack join the pull.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear the alley first, then pull. Kill the two spiders before Witherfang.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Cure the poison on the tank.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="His Knockout hits the tank very hard and drops the tank's threat.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Groups have died here. A tank below full health can die to one Knockout.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Pull him away from the skeleton packs. Keep stunning him so he can't use Knockout.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Ranged stay back, since he cleaves. Tanks take him back right after a Knockout.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Tank him with your back to a wall, so Knockout can't throw you into a pack.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="To go on, you jump the wall behind him. Hunters and Warlocks, dismiss your pet first.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Optional. Lighting the chimney fire brings five waves of undead with no time to drink.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Then Viktor comes and hits very hard. Tanks at 16 or 17 struggle.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Start it only with full health and mana. Skip him if anyone is unsure.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="A curse in the skeleton waves cuts healing taken by 75%. Remove it fast.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Crossing into Market Street wakes the statue. Three waves of undead come before he does.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He freezes the group in place, chills anyone who hits him and drains the tank's life.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear the enemies around the statue first, and have full mana for the waves.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Interrupt or stun his Drain Life.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill everything round the statue, the tower too, or he won't come. If a wave stalls, find the stuck enemy and pull it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Bjork patrols a long path. Clear the trash along it before you pull.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="His Anti-Magic Shield blocks spells for 3 seconds. Casters wait or use a wand.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="He's a rare spawn, so he may not be there.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="The last boss. His Flamestrike lands where the tank stands, and it hits hard. Melee step away when he casts.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Interrupt or stun Flamestrike. If it lands, the tank drags him out of the fire at once.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear the ghoul packs before him one at a time. They stand close together.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="The letter lies on the ground by Rath'mael.",w=1},{t="Walk back to Captain Truman where you came in. Don't hearth out before you hand this in.",tp=1},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 10 Rough Dynamite, made by Engineers or bought on the Auction House.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It sends you back to Alba Fairmoon in Westfall, on your way to the Deadmines.",tp=1},{t="It follows Sprite Jumpsprocket's dynamite errand, which needs Rough Dynamite.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It follows Sprite Jumpsprocket's dynamite errand, which needs Rough Dynamite.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Alba Fairmoon offers this once you've done Sprite Jumpsprocket's dynamite errands in Stormwind.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gryan Stoutmantle stands up on the peak of the Sentinel Hill tower.",tp=1},{t="Wiley the Black is upstairs in the Lakeshire inn.",w=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 headquarters in Old Town.",w=1},{t="The Defias Messenger starts in Moonbrook and walks the road north, past Jangolode Mine and the Gold Coast Quarry.",tp=1},{t="He comes back quickly after he dies. If he isn't on the road, look for him at Moonbrook.",tp=1},{t="The Defias Traitor isn't always at his spot. If he's gone, wait for his respawn.",tp=1},{t="Defias attack the escort when it reaches Moonbrook. Stay at the Traitor's side all the way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only the Whitestone Oak Lumber is in here: the Goblin Woodcarvers in Sneed's room drop it.",tp=1},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The mine starts in the big house in the middle of Moonbrook. Go in and follow the tunnel down.",w=1},{t="This one is done outside the instance, in the mine before the portal.",tp=1},{t="Finished outside the instance, in the mine on the way down to the portal.",tp=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Go into the building in the middle of Moonbrook and follow the mine tunnel down to the portal.",s="classic"},{t="Most bosses are level 20 and VanCleef is 21. Under 19, the end of the run is hard on the tank.",s="reported"},{t="Patrols come up behind you after the early bosses. Drink with your back to a cleared room.",s="reported"},{t="Some Defias stun the tank again and again. Pull small.",s="reported"},{t="Bandanas drop from the Defias inside the Deadmines too, so you can finish this during the run.",tp=1},{t="Only this part of the quest is in here. Its other parts are elsewhere, so it isn't handed in after this run.",s="questie"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="His Slam stuns the tank for 3 seconds and hits very hard. Keep the tank's health up before every Slam.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Two Defias stand near him. Wait until he moves away from them, then pull him alone.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Defias Miners stand around him and join the pull.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He's a rare spawn, so he may not be there. Kill the Miners first, then him.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The shredder's Terrify sends a player running. Clear the goblins in the room first, or you'll run into them.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="When the shredder dies, Sneed jumps out and fights on. He disarms the tank. Tank him at once and loot only when he's dead.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Goblin Engineers call golems that keep coming while the engineer lives. Kill or stun the engineer first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="The goblins in his foundry are the hard part. Pull them a few at a time before you take Gilnid.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Plant the Extra-Destructive Explosives near the middle of Gilnid's foundry.",u=254553},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Two hidden Blackguards jump you at the ship ramp before he charges in. His Smite Slam stuns the tank too.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="At two-thirds and one-third health he stomps and stuns the whole group. Kill his two guards first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="After each stomp he walks to his chest to change weapons. Heal up while he's away.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He runs when he's low and can bring more pirates back. Clear the mobs around him first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His Poisoned Harpoon hurts for a full minute. Druids, Shamans and Paladins can cure it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="He walks the ship's deck. Watch his path so he doesn't join the pack before him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="A caster and a fighter come with him. Crowd-control the Squallshaper and face him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Two Blackguards fight beside him from the start, and two more come at half health.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Crowd-control one guard, and stun him as he nears half health to stop the second pair.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Starts from an item Edwin VanCleef drops.",s="questie"},{t="Alba waits outside the Deadmines' back exit, on the coast below Moonbrook.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can only do it after planting the explosives inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can only do it after planting the explosives inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Deadmines, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Paladin quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Warlocks only. Its fragments come from two dungeons, this one and Blackfathom Deeps.",y=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="The keep is on the hill above Pyrewood Village, south of the Sepulcher.",s="classic"},{t="Undead in the courtyard silence everyone near them for about 5 seconds, often. Casters stand back.",s="reported"},{t="The Lupine Horror room above the courtyard comes all at once if you rush in. Pull from the door.",s="reported"},{t="The horses in the stables pull together. Hold one while the group kills the rest, one by one.",s="reported"},{t="Trash near the end is level 25. At 20, bring a full group.",s="reported"},{t="Only this part of the quest is in here. Its other parts are elsewhere, so it isn't handed in after this run.",s="questie"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only the Large Soran'ruk Fragment is in here, from Shadowfang Darksouls. The three small ones are in Blackfathom Deeps.",s="questie"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="His Soul Drain roots you for 10 seconds while it drains you. Pull his two worgs off him first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Once he's dead, talk to your faction's prisoner in the cells. He opens the courtyard door.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Horde: Deathstalker Adamant. Alliance: Sorcerer Ashcrombe.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="A patrol walks past outside his kitchen. Kill it before you pull him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His Veil of Shadow cuts healing on its target by 75% for 15 seconds. Mages and Druids can remove it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="The Wailing Guardsman with him silences everyone near it. Tank it away from the group.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Kill the Haunted Servitor first, then Springvale. Interrupt his Holy Light.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He shields himself when low and heals inside it. Save your interrupt for the Holy Light after.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He howls three times, and each howl makes him and his two bats hit harder. Kill the bats first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="A rare, the Deathsworn Captain, can stand past Odo. He cleaves: tank him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="When he dies, Arugal sends four Voidwalkers. They heal each other, so focus one down before the next.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His four elite worgs attack before he does, and he calls more during the fight. Start at full health.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Void Bolt can kill a cloth wearer in three or four hits. Interrupt it every time you can.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His curse makes a player a worgen that fights you for 10 seconds. Stop hitting them; fear or polymorph them.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Thundershock stuns everyone near him for 5 seconds.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="He teleports between the raised ledges. Don't chase him; ranged keep shooting, melee wait for him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Each teleport wipes his threat. Hold your damage until the tank has him again.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="The Black Tome lies on the table up the stairs behind Arugal's room.",w=1},{t="Optional. Use it at the Ambermill Leyline Focus, in Ambermill's town hall in Silverpine. It becomes the Tome of Dalaran, which calls a hidden boss in the City of Dalaran.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Doan Karhan takes it once you carry all four fragments, from this run and Blackfathom Deeps.",w=1},{t="A Warlock quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A lead-in only: Gershala Nightwhisper gives Researching the Corruption without it.",y=1},{t="A lead-in: Gershala Nightwhisper offers Researching the Corruption without it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Paladins only: the Kor Gem is one of the four items The Test of Righteousness asks for.",y=1},{t="Warlocks only. Its fragments come from two dungeons, this one and Shadowfang Keep.",y=1},{t="The Corrupted Kor Gem drops from the Blackfathom naga, in the flooded cave and inside the dungeon.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Experienced Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Ruins in the water off the Zoram Strand, on Ashenvale's west coast. The portal is under water: swim down.",s="classic"},{t="Dive into the pool among the ruins. The cave under the water leads past naga to the portal. Watch your breath.",s="reported"},{t="Threshers in the water below can reach you through the floor of the room above. Keep off the edges.",s="reported"},{t="Some Twilight cultists are level 26 or 27 and can take control of a player. Kill them first.",s="reported"},{t="A Pitted Iron Chest under the water, where the turtles swim, holds Lorgalis' Manuscript.",w=1},{t="Argent Guard Thaelrid can repair your gear.",tp=1},{t="Only the three small Soran'ruk Fragments are in here, from Twilight Acolytes. The large one is in Shadowfang Keep.",s="questie"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Thick armor makes him a slow kill for melee. His Trample hits everyone standing close.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Forked Lightning hits everyone in front of her. Tank turns her away from the group; interrupt it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="She moves around her cave during the fight. Clear it first so she doesn't drag in more naga.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Murlocs in his room run when they're low and bring help, him included. Kill them before they flee.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="When he's dead, gather by the shrine in his room, then one of you clicks it. It gives the Blessing of Blackfathom once.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He stands in one of a few spots, from the tunnel past Gelihast to the first Twilight cultists.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His cave is under water with no air. Without Unending Breath or Water Breathing, leave him alone.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Warlocks (Unending Breath) and Shamans (Water Breathing): cast it on everyone before you swim down.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He heals himself over time. Don't start unless your group can out-damage it.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Once he dies, the altar's four fires open Aku'mai's door. Each brings a wave, so light one and clear it before the next.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Clear his room before you wake him. He puts a player to sleep, often the tank, and Mind Blasts.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Have someone ready to hold him while the tank sleeps.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="She hits very hard and can kill a tank in a few swings. Start at full health and mana.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="She enrages near the end and attacks much faster. Save your cooldowns for it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Her room is wide and she notices you from far off. Pull the last turtles back toward the door, or she joins in.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Her Poison Cloud hurts everyone near her for 15 seconds. Ranged and healer keep their distance. Cure the poison.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="You finish it inside Blackfathom Deeps, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Doan Karhan takes it once you carry all four fragments, from this run and Shadowfang Keep.",w=1},{t="A Warlock quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Dark Iron in Dun Modr is an elite, levels 27 to 31. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dark Iron Saboteurs can blow themselves up (Sapper Explode), burning anyone close. Keep your health high near one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bombs come nonstop from Dark Iron Demolitionists at range. Close in fast or pull them out of sight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Kam Deepfury is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The end of the Stockade chain, back with Warden Thelwater. Hand it in if you're passing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The end of the Stockade chain, back with Warden Thelwater. Hand it in if you're passing.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="This needs The Unsent Letter done first, in Deadmines.",s="questie"},{t="Bazil Thredd is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Kill Defias Captives first. Their Infected Wound makes the tank take more damage for 5 minutes.",s="reported"},{t="Every cell can hold a pack. Pull one cell at a time.",s="reported"},{t="A rare dwarf, Bruegal Ironknuckle, is sometimes in a cell in the west hall.",s="reported"},{t="Players report the bandanas drop rarely. You may need a second run.",tp=1},{t="Items of Some Consequence, later in the Defias story, asks for 3 Silk Cloth.",y=1},{t="Keep 3 Silk Cloth from the prisoners in here. Items of Some Consequence asks for them after the run.",tp=1},{t="He swings two weapons with extra attacks and can enrage. Healers, keep the tank's health high.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His Shield Slam stuns the tank for 2 seconds. Don't let a stun cost you the adds.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Crowd-control one of the prisoners by him and kill the other first.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Kam Deepfury is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Interrupt his Chain Lightning. It hits hard and jumps to two more players, so don't bunch up.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Purge or dispel his Bloodlust. Two Defias sit with him: crowd-control one, kill the other.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His shout fears everyone near him for 6 seconds. Clear the nearby cells first; ranged stand back.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="He dual wields and can kill a tank fast. Two guards come with him: crowd-control one or pull it away.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="While his Smoke Bomb stuns the tank, he hits the next player down. Healers stay out of its range.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His Smoke Bomb stuns everyone near him for 4 seconds. Kill the Defias Insurgent first.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Bazil Thredd is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bazil Thredd is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 3 Silk Cloth and two of Clara's apples from Elwynn Forest.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Clara's Fresh Apples sit on a table inside her farm house, north-west of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest.",w=1},{t="It needs 3 Silk Cloth and two of Clara's apples from Elwynn Forest.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 3 Silk Cloth and two of Clara's apples from Elwynn Forest.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs 3 Silk Cloth and two of Clara's apples from Elwynn Forest.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="In a group, let everyone finish Items of Some Consequence first: the scene starts for whoever takes this quest first.",tp=1},{t="Wait in the middle of the Stormwind Keep garden. Lord Gregor Lescovar and Marzon the Silent Blade arrive after about two minutes of talk.",w=1},{t="Both fight you at once: Lescovar is level 31, Marzon 30.",d=1},{t="Master Mathias Shaw is upstairs in the SI:7 headquarters in Old Town.",w=1},{t="Baros Alexston is inside the building at the edge of Cathedral Square.",w=1},{t="Kam Deepfury is elite: a hard fight alone.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="An outdoor dungeon. Stay out of the tall grass. Hidden raptors spawn in it and join any fight.",s="reported"},{t="Bring cures. Raptors cause bleeds, spiders poison you, and crocs and spiders spread diseases.",s="reported"},{t="Raptors follow you into the water. A bad pull resets on the wooden planks, not in the water.",s="reported"},{t="Some raptors are stealthed. Move slowly, and keep the healer out of the grass.",s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Saltspine patrols around the swamp and can walk into your fight with a croc pack.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear the crocs near his path, then pull him in the open.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Casters stay 10 yards away. His Dust Storm makes nearby attacks miss.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Two Thicket Hunters come with him. His roar fears the group for 5 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Feared players run into the tall grass, and hidden raptors join the fight.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He patrols the raptor path. A screeching roar means he's coming: clear the area before he arrives.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Keep both Hunters out of the fight (Hibernate, roots, Polymorph). Thicket Matriarchs call more raptors when low.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Fear Ward, Tremor Totem or Berserker Rage stop the fear. Save stuns for his enrage at low health.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Don't drag him into the water: he resets.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="It roots everyone near it with Entangling Roots. Healers stand back.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="The Dragonmaw campfires burn anyone within 5 yards, players too.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="It sits in an alcove at the Dragonmaw camp, off the path. Pull it away from the Dragonmaw.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Drag it through the campfires to burn it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Level 31. He hits the tank very hard and may stun the tank for 5 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="His knockback drops the tank's threat, and he turns on whoever is next.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Click the Archival Panel at his right to wake him, once everyone is ready.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Stay 10 yards out of Thunderclap. Damage dealers ease off after each knockback.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Experienced Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Players report the way in is a sewer grate on the Lordamere Lake shore, on the Silverpine side, by the Image of Archmage Modera.",s="reported"},{t="Almost every enemy is immune to Arcane. Arcane spells, Arcane Shot and Counterspell won't work.",s="reported"},{t="Mana Phantoms Mana Burn your healer. Interrupt them or kill them first.",s="reported"},{t="Some ledges in the city are high enough that the fall kills you.",s="reported"},{t="You get in through a sewer grate by the lake.",s="reported"},{t="The bosses are level 30 to 33. Level 31 is safer.",s="reported"},{t="Fragmented Sentinels smash everyone in front of them. Pull them one at a time.",s="reported"},{t="Fast Arcane Manalings patrol in fives, and Mana Fiends explode for about 250 when they die. Step away from them.",s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Waves of Fallen and Necromancers come first, then him. He fears.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He raises skeletons, disarms the tank and speeds up his attacks with Unholy Frenzy.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Pull the three Necromancers round his path one or two at a time while he walks away.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill the skeletons as they come, but let the tank grab them before you hit them all.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Tanks keep a shield on for this fight.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="A hidden boss and a hard one. Shadow Bolt Volley hits the whole group.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Curse of Thorns makes your own attacks hurt you.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Optional. The Tome of Dalaran from Shadowfang Keep summons him. Past Atrexis, go straight on into the side room, not up the ramp, and use it on the circle.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Remove his curse fast and kill the two skeletons he raises.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Focal Blast is a beam that sweeps around the room. Standing in it can kill you.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Small adds wait at the room's edge.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Fight inside the circle on the platform so the adds at the edge stay out.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="The beam can turn either way. Watch it and step out of its path.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="It silences everyone in melee range, the tank too.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Manamorph turns a random player into a sheep. Dispel it.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill its two Mana Phantoms first, then hit the Manalings it calls with area damage.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="After a short wind-up, Malfunction hits everyone within 25 yards every 2 seconds for 6 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Arcing Smash hits everyone in front of him.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill the Angry Tomes that come out of the buildings before you pull.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Ranged stay 25 yards away. Melee run out when he winds up. A stun during the wind-up stops it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Fel Timbers leaves a green pool that burns anyone in it for 10 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Entangle roots two players. Rooted in a pool, you can't step out.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="A barrier blocks Runeweaver Square. Talk to Grindle Firespark to drop it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Step out of green pools at once. Blessing of Freedom and Escape Artist break the roots.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="The blossoms grow in the corners of the Fel Ancient's room.",w=1},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Debilitate hits everyone within 45 yards and drains 200 mana. The group runs dry fast.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Trash left near him joins the fight.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear every pack around him first, then kill him as fast as you can.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="His Drain Vitality keeps hurting the tank. Healers, watch for it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="His parlor crowns the Violet Citadel. Don't jump off the edge: the fall kills. Take the teleport down.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Bounding Mana flies to one player and back. Anyone in its path takes about 300 and is silenced.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="When his mana runs out, he polymorphs the group and refills with Evocation. Mana Phantoms go for the healer.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Talk to Archmage Modera at the foot of the Citadel. She opens the way up.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Spread out and keep out of the orb's path. Casters stay 20 yards away from Arcane Explosion.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Damage dealers kill the Mana Phantoms. Stay inside his room the whole fight, or he resets.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Brother Sarno is inside the Cathedral of Light.",w=1},{t="Gnoarn stands in Tinker Town, a few steps from Tinkmaster Overspark.",w=1},{t="Go in at Gnomeregan's gate and down into the caves. The irradiated troggs and lepers are there, outside the portal.",w=1},{t="Techbot is an elite in the caves outside Gnomeregan's portal.",w=1},{t="First loot a White Punch Card from the irradiated troggs and lepers in the caves, then use it at Matrix Punchograph 3005-A, also out there.",tp=1},{t="Then use B in the Dormitory, C on the Electrocutioner's platform and D in the Engineering Labs below.",tp=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Experienced Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Take the elevator at the airfield in western Dun Morogh down into the tunnels. The front door is past the Train Depot.",s="classic"},{t="Kill Mobile Alert Systems and Alarm-a-bombs at once. They call elites.",s="reported"},{t="Don't fall off the central structure. Mobs below walk round with about a dozen more.",s="reported"},{t="Techbot, an elite near the start, stuns, roots and calls bugs that heal it. Kill the bugs and treat it as a real fight.",s="reported"},{t="Arcane Nullifier X-21 sends spells back and ignores bleeds and poisons. Dark Iron Agents lay mines.",s="reported"},{t="A rare, the Dark Iron Ambassador, can stand in the tunnel before Tinkers' Court. He casts Fireball and calls a fire add.",s="reported"},{t="Kernobee wanders the Dormitory, next door to the Clean Zone by the way in.",w=1},{t="Walk him back to the Clockwerk Run exit at the start and keep him alive on the way.",tp=1},{t="The fallout doesn't last. Fill the phial on your way out, then go straight to Ozzie in Kharanos.",tp=1},{t="It needs a Grime-Encrusted Item, a random drop in here, and 3 silver. Skip it if nothing dropped.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Gnomeregan, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Gnomeregan, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Gnomeregan, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only if the Grime-Encrusted Ring dropped for you. Cleaning it costs 3 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only if the Grime-Encrusted Ring dropped for you. Cleaning it costs 3 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Talking to Emi Shortfuse starts waves of troggs from the tunnels. Keep them off her the whole time.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="When she counts down to blow a tunnel, get out of it. Grubbis and his basilisk come after the last wave.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He looks like the other oozes nearby. Type /target Viscous Fallout to find him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Bring a poison cure. Each hit on him stacks a debuff that lowers your physical damage.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Chain Bolt jumps between up to three players for heavy damage. Spread out and interrupt it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His Megavolt hits everyone in front of him. Face him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Crowd Pummel knocks everyone round him back, behind him too. Tank with a wall at your back and keep off the platform's edge.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Arcing Smash hits everything in front of him. The tank turns him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Crowd Pummel hits everyone near him and stops their casts, so casters stay back.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He switches on bomb machines on the walls. Their Walking Bombs chase a player and blow up everyone near.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="He knocks the tank away and drops their threat. Taunt him back fast; healers hold still and let the tank pick him up.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Give one player the job of pressing the button on the side of each working machine. It stops the bombs.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Only if the Grime-Encrusted Ring dropped for you. Cleaning it costs 3 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Sparklematic 5200 cleans the ring for 3 silver. It's in the Clean Zone, back by the way in.",tp=1},{t="Only if the Grime-Encrusted Ring dropped for you. Cleaning it costs 3 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can keep the ring as it is, or take it back to its maker.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can keep the ring as it is, or take it back to its maker.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Talvash del Kissel is in the Mystic Ward, at its north end.",w=1},{t="It needs a Silver Bar and a Moss Agate, from Mining or the Auction House, and 30 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Silver Bar and a Moss Agate, from Mining or the Auction House, and 30 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Players report the journal missing from his body on the beta. Skip this if it isn't there.",tp=1},{t="The Crate With Holes, Command Stick and Owner's Manual lie beside Mebok. Pick up all three.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Razorfen Kraul, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Razorfen Kraul, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Razorfen Kraul, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Warrior quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Warrior quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Warrior quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Experienced Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="In the far south of the Barrens, inside the Razorfen thorns by the Thousand Needles border.",s="classic"},{t="Bats silence you for about 10 seconds. Casters and healers stay back in the bat room.",s="reported"},{t="Many quilboar drop totems, healing ones too. Kill the totems first.",s="reported"},{t="Quilboar packs stun, knock down and heal each other. Pull one pack at a time and interrupt the heals.",s="reported"},{t="Two rares can be here: Earthcaller Halmgar and the Blind Hunter, who silences.",s="reported"},{t="Inside, turn left at the first fork and follow that passage to the big vine. Jump down to the Agam'ar pit beneath it and clear it.",w=1},{t="Open the Crate With Holes down in the pit to call a gopher",u=5880},{t="Point the Command Stick at the gopher so it digs, and loot each tuber it finds, six in all. One crate holds five gophers.",tp=1},{t="He's off the main path, past the first left and across the big vine. He calls a Stone Rumbler to help.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Only this part of the quest is in here. Its other parts are elsewhere, so it isn't handed in after this run.",s="questie"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Interrupt his Chain Heal. He calls a Boar Spirit to help, so hold it or kill it first. Step out of the red on the ground.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He takes control of a player. Interrupt or dispel it, and never finish off a friend he controls.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Kill his guards first while someone keeps him busy. Interrupt his Shadow Bolts. His guards burn mana.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Two elite Spearhide guards fight with him. Crowd-control them, or tank him while the group kills them.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His pack runs when it's low. Slow or stun runners before they bring help.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His wall opens once the Ward Guardians and the Seer in the bat room are dead. Then he charges out.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His Rampage stuns everyone close to him. Healers and ranged keep their distance.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Her Chain Bolt hits up to three players for heavy damage. Spread out so it reaches fewer.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Stuns don't work on her and Shadow does nothing. Warlocks and Shadow priests: use other spells.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Dispel or purge her Renew. When she shields herself, wait it out: it clears your debuffs on her.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Heralath Fallowbrook's body lies past Charlga Razorflank, in the dungeon's last part.",w=1},{t="Treshala's Pendant drops from any quilboar in here. Kill what attacks on the walk out with Willix.",tp=1},{t="Drop down behind Charlga's platform. Willix is in the tent below.",w=1},{t="A big pack of casters stands by the tent. Pull it before you talk to him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Camping 101: Mining, from the adventurer near your first town: at skill 20 your trainer teaches you the Lodestone, a camp feature for your campfire (1 Rough Stone and 1 Copper Bar).",s="client"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Copper Vein (skill 1), Poor Copper Vein (skill 1, new in Forever). About 79 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 4-12.",s="questie"},{t="Journeyman: it needs skill 50 and level 10, as players saw in the beta.",s="author"},{t="Tin Vein (skill 65), Copper Vein (skill 1). About 53 nodes on a 6-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75), Bronze (a point every time until 65, none from 115).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 9-26.",s="questie"},{t="Camping 101: Mining, from the adventurer near your first town: at skill 20 your trainer teaches you the Lodestone, a camp feature for your campfire (1 Rough Stone and 1 Copper Bar).",s="client"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Copper Vein (skill 1), Poor Copper Vein (skill 1, new in Forever). About 79 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 5-11.",s="questie"},{t="Journeyman: it needs skill 50 and level 10, as players saw in the beta.",s="author"},{t="Tin Vein (s