angos"},{t="Expert First Aid comes from a book, not a trainer: Expert First Aid - Under Wraps. It needs First Aid 125.",s="client"},{t="The book asks no level, but the trip does: buy it at the Auction House or ask a friend to mail it. Else Balai Lok'Wein sells it in Brackenwall Village, Dustwallow Marsh (level 35-45), with the Heavy Silk Bandage manual: buy both.",w=1},{t="On your way, Silk Cloth drops from Laughing Sister and Razormane Stalker in Ashenvale and The Barrens (level 22-25). Watch for Hagg Taurenbane (elite, level 26) close by.",s="vmangos"},{t="On your way, Mageweave Cloth drops from Drywhisker Digger in Arathi Highlands (level 36-37). Before you get there, the Auction House has it.",s="vmangos"},{t="Your trainer teaches it. The skill it needs isn't confirmed for Forever yet: 120 at the latest.",s="author"},{t="For the whole step: about 12 crafts, 24 Wool Cloth, 24 Fine Thread.",s="client"},{t="Your trainer teaches it. The skill it needs isn't confirmed for Forever yet: 150 at the latest.",s="author"},{t="For the whole step: about 42 crafts, 42 Silk Cloth.",s="client"},{t="Taught by Manual: Heavy Silk Bandage, sold by Deneb Walker in Arathi Highlands.",s="client"},{t="Taught by Manual: Heavy Silk Bandage, sold by Balai Lok'Wein in Dustwallow Marsh.",s="client"},{t="For the whole step: about 42 crafts, 84 Silk Cloth.",s="client"},{t="Taught by Manual: Mageweave Bandage, sold by Deneb Walker in Arathi Highlands.",s="client"},{t="Taught by Manual: Mageweave Bandage, sold by Balai Lok'Wein in Dustwallow Marsh.",s="client"},{t="For the whole step: about 18 crafts, 18 Mageweave Cloth.",s="client"},{t="Every Legacy challenge counts for your whole account. A dungeon counts when you kill its last boss.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Durgen Dirgehammer. Opens at level 13.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Bjork. Opens at level 15.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Mutanus the Devourer. Opens at level 15.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Edwin VanCleef. Opens at level 17.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Archmage Arugal. Opens at level 20.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Relic Guardian. Opens at level 26.",s="client"}},
quests={[5]={t="Jitters' Growling Gut",lv=20,min=17,nx=93,ot="Speak with Chef Grual.",st="I've been stuck hiding in this ghost town for weeks, and I haven't eaten anything but grubs and weeds!  I need some decent food, and I'm willing to trade well for it.$B$BBring me a feast and I'll pay you handsomely.$B$BI heard Chef Grual at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire makes very good Dusky Crab Cakes..."},[6]={t="Bounty on Garrick Padfoot",lv=5,min=2,pre1={18},rwc={[1]=2,[2]=2,[3]=2,[4]=2,[5]=1,[8]=1,[9]=1},ot="Kill Garrick Padfoot and bring his head to Deputy Willem at Northshire Abbey.",st="Garrick Padfoot - a cutthroat who's plagued our farmers and merchants for weeks - was seen at a shack near the vineyards, which lies east of the Abbey and across the bridge.  Bring me the villain's head, and earn his bounty!$B$BBut be wary, $n.  Garrick has gathered a gang of thugs around him.  He will not be an easy man to reach.",how={{"loot",182,{103}}}},[7]={t="Kobold Camp Cleanup",lv=2,min=1,pre1={783},nx=15,si=247834,ot="Kill 10 Kobold Vermin, then return to Marshal McBride.",st="Your first task is one of cleansing, $n.  A clan of kobolds have infested the woods to the north.  Go there and fight the kobold vermin you find.  Reduce their numbers so that we may one day drive them from Northshire.",how={{"kill",6}}},[9]={t="The Killing Fields",lv=15,min=8,rwc={[8]=1},ot="Farmer Saldean wants you to kill 20 Harvest Watchers.",st="Look at what has happened to this place!  These lands were once occupied by good farm folk.  But the damned thieves have driven them all off.  Not me, though!  But it seems some Harvest Watchers have taken over the fields.$b$bIf you're up for the work, I'd like you to go out and kill twenty of them.  Come back when you're done for your pay.  If you finish up with the ones in my field, clear them from the neighboring fields as well.",how={{"kill",114}}},[11]={t="Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty",lv=10,min=6,pre1={76},ot="Bring 8 Painted Gnoll Armbands to Deputy Rainer at the Barracks.",st="Gnolls, brutish creatures with no decent business in these lands, have been seen along the borders of Elwynn Forest.  A large pack of them, many more than we can handle alone, have infested the woods south of the guard tower yonder.  Another group has infested the areas near Stone Cairn Lake to the east.$B$BThe Stormwind Army will commend whomever helps kill them.  Bring me their painted gnoll armbands as proof of your deed.",how={{"loot",782,{478}}}},[12]={t="The People's Militia",lv=12,min=9,nx=13,ot="Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to him on Sentinel Hill.",st="The People's Militia has but one goal:  To defend the lands of Westfall and return peace to our surroundings.  Unfortunately, the price of peace is often blood. $b$bOne of my scouts has brought word of a band of Defias Trappers wreaking havoc nearby.  I have reports of Defias Trapper sightings near the Jangolode Mine to the Northwest as well as at the Molsen Farm and Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm. If you seek to join our ranks, slay 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to me.",how={{"kill",504},{"kill",95}}},[13]={t="The People's Militia",lv=14,min=9,pre1={12},nx=14,ot="Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters and return to him on Sentinel Hill.",st="A band of vicious Defias Pillagers has been seen plundering the Gold Coast Quarry, Moonbrook and the Alexston Farmstead.  The People's Militia will not stand for such behavior.  Dispatch immediately, $n, and make the Light's presence known in Westfall.$b$bThe Gold Coast Quarry is near the shore, to the West of the tower.  As the next step of your training, I want you to kill 15 of those foul Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters.",how={{"kill",589},{"kill",590}}},[14]={t="The People's Militia",lv=17,min=9,pre1={13},ot="Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Highwaymen, 5 Defias Pathstalkers and 5 Defias Knuckledusters then return to him on Sentinel Hill.",st="Some Defias have eluded us.  My most trusted scout reports that these Defias have been looting and pillaging the countryside, all the way into Southern Westfall.  We believe they are hiding out in the Dagger Hills, plotting their next move.   Slay the wretches in the name of The People's Militia.",how={{"kill",122},{"kill",121},{"kill",449}}},[15]={t="Investigate Echo Ridge",lv=3,min=1,pre1={7},nx=21,ot="Kill 10 Kobold Workers, then report back to Marshal McBride.",st="$n, my scouts tell me that the kobold infestation is larger than we had thought.  A group of kobold workers has camped near the Echo Ridge Mine to the north.$B$BGo to the mine and remove them.  We know there are at least 10.  Kill them, see if there are more, then report back to me.",how={{"kill",257}}},[18]={t="Brotherhood of Thieves",lv=4,min=2,pre1={783},rwc={[1]=3,[2]=4,[4]=1,[5]=2,[8]=5,[9]=1},ot="Bring 12 Red Burlap Bandanas to Deputy Willem outside the Northshire Abbey.",st="Recently, a new group of thieves has been hanging around Northshire.  They call themselves the Defias Brotherhood, and have been seen across the river to the east.$B$BI don't know what they're up to, but I'm sure it's not good!  Bring me the bandanas they wear, and I'll reward you with a weapon.",how={{"loot",752,{38}}}},[19]={t="Tharil'zun",lv=25,min=18,pre={20,98387},ot="Bring Tharil'zun's Head to Marshal Marris in Redridge.",st="Blackrock Outrunners and Renegades are running ambushes between here and Stonewatch Keep.  The leader of the Outrunners is an orc named Tharil'zun--we want this orc.  Bring me the head of Tharil'zun!",how={{"loot",1260,{486}}}},[20]={t="Blackrock Menace",lv=21,min=18,nx=19,ot="Bring 10 Battleworn Axes to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.",st="The Blackrock orcs have travelled from the Burning Steppes and claimed Stonewatch Keep to the north.  From there they maraud the areas north of Lakeshire and keep its citizens in town, penned like cattle.$B$BHelp rid Lakeshire of this menace.  Kill these Blackrock orcs and bring me ten of their Battleworn Axes as proof.$B$BAnd although Blackrocks threaten us from the north, we've received reports of more in the southeastern pocket of Redridge.  If you find any there, then they too should be hunted.",how={{"loot",3014,{485,440,437}}}},[21]={t="Skirmish at Echo Ridge",lv=5,min=1,pre1={15},nx=54,rwc={[1]=2,[2]=2,[3]=1,[4]=1,[5]=3,[8]=3,[9]=3},ot="Kill 12 Kobold Laborers, then return to Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey.",st="Your previous investigations are proof that the Echo Ridge Mine needs purging.  Return to the mine and help clear it of kobolds.$B$BWaste no time, $n.  The longer the kobolds are left unmolested in the mine, the deeper a foothold they gain in Northshire.",how={{"kill",80}}},[22]={t="Goretusk Liver Pie",lv=12,min=9,ot="Salma Saldean needs 8 Goretusk livers to make a Goretusk Liver Pie.",st="The onions are peeled.  The garlic is minced.  The rosemary is crushed.  The crust has been baked.  The dill weed is chopped.  The gravy is simmering.  Now all I need for my famous meat pie are 8 Goretusk Livers!",how={{"loot",723,{454,157}}}},[26]={t="A Lesson to Learn",lv=16,min=16,nx=29,ot="Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.",st="$n, I have been following your progress with much delight.  You are most assuredly developing yourself into a valued protector of nature.$B$BThe time has come for you to learn more about one of the various animal aspects that Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to change into - one that affords you command and mastery of the water.  For this, you must travel to the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle there.  He will guide you further."},[29]={t="Trial of the Lake",lv=16,min=16,pre1={26},nx=272,si=15877,ot="Find a Shrine Bauble in Lake Elune'ara, and take it to the Shrine of Remulos in northwestern Moonglade.  Once there, use the Shrine Bauble.$B$BYou must speak with Tajarri at the shrine afterwards in order to complete the trial.",st="For your first trial, search the depths of Lake Elune'ara to locate a Shrine Bauble.  It decays rapidly, so proceed with it to the Shrine of Remulos post haste.  Use the bauble at the shrine, and then speak with Tajarri there; she is one of Moonglade's most trusted wardens.$B$BYou only have a set amount of time to complete the task, and you may be competing against other druids searching for baubles themselves.  Mental and physical dexterity will be critical to your success.$B$BGood luck, $n.",how={{"click",15885}}},[33]={t="Wolves Across the Border",lv=2,min=1,rwc={[1]=2,[2]=2,[3]=2,[4]=2,[5]=1,[8]=1,[9]=1},ot="Bring 8 pieces of Tough Wolf Meat to Eagan Peltskinner outside Northshire Abbey.",st="I hate those nasty timber wolves!  But I sure like eating wolf steaks...  Bring me tough wolf meat and I will exchange it for something you'll find useful.$B$BTough wolf meat is gathered from hunting the timber wolves and young wolves wandering the Northshire countryside.",how={{"loot",750,{69,299,705}}}},[34]={t="An Unwelcome Guest",lv=24,min=18,ot="Martie Jainrose of Lakeshire wants you to kill Bellygrub.  Bring her his tusk as proof.",st="Once again my garden was trampled and pillaged.  And I know the brute who is doing it.  It's that forsaken boar, the one Marshal Marris has taken to calling Bellygrub.$b$bI won't be able to re-plant the daffodils until next season now.  Ruined!  All ruined by that one menacing boar.  Put an end to that pest!  Show me his tusk and I'd be happy to reward you.  He seems to spend his time foraging in the field southwest of Lakeshire but occasionally he roams over here and into my garden.",how={{"loot",3631,{345}}}},[35]={t="Further Concerns",lv=10,min=7,pre1={40},nx=37,ot="Marshal Dughan wants you to speak with Guard Thomas.",st="If you are concerned that the rumors of murlocs are true, then do this -- travel to the eastern Elwynn bridge and speak with Guard Thomas.  He has been stationed at the bridge for the past week and will know the state of the area.$B$BBring me his report."},[36]={t="Westfall Stew",lv=10,min=9,nx=38,si=2832,ot="Verna Furlbrow wants you to deliver her recipe for Westfall Stew to Salma Saldean.",st="I never thought the day would come when I'd leave the farm.  But the fields are overrun with thieves and it's far too dangerous for us here now.  As soon as Farmer Furlbrow gets the wagon fixed, we'll be on our way.  $b $bMaybe you could do me a favor?  Let me scribble down my recipe for Westfall stew.  Please take it to Salma Saldean over on the farm yonder.  The Saldean's farm is just beyond the fork in the road."},[37]={t="Find the Lost Guards",lv=10,min=7,pre1={35},nx=45,ot="Guard Thomas wants you to travel north up the river and search for the two lost guards, Rolf and Malakai.",st="A few days ago we sent two Guards, Rolf and Malakai, to investigate along the river, and they have not yet returned.  To complete my report, I must know what happened to those men.$B$BTravel north along the river and find the guards... or their remains."},[38]={t="Westfall Stew",lv=13,min=9,pre1={36},ot="Salma Saldean wants 3 Stringy Vulture Meat, 3 Goretusk Snouts, 3 Murloc Eyes, 3 Okra.",st="Help me make some Westfall Stew!  Come back with the following ingredients: $b $b 3 Stringy Vulture Meat $b 3 Goretusk Snouts $b 3 Murloc Eyes $b 3 Okra",how={{"loot",729,{199,1109}},{"loot",730,{126,515}},{"loot",731,{454,157}},{"loot",732,{114}}}},[39]={t="Deliver Thomas' Report",lv=10,min=7,pre1={71},nx=59,ot="Report to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.",st="Tell Marshal Dughan of Malakai and Rolf's deaths, and report to him that the Murlocs in eastern Elwynn cannot be contained by our current troop presence.$B$BI know we don't have many troops to spare, but hopefully Dughan can find someone."},[40]={t="A Fishy Peril",lv=10,min=7,nx=35,ot="Remy \"Two Times\" wants you to speak with Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.",st="$n, there's a new threat in Elwynn Forest!  Murlocs are swimming up the streams of eastern Elwynn, scaring away fish and attacking gentle folk!$B$BI warned Marshal Dughan, but he's more worried about the gnolls and the bandits.  He's not convinced that the murlocs are a danger.$B$BPlease, $n, speak to Dughan and persuade him to send more troops to the east!"},[45]={t="Discover Rolf's Fate",lv=10,min=7,pre1={37},nx=71,ot="Search the murloc village for Rolf, or signs of his death.",st="Upon further searching the area, you find webbed footprints leading east along the shore of Stone Cairn Lake.  In the distance to the east, you can just barely see a Murloc village.$B$BPerhaps Rolf's fate ended there..."},[46]={t="Bounty on Murlocs",lv=10,min=7,pre1={39},ot="Bring 8 Torn Murloc Fins to Guard Thomas at the east Elwynn bridge.",st="The Stormwind Army has placed a bounty on murloc lurkers and foragers in Elwynn.  Slaughter them and bring me their torn murloc fins, and the Stormwind Army will reward you well.$B$BThe murlocs have built a village at Stone Cairn Lake north of here, and another to the south where the stream forks.",how={{"loot",780,{46,732}}}},[47]={t="Gold Dust Exchange",lv=7,min=4,ot="Bring 10 Gold Dust to Remy \"Two Times\" in Goldshire.  Gold Dust is gathered from Kobolds in Elwynn Forest.",st="The Kobolds in these parts sometimes carry Gold Dust on them.  I could really use the stuff - bring me a load of it and I'll give you the best price in town...best price in town!$B$BYou can find kobolds in the Fargodeep Mine to the south, and around the Jasperlode Mine to the northeast.",how={{"loot",773,{475,40}}}},[52]={t="Protect the Frontier",lv=10,min=7,ot="Kill 8 Prowlers and 5 Young Forest Bears, and then return to Guard Thomas at the east Elwynn bridge.",st="Hail, $n.  Wild animals are growing more and more aggressive the farther we get from Goldshire, and the Eastvale Logging Camp suffers nearly constant attacks from wolves and bears!$B$BWe could use your help out here.",how={{"kill",118},{"kill",822}}},[54]={t="Report to Goldshire",lv=5,min=1,pre1={21},si=745,ot="Take Marshal McBride's Documents to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.",st="$n, you are a $c with proven interest in the security of Northshire.  You are now tasked with the protection of the surrounding Elwynn Forest.$B$BIf you accept this duty, then I have prepared papers that must be delivered to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.  Goldshire lies along the southern road, past the border gates."},[56]={t="The Night Watch",lv=24,min=18,nx=57,ot="Commander Althea Ebonlocke of Darkshire wants you to kill 8 Skeletal Warriors and 6 Skeletal Mages.",st="As Commander of The Night Watch it is my sworn duty to protect the citizens of Darkshire.  Stormwind has retracted their commissioned guards from their posts here, leaving us to our own devices.$b$bIf you feel worthy of the task, we need your help! Assist The Night Watch by venturing forth into Tranquil Gardens, just south of Darkshire, and slaying 8 Skeletal Warriors and 6 Skeletal Mages.  The undead threat must be thwarted!",how={{"kill",48},{"kill",203}}},[57]={t="The Night Watch",lv=26,min=18,pre1={56},nx=58,ot="Commander Althea Ebonlocke of Darkshire wants you to kill 15 Skeletal Fiends and 15 Skeletal Horrors.",st="$n, I'm getting reports of an undead infestation in the forest!  If you're up to the job, journey to the Raven Hill graveyard and slay 15 of those vile Skeletal Fiends and 15 Skeletal Horrors.  There are also reports of skeletons just south of Darkshire, in and around Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.  The undead must be driven from Duskwood!",how={{"kill",531},{"kill",202}}},[59]={t="Cloth and Leather Armor",lv=10,min=7,pre1={39},si=748,ot="Give Sara Timberlain the Stormwind Armor Marker.",st="For your shrewdness and valor, I have a marker here that is good for one piece of armor.  I want you to take it to Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp.  Give her the marker, and she will fashion the armor for you.  And after you receive it, $n, use it in the defense of Elwynn.$B$BThe Eastvale Logging Camp is beyond Guard Thomas' post to the east."},[60]={t="Kobold Candles",lv=7,min=3,nx=61,ot="Bring 8 Large Candles to William Pestle in Goldshire.",st="Hello, $ggood sir:my lady;!  Do you have a moment?$B$BMy brother and I run an apothecary in Stormwind, and I'm here to gather large candles for their wax.  Can you help me?$B$BYou can get large candles from kobolds, and I hear rumors that kobolds are infesting the Elwynn mines ... the Fargodeep mine to the south and Jasperlode Mine to the east.  I suggest looking for candles in one of those places.",how={{"loot",772,{475,40}}}},[61]={t="Shipment to Stormwind",lv=7,min=3,pre1={60},rwc={[1]=1,[2]=1,[4]=1,[5]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[9]=1},si=957,ot="Bring William's Shipment to Morgan Pestle in the Stormwind Trade District.",st="My brother Morgan is waiting in Stormwind for my shipment of candles.  I don't have enough time to make the trip myself, but if you'd like to take him the shipment, he'll pay you well.$B$BI've packed up the candles, and you can find Morgan in our shop, Pestle's Apothecary, in the Stormwind Trade District."},[62]={t="The Fargodeep Mine",lv=7,min=4,nx=76,ot="Explore the Fargodeep Mine, then return to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.",st="The mine in Northshire isn't the only one with problems!  I have reports that the Fargodeep Mine in Elwynn has also become a haven for Kobolds.$B$BExplore the mine and confirm these reports, then return to me.  The mine is almost due south of Goldshire, between the Stonefield and Maclure homesteads."},[64]={t="The Forgotten Heirloom",lv=12,min=9,ot="Farmer Furlbrow wants you to retrieve his pocket watch from the wardrobe in his farmhouse at the pumpkin farm to the West.",st="It was horrible!  Verna woke me when she heard a ruckus in the fields.  The fields were full of hooligans.  We left in a rush and I forgot to pack my pocket watch.  Verna's pa gave me that watch on our wedding day and I feel just sick knowing those thieves have it.  I left the pocket watch in the wardrobe at the farmhouse.  Look for the field of pumpkins to the West -- you can't miss it.  If you bring it back to me, I'd sure be grateful!",how={{"open",841,{290}}}},[65]={t="The Defias Brotherhood",lv=18,min=14,nx=132,ot="Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to talk to Wiley in Lakeshire.",st="The band of wretches responsible for driving the good people of Westfall from the land call themselves The Defias Brotherhood.  I need you to infiltrate this clan of thugs.  We need to know who heads up the cartel and where they are hiding out.  In Lakeshire, in the inn, there is a rogue by the name of Wiley who owes me a favor.$b$bTravel to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains, east of Elwynn, and find out what you can."},[66]={t="The Legend of Stalvan",lv=28,min=22,nx=67,ot="Seek out the Clerk Daltry in the Darkshire Town Hall.",st="Last night a horrible disturbance rippled through my veins.  I sensed that my granddaughter, Alyssa, was in great danger.  I consulted the cards and Death stared up at me from the table.$b$bAfter taking a long journey through a dark trance I was able to uncover a clue to this terrifying mystery.  A name came to me, the name of Stalvan.$b$bSeek out the Clerk in the Town Hall and see if you can find out more about this character.  I fear for us all."},[67]={t="The Legend of Stalvan",lv=28,min=22,pre1={66},nx=68,ot="Travel to the Moonbrook Schoolhouse and bring back any updated information about Stalvan to Clerk Daltry.",st="Stalvan, eh?  Let me check the town registry.$b$bStalvan. . .Stalvan. . .let's see.  Ah, here we go!  I have a record of a Mr. Stalvan Mistmantle.  The last recorded address is the Moonbrook Schoolhouse.  My, talk about outdated!$b$bDo me a favor will you, friend?  If you happen to go out to Moonbrook, let me know if you get any update on this fellow.  I like to keep the records clean."},[68]={t="The Legend of Stalvan",lv=28,min=22,pre1={67},nx=69,si=889,ot="Take the Dusty Unsent Letter to Clerk Daltry.",st="You find a Dusty Unsent Letter in the old footlocker."},[69]={t="The Legend of Stalvan",lv=28,min=22,pre1={68},nx=70,ot="Go to The Lion's Pride Inn to see if anyone there has heard of the name Stalvan.",st="Oh my!  Must have missed this the first time.  In the registry, right beneath the first address for Stalvan there's another one listed, only partially scratched out.  Looks like he was headed to The Lion's Pride Inn over in Goldshire.  Might want to check there, $n."},[70]={t="The Legend of Stalvan",lv=28,min=22,pre1={69},nx=72,ot="Retrieve Stalvan's Undelivered Letter from the chest and deliver it to the Canal District in Stormwind.",st="The name Stalvan rings a bell.  I remember now.$b$bMany years back, on a stormy night, a messenger came in, seeking refuge for the night.  Near the stroke of midnight, the man ran down the stairs screaming, his face pale with fear.  Still wearing his bedclothes, he disappeared into the downpour.$b$bIn his haste he forgot his letters in the chest upstairs.  He never returned for them. One remains from that Stalvan fellow, intended for the Canal District in Stormwind.  Help yourself to it.",how={{"open",910,{1560}}}},[71]={t="Report to Thomas",lv=10,min=7,pre1={45},nx=39,si=735,ot="Deliver Rolf and Malakai's Medallions to Guard Thomas at the eastern Elwynn bridge.",st="Now that you have both medallions, deliver them to Guard Thomas at the bridge so that he might know the fate of his murdered guards."},[72]={t="The Legend of Stalvan",lv=28,min=22,pre1={70},nx=74,ot="Search through the packed up possessions for a clue.",st="My father was the caretaker of the estate long before I was.  He had to mop the blood up after the massacre.  But that's neither here nor there.$b$bThe last funds of the Flintridge trust have dried up.  Now the last of the family possessions are headed for auction.  Blame the tax vultures.  I guess if you're really itching to learn more you're free to look through this junk.  Who knows what you might find."},[76]={t="The Jasperlode Mine",lv=10,min=4,pre1={62},nx=239,ot="Explore the Jasperlode Mine, then report back to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.",st="Thanks to you we know the Fargodeep Mine is infested with kobolds.  Now we need a scout to investigate the more distant Jasperlode Mine.$B$BExplore Jasperlode and confirm any kobold presence.  To reach the mine, travel east along the road until you reach the Tower of Azora.  From the tower, head north and you'll find the mine in the foothills."},[83]={t="Red Linen Goods",lv=9,min=4,ot="Bring 6 Red Linen Bandanas to Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp.",st="The Defias gang in Northshire wears burlap masks, but the Defias in Elwynn wear linen which I can use to make fine linen goods.$B$BBring me red linen bandanas and I'll use them to fashion something for you.$B$BDefias gang members have camps pocketed throughout Elwynn.",how={{"loot",1019,{116}}}},[84]={t="Back to Billy",lv=6,min=5,pre1={86},nx=87,si=962,ot="Bring the Pork Belly Pie to Billy Maclure at the Maclure Vineyards.",st="Here you go.  And when you give this pie to that Billy, you tell him I hope he chokes on it!"},[85]={t="Lost Necklace",lv=6,min=5,nx=86,ot="Speak with Billy Maclure.",st="I lost my necklace, and think that guttersnipe Billy Maclure took it!  He's usually scuttling like a rat around the Maclure vineyards east of here. $B$BGet my necklace back for me, and you'll warm an old widow's heart."},[86]={t="Pie for Billy",lv=6,min=5,pre1={85},nx=84,ot="Bring 4 Chunks of Boar Meat to Auntie Bernice Stonefield at the Stonefield's Farm.",st="Maybe if I got a pie, I could tell you who has that necklace.  And you know, I think that old Bernice lady at that other farm makes great Pork Belly Pies... $B$BMaybe if you gave her some chunks of boar meat from the boars that hang around our farms, and told her what it was for, she'd bake up a pie for you.",how={{"loot",769,{113}}}},[87]={t="Goldtooth",lv=8,min=5,pre1={84},ot="Bring Bernice's Necklace to \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield at the Stonefield Farm.",st="I was playing near the Fargodeep Mine, and I think I dropped, er...I mean I saw, the old lady's necklace.  Don't ask me how it got there...it wasn't me!$B$BWell anyway, I saw this big, gold-toothed kobold pick up the necklace and run into the mine.  Go find that kobold and you'll find the necklace, I swear!",how={{"loot",981,{327}}}},[88]={t="Princess Must Die!",lv=9,min=6,rwc={[1]=2,[2]=2,[3]=1,[4]=1,[5]=3,[8]=3,[9]=3},ot="Kill Princess, grab her collar, then bring it back to Ma Stonefield at the Stonefield Farm.",st="The Brackwells have a prize-winning pig, Princess.  The sow is HUGE, and she got that way from sneaking over here and eating my veggies!$B$BSo before she comes to our fields...Princess must die!  Bring me her collar as proof of the deed and I'll give you something for your time!$B$BPrincess is usually over at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, to the east and beyond the Maclure farm.  Get her before she gets hungry and comes back here!",how={{"loot",1006,{330}}}},[89]={t="The Everstill Bridge",lv=20,min=15,pre1={125},nx=98386,rwc={[8]=1},ot="Bring 5 Iron Pikes and 5 Iron Rivets to Foreman Oslow in Lakeshire.",st="During the last orc invasion we were forced to smelt our iron down to make bullets, swords and armor.  We sent word to Stormwind for a new shipment of materials but a band of Redridge gnolls hijacked the caravan and ran off into the hills behind Lakeshire.$b$bNow we're coming up short on supplies to get this bridge rebuilt.  If you can bring me 5 iron pikes and 5 iron rivets, $n, I'll make sure you're rewarded. $b$bNow let's get to work!",how={{"loot",2856,{430,426}},{"loot",1013,{430,426}}}},[90]={t="Seasoned Wolf Kabobs",lv=25,min=18,ot="Gather 10 Lean Wolf Flanks and return to Chef Grual in Darkshire.",st="Seasoned Wolf Kabobs are a house favorite!  Sure, I can make you some.  But first I'll need the supplies.  Bring me 10 Lean Wolf Flanks. Given the many wolves here in the forest, I am sure finding the Flanks will be no problem.  Fortunately for you, I just received my recent shipment of Stormwind Seasoning Herbs, so all I need are the flanks to get started.",how={{"loot",1015,{213,565,628,923}},{"buy",2665,{1303}}}},[91]={t="Solomon's Law",lv=23,min=17,ot="Bring 10 Shadowhide Pendants to Bailiff Conacher in the Lakeshire Town Hall.",st="An enemy of Stormwind has taken up residence in the eastern foothills of Redridge. This wicked villain uses the Arcane to spread terror and misery upon our town and our people. Under the name, Morganth, he conducts his evil business.$b$bMorganth now controls the Shadowhide Gnoll Clan to perform his biddings. As stated by the Law of Lakeshire, aiding a criminal of the Kingdom is punishable by death.$b$bThese vile gnolls must be killed!$b$bTurn in 10 Shadowhide Pendants to me, and you shall be rewarded.",how={{"loot",1075,{568,432,947}}}},[92]={t="Redridge Goulash",lv=18,min=15,ot="Chef Breanna of Lakeshire wants five pieces of Tough Condor Meat, five Great Goretusk Snouts and five helpings of Crisp Spider Meat.",st="Nothing would please me more than to make you some Redridge Goulash. But there's a slight problem. During the recent orc uprising I fed the entire brigade of Stormwind troops. My cupboard is now bare. But if you can provide me with the ingredients, I'd be happy to oblige.$b$bJust bring me five pieces of Tough Condor Meat, five Great Goretusk Snouts and five helpings of Crisp Spider Meat.",how={{"loot",2296,{547}},{"loot",1080,{428}},{"loot",1081,{505,442}}}},[93]={t="Dusky Crab Cakes",lv=20,min=17,pre1={5},nx=240,ot="Gather 6 Gooey Spider Legs and bring them to Chef Grual in Darkshire.",st="I'll let you in on a little secret - Dusky \"Crab\" Cakes are really made from spider legs!  I know it's a bit disgusting, but the cakes have a nice, tangy flavor and make great snacks!  Bring me Gooey Spider Legs and I'll whip you up a few of them.$B$BI hear Venom Web Spiders are a good source - they nest to the north, between the foothills and the river.",how={{"loot",2251,{930,217,569,539,949}}}},[94]={t="A Watchful Eye",lv=21,min=20,nx=248,si=1083,ot="Take the Glyph of Azora to the Lion Statue near the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge.",st="My rival, Morganth, is a vicious mage of great power who lives in the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge.  I have developed a means of spying on him, the Eye of Azora, and can now view him from afar.$B$BBut to study his thoughts ... I require further aid.$B$BIf you are willing, then take my Glyph of Azora to the Tower of Ilgalar.  Place it upon the Lion Statue near the Tower.$B$BWhen this is done, the power of Azora will grant visions of Morganth's future plans."},[95]={t="Sven's Revenge",lv=25,min=20,nx=230,ot="Go to Sven's Farm and find what was buried behind the old stump.",st="I used to work one of the farms to the southeast...until Dark Riders from Deadwind Pass descended upon my farm and slaughtered my family when I was away!$B$BWhen I returned I saw a shadowy figure skulking near my barn, burying something.  He fled before I could catch him, and I couldn't linger for I was hot on the heels of the Dark Riders.  So I never discovered what was hidden.$B$BIf you can find what that shadowy figure buried, I would be grateful.  The hiding spot is behind the old stump near my barn."},[101]={t="The Totem of Infliction",lv=25,min=18,ot="Bring 10 Ghoul Fangs, 10 Skeleton Fingers and 5 Vials of Spider Venom to Madame Eva in Darkshire.",st="As the mystical taint creeps through the forest, the need for self-protection is undeniable, $n.  The winds whisper to me and they speak of a great danger which waits patiently for you in the near future.$b$bIf you wish to protect yourself, noble $c, bring to me 10 ghoul fangs, 10 skeleton fingers and 5 vials of spider venom.  For you I shall enchant a Totem of Infliction which will harm those who attempt violent acts against you.",how={{"loot",1129,{3,948,210}},{"loot",1130,{949,930}},{"loot",2378,{531,202}}}},[102]={t="Patrolling Westfall",lv=14,min=8,rwc={[8]=1},ot="Bring 8 Gnoll Paws to Captain Danuvin on Sentinel Hill.",st="Stormwind has abandoned us.  A foul wind of depravity rustles through the plains of Westfall.  This was my homeland and I will not turn my back on the citizens who choose to remain here.  We, the former farmers, shall make our stand.$b$bYour task, should you choose to accept, is to patrol the grasslands of Westfall.  Track down and slay the vile Gnolls that seem to be working in conjunction with the Deadmines thieves. Bring me eight Gnoll Paws and I will reward your bravery.",how={{"loot",725,{117,500}}}},[103]={t="Keeper of the Flame",lv=16,min=10,rwc={[8]=1},ot="Bring 5 Flasks of Oil to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.",st="The night the Lighthouse Keeper's family died was horrible.  I watched, helpless, as Old Murk-Eye led the attack.  But what's done is done and now my concern is for the lives of the sailors on The Great Sea whose ships come close to the perilous rocks of the coastline.  With no one to keep watch on the flame the responsibility has fallen upon me.$b$bHelp me keep the torch lit by bringing me 5 flasks of oil from the Harvest Monsters.",how={{"loot",814,{114,36,480}}}},[104]={t="The Coastal Menace",lv=20,min=15,rwc={[8]=3},ot="Bring a scale of Old Murk-Eye to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.",st="When my life was ended upon the rocks, I had no clue what the afterlife held for me.  The Lighthouse was black that night because Old Murk-Eye had scared the keeper's family off.  They returned and re-lit the flame but Old Murk-Eye coerced the weaker minded murlocs to raid the Lighthouse with him once again.  The second time the family was not so lucky and before my eyes they perished helplessly.$b$bSlay Old Murk-Eye if you see him along the shore and bring me one of his scales and I shall reward you.",how={{"loot",3636,{391}}}},[106]={t="Young Lovers",lv=6,min=5,nx=111,si=1208,ot="Give Maybell's Love Letter to Tommy Joe Stonefield.",st="Oh, I'm cursed!  My heart belongs to Tommy Joe Stonefield, but our families are bitter enemies.  So I can't see him, even though my eyes ache to gaze upon that handsome face!$B$BPlease, take this letter and give it to Tommy Joe.  He's usually at the river to the west of the Stonefield Farm, which is due west of here."},[107]={t="Note to William",lv=6,min=5,pre1={111},nx=112,si=1252,ot="Take Gramma Stonefield's Note to William Pestle.",st="I bet William Pestle has a potion to unite our two young lovers!$B$BHere, take this note to William.  He's staying at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire."},[109]={t="Report to Gryan Stoutmantle",lv=10,min=9,ot="Talk to Gryan Stoutmantle.  He usually can be found in the stone tower on Sentinel Hill, just off the road, in the middle of Westfall.",st="Looks to me you've seen quite a bit of combat in your time, $c.  If you haven't already, you should report to Gryan Stoutmantle.  He heads up the People's Militia, aimed at protecting the farmlands of Westfall.  I bet he could use your help.  You can usually find him in the stone tower on Sentinel Hill, just off the road in the middle of Westfall."},[111]={t="Speak with Gramma",lv=6,min=5,pre1={106},nx=107,ot="Speak with Gramma Stonefield.",st="Please, $n, talk with my Gramma.  If anyone can find a way to bring me together with Maybell, she can.$B$BShe's inside our house east of here."},[112]={t="Collecting Kelp",lv=7,min=5,pre1={107},nx=114,ot="Bring 4 Crystal Kelp Fronds to William Pestle in Goldshire.",st="I can make an invisibility liquor for Maybell, so she can slip away from the Maclure Vineyards and go to Tommy Joe.  But to make the Liquor, I need some crystal kelp.$B$BAlthough the kelp usually grows in the ocean... sometimes murlocs collect it.  See if the murlocs near Crystal Lake have any.  Crystal Lake is just east of Goldshire.",how={{"loot",1256,{285,735}}}},[114]={t="The Escape",lv=7,min=5,pre1={112},si=1257,ot="Take the Invisibility Liquor to Maybell Maclure.",st="Take this invisibility liquor to young Maybell.  It should last long enough for her to visit Tommy Joe."},[115]={t="Shadow Magic",lv=23,min=18,pre={20,98387},ot="Bring 3 Midnight Orbs to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.",st="The Blackrock orcs enlisted shadowcasters to aid their attacks in Redridge, and they have brought with them devices of dark power--midnight orbs.  These orbs have struck telling blows against Redridge's defenders, and it's imperative we remove the demon-tainted items from the conflict.$B$BFind and deliver to me midnight orbs from slain Blackrock shadowcasters.  I will then have them disposed of, for this world would be a better place without them!",how={{"loot",1261,{436}}}},[118]={t="The Price of Shoes",lv=18,min=14,nx=119,si=1283,ot="Take Verner's Note to Smith Argus in Goldshire.",st="I've been using so much iron keeping the Stormwind Guards outfitted, I don't have enough to supply the stable's horses with shoes!$B$BTake this note to Blacksmith Argus in Goldshire.  It explains to him my problem and requests a shipment of horseshoes."},[119]={t="Return to Verner",lv=18,min=13,pre1={118},si=1284,ot="Return to Verner Osgood in Redridge.  Give him the Crate of Horseshoes.",st="Ok, I'll give him his 50 horseshoes...$B$BHere they are, all boxed up and ready to go!  Tell Verner it was a pleasure doing business, and be sure he reads the note attached to this crate!"},[120]={t="Messenger to Stormwind",lv=14,min=14,nx=121,si=1293,ot="Magistrate Solomon has given you a report which must be delivered to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind.  The judge wants you to return to him as soon as the delivery has been made.",st="These are trying times, $c.  The township is under constant siege.  Without reinforcements, we will certainly face defeat.  The message I now entrust to you is of utmost importance.  Get this report to General Marcus Jonathan of Stormwind immediately.  Once your delivery is made, return to me at once with any news, be it good or bad. $b$bNow make haste!"},[121]={t="Messenger to Stormwind",lv=14,min=14,pre1={120},nx=143,si=1294,ot="Take General Marcus Jonathan's letter of response to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.",st="While I wait for a response from the King I want you to carry this letter to Magistrate Solomon. $b$bDismissed, $c!"},[122]={t="Underbelly Scales",lv=18,min=14,pre1={119},ot="Gather 6 Underbelly Whelp Scales from Black Dragon Whelps, and bring them to Verner Osgood in Redridge.",st="I need some underbelly scales from black dragon whelps to pay for the shoes Argus sent me from Goldshire.  If you can get 6 of them for me, then I can pay Argus with some... and have enough left to fashion something for you.$B$BBlack dragon whelps are often flying around south of Lakeshire, but they like to wander.  You might have to just keep an eye out and hunt them when you see them.",how={{"loot",1221,{441}}}},[123]={t="The Collector",lv=10,min=7,nx=147,si=2223,ot="Go to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire and give him The Collector's Schedule",st="This note is a schedule with a list of days and times when a person -- described only as \"The Collector\" -- will receive a shipment of gold from the mines in Elwynn Forest.$B$BFrom the schedule, it looks as if the Collector resides near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn.$B$BThis sounds important.  You should report it to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire."},[124]={t="A Baying of Gnolls",lv=20,min=15,pre1={119},nx=126,ot="Kill 10 Redridge Brutes and 8 Redridge Mystics, then return to Verner Osgood.",st="As if the attacking orcs weren't enough!  Now I have gnoll brutes and mystics prowling along the ridge north of my stable, taking my horses when they stray...$B$BIf you can get rid of those gnolls, my horses and I would be very grateful.",how={{"kill",426},{"kill",430}}},[125]={t="The Lost Tools",lv=16,min=15,nx=89,ot="Foreman Oslow of Lakeshire wants you to retrieve his toolbox from the bottom of Lake Everstill.",st="I could really use a hand here, $n.  With the town under siege, it's been hard to get supplies.  My tools were being delivered from Goldshire by wagon but the bridge was blown out.  We put the tools in a boat but the orcs hit it with a catapult.  Just my luck, my toolbox sank right to the bottom of the lake.$b$bRetrieve my toolbox, $n, and I'll make it worth your while.",how={{"open",1309,{32}}}},[126]={t="Howling in the Hills",lv=25,min=15,pre1={124},ot="Bring Yowler's Paw to Verner Osgood in Lakeshire.",st="$n, the gnolls are still out there.  I can hear their baying as they hunt in the hills above Lakeshire.  And one cry is louder than the rest - Yowler,  their leader.$B$BKill Yowler and send his pack scattering!  Bring me his paw as proof.$B$BAnd be careful, this gnoll is their leader for a reason.  He is no Mongrel...",how={{"loot",3614,{518}}}},[127]={t="Selling Fish",lv=21,min=16,ot="Bring 10 Spotted Sunfish to Dockmaster Baren in Lakeshire.",st="Lake Everstill is famous for its spotted sunfish.  There's always demand for them...and I'm running low!$B$BBring me a batch of 10 and I'll barter well for them.  If you can't fish yourself, then...maybe you can get them off the murlocs!",how={{"loot",1467,{422,548,1083}}}},[128]={t="Blackrock Bounty",lv=25,min=20,ot="Kill 15 Blackrock Champions and Guard Howe in Lakeshire will reward you.",st="The Blackrock Clan must be destroyed. The Enemy has invaded our lands. These mountains fall under the sovereign right of the King of Stormwind. Our sources tell us that the leaders of each unit within the Clan are known as Champions. You'll find them in their encampment to the north, just west of the road to the Burning Steppes.$b$bMagistrate Solomon wants these foul brutes dead. Slay 15 Blackrock Champions and return to me.",how={{"kill",435}}},[129]={t="A Free Lunch",lv=15,min=12,nx=130,si=5534,ot="Bring Parker's lunch to Guard Parker.  He patrols the road leading to Darkshire.",st="Can you do me a favor?  I've prepared a lunch for Guard Parker, but he's out on patrol...he's a big, strong Stormwind guard who can defend himself, but it's much too dangerous out there for a townsperson like me.$B$BSo if you deliver his lunch for me, then come back here and I'll give you a free lunch!  Parker patrols the stretch of road leading to Duskwood."},[130]={t="Visit the Herbalist",lv=15,min=12,pre1={129},nx=131,ot="Speak with the Redridge Herbalist, Martie Jainrose.",st="Before you go back to Darcy, can you bring her some flowers for me?  You can get them at the herbalist shop back in Lakeshire, at the west end of town.$B$BBut when you get the flowers...don't tell the herbalist, Martie, whom they're from, or whom they're for..."},[131]={t="Delivering Daffodils",lv=15,min=12,pre1={130},si=1325,ot="Give Darcy the Daffodil Bouquet.",st="Here is your bouquet.  I chose Daffodils for you.  They're my favorite!"},[132]={t="The Defias Brotherhood",lv=18,min=14,pre1={65},nx=135,si=1327,ot="Take Wiley's Note to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.",st="What I am about to tell you could cost me my life.  The Defias gang is up to something big.  Last I heard they were working in conjunction with various gnolls, kobolds and even goblins.$b$bTake this note to Stoutmantle.  It explains as much as I know on the subject."},[135]={t="The Defias Brotherhood",lv=18,min=14,pre1={132},nx=141,si=1327,ot="Take Wiley's Note to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.",st="I wonder what Wiley meant when he mentioned the Stonemasons.  Perhaps that was a slip of tongue.  Could the Defias gang be related to the Stonemasons?  Only one man would know for sure:  Mathias Shaw, head of SI:7. Show him Wiley's Note and see if he has anything to add to this growing mystery. If you have trouble finding Shaw, check the Barracks in Old Town."},[136]={t="Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure",lv=16,min=10,nx=138,ot="Find Captain Sanders' footlocker and search it for the next clue.",st="If ye be readin' this, it means that Ol' Captain Sanders is in a watery grave.  So my treasure is yours now, ye jest need to follow the clues. $b$bFirst ye need to find me footlocker.  It's probably half-buried in sand by now, along the Western Coast of Westfall near the shipwreck.  There be lots of shipwrecks but only one rusty anchor on the coast.  Find that anchor and you'll find me locker!  Look in there for the next clue."},[138]={t="Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure",lv=16,min=10,pre1={136},nx=139,si=1358,ot="Find the old barrel near the ruined chimney and search it for your next clue.",st="The clue to the treasure reads: Good work, matey!  Now ye need to head due east.  East up the bluffs, east to the road.  Look for the ol' chimney ruins near the side of the road.  There you'll find an old barrel with your next clue."},[139]={t="Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure",lv=16,min=10,pre1={138},nx=140,si=1361,ot="Search the empty jug next to the windmill for the next clue.",st="Searching through the barrel you discover another piece of parchment.  This one reads:  Now from this here barrel, face ye North.  Straight as the crow flies, keep ye walkin' till you see the empty jug next to the lone windmill on the sea bluffs.  If ye poke around that jug, ye just might find what you're lookin' for."},[140]={t="Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure",lv=16,min=10,pre1={139},si=1362,ot="Locate Captain Sanders' chest and open it for your reward.",st="Sure enough, deep within the Old Jug there is another clue to Sander's treasure.  The ink has run in some places and the paper smells like whiskey but you can make out some of the text:  Now that ye found me ol' whiskey jug, you're almost to the treasure!  Just face West from the bottle and walk down to the shore.  Once ye get to the water, keep going!  Swim straight west till you find the island with me treasure chest!"},[141]={t="The Defias Brotherhood",lv=18,min=14,pre1={135},nx=142,si=1353,ot="Take Shaw's report to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.",st="The Stonemasons' Guild was run by a man named Edwin VanCleef.  VanCleef was responsible for rebuilding Stormwind after the orcs razed it in the First War.  Apparently, VanCleef and his men were unhappy with their treatment by the King after the reconstruction was complete.  That just might explain a thing or two.$b$bI have written a more detailed account for your Master in Westfall.  Take this to him at once!"},[142]={t="The Defias Brotherhood",lv=18,min=14,pre1={141},nx=155,ot="Track down the Defias Messenger in Westfall and bring his message to Stoutmantle.",st="We need to discover the location of the Defias hideout.  $n, my scout reports that a Defias Messenger has been seen on the roads between Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry and the Jangolode Mine.  I want you to capture him.  If he resists, kill him and bring me whatever he is carrying.",how={{"loot",1381,{550}}}},[143]={t="Messenger to Westfall",lv=14,min=14,pre1={121},nx=144,si=1407,ot="Magistrate Solomon wants you to take his written plea to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.",st="Something odd is afoot with the Stormwind Army.  They should have been here in force by now.  Time is a luxury we don't have, however.  I will not stand by and watch the people of Lakeshire give their lives without trying to enlist more help.  I've heard word of a people's militia forming in Westfall.$b$bTake this plea to their leader, Gryan Stoutmantle.  Perhaps Stoutmantle's men can lend some support here until the King sends reserves."},[144]={t="Messenger to Westfall",lv=14,min=14,pre1={143},nx=145,si=1408,ot="Return to Magistrate Solomon with Gryan Stoutmantle's response.",st="Magistrate Solomon's note pains me to read.  But it is obvious he knows not the war which is waged in Westfall or else he would know better than to expect aid from the Militia.  If Stormwind had not deserted us as well, we would not have the need for the Militia.$b$bTake this response to your master in Redridge, $c.  And let him know that my heart is heavy with the loss of good men."},[145]={t="Messenger to Darkshire",lv=18,min=18,pre1={144},nx=146,si=1409,ot="Magistrate Solomon wants you to take a letter to Lord Ebonlocke in Darkshire.",st="I require your assistance once again.  I have written to Lord Ebonlocke, requesting that he sends his trained guards, the Night Watch, to help with Lakeshire's defense.  It is imperative this message makes it to him swiftly.  You must exercise extreme caution.  Ebonlocke is the mayor of Darkshire, in the heart of Duskwood.  Do not stray from the roads."},[146]={t="Messenger to Darkshire",lv=18,min=18,pre1={145},si=1410,ot="Return to Magistrate Solomon with Lord Ebonlocke's letter of response.",st="If I did not know Magistrate Solomon personally, I would say the man has gone mad.  Send the Night Watch to Lakeshire because Stormwind refuses aid?  The Night Watch was formed because Stormwind left us when this foul magic seeped into the land.  If I sent my Night Watch, this town would be overrun by evil before the guards even reached the forest's edge.$b$bTake this letter of response to your Master in Lakeshire."},[147]={t="Manhunt",lv=10,min=7,pre1={123},ot="Find and kill \"the Collector\"  then return to Marshal Dughan with The Collector's Ring.",st="If the \"Collector\" is taking gold from our mines then he's stealing from the kingdom!  Bring the Collector to justice, and bring me the ring mentioned in the pickup schedule you gave me.  It may tell us whom the Collector is working for...$B$BThat Pickup Schedule says the Collector is hiding out at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch.  You should search for him there.",how={{"loot",2239,{473}}}},[148]={t="Supplies from Darkshire",lv=24,min=20,nx=149,ot="Speak with Madame Eva.",st="Oh, what is a poor old man to do?  I need some supplies from Darkshire, but the village is so far away and I am so old and feeble...I would never make the trip.$B$BCan you go to Darkshire and bring me back some Ghost Hair Thread?  You can get it from Madame Eva at her home on the Darkshire square."},[149]={t="Ghost Hair Thread",lv=24,min=20,pre1={148},nx=154,si=1453,ot="Bring the Spectral Comb to Blind Mary.",st="There is a poor, sad spirit, Blind Mary, who haunts an old farm house in the hills south of Darkshire.$B$BHere, take this Spectral Comb and ask Blind Mary to comb her hair.  Then bring back the comb and I will glean from it the Ghost Hair I'll need for the thread.$B$BAnd take care, for dark things now lurk near that house..."},[150]={t="Murloc Poachers",lv=20,min=20,ot="Bring 8 Murloc Fins to Dockmaster Baren in Lakeshire.",st="Murlocs are becoming a problem.  Larger groups of the fishmen are dropping anchor along the shores of Lake Everstill and fishing up a storm!  We need them gone before they eat all the fish in the lake!$B$BHunt murlocs!  Bring me eight of their fins and I might have something for you...",how={{"loot",1468,{545,578,422,548,1083,544}}}},[151]={t="Poor Old Blanchy",lv=14,min=9,ot="Verna Furlbrow in Westfall wants you to bring her 8 Handfuls of Oats.",st="Poor Old Blanchy!  Such a tired beast after all the work we put her through. I fed her before we left the farm, but we weren't expecting the wagon to break on us. If you could bring her a few handfuls of oats from the fields, I'd be grateful.$B$BI bet you could find some around all of the farms in Westfall, if you can steer clear of those horrific machines that have taken over. There are several farms southwest of here.",how={{"open",1528,{2724}}}},[152]={t="The Coast Isn't Clear",lv=19,min=10,ot="Kill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and return to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.",st="You probably noticed all of the shipwrecks along the coast.  The Great Sea is treacherous indeed.  The coast of Westfall needs to be kept clear, so that if sailors find their way to our beaches, they are safe.  The Murlocs are trouble though.$b$bKill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and I will see to it that you are rewarded.",how={{"kill",126},{"kill",171},{"kill",127},{"kill",517}}},[153]={t="Red Leather Bandanas",lv=15,min=10,rwc={[8]=2},ot="Bring 15 Red Leather Bandanas to Scout Galiaan at Sentinel Hill.",st="The Defias Front is constantly shifting.  I've been following their movements for quite some time now.  On a side note, I've ascertained that many members of the gang can be tracked by the Red Leather Bandanas they wear.$b$bBring me 15 of these Bandanas and I'll see to it you are rewarded.",how={{"loot",829,{95,504}}}},[154]={t="Return the Comb",lv=24,min=20,pre1={149},nx=157,si=1518,ot="Return the Ghost Hair Comb to Madame Eva in Darkshire.",st="NO!!!!!$B$BTake it, take this comb away from me!$B$BI'm a monster, and no one will ever think me lovely again!"},[155]={t="The Defias Brotherhood",lv=18,min=14,pre1={142},nx=166,ne=1,ot="Escort the Defias Traitor to the secret hideout of the Defias Brotherhood.  Once the Defias Traitor shows you where VanCleef and his men are hiding out, return to Gryan Stoutmantle with the information.",st="So Stoutmantle sends a scrawny $r like you to protect me?  Guess you'll have to do.  Better bring some friends too. $b$bYou know the deal, right?  You watch my back and I'll take you to the Defias hideout.  But you better be close by my side.  The Defias gang wants my head now.  If they see me with you, they'll try to kill me.$b$bLet me know when you and any friends you can round up are ready to go."},[156]={t="Gather Rot Blossoms",lv=24,min=20,pre1={158},nx=159,ot="Gather 8 Rot Blossoms and bring them to Tavernkeep Smitts in Darkshire.",st="If you bring me some rot blossoms then I can brew you up a batch of zombie juice.$B$BRot blossoms grow in strange places.  In particular, I hear you can find them inside the skulls of Skeletal Horrors and Skeletal Fiends... not that I've gotten close enough to look!$B$BThe Raven Hill Cemetery and the Tranquil Gardens are both lousy with those skeletons.  You may as well get rid of them while you're looking for rot blossoms.  The town of Darkshire would be grateful.",how={{"loot",1598,{202,531,2454}}}},[157]={t="Deliver the Thread",lv=24,min=20,pre1={154},nx=158,si=1596,ot="Bring the Ghost Hair Thread to Abercrombie, in his shack north of the Raven Hill Cemetery.",st="Here is your thread, $n.  It has a thousand uses, from binding evil spirits to sewing life into inanimate objects."},[158]={t="Zombie Juice",lv=24,min=20,pre1={157},nx=156,ot="Speak with Tavernkeep Smitts.",st="I need a bottle of a certain liquor - Zombie Juice.  Tavernkeep Smitts at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire should have some.$B$BAnd please hurry, $n.  These nights get cold, and I need that drink to put fire in my veins again!"},[159]={t="Juice Delivery",lv=24,min=20,pre1={156},nx=133,si=1451,ot="Bring the Zombie Juice to Abercrombie at his shack.",st="Here's your Zombie Juice...$B$B...and be careful with this stuff.  It's strong enough to raise the dead!"},[161]={t="A Dark Threat Looms",lv=18,min=16,pre1={199},nx=274,si=2563,ot="Chief Engineer Hinderweir wants you to take the strange smelling powder to Ashlan Stonesmirk, the explosives expert in Dun Modr.",st="If my suspicions are correct, this is some type of explosive powder.  This must be analyzed by an explosives expert so we know just what we're dealing with here.  Ashlan Stonesmirk was assigned to the regiment guarding Dun Modr and the Thandol Span.  I need you to make a grave and perilous journey, $n.$b$bTravel through the Algaz Gate, follow the road through the Wetlands and seek out Stonesmirk in Dun Modr.  Heed my advice: stick to the roads and stop for nothing!"},[163]={t="Raven Hill",lv=20,min=17,nx=5,bc=5,ot="Find out what is haunting Raven Hill.",st="Something's amiss at Raven Hill, $n. Calor swears that someone--or something--is haunting the buildings there. Two nights running he's noticed the shadows moving, and the third before that he says he saw light in one of the windows.$b$bIf, as you say, you care about the safety of Duskwood, find out what monster haunts in Raven Hill."},[164]={t="Deliveries to Sven",lv=23,min=17,nx=95,bc=95,si=1922,ot="Deliver the supplies to Sven.",st="Do you know Sven? Now, there is a man who does the work of the Light! He and his followers keep a camp at the northwestern edge of Duskwood.$b$bUnfortunately, because they are so few, they cannot even spare a man to fetch supplies from town. Will you deliver these supplies to him?"},[165]={t="The Hermit",lv=25,min=17,nx=148,bc=148,ot="Check on the old man in the shack near Raven Hill cemetery.",st="There was an old man who used to come into town to buy supplies rather frequently, but I haven't seen him for quite some time now. He lives out in a shack overlooking Raven Hill cemetery, if I remember correctly. Perhaps you should go see if something is amiss."},[166]={t="The Defias Brotherhood",lv=22,min=14,pre1={155},si=2874,ot="Kill Edwin VanCleef and bring his head to Gryan Stoutmantle.",st="There is but one task left for you to complete.  Edwin VanCleef must be assassinated.  While it saddens me to condemn any man to a death sentence, it is for the greater good of the people of Westfall that VanCleef is laid to rest once and for all.  Bring me the villain's head once the deed is done.",how={{"loot",3637,{639}}}},[167]={t="Oh Brother...",lv=20,min=15,ot="Bring Foreman Thistlenettle's Explorers' League Badge to Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind.",st="We were deep in a vast mine in Westfall, hidden beneath a barn in Moonbrook. No clue where these stinkin' thieving types came from. Anyway, the mine tunnel collapsed on us. I got out but the others... well... the others haven't been heard from.$b$bYou look like you might have better luck in there. If you could look for my brother, I'd be thankful.  He always carried his Explorers' League Badge. If you can't find him, that badge would at least give me some peace of mind.",how={{"loot",1875,{626}}}},[168]={t="Collecting Memories",lv=18,min=14,ot="Retrieve 4 Miners' Union Cards and return them to Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind.",st="Many of my friends perished that horrible day when the mine tunnel caved in.  If your adventures happen to bring you into that wing of the mine in Moonbrook, please keep an eye out for any sign which might identify them.  If you come across any of their Miners' Union Cards, bring them back to me and I'll make sure their families get some resolution from this horrible accident.",how={{"loot",1894,{624,623,625}}}},[169]={t="WANTED: Gath'Ilzogg",lv=26,min=15,ot="Kill Gath'Ilzogg and bring his head to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire for the reward.",st="Wanted! Gath'Ilzogg, Leader of the Blackrock attacks on Stonewatch Keep and raids against the township of Lakeshire. $b$bGath'Ilzogg is extremely dangerous.  He is reportedly holed up in the recently conquered keep plotting the Blackrock clan's further crimes against humanity.  The orc infestation must be quelled at all costs.  A gracious reward will be given to whatever brave soul can deliver the head of Gath'Ilzogg to Magistrate Solomon.",how={{"loot",3633,{334}}}},[170]={t="A New Threat",lv=2,min=1,pre1={179},rwc={[8]=3},ot="Balir Frosthammer wants you to kill 6 Rockjaw Troggs and 6 Burly Rockjaw Troggs.",st="I hope you're here to lend us a hand, $c. After the last trogg attack, we could use all the help we can get.$b$bI hear the buggers have been popping up all across the lands, and it seems Coldridge Valley is no exception. They've been spotted all over the hills to the southeast and near the frozen lake.$b$bAnd that's not all, just a few nights ago, they attacked and overran our camp to the west! $b$bWe're a bit shorthanded here, $g lad : lass;, and we need strong arms to help drive the troggs back.",how={{"kill",707},{"kill",724}}},[174]={t="Look to the Stars",lv=25,min=20,nx=175,ot="Viktori Prism'Antras of Darkshire wants you to bring him a bronze tube.",st="My Gnomish friend, Cog, has promised to help me build a device which will let me peer towards the stars.  A truth exists, beyond magic, that can explain the strange transformation in the forest.$b$bBring to me a bronze tube made by a skilled engineer.  That is the first step, according to Cog's blueprint.",how={{"open",4371,{19019,19020}}}},[175]={t="Look to the Stars",lv=25,min=20,pre1={174},nx=177,ot="Locate Mary and persuade her to give up a reflective surface for Viktori's project.",st="According to Cog's blueprint, what I need now is a way to reflect light.  I remember a woman by the name of Mary who became well known around these parts for always carrying a looking glass.  Perhaps you can track Mary down and see if she might lend us a reflective surface for this project?  I believe she once resided in southern Duskwood. . ."},[176]={t="WANTED: \"Hogger\"",lv=11,min=5,ot="Slay the gnoll Hogger and bring his Huge Gnoll Claw to Marshal Dughan.",st="Wanted: Hogger$B$BA huge gnoll, Hogger, is prowling the woods in southwestern Elwynn.  He has overpowered all attempts at his capture.$B$BThe Stormwind Army has placed a generous bounty on the Gnoll.  To earn the reward, bounty hunters should bring proof of Hogger's demise to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.",how={{"loot",1931,{448}}}},[177]={t="Look to the Stars",lv=25,min=20,pre1={175},nx=181,ot="Retrieve Blind Mary's Looking Glass from the Insane Ghoul and give it to Viktori in Darkshire.",st="The looking glass was one of my finest treasures until. . .the incident.  After that happened, I discarded it behind the barn.  There was an Insane Ghoul who used to roam back there.  Perhaps he picked it up.  Rumor has it the devilish beast resides in the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.",how={{"loot",1946,{511}}}},[179]={t="Dwarven Outfitters",lv=1,min=1,rwc={[8]=3},ot="Sten Stoutarm would like 8 pieces of Tough Wolf Meat.",st="What do we have here? You look as though you might need something to keep your hands warm, hm?$b$bI'll tell you what would help: a pair of nice, warm gloves. And, being the kind soul that I am, I'd be more than happy to provide you with a suitable pair. I've one condition, however.$b$bI need you to go get me some wolf meat. Nice arrangement, hm? You bring me some wolf meat, and I'll make sure you don't lose any digits to frostbite. Well, what do you say?",how={{"loot",750,{705,69,299}}}},[180]={t="WANTED: Lieutenant Fangore",lv=26,min=15,ot="Kill Lieutenant Fangore and return to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire with his paw.",st="Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore$b$bKnown leader of the Shadowhide Gnoll Clan, working under the enemy of the Township and Kingdom, Morganth.  By mandate of Magistrate Solomon, this vile betrayer of Stormwind is wanted dead.  Show his paw to the Magistrate as proof of his death.",how={{"loot",3632,{703}}}},[182]={t="The Troll Cave",lv=4,min=1,nx=218,rwc={[8]=4},ot="Grelin Whitebeard would like you to kill 14 Frostmane Troll Whelps.",st="My brother Senir and I were sent to different parts of Dun Morogh to investigate the threat posed by the trolls. The Senate has its hands full with the troggs, so they've no need for further annoyances.$b$bFrom what I've seen, the trolls aren't well situated here in Coldridge Valley--mostly the southern cave. I'd say that the army will not be necessary. A few strong arms should be more than enough.$b$bPerhaps you'd like to assist in this endeavor? I have the authority to offer compensation for your help.",how={{"kill",706}}},[183]={t="The Boar Hunter",lv=3,min=1,ot="Talin Keeneye would like you to kill 12 Small Crag Boars.",st="Nothing like a day of boar hunting, eh?$b$bThough, here in Coldridge Valley, there are so many boars it almost takes the fun out of it. No need to get them charging. They're all angry and ready without any help. In fact, recently, there've been so many boars in the area, it's become dangerous for me to do my daily hunting.$b$bLong story short, if you could help me kill some of the boars, I would appreciate it.",how={{"kill",708}}},[184]={t="Furlbrow's Deed",lv=9,min=8,si=1971,ot="Bring Furlbrow's Deed to Farmer Furlbrow.",st="This is the deed to an expanse of farmlands within Westfall.  It is signed by a Theodore Furlbrow and cosigned by his wife, Verna.  And on the back of the deed are hastily scrawled words:$B$B\"We leaned on Furlbrow and got his deed.  Thought it might be handy if you wanted to forge one of these for your own place.$B$BThe Furlbrows won't give us trouble.  Last I saw them they were on their way out of Westfall, stuck with a broken wagon.\"$B$BYou think the Furlbrows might want their deed back..."},[199]={t="A Dark Threat Looms",lv=18,min=16,pre1={250},nx=161,si=2563,ot="Return to Chief Engineer Hinderweir and show him the clue that you discovered.",st="You take a sample of the strange smelling powder."},[214]={t="Red Silk Bandanas",lv=17,min=14,pre1={155},ot="Scout Riell at the Sentinel Hill Tower wants you to bring her 10 Red Silk Bandanas.",st="It's no secret that the trademark of the Defias Gang is their Red Bandanas.  But we've learned that the material from which these bandanas are made signifies the member's rank.$b$bThat being said, I want you to eliminate as many high ranking Defias members as you can.  The highest ranking members will undoubtedly be found in VanCleef's secret hideout.  When you're done bring me 10 Red Silk Bandanas as proof of their deaths and I will reward you.  Good luck, $n.",how={{"loot",915,{598,634,1729}}}},[217]={t="In Defense of the King's Lands",lv=17,min=10,pre={263,267},ot="Kill the Trogg leader, Grawmug, and his two guards, Gnasher and Brawler then report back to Captain Rugelfuss in the southern guard tower.",st="$n, our scouts have identified the leader of this recent Trogg incursion.  It appears that these beasts in Loch Modan are following the lead of a chieftain named Grawmug.  Grawmug is heavily guarded, however.  Two of his most elite guards, Gnasher and Brawler, never leave his side.$b$bIf you feel yourself worthy, $n, I want you to lead the assassination mission on Grawmug and his two thugs.  With the Trogg leadership dead, we just might stand a chance at pushing these beasts back into the ground.",how={{"kill",1205},{"kill",1206},{"kill",1207}}},[218]={t="The Stolen Journal",lv=5,min=1,pre1={182},nx=282,ot="Grelin Whitebeard wants you to kill Grik'nir the Cold, and retrieve his journal.",st="My journal! They took it away to the cave. The one that had it... It was a big brute with some odd markings on his skin and face. I didn't get a much better look than that.$b$bYou've had some luck with the trolls, maybe you could go get it back for me?",how={{"loot",2004,{808}}}},[219]={t="Missing In Action",lv=25,min=19,ne=1,ot="Protect Corporal Keeshan on the journey back to Redridge.",st="At last, friends of the Alliance!$b$bHelp... please... $b$bThe last thing I remember these foul Orcs overpowered our regiment.  Most the men were killed. I took a strong blow to the head and everything went black. Now I am held captive in this cave.  Help me, I am hurt badly.$b$bI'll need help getting back to town... please... you're my last hope..."},[224]={t="In Defense of the King's Lands",lv=12,min=10,nx=237,ot="Mountaineer Cobbleflint of the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts.",st="We need to protect the Loch, $n!  With so many of the King's soldiers fighting valiantly on remote battlefields, we've become overwhelmed on the home front.  Troggs are tunneling up from every crevice!  The Trogg infestation poses the largest threat to Ironforge.  These disgusting mutants must be destroyed.$b$bWe need you, brave adventurer, to venture forth and lay waste to the Trogg threat.  Slay 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts and report back.",how={{"kill",1161},{"kill",1162}}},[226]={t="Wolves at Our Heels",lv=21,min=19,ot="Kill 12 Starving Dire Wolves and 8 Rabid Dire Wolves, then return to Lars at Sven's Camp on the western border of Duskwood.",st="Sven and I have dangerous days ahead of us, what with the Necromancer to the east and all.  And out here alone as we are, we have to hunt for our own food.  It seems every time I'm heading back to camp with some meat on me, starving or rabid dire wolves come out of the forest wanting a bite.  It goes without saying, living out here is dangerous work!$B$BBut if you can rid us of some of those wolves, we'd have an easier time of it.  They mostly prowl north and east of here, near the river.",how={{"kill",213},{"kill",565}}},[230]={t="Sven's Camp",lv=25,min=20,pre1={95},nx=262,si=2161,ot="Bring the Book from Sven's Farm to Sven.",st="Digging through the mound, you find a small, dirt-stained book.$B$BThe book has no title, but...it has information Sven would like to know."},[233]={t="Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery",lv=3,min=1,pre1={179},nx=234,si=2187,ot="Deliver the stack of letters to Talin Keeneye.",st="Hm, I don't suppose you'd be willing to do a favor for me, $g lad : lass;? A stack of letters came through the pass today, but I don't have the time to send them along.$b$bThey're all addressed to Talin Keeneye. You can find him to the west down the road. He's set up camp next to the frozen lake.$b$bWhat do you say?"},[234]={t="Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery",lv=4,min=1,pre1={233},si=2188,ot="Deliver the letter to Grelin Whitebeard.",st="If I remember correctly, Grelin's camp is down the road to the southeast. No doubt he'll be eager to get his mail."},[237]={t="In Defense of the King's Lands",lv=15,min=10,pre1={224},nx=263,ot="Mountaineer Gravelgaw in the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers and report back to him.",st="Mountaineer Cobbleflint had nothing but good things to say about you, $r.  For that reason I am going to entrust upon you a mission of utmost importance.  We need to keep pressure on the invading Trogg forces until our Dwarven brethren return from the Alliance front.$b$bSet forth into the southern hills and kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers.  Your attacks will buy us some time.  Report back when your mission is complete.",how={{"kill",1163},{"kill",1166}}},[239]={t="Westbrook Garrison Needs Help!",lv=10,min=6,pre1={76},nx=11,bc=11,ot="Go to the Westbrook Garrison and speak with Deputy Rainer.",st="The Garrison on our western border sends word of increasing gnoll and thief activity.  They're requesting we send more Stormwind soldiers... but we just don't have any to spare!$B$BIf you can help, we could use it.  Go and speak with Deputy Rainer at the Westbrook Garrison and see what he needs done.$B$BThe Garrison is down the road to the west.  After you cross the bridge over the small brook it will be to the right."},[240]={t="Return to Jitters",lv=20,min=17,pre1={93},si=2250,ot="Return to Jitters with the Dusky Crab Cakes.",st="And here we are - \"Crab\" Cakes ala Grual!"},[244]={t="Encroaching Gnolls",lv=16,min=11,nx=246,ot="Report to Deputy Feldon.",st="Hail, $c.  I am charged to patrol this stretch of road.  Although the road is safe for now, I've seen gnoll encampments to the north and east of here.$B$BLakeshire must know of the gathering gnoll force!  Report to Deputy Feldon in Lakeshire and tell him of the gnolls.  Do this, and I'm sure Feldon will offer you a scout's wage.$B$BFeldon's usually inspecting the area south of the bridge to Lakeshire."},[245]={t="Eight-Legged Menaces",lv=21,min=17,ot="Kill 15 Pygmy Venom Web Spiders, and then report back to Watcher Dodds in Duskwood.",st="Hail, $c. Perhaps you've seen those spiders that have taken over the western border? The eight-legged menaces are too much for us to handle, and the Commander hasn't enough manpower to spare so far from Darkshire.$b$bI hate to ask this of you, but you seem like you might be able to handle them. I can't promise you anything of great value, but I can reward you if you can help root out the filthy bugs.$b$bOh, and a word of advice, you'll want to avoid their venom if you can.",how={{"kill",539}}},[246]={t="Assessing the Threat",lv=17,min=11,pre1={244},ot="Kill 10 Redridge Mongrels and 6 Redridge Poachers, then report back to Deputy Feldon in Lakeshire.",st="We don't have men to spare, but something must be done about those gnolls you reported to me.$B$BScout southern Redridge for gnolls.  Harry them, kill those you can and report back to me with a count of their numbers and an assessment of the threat they present.  You may find those gnolls camped all along the southern road of Redridge.$B$BDo this for the Stormwind Army, $n, and you will be rewarded.",how={{"kill",423},{"kill",424}}},[248]={t="Looking Further",lv=22,min=20,pre1={94},nx=249,si=1083,ot="Climb the intact watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep.$B$BFind a suitable container to place the Glyph of Azora.",st="I have been watching the Tower of Ilgalar, and can detect that Morganth is in conflict with the Orcs in Stonewatch Keep.  I do not know the reason behind their contention, but you may aid me in unraveling this mystery.$B$BTake another Glyph of Azora, then go to the top of the intact watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep.$B$BFind a suitable object on which to place the Glyph.  A chest or a jar -- some place where the glyph will not be noticed -- will suit my purpose."},[250]={t="A Dark Threat Looms",lv=18,min=16,nx=199,ot="Investigate the area near the eastern ramp of the Dam and bring Chief Engineer Hinderweir a clue that might reveal what the Dark Iron Dwarves are up to.",st="Thank the stars someone is concerned about the well-being of the Dam.  First the destruction of the Thandol Span and then the pillaging of Dun Modr!  I have no doubt that the Dam will be the target of the next Dark Iron threat.  Most of the security detail here was reassigned to the Alliance Front, including my top inspector.$b$bThat's why I need you, $n.  I spotted some Dark Iron Sappers milling about the eastern ramp of the Dam.   Investigate the area and bring back a clue."},[255]={t="Mercenaries",lv=19,min=15,ot="Magistrate Bluntnose of Thelsamar has hired you to kill 4 Mo'grosh Ogres, 4 Mo'grosh Brutes and 4 Mo'grosh Enforcers.",st="Two months just to hear from Ironforge that we'll be spared a handful of soldiers for our own defense, and another two months until they arrive! Bad enough that our town goes unprotected, but the excavation and the dam--the dam!--are open to attacks as well.$b$bI've no choice then, it seems. I'll need hired arms.$b$bHow about you? You seem a likely sort, $c. A group of ogres has set up camp on the northeast of the lake. Perhaps you could recruit some others and help remove the threat to our town?",how={{"kill",1178},{"kill",1180},{"kill",1179}}},[257]={t="A Hunter's Boast",lv=16,min=11,nx=258,rwc={[8]=2},ot="Kill 6 Mountain Buzzards and return to Daryl the Youngling in the Farstrider Lodge within 15 minutes.",st="Think you can match wits with Daryl the Bold, huh? I should think not! Of course, you're more than welcome to try. Here's a challenge that should prove to be above your abilities, so don't feel too bad if you can't face up to it.$b$bA flock of buzzards has nested here in Loch Modan. Why don't you try to take down some of the beasts? Tell you what, if you meet my challenge in fifteen minutes, I'll give you my bow or gun.$b$b<He looks you over dismissively.>$b$bIt seems you haven't much to lose, anyways.",how={{"kill",1194}}},[258]={t="A Hunter's Challenge",lv=17,min=11,pre1={257},nx=271,ot="Kill 5 Elder Mountain Boars and return to Daryl the Youngling in the Farstrider Lodge within 12 minutes.",st="$nath, is it? I can tell you're bursting with pride over completing the first test, hm? As I told you before, it's no large feat.$b$bYou should try your hand at boar hunting. Trust me, this is no Coldridge Valley boar hunt, so you'd best have a care with them. I'll give you just twelve minutes this time.$b$bDon't feel bad if you fail. I'd give you the shirt off my back if you succeeded!$b$bHave I ever related to you the story of how I received my famous scar? No? It was two years ago...",how={{"kill",1192}}},[262]={t="The Shadowy Figure",lv=25,min=20,pre1={230},nx=265,si=2161,ot="Take the book you found at Sven's farm and show it to townsfolk in Darkshire.",st="I must know who was that skulker in the shadows I saw the night my family was killed!$B$BPlease, $n, you have shown your resourcefulness.  Please find that shadowy figure.  I must learn what secrets he holds!$B$BI do not have clues that you do not already know, but here - take the book you found at my farm.  Perhaps some of the townsfolk can link this book with its owner."},[263]={t="In Defense of the King's Lands",lv=15,min=10,pre1={237},nx=217,ot="Mountaineer Wallbang in the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers.",st="The Mountaineers tell me you are quite brave and capable, $n.  We need a $r like you around here.  The Trogg problem isn't getting any better.  The reserves have been called to the front and we're all alone out here.  But now that we have a seasoned $c here, let's see what you can do.$b$bGo out and kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers.  Let's see if you live up to your reputation, Trogg-Slayer.",how={{"kill",1197},{"kill",1164}}},[265]={t="The Shadowy Search Continues",lv=25,min=20,pre1={262},nx=266,si=2161,ot="See if other townsfolk have clues about the shadowy figure.",st="Here is your book back, $n, and I bid you fortune with your search.  If you ask others in town, perhaps they can offer you more clues.$B$BAnd here is one more for you - although the author of this book is a stranger to Darkshire, the book itself was purchased here."},[266]={t="Inquire at the Inn",lv=25,min=20,pre1={265},nx=453,si=2161,ot="Search the inn for clues about the shadowy figure.",st="Here is your book, and good luck with your inquiries.$B$BYou might want to expand your search to the inn.  If the person whom you seek spent time in town, then chances are someone saw him there."},[267]={t="The Trogg Threat",lv=12,min=10,ot="Bring 8 Trogg Stone Teeth to Captain Rugelfuss in the southern guard tower.",st="$C, you may or may not be aware of the Trogg threat looming over Dwarven lands.  With the Ironforge Reserve called up to the Alliance Front, we are left with a fraction of the defense forces needed to keep these lands safe.  My regiment is assigned to watch over the Gate here and we cannot leave our post for fear of invasion.$b$bBut we need some pressure put on those damned Troggs lurking in the hills.  If you're up to the task, wage an assault on the Troggs.  Bring me back 8 Trogg Stone Teeth as proof.",how={{"loot",2536,{1161,1162,1166}}}},[268]={t="Return to Sven",lv=25,min=20,pre1={453},nx=323,si=2560,ot="Return to Sven with Jitters' completed journal.",st="The book you found was only half finished.  I had to leave it at Sven's farm when I fled there...$B$BHere.  Take my completed journal to Sven.  It describes more fully what happened at his farm.$B$BAlthough this journal has been my only company these past weeks, if giving it up keeps me from having to face Sven and his wrath, then I do it willingly!"},[269]={t="Seeking Wisdom",lv=29,min=20,pre1={323},nx=270,si=2560,ot="Give Jitters' Completed Journal to Bishop Farthing in Stormwind.",st="Go to the city of Stormwind and speak with Bishop Farthing in the Cathedral of Light.  Give him Jitters' journal and tell him you mean to face Morbent Fel.$B$BAlthough Stormwind has forsaken Darkshire, Farthing is a kind soul and very wise.  He may help you on your quest to save us.$B$BYour mission is perilous, but hurry, $n.  With each passing hour, the shadows of Duskwood grow ever darker."},[271]={t="Vyrin's Revenge",lv=20,min=15,pre1={258},nx=531,ot="Kill Ol' Sooty then show your handiwork to Daryl the Youngling at the Farstrider Lodge.",st="I don't suppose you'd be interested in a little payback for His Boldness? Daryl does have some skill, it pains me to say.$b$bA year ago, a large bear had been the target of the Farstrider Lodge, but none of the hunters had any luck with him. So, Daryl thought he'd try his hand against him. All he had to show for his effort was that ugly scar over his eye.$b$bKill the bear, and I'm sure even Daryl would be speechless for once.$b$bThe bear, Ol' Sooty, can be found around his lair in the hills over Thelsamar.",how={{"loot",2713,{1225}}}},[272]={t="Trial of the Sea Lion",lv=16,min=16,pre1={29},nx=5061,si=15883,ot="Find the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance.  Speak with the residents of Moonglade to learn clues as to where these items may be located.$B$BForm the Pendant of the Sea Lion from the two pendant halves.  You need to be in proximity of the Shrine of Remulos to do this.$B$BBring the joined pendant to Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.",st="For the second trial, you'll need the two halves that make the Pendant of the Sea Lion.  One half draws power from the agility of the sea lion aspect, gliding through water; the other draws power from the incredible endurance of the sea lion aspect.  Druids draw on both these traits equally to embody the aspect of their aquatic form.$B$BSpeak with the locals of Moonglade to learn where the parts may lie, and bring both here to join them together.  Once formed, take the pendant to Dendrite Starblaze.",how={{"open",15885,{15885}}}},[273]={t="Resupplying the Excavation",lv=15,min=10,pre1={302},nx=454,ot="Speak with Huldar.",st="It's not too late though, you're welcome to go look for Huldar. He can't have made it very far, strong as they are, Miran and Saean can only move so fast laden down with those barrels.$b$bThey're taking the normal route to the site, leaving south out of town and following the curve of the Loch.$b$bShouldn't have a problem finding them unless they've already gotten there.",how={{"talk",1379},{"talk",2057}}},[275]={t="Blisters on the Land",lv=26,min=20,pre1={277},ot="Kill 12 Fen Creepers, then return to Rethiel the Greenwarden in the Wetlands.",st="I do not know why, but a festering grows within the Wetlands. Fen Creepers have risen. They are diseased, fevered blisters on the land, and for the fever to break they must be dispatched and allowed to settle back into the marshes.$B$BThe Fen Creepers shamble amidst the waterways of the Wetlands.",how={{"kill",1040}}},[276]={t="Tramping Paws",lv=21,min=20,nx=277,ot="Kill 15 Mosshide Gnolls and 10 Mosshide Mongrels, then return to Rethiel the Greenwarden in the Wetlands.",st="The Mosshide Gnolls have lived in the Wetlands peacefully for many years, but now grow in numbers. Their feet stamp flat the fen's bushes and flowers, and their foul axes cut too much wood to fuel their fires.$B$BThey are no longer in balance with the land. For the Wetlands to survive, the Gnolls must be reduced.$B$BKill 15 Mosshide Gnolls and 10 Mosshide Mongrels. Hunt them to the south, near the Dwarven gate of Algaz. After you do this, return to me.",how={{"kill",1007},{"kill",1008}}},[277]={t="Fire Taboo",lv=23,min=20,pre1={276},nx=275,ot="Bring Rethiel the Greenwarden 9 Crude Flints.",st="The Mosshides are cutting the trees of the Wetlands, using the trees' flesh to warm themselves with fire. I will suffer this pain no longer!$B$BRid the Mosshides of their crude flints, the tools they use to make fire. The flints are borne by all Mosshides except the smaller Mosshide gnolls and Mosshide mongrels.",how={{"loot",2611,{14425,1014,1013}}}},[279]={t="Claws from the Deep",lv=22,min=20,nx=281,ot="Kill 12 Bluegill Murlocs.$B$BSlay Gobbler and take his head.$B$BBring Gobbler's Head to Karl Boran in Menethil Harbor.",st="Murlocs are crawling out from the deep waters and building their villages on the coastline.  They are harassing our fishers and merchants and must be stopped.$B$BOne of these Murlocs, Gobbler, skulks with other Bluegill Murlocs and harries merchants along the road, always then retreating to the safety of the nearby Murloc hovels.  Our merchants are in jeopardy, and we will pay to secure them.$B$BGobbler prowls the river inlet north of here.  Find him, slay his kin, and bring me his head.",how={{"kill",1024},{"loot",3618,{1259}}}},[281]={t="Reclaiming Goods",lv=25,min=20,pre1={279},nx=284,ot="Search the crates and barrels at the coastal Murloc camps.",st="Not long ago a merchant vessel, the Blind Princess, was raided by Murlocs.  Although the ship escaped intact, much of its cargo was dragged overboard by the creatures, including a very valuable statuette of Terenas Menethil.  We want that statuette recovered.$B$BSearch the coastal Murloc hovels for crates, barrels and other evidence of lost cargo.  Find the Menethil Statuette and return it to me."},[282]={t="Senir's Observations",lv=5,min=1,pre1={218},ex={287},nx=420,si=2619,ot="Speak with Mountaineer Thalos.",st="I was planning on sending my apprentice to my brother Senir with my report, but I would feel much better were it placed in more... reliable hands. That is, of course, if you wouldn't mind?$b$bHmm... you'll have to take the tunnel to get to Kharanos.$b$bSpeak with Mountaineer Thalos before going through the tunnel. It's completely infested with troggs now.$b$bFollow the road back to Anvilmar, then keep heading east to the tunnel, Thalos is stationed nearby."},[284]={t="The Search Continues",lv=25,min=20,pre1={281},nx=285,ot="Search for the Menethil Statuette.",st="You thoroughly search this cluster of Murloc hovels, and find no trace of the Menethil Statuette.$B$BPerhaps one of the two nearby hovels to the north and northeast will have more clues."},[285]={t="Search More Hovels",lv=25,min=20,pre1={284},nx=286,ot="Continue searching the Murloc hovels for the Menethil Statuette.",st="This grouping of Murloc hovels, after a thorough inspection, reveals nothing.$B$B...but you're certain that the next clue you find will be fruitful.$B$BOne of the hovels to the north must have the Menethil Statuette!"},[286]={t="Return the Statuette",lv=25,min=20,pre1={285},nx=98189,si=2625,ot="Bring Karl Boran the Menethil Statuette.",st="After pulling the barrel free from the muck and opening it, a silvery figurine is found packed in fine straw.  It depicts a young, long-haired Paladin with hammer upraised.$B$BThis must be the Menethil Statuette!  You must now return it to Karl Boran in Menethil Harbor."},[287]={t="Frostmane Hold",lv=9,min=7,rwc={[8]=2},ot="Explore Frostmane Hold, and kill 5 Frostmane Headhunters for Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.",st="I'm behind on my report, and could use your help, $n. I just managed to find where the trolls are holed up, but I saw so many trolls, I was afraid to go in.$b$bHere's what I need... Go down to the cave, poke around inside, kill a few of the trolls, then come back here.$b$bTake the road north out of Kharanos, when you get to the bridge, follow the frozen river west until you reach Iceflow Lake. You'll find Brewnall Village on the west bank. The Hold is southwest of the village.",how={{"kill",1123}}},[288]={t="The Third Fleet",lv=27,min=22,nx=289,ot="Buy First Mate Fitzsimmons a Flagon of Mead.",st="I was once First Mate on the Wave Mistress, ship-of-the-line in the Kul Tiras Third Fleet. The Doomed Fleet. Doomed, for on its last voyage the fleet was attacked by Red Dragons. Dragons controlled by Orcs!$B$BWe didn't stand a chance against that dragonfire...and our fleet was burned and sunk off this here coast. I'm the sole survivor of those poor vessels...$B$B...Oh, my head hammers and pounds! I'll need a fresh drink if I'm to get a handle on this hangover and continue my tale.",how={{"buy",2594,{1464,5111,5112}}}},[291]={t="The Reports",lv=10,min=1,pre={287,98323},si=2628,ot="Deliver Senir's report to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge.",st="Excellent! Take my report to Senator Barin Redstone. He's a sour type, so don't let his less-than-sunny disposition get to you. He's in Ironforge, in the chamber where King Magni holds court.$b$bDon't know the way to Ironforge? Take the road out of Kharanos north, cross the bridge, then follow the road east--there are large banners flanking the road--up the mountainside.$b$bBy the way, if you might avoid mentioning how you assisted me? Can't let them think I'm not working hard out here, you know?"},[294]={t="Ormer's Revenge",lv=24,min=22,nx=295,ot="Ormer Ironbraid at the Whelgar Excavation Site wants you to kill 10 Mottled Screechers and 10 Mottled Raptors.",st="The situation is severe, that much is for sure. When we uncovered these bones it attracted the Raptors. These filthy beasts killed my brethren and trapped me, Merrin and the poor Prospector up here.$b$bHelp clear the Wetlands of these Raptors, $n. Mottled Raptors and Mottled Screechers are just West of the bluff there. Kill 10 of each, if you can.$b$bThat will be a good start to the vengeance I have planned for them.",how={{"kill",1020},{"kill",1021}}},[297]={t="Gathering Idols",lv=18,min=13,ot="Bring Magmar Fellhew 8 Carved Stone Idols.",st="Recently, just before the Troggs surfaced within the site, we had uncovered a large number of strange, carved idols.  But we didn't have the chance to study them, for soon after their discovery the Troggs chased us away from the ruins!  And those idols have a strange effect on the Troggs.  It makes them go berserk!$B$BBring me 8 idols - I want to study them, and I want them out of Trogg hands!  You can find the idols on the Troggs infesting the site.",how={{"loot",2636,{1165,1393,1167}}}},[298]={t="Excavation Progress Report",lv=15,min=10,nx=301,si=2637,ot="Bring Ironband's Progress Report to Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar.",st="I need a progress report sent to Thelsamar - a progress report, and a restatement of my request for more blastpowder!  Here's the report.  Take it to Jern Hornhelm.  He's our local contact in Thelsamar.$B$BIt's not a difficult task, but it must be done."},[301]={t="Report to Ironforge",lv=15,min=10,pre1={298},nx=302,si=2637,ot="Take Ironband's Progress Report to Prospector Stormpike.",st="We'll need approval to get Ironband more blastpowder. You'll have to take his report to the Explorers' League headquarters in Ironforge.$B$BHere's the report. Give it to Prospector Stormpike, and don't forget to duck after you deliver it. Stormpike is hotheaded, and he won't be happy to hear of Ironband's slow progress at the site.$B$BYou'll find Stormpike in the Assembly of Explorers."},[302]={t="Powder to Ironband",lv=15,min=10,pre1={301},nx=273,ot="Speak with Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar.",st="If Ironband still needs blastpowder, then by Magni he'll have it!  I sent the approval on ahead with a messenger to Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar.  He'll prepare the powder and other supplies to take to Ironband.$B$BAnd one more thing: I want you to personally see that the shipment of powder reaches its destination.  The last one didn't, so keep your mind sharp and your eyes open."},[303]={t="The Dark Iron War",lv=30,min=25,nx=378,ot="Motley Garmason at Dun Modr wants you to kill 15 Dark Iron Dwarves, 5 Dark Iron Tunnelers, 5 Dark Iron Saboteurs and 5 Dark Iron Demolitionists.",st="War rages both home and abroad. While mighty Dwarven soldiers give their lives in far off territories in the name of the Alliance, our own lands fall prey to the evil deeds of the Dark Iron Dwarves.  They laid waste to the Thandol Span. Dun Modr fell soon after.$b$bWe need you to gather force and push the front back.  If you can kill 15 Dark Iron Dwarves, 5 Tunnelers, 5 Saboteurs and 5 Demolitionists, the reserve might arrive in time to finish the drive.$b$bNow make haste!",how={{"kill",1051},{"kill",1053},{"kill",1052},{"kill",1054}}},[305]={t="In Search of the Excavation Team",lv=24,min=21,nx=306,ot="Tarrel Rockweaver wants you to travel to the Excavation Site and contact Merrin Rockweaver.",st="You cannot imagine how worried I have been.$b$bMy wife, Merrin, has been sending me letters each week for the past month. She is part of the Whelgar Excavation team. But it has been nearly two weeks since her last correspondence. Surely something is wrong!$b$bLongbraid said that he would send a scout to check up on things if we did not hear from the team soon. I assume that scout is you, $n. Find Merrin at the excavation site to the east!"},[306]={t="In Search of the Excavation Team",lv=24,min=21,pre1={305},si=2639,ot="Return to Tarrel Rockweaver with Merrin's note.",st="It was horrible! We were uncovering some rare artifacts and we began to discover these large bones.$b$bBefore we knew what was happening, these Mottled Raptors overwhelmed the dig site. Many lives were lost.$b$bOrmer here -- so brave -- saved the Prospector and me. He defended us as we ran for shelter. Now we are trapped. And our hard work lies in ruin.$b$bHere, take this note back to my sweet Tarrel. It will explain the situation to him."},[307]={t="Filthy Paws",lv=15,min=9,rwc={[8]=2},ot="Go to the Silver Stream Mine and collect 4 loads of Miners' Gear.$B$BReturn to Mountaineer Stormpike.",st="The Silver Stream Mine to the east ran dry long ago.  It was converted by the Miners' League into a storage depot, but now Kobolds have moved in, putting their filthy paws on good, Dwarven tools!$B$BWe'll root out those vermin soon enough, but the League wants someone to get their gear out of the mine before we warriors tromp in there and break things.  It'll be a tough delve - you might want cohorts at your side.$B$BThe gear is stored in Miners' League Crates throughout the mine.  Good luck.",how={{"open",2640,{271}}}},[308]={t="Distracting Jarven",lv=7,min=1,how={{"buy",2686,{1247,1682,7744}}}},[309]={t="Protecting the Shipment",lv=15,min=10,pre1={454},ne=1,ot="Ensure Miran and the shipment arrive at the excavation site, then inform Prospector Ironband.",st="Ready to go, $n?$b$bFirst, we need to get this powder to Ironband. It'll be a lot for me to carry, and these parts can get dangerous -- and who knows what else the Dark Irons might have in store for me.$b$bI'll feel a lot better with you coming along."},[310]={t="Bitter Rivals",lv=6,min=2,nx=311,si=2548,ot="In the basement of the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, replace a barrel of Thunder Ale with a Barrel of Barleybrew Scalder.",st="I have to admit, those Thunderbrews make some good drinks. But they need to learn that theirs isn't the only decent brew! Maybe you can help me teach them that lesson...$B$BHere, take this barrel of Barleybrew Scalder. Sneak into the basement of the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos and switch it with one of their barrels of Thunder Ale. Then we'll see how their patrons like my brew over theirs!$B$BAnd if the barrels are guarded, then you might have to distract the guard..."},[311]={t="Return to Marleth",lv=7,min=2,pre1={310},si=2666,ot="Bring the barrel of Thunder Ale to Marleth Barleybrew at the Brewnall Village.",st="Having inserted a barrel of Marleth's Scalder in the Kharanos Distillery's cellar, you grab a barrel of Thunder Ale as proof of the deed..."},[312]={t="Tundra MacGrann's Stolen Stash",lv=12,min=7,rwc={[8]=1},ot="Retrieve Tundra MacGrann's dried meats from the stolen meat locker in Old Icebeard's cave.",st="I had a month's worth of dried meats salted and locked away for the cold season.  Kept it locked so the bears wouldn't get it!  But while I was off hunting deer, that beast, Old Icebeard, made off with the meat locker.  He won't be able to smash through that Thorium though.  But I'll starve if I can't get my meats back.$b$bYou seem a bit more stealthy than me.  Perhaps you can retrieve my stash?  I'll never make it in and out of that cave fast enough with this bum leg of mine.",how={{"open",2667,{272}}}},[313]={t="The Grizzled Den",lv=7,min=4,ot="Gather 8 Wendigo Manes and bring them to Pilot Stonegear.",st="Driving a Siege Engine isn't for everyone.  It takes an iron grip and nerves of steel...lucky I have both!  How about you?  How's your mettle?  Want to prove it to me?$B$BWell...I'm looking to make my engine, Trollplow, a little more cozy.  How about you get me a heap of Wendigo Manes from the Grizzled Den, west of Kharanos.  Those manes would make a great rug for Trollplow's inside deck!",how={{"loot",2671,{1135,1134,1271}}}},[314]={t="Protecting the Herd",lv=12,min=6,rwc={[8]=3},ot="Rudra Amberstill wants you to slay Vagash and bring his fang to her at the Ram ranch.",st="We heard the cries in the middle of the night.  Then this morning, sure enough, the herd was missing two rams.  That dastardly beast known as Vagash has been preying on our livelihood.  With most of King Magni's army off in distant lands fighting with the Alliance, there is no one to keep Vagash at bay.$b$bPerhaps you are brave enough to seek out the beast and slay him.  Bring me one of his fangs and I will reward you.  Vagash lurks just above the ranch here, but be warned, he is deadly.",how={{"loot",3627,{1388}}}},[315]={t="The Perfect Stout",lv=9,min=5,nx=413,rwc={[8]=1},ot="Bring 6 Shimmerweeds to Rejold Barleybrew in the Brewnall Village.",st="I'm on a quest, a quest to make the perfect stout.  I know I can do it -- brewing's in my blood.  I just need to find the right recipe...$B$BThe Frostmane trolls grow a plant, shimmerweed, high up in the hills to the east.  They use it in their strange, tribal rituals.  We dwarves haven't found much use for it, but it has a unique taste...and I want to experiment with it in my brews!$B$BGet me some shimmerweed from Frostmane seers, or swipe it from the trolls' shimmerweed baskets.",how={{"loot",2676,{1397}}}},[317]={t="Stocking Jetsteam",lv=6,min=2,nx=318,ot="Gather 4 Chunks of Boar Meat and 2 Thick Bear Furs, and deliver them to Pilot Bellowfiz at Steelgrill's Depot.",st="I'm preparing to start a mission for the Siege Brigade.  It's a long one, and I need to stock Jetsteam with a month's worth of supplies.  So while Steelgrill is working on my tank, can you do some hunting for me?$B$BI'll need some fur for bedding, and boar meat for food.  You can get meat from boars and fur from the bears... you can find them both in the snow fields south of the Grizzled Den.",how={{"loot",769,{1125,1126,1127}},{"loot",6952,{1128,1196,1129}}}},[318]={t="Evershine",lv=7,min=2,pre1={317},nx=319,ot="Get a cask of Evershine from Rejold Barleybrew in Brewnall Village.",st="Rejold Barleybrew experiments with his brews.  Some of them taste good, some bad, and some...well, some will lay all but the stoutest dwarf flat.$B$BHe lives at Brewnall Village, west of Kharanos, and one of his drinks, Evershine, is what I want.  It'll help keep me warm while I'm on the cold road.$B$BAnd...the blessed stuff burns so hot I can throw it in Jetsteam's furnace for a burst of power!  That little tactic has gotten me out of more than one tight spot."},[319]={t="A Favor for Evershine",lv=8,min=2,pre1={318},nx=320,ot="Kill 6 Ice Claw Bears, 8 Elder Crag Boars, and 8 Snow Leopards, and then return to Rejold Barleybrew in Brewnall Village.",st="I have a cask of Evershine handy, but...can you do me a favor?  Brewnall village could use a hand against the wild animals that wander the nearby snows.  Sometimes they wander close.$B$BWe're not afraid of these bears and cats and boars - no self respecting dwarf would be - but if you can take care of those animals for us, then we'd have more time for our crafting and brewing.",how={{"kill",1196},{"kill",1127},{"kill",1201}}},[320]={t="Return to Bellowfiz",lv=8,min=2,pre1={319},rwc={[8]=2},si=2696,ot="Give the cask of Evershine to Pilot Bellowfiz at Steelgrill's Depot.",st="Here's your cask of Evershine, $n.  And again, thank you for the hunting earlier."},[323]={t="Proving Your Worth",lv=28,min=20,pre1={268},nx=269,ot="Kill 15 Skeletal Raiders, 3 Skeletal Healers and 3 Skeletal Warders, and then return to Sven.",st="Morbent Fel is a necromancer, and an ally to the dark riders.  I would pit you against the power of Morbent Fel, but I will not send you against that vile fiend without first knowing your strength.$B$BYou have already proven your bravery to me, but if you truly wish to face the necromancer, then you must now prove your skill against his minions.",how={{"kill",1110},{"kill",787},{"kill",785}}},[337]={t="An Old History Book",lv=25,min=20,nx=538,si=2794,ot="Return the book: The History of Stormwind, to the Stormwind Library.",st="Although the cover of this book is marred by scratches and caked with mud, the words \"The History of Stormwind\" can still be read along its spine.  Upon opening the book, the seal of the Stormwind Library is clearly stamped on the book's first page.$B$BIt looks like someone checked out this book, and never returned it...",how={{"kill",205},{"kill",533},{"kill",898},{"kill",920}}},[343]={t="Speaking of Fortitude",lv=24,min=20,nx=344,ot="Go to the Royal Library in Stormwind Keep and speak with Milton Sheaf.  He can find for you the book on metallurgy that Brother Kristoff needs for his speech.",st="I'm giving a speech on the Fortitude of the Spirit, and I'd like to recite passages from a particular book on metallurgy - \"The Stresses of Iron.\"  A copy of this book should be in the Royal Library, within Stormwind Keep.  Can you retrieve it for me?  If so, then may the blessings of the Light be with you!$B$BThe Royal Library is very large, but the head librarian, Milton Sheaf, knows each shelf like it was his own son.  Speak to him, he'll retrieve the book for you."},[344]={t="Brother Paxton",lv=24,min=20,pre1={343},nx=345,ot="Speak with Brother Paxton in the Northshire Abbey.",st="The Stresses of Iron?  Yes, I know the book.  Quite a good one, written by the Dwarven miner Margulf Blaggon a few decades ago.  He spent most his time deep in the mountains of Khaz Modan, digging ore.  Smart fellow!$B$BBut where was I?  Oh yes, the Stresses of Iron!  I'm afraid the book was moved to the Northshire Abbey.  The caretaker of the Abbey's library, Brother Paxton, wanted to make a copy of the book for his own shelves.$B$BBut that was months ago.  I wonder why it's taking him so long..."},[345]={t="Ink Supplies",lv=24,min=20,pre1={344},nx=347,ot="Speak with Foreman Oslow in Lakeshire and ask him for Rethban Iron Ore.",st="I've been meaning to finish my copy of The Stresses of Iron, but...$B$BWell you see, I make my own ink for books I copy.  It's my own recipe; it doesn't run or smear, and it dries very quickly  Unfortunately, it dries too quickly!  My last batch dried up before I could finish the copying job, and I haven't had the chance to make more ink!$B$BTo make more I need Rethban Iron Ore from the Redridge Mountains.  Foreman Oslow in Lakeshire is my usual supplier."},[346]={t="Return to Kristoff",lv=24,min=20,pre1={347},si=2795,ot="Return to Brother Kristoff in the Cathedral Square.  Give him the book The Stresses of Iron.",st="Now that I've finished copying the book, here's the original Stresses of Iron.  Thank you for your patience, and if you see Milton please tell him I'm sorry for the long delay."},[347]={t="Rethban Ore",lv=24,min=20,pre1={345},nx=346,ot="Gather 5 loads of Rethban Ore and bring it to Brother Paxton in the Northshire Library.",st="Rethban Ore is named after the man who first found it, Bart Rethban.  When smelted it's not as strong as iron, but its ore has a dark, flat color that some scribes use in their dyes.  It can be found in the Rethban Caverns, north of here.$B$BWe usually have some in stock, but we're too busy preparing for Orc attacks to gather any.  And besides...Redridge Gnolls are now living in the Rethban Caverns and their Drudgers are gathering the ore themselves.$B$BSo if you need some, you'll have to get it yourself.",how={{"loot",2798,{580}}}},[350]={t="Look to an Old Friend",lv=31,min=16,pre1={393},nx=2745,ot="Speak to Elling Trias in Stormwind.",st="That Marzon would be contacting a member of the Defias and have ties to Lescovar...$B$BHaving killed VanCleef and Thredd, it would be hard to see Lescovar brought to proper justice, as your evidence is nothing without their testimonies. That is not even considering the fact that Lescovar is a noble and well connected. It effectively makes him above the law.$B$BYou'll need other help. I loathe to do so, but there is someone I know that will aid us. You'll find Trias in the Trade District of the city."},[353]={t="Stormpike's Delivery",lv=15,min=9,si=2806,ot="Deliver the Package for Stormpike to Mountaineer Stormpike in Loch Modan.",st="The Stormpikes are a respected dwarven clan, and are well known for their fine and discerning tastes.  So it's no wonder that Gringer Stormpike, a Mountaineer of Ironforge, commissioned me to craft him a weapon.$B$BThe weapon is finished, but... Mountaineer Stormpike is far away, in distant Loch Modan.  If you plan on traveling to the north, can you deliver this package to him?$B$BMy last message from Mountaineer Stormpike said he's stationed at the northern guard tower in Loch Modan."},[373]={t="The Unsent Letter",lv=22,min=16,nx=389,si=2874,ot="Deliver the Letter to the City Architect to Baros Alexston in Stormwind.",st="Searching Edwin VanCleef's person, you discover, among other things, an unsent letter. It is addressed to Baros Alexston, the City Architect of Stormwind, City Hall, Cathedral Square.$B$BIt appears to be recently written and sealed."},[377]={t="Crime and Punishment",lv=26,min=22,ot="Councilman Millstipe of Darkshire wants you to bring him the hand of Dextren Ward.",st="As if the neglect for the residents of Duskwood was not bad enough, now the House of Nobles spits in the eye of the Darkshire Council with their decision to imprison Dextren Ward in Stormwind rather than behead the villain as per Lord Ebonlocke's sentence.$b$bWard was caught selling bodies from the cemetery to Morbent Fel, a crime punishable by death.  Yet Stormwind claims Ward as their prisoner.$b$bAssassinate Ward in The Stormwind Stockade - bring me his hand - and I shall reward you.",how={{"loot",3628,{1663}}}},[378]={t="The Fury Runs Deep",lv=27,min=22,pre1={303},ot="Motley Garmason wants Kam Deepfury's head brought to him at Dun Modr.",st="You have proven your loyalty to King Magni, $c.  And your hatred for the Dark Iron scum is as great as my own.$b$bThere is a task I wish to complete myself but I am bound by honor to stay with Longbraid.  But Roggo has gathered intelligence that proves Kam Deepfury was a conspirator in the attack on the Thandol Span.  It was by Deepfury's planning that Longbraid lost his kin.$b$bDeepfury is being held for political reasons in the Stormwind Stockade.  I want him dead, $n.  For Longbraid!  Bring me his head!",how={{"loot",3640,{1666}}}},[384]={t="Beer Basted Boar Ribs",lv=7,min=5,ot="Ragnar Thunderbrew in Kharanos wants 6 Crag Boar Ribs and a mug of Rhapsody Malt.",st="Nothing my tavern patrons enjoy more than some Beer Basted Boar Ribs!  Only problem is, the local trapper who used to bring me supplies enlisted in the King's Army to help with the war on the Alliance front. $b$bMaybe you can help me out?  If you bring me six crag boar ribs and a Rhapsody Malt from the tavern here, I'll give you the family recipe for my famous Beer Basted Boar Ribs, not to mention a free sample!  The secret's in the Malt!",how={{"loot",2886,{1127,1125,1126}},{"buy",2894,{1247,1682,7744}}}},[385]={t="Crocolisk Hunting",lv=15,min=10,ot="Get 5 pieces of Crocolisk Meat and 6 Crocolisk Skins for Marek Ironheart at the Farstrider Lodge.",st="Many a hunter is attracted to Loch Modan to hunt our famous crocs. There are always merchants who seek out crocolisk skins for clothing items or armor, and there are also some who enjoy the taste of their meat.$b$bWe do some trade in this, but not a huge amount, as the crocolisks are ferocious and have entrenched themselves on the islands in the Loch. But don't let me dissuade you, it's quite an experience, wrestling with the jaws of the beasts.$b$bWhy, this one time...",how={{"loot",2924,{1693}},{"loot",2925,{1693}}}},[386]={t="What Comes Around...",lv=25,min=22,ot="Bring the head of Targorr the Dread to Guard Berton in Lakeshire.",st="Targorr the Dread served under Gath'Ilzogg as supreme Executioner.  His methods were ruthless, even by filthy orc standards.  Men who fought bravely to defend the Kingdom were tortured on his whim.  Now he is being held in the Stormwind Stockade, sentenced to die.  Yet something is amiss.  One of the bureaucratic nobles put a hold on his execution.  I am sure foul play is in the works.$b$bPut an end to Targorr the Dread, $n.  Travel to The Stockade and behead him before trickery is upon us.",how={{"loot",3630,{1696}}}},[387]={t="Quell the Uprising",lv=26,min=22,ot="Warden Thelwater of Stormwind wants you to kill 10 Defias Prisoners, 8 Defias Convicts, and 8 Defias Insurgents in The Stockade.",st="The uprising must be quelled!  I need your assistance.  If word gets out that the prison is overrun I will lose my job!  This is a case of foul play if I've ever seen one.  But what's important now is forcing these prisoners into submission for the safety of Stormwind.$b$bThe punishment for insurgency is death.  Kill some of these deviants!  That ought to get things under control.",how={{"kill",1706},{"kill",1711},{"kill",1715}}},[388]={t="The Color of Blood",lv=26,min=22,ot="Nikova Raskol of Stormwind wants you to collect 10 Red Wool Bandanas.",st="Bitterness flows through my veins like a cold river.  My grandson, Mac, was such a good boy.  A mere 14 years old.  When the army was sent off to the front, Mac took up arms to defend the city.  He was a guard in The Stockade, where the Defias gang is locked up.  Mac reprimanded some of the prisoners for tearing their wool blankets to make scarves, a symbol of their gang.  For that Mac was stabbed in the back.$b$bI want revenge.  Bring me 10 of their precious Wool Bandanas.  They are the color of blood.",how={{"loot",2909,{1663,1706,1707}}}},[389]={t="Bazil Thredd",lv=22,min=16,pre1={373},nx=391,ot="Speak with Warden Thelwater in the Stockade.",st="VanCleef and I were members of the Stonemasons Guild. Our main project was to rebuild Stormwind after the War.$B$BWhen we had finished our duties, we were cheated. The nobles refused to pay us for our work. Some of the more senior of the Stonemasons were offered governmental jobs, but VanCleef refused it out of loyalty to all the Stonemasons. He led a riot and left the city, swearing revenge.$b$bHis lieutenant, Bazil Thredd, might know more about VanCleef's plans. He's being held prisoner in the Stockade."},[391]={t="The Stockade Riots",lv=29,min=16,pre1={389},nx=392,ot="Kill Bazil Thredd and bring his head back to Warden Thelwater at the Stockade.",st="Let's get one thing straight, $n: I don't trust you. But, with the situation as it is, you probably won't make a difference.$B$BSo here's how it's going to be: go down there and have your talk with Thredd. If you're really on our side, then kill him and bring me his head when the job's done. And if it turns out you're on his side, and don't come out... when we find you, you'll die along with the rest of the maggots.",how={{"loot",2926,{1716}}}},[392]={t="The Curious Visitor",lv=29,min=16,pre1={391},nx=393,si=8687,ot="Bring the Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor to Baros Alexston in Stormwind.",st="During the first years of Thredd's imprisonment, he never had any visitors. I figured that he was no longer of use to the Brotherhood, so they abandoned him.$B$BAnyway, a few months ago, that all changed; he started to get regular visits... once, maybe twice a week. It was a strange man--the quiet type. I had my suspicions, but all his papers checked out.$B$BHis documents claimed his name was Maelik; here's his description. I don't think he'll be coming to visit Thredd anymore."},[393]={t="Shadow of the Past",lv=29,min=16,pre1={392},nx=350,si=8687,ot="Bring the Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.",st="I really haven't a clue, $n. There is someone else who might be able to help you, and it so happens that he owes me a favor for--well, let's not get into that. Master Mathias Shaw of SI:7 can be found in the barracks in Old Town. Shaw has his thumb on most of the shady, or underhanded dealings of the city.$B$BIf anyone knows, it'd be him."},[394]={t="The Head of the Beast",lv=31,min=16,pre1={434},nx=395,ot="Speak to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.",st="Find Shaw in Old Town. Let him know that the Lescovar threat has been dealt with and about your involvement in the Lord's plots against the city. I'm sure he'll be proud to have another hero among Stormwind's citizens.$B$BHe'll more than likely send you off to meet with the Prince or some other noble. Don't let it get to your head, $n. The nobles can think they rule the city all they want, but some things remain out of their hands."},[395]={t="Brotherhood's End",lv=31,min=16,pre1={394},nx=396,ot="Speak with Baros Alexston in Stormwind.",st="Ah, I almost forgot. Alexston came while you were away, he wished to speak with you. No doubt he wishes to report the goings-on of the Defias Brotherhood to the nobles.$B$BA bit of advice, $n: if anyone should ask, I would provide all details but that it was your hand that slew Lescovar. Trust me. I am... acquainted... with the ways of such things.$B$BAnd as far as Trias goes, well, speak to no one of him... ever... if you can help it."},[396]={t="An Audience with the King",lv=31,min=16,pre1={395},si=2956,ot="Deliver Baros Alexston's report on the Defias Brotherhood to King Varian Wrynn in Stormwind Keep.",st="I have prepared a report for the King. I believe you should be the one to deliver it to him, along with an account of your findings. Do not worry, there is no doubt that he will commend you for doing your duty to the people of Stormwind.$B$BYour audience is scheduled soon, so you'd best hurry, it's a bit of a ways to Stormwind Keep."},[399]={t="Humble Beginnings",lv=15,min=10,ot="Go to Baros Alexston's house in Westfall and search for his compass, then return it to him in Cathedral Square of Stormwind.",st="It seems an eternity since I was a boy working the farm in Westfall. They say you can never go back, and it's true. Doubly true in my case, my family's home has been burned down and taken over by thieves.$b$bI have spoken with my father about the fate of some of my possessions, including my first compass. He was unable to save them. However, he also says that they should be hidden away on the farm.$b$bYou'll find the Alexston Farmstead west of Sentinel Hill. Perhaps you could go and retrieve it for me?",how={{"open",2998,{1166}}}},[400]={t="Tools for Steelgrill",lv=5,min=2,si=2999,ot="Deliver Steelgrill's Tools to Beldin Steelgrill.",st="Beldin Steelgrill owns the local mechanic shop, and he's the best siege engine tech there is!  But he's not forgiving to his tools.  I swear he almost breaks more arclight spanners than we can supply him with!$B$BWe just filled his last order for tools.  If you deliver it to him I'm sure he'll make it worth the effort.$B$BHis shop, Steelgrill's Depot, is just northeast of Kharanos.  And it's a local haunt for veteran siege engine pilots, so keep your ears open for opportunities while you're there."},[412]={t="Operation Recombobulation",lv=10,min=7,ot="Bring Razzle Sprysprocket in Kharanos 8 Restabilization Cogs and 8 Gyromechanic Gears.",st="Upon further analysis of the Gnomeregan situation, it would appear as though we not only failed to eradicate the troggs but we also happened to turn most of the gnomish race into horrific, mindless, evil-doing leper gnomes.$b$bOzzie and I plan to reverse the horrible leper effect with our latest invention: The Recombobulator.  The machine is almost complete but we are in dire need of some Restabilization Cogs and Gyromechanic Gears.  Retrieve some from the leper gnomes out front of Gnomeregan for us.",how={{"loot",3083,{1211,8503}},{"loot",3084,{1211,8503}}}},[413]={t="Shimmer Stout",lv=10,min=8,pre1={315},nx=414,si=3085,ot="Take the Barrel of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Barleybrew.",st="I'd like my brother Wellart to try my new Shimmer Stout.  He's a Mountaineer stationed in the southern guard tower, one of two towers on the border to Loch Modan.$B$BHe may not be a brewer like the rest of us Barleybrews, but he loves his drinks and I know he'll like this one.$B$BCan you bring him this Barrel of Shimmer Stout for me?"},[414]={t="Stout to Kadrell",lv=10,min=8,pre1={413},si=3086,ot="Take the Cask of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Kadrell.",st="I've been drinking more of that Shimmer Stout my brother made - it's great stuff!  I want a fellow Mountaineer to try it.  His name's Kadrell, and he's usually patrolling the road through Thelsamar in Loch Modan.$B$BTo get to Thelsamar, go southeast through the tunnel, then turn northeast when the path forks into a road.  Follow that road straight into Thelsamar.$B$BGive Mountaineer Kadrell this cask of Shimmer Stout and see what he thinks!"},[416]={t="Rat Catching",lv=11,min=10,rwc={[8]=2},ot="Bring 12 Tunnel Rat Ears to Mountaineer Kadrell in Thelsamar.",st="We have a real infestation problem to the west.  Tunnel rat kobolds have moved into the foothills, setting up dens and fouling our land with their filth!$B$BWe want them eliminated.  Hunt them, bring me their ears and earn their bounty.$B$BYou can find tunnel rat kobolds and their dens west of Thelsamar, littered along the mountainside.",how={{"loot",3110,{1172,1173,1202}}}},[417]={t="A Pilot's Revenge",lv=11,min=8,pre1={419},rwc={[4]=1,[8]=1},si=3117,ot="Kill Mangeclaw.$B$BBring his Mangy Claw and Hildelve's Journal to Pilot Hammerfoot.",st="Hildelve wrote in his journal that he was attacked by Mangeclaw, a \"huge Ice Claw Bear.\"  He drove off the beast, but not before it mauled him savagely.$B$BJudging from the state of Hildelve's body, Mangeclaw must have later returned and killed him.$B$BHowever, Hildelve wrote in his journal his one, final wish:$B$BRevenge against Mangeclaw.",how={{"loot",3183,{1961}}}},[418]={t="Thelsamar Blood Sausages",lv=11,min=7,ot="Bring 3 pieces of Bear Meat, 3 Boar Intestines, and 3 Spider Ichor to Vidra Hearthstove in Thelsamar.",st="There's never a shortage of empty bellies here in Thelsamar, kids running in and out, workers from the excavation coming in after  a hard day's work. We're famous for our blood sausages, I don't suppose you've ever tried them?$b$bNo? Well, around here you've got to work for your meals, and don't think just because you're a fancy $c, you'll be any exception.$b$bI'll need bear meat, boar intestines for the casings, and spider ichor for spice. You get me some of those, and leave the cooking to Vidra!",how={{"loot",3172,{1190}},{"loot",3173,{1186}},{"loot",3174,{1195}}}},[419]={t="The Lost Pilot",lv=10,min=8,nx=417,ot="Find Pilot Hildelve.",st="My friend and fellow Siege Engine pilot, Mori Hildelve, is lost in the hills.  We were looking for a rare ore that's needed for a high-grade blastpowder, and during our search he drove his engine up a steep hill and busted it!$B$BStill convinced that ore was in these mountains, Hildelve charged me to guard our engines while he continued on foot, searching.$B$BIt's been days, and I've heard some beastly growls in the hills at night.  Mori's tough as nails, but I'm worried.$B$BPlease, $n.  Find him."},[420]={t="Senir's Observations",lv=5,min=1,pre1={282},si=2619,ot="Deliver Grelin's report to Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.",st="The troggs in the tunnel are extremely hostile, and haven't shown any hesitation in attacking travelers through the tunnel. You seem tough enough, though, so you should probably be safe.$b$bDirections? If you're going to speak with Senir, you'll find him in Kharanos.$b$bMake your way through the tunnel, and after you come out on the other side, just keep following the road, it'll run right into Kharanos."},[432]={t="Those Blasted Troggs!",lv=9,min=5,si=268548,ot="Kill 6 Rockjaw Skullthumpers for Foreman Stonebrow at the Gol'Bolar quarry.",st="Those Light-blasted troggs, turning my work site into a wreck! Look at that, there goes another barrel of powder!$b$bOhhh, I wish I could go down there and wring every one of their scrawny little necks! I want to kill them all!$b$bThis can't be good for my health, all this stress and anger... What have they left me with? Nothing!$b$bI'd kill them myself, but my aim's no good anymore! You go into the quarry and kill some of the filthy buggers! I'll pay you! Just hurt them, kill them!",how={{"kill",1115}}},[433]={t="The Public Servant",lv=11,min=6,si=268548,ot="Kill 10 Rockjaw Bonesnappers for Senator Mehr Stonehallow at the Gol'Bolar quarry.",st="As a member of the Senate and the Explorers' League, I've taken it upon myself to take care of this part of the trogg infestation that has gripped our lands.$b$bThey've certainly made a mess of Gol'Bolar quarry, and for no reason. As we dug deep into the earth, they poured out, destroying our equipment and driving the miners out. There's not much for us to do but to exterminate the lot of them, rebuild, then get back to work.$b$bIf you help me with the troggs, I'll gladly recompense you for your time.",how={{"kill",1117}}},[434]={t="The Attack!",lv=31,min=16,pre1={2746},nx=394,ot="Remain in the garden until Lord Gregor Lescovar and Marzon the Silent Blade have had their conversation. Afterwards, kill them both before returning to Elling Trias in Stormwind.",st="After I put on Spybot's disguise, he'll head in to talk to Lescovar. The guards should let him pass no problem.$B$BWhile you were getting materials for me, I took care of informing Marzon that it was time for him and Lescovar to meet again. I even dropped some false information.$B$BLescovar will dismiss his guards and wait for Marzon out here in the garden. After you catch wind of talk about the Defias, make your move. You need to kill them both before the guards return! When you're done, speak to Trias.",how={{"talk",1754},{"talk",1755}}},[436]={t="Ironband's Excavation",lv=18,min=13,nx=297,bc=297,ot="Speak with Explorer Fellhew.",st="Prospector Ironband is heading an excavation of ancient ruins east of the lake.  His progress has been slow lately, especially considering all the supplies we've sent him.$B$BIronband's a stout, honest dwarf who values results, which has me worried that forces are at work against him.$B$BGo to Ironband's Excavation and speak with Magmar Fellhew.  He manages the details of the site and will know why there's a slowdown.$B$BTo get to the excavation site, go around the southern tip of the lake, then head east."},[453]={t="Finding the Shadowy Figure",lv=25,min=20,pre1={266},nx=268,si=2161,ot="Find the Shadowy Figure.  Your clues:$B$BHe is not native to Darkshire.$B$BHe is a nervous, jittery person.$B$BHe left Darkshire and headed west.",st="Good luck, $n.  I hope you find the chap, and I hope you find him alive.$B$BIf he's left the safety of Darkshire then he could be prey to the beasts of the wilds."},[454]={t="After the Ambush",lv=15,min=10,pre1={273},nx=309,ot="Speak with Miran.",st="We'd been hauling the barrels of powder back and forth in trips before this... business. Now we have to split up the work, Miran's taking the barrels and I'm watching over the other ones.$b$bI don't feel safe letting Miran haul the rest of the shipment by himself. When he's ready to go, maybe you could escort him on his next trip?"},[456]={t="The Balance of Nature",lv=2,min=1,nx=457,rwc={[3]=1},ot="Kill 7 Young Nightsabers and 4 Young Thistle Boars and return to Conservator Ilthalaine.",st="Greetings, $n.  I am Conservator Ilthalaine.  My purpose in Shadowglen is to ensure that the balance of nature is maintained.$b$bThe spring rains were particularly heavy this year, causing some of the forest's beasts to flourish while others suffered.$b$bUnfortunately, the nightsaber and thistle boar populations grew too large.  Shadowglen can only produce so much food for the beasts.  Journey forth, young $c, and thin the boar and saber populations so that nature's harmony will be preserved.",how={{"kill",2031},{"kill",1984}}},[457]={t="The Balance of Nature",lv=3,min=1,pre1={456},rwc={[1]=2,[3]=2,[4]=2,[5]=2,[11]=2},ot="Conservator Ilthalaine needs you to kill 7 Mangy Nightsabers and 7 Thistle Boars.",st="Thinning the younger population of creatures here in Shadowglen was a good start, $n, but there is still work to be done.$b$bThe resources of the forest will be depleted too quickly if the problem is not addressed.  Killing nature's beasts is a necessary evil for the good of all who share the land.  Venture into the forest and slay mangy nightsabers and thistle boars in the name of balance.",how={{"kill",2032},{"kill",1985}}},[458]={t="The Woodland Protector",lv=1,min=1,nx=459,ot="Seek out the dryad known as Tarindrella.",st="Thank goodness you are here, $c. Strange news has traveled to me through the whisperings of the forest spirits.$b$bThe mysterious woodland protector, Tarindrella, has returned to Shadowglen. The dryad's presence has not been felt in the forests of Kalimdor in years. Something is surely amiss if she has journeyed back to this land.$b$bSeek out Tarindrella and see what business she tends to in our grove. One of the Sentinels reported seeing her to the southwest of Aldrassil."},[459]={t="The Woodland Protector",lv=3,min=1,pre1={458},rwc={[11]=1},ot="Collect 8 Fel Moss and bring them to Tarindrella.",st="Something evil is brewing in the forests of Teldrassil.  Look long the hills to where the peaceful furbolgs used to dwell.  They have deserted their homes and are amassing under the name of the Gnarlpine tribe.$b$bOnly the corruption of wicked Fel Moss could cause such a transformation.  The grells and grellkin have infested the area and are threatening the residents of Shadowglen.  $b$bEngage these grells and grellkin, $n, and see if they are indeed caught under the enchantment of the wicked Fel Moss.",how={{"loot",3297,{1988,1989}}}},[463]={t="The Greenwarden",lv=21,min=20,nx=276,bc=276,ot="Find the Greenwarden.",st="You've heard of the Greenwarden? You're not looking for him, are you? Well I say you're crazy if you are, but who am I to keep a fool from $ghis:her; death?$B$BIf you are seeking that beast, then I hear he is in the marsh, east of the road where it forks to Dun Modr. He's lurking there among the crocs...and worse!$B$BAnd leave your money here. You won't need it where you're going...and you don't want to chip ol' Greenie's tooth on your gold when he bites you in half, do you?"},[470]={t="Digging Through the Ooze",lv=24,min=19,ot="One of the oozes at Ironbeard's Tomb has Sida's bag, retrieve it and bring it back to her in Menethil Harbor.",st="On my weekly visit to Ironbeard's Tomb I was attacked by dreadful, dripping oozes! Naturally, I panicked.$b$bI threw my bag at one, but it didn't do anything! The ooze just sucked it right up... Luckily, it did give me enough time to get away.$b$bThe bad news is that I really need to get the contents of my bag!$b$bI don't know which ooze I threw my bag at; they all looked the same! Ironbeard's Tomb is northeast of here, near Dun Modr. Thank you so much!",how={{"loot",3349,{1032,1031,1033}}}},[471]={t="Apprentice's Duties",lv=26,min=18,pre1={484},ot="Collect 6 Giant Crocolisk Skins and bring them to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.",st="I sent my apprentice out into the marshes to skin some of our famous giant Wetlands crocolisks. When he didn't return, I went out to look for him... Let's just say it wasn't a pretty sight.$b$bMidwife says he might pull through, but in the meantime I still need my skins!$b$b...If you'd like to kill a few more of the brutes, I wouldn't be opposed, after what they did. You'll find the crocs north up the coast, beyond the murloc hovels.",how={{"loot",3348,{2089}}}},[475]={t="A Troubling Breeze",lv=6,min=4,nx=476,ot="Seek out Gaerolas Talvethren in Starbreeze Village.",st="A troubling breeze blows through the forest.$b$bGaerolas Talvethren serves as Great Warden to the hibernating Druids of the Talon in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.  His duty as the chosen protector of the Sleeping is to ensure their safety so that their pact with Ysera remains fulfilled.$b$bBut word from Gaerolas is now delayed and I grow nervous.  Travel east to Starbreeze Village and bring back a report from Gaerolas so that I can put my worries to rest, knowing my dreaming brethren slumber safely."},[476]={t="Gnarlpine Corruption",lv=6,min=4,pre1={475},nx=483,ot="Return to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.",st="The Gnarlpine tribe has been corrupted!$b$bThe once peaceful furbolgs have turned against the protectors of the forest.  They ambushed me as I left for the Ban'ethil Barrow Den and proceeded to pillage Starbreeze Village.  Ursal the Mauler, their chieftain, is using the evil powers of the Fel Moss to drive them mad.$b$bI am too wounded to return to Athridas to bring him this grave news.  The task is left to you, young $c.  We can only hope that the deranged Gnarlpines have not made it to Ban'ethil yet!"},[483]={t="The Relics of Wakening",lv=9,min=4,pre1={476},nx=486,ot="Retrieve the Relics of Wakening and bring them to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.",st="Gnarlpine invaders were seen ravaging the Ban'ethil Barrow Den to the west.$b$bThe slumbering druids will be trapped in the Emerald Dream for eternity, unaware of their fate, unless we help. The delicate hibernation ritual cannot be broken without the Relics of Wakening.$b$bJourney to the Den and retrieve the Raven Claw Talisman, Black Feather Quill, Sapphire of Sky, and Rune of Nesting. The druids store them in sacred chests.  Return them to me and I will prepare the awakening ritual.",how={{"open",3405,{2740}},{"open",3406,{2739}},{"open",3407,{2741}},{"open",3408,{2742}}}},[484]={t="Young Crocolisk Skins",lv=22,min=18,nx=471,ot="Obtain $1oa Young Crocolisk Skins for James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.",st="I'm James Halloran, the tanner. My cured crocolisk skins are sought after all over, shipments leaving by boat to ports around the world.$b$bMet Einar? He's one of the hunters that brings crocolisk skins in for me.$b$bI'm a bit short on the softer skins that come off crocolisk young.$b$bBeing that I'm running low, I'll pay you top coin for a stack of the skins. You can find the young crocs in the waters right outside of town.",how={{"loot",3397,{1417}}}},[486]={t="Ursal the Mauler",lv=12,min=4,pre1={483},ot="Kill Ursal the Mauler and return to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.",st="Now the time has come to save the Druids of the Talon. If we fail now, $n, they will be forever lost in sleep.$b$bI shall prepare the Relics of Wakening and perform the ritual. For my work to take effect, the cursed beast responsible for this horrible situation must be slain. Only then will the ritual be complete.$b$bIt was Ursal the Mauler who meddled with our brethren's calling and it is Ursal the Mauler who must now pay so they can be freed. Travel to Gnarlpine Hold in the southwest and slay him.",how={{"kill",2039}}},[487]={t="The Road to Darnassus",lv=8,min=5,ot="Slay 6 Gnarlpine Ambushers and return to Sentinel Amara Nightwalker outside of Dolanaar.",st="The road to Darnassus must be kept safe.  Travelers heading from Dolanaar to Darnassus have been reporting ruthless attacks by corrupted furbolgs from the Gnarlpine tribe.$b$bImportant news and commerce travels to and from Darnassus by way of this road daily.  We cannot afford to have a rogue band of heathens terrorizing people.$b$bTake up arms in the name of the sacred forest, $c.  Their den lies somewhere below this vantage point.  Slay 6 of these Gnarlpine ambushers and report back to me.",how={{"kill",2152}}},[488]={t="Zenn's Bidding",lv=5,min=4,nx=489,ot="Bring Zenn Foulhoof outside of Dolanaar 3 Nightsaber Fangs, 3 Strigid Owl Feathers and 3 swatches of Webwood Spider Silk.",st="Eager for work, I see.  Lucky for you a day never goes by that I don't wish I had a fledgling $c to perform my bidding.$b$bYou see, $n, I can make you very happy and provide you with things you never dreamed of having.  But in order for that to happen you must bring me certain items.$b$bMy business in the forest often requires certain. . .reagents.  Fetch for me 3 Nightsaber Fangs, 3 Strigid Owl Feathers and 3 swatches of Webwood Spider Silk.$b$bLet's keep this our little secret, $r.",how={{"loot",3409,{2042}},{"loot",3411,{1995}},{"loot",3412,{1998}}}},[489]={t="Seek Redemption!",lv=7,min=4,pre1={488},ot="Collect 3 Fel Cones and give them to Zenn Foulhoof outside of Dolanaar.",st="The Council of the Forest has news that you aided Zenn Foulhoof. The satyr is an enemy of the forest. As a $r, you should know better than to defile the forest by killing Nature's creatures.$b$bYou must redeem yourself in the eyes of the Council if you wish to remain a friend of Teldrassil.$b$bTeach Foulhoof a lesson and you shall be redeemed. Fel Cones are corrupted seeds that fall from the trees. They billow with green smoke.$b$bGive some to Foulhoof. He'll think you have brought him a harmless snack.",how={{"open",3418,{1673}}}},[490]={t="Bounty: Gnarlpine Furbolg",lv=8,min=5,ot="Shayla Nightbreeze on the road outside of Darnassus wants you to bring her $1oa Gnarlpine Fangs.",st="By strict orders from the Sentinels, I am commissioning a bounty on the Gnarlpine. They are no longer friends of the forest. Their corruption has left them mindless threats to our people and the creatures of the glade.\r\n\r\nAs decreed, you shall be rewarded for removing the furbolg menaces from Teldrassil. Bring to me their fangs as proof of your deeds.\r\n\r\nYou will find furbolg concentrated in Ban'ethil Hollow, west of Dolanaar and south of the road, and in Starbreeze Village to the east.",how={{"loot",5220,{2152,2009,2010}}}},[531]={t="Vyrin's Revenge",lv=20,min=15,pre1={271},si=2713,ot="Bring Ol' Sooty's head to Vyrin Swiftwind at the Farstrider Lodge.",st="Light! Don't bring things like that into the Lodge... it's unsanitary, unspeakable, un... un... unsanitary!$b$bJust get it out of here, will you? No one wants to see your bloody little trophy, really!"},[729]={t="The Absent Minded Prospector",lv=20,min=15,nx=731,ot="Travel south and check on Prospector Remtravel.",st="What an honor it was when Master Greywhisker assigned me to work under the guidance of the great Prospector Remtravel. At the academy in Ironforge everyone knew of Remtravel's great discoveries.$b$bBut the prospector is rather... um... oblivious ...to his surroundings.$b$bWe had uncovered evidence of a great society. Horrible golems sprang forth from the ground and overran the site. Remtravel never seemed to notice. I ran back to Auberdine for help.$b$bPlease travel south and see if the prospector is ok!"},[730]={t="Trouble In Darkshore?",lv=14,min=14,nx=729,bc=729,ot="Travel to Auberdine and look for signs of the dwarven excavation team.",st="How nice it is to see a $c interested in the great archeological wonders of our world.$b$bOftentimes our work is dismissed as mere hobby by our friends in the Alliance. But what many fail to realize is that recent discoveries in Khaz Modan have proven that a great and powerful force threatens all of Azeroth, from Lordaeron to Kalimdor.$b$bI am most worried about my crew that I sent to Darkshore. They haven't sent word in weeks.$b$bTravel to Auberdine and look for a clue as to their whereabouts."},[731]={t="The Absent Minded Prospector",lv=20,min=15,pre1={729},nx=741,ne=1,si=13536,ot="Protect Prospector Remtravel as he searches for the mysterious fossil, then return to Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine.",st="So then, Hollee... oh that's right, you are not Hollee. Where's Hollee?$b$bBah, that's beside the point. We must find that stone brush... I mean the mysterious fossil! We must find that fossil. The Explorers' League in Darnassus will want some indication as to what I've been doing.$b$bLet me know when you are ready and we will hunt down that brush.... I mean fossil! We shall find something in writing to satisfy the League.$b$bSo are you ready yet?",how={{"kill",2159},{"kill",2160}}},[741]={t="The Absent Minded Prospector",lv=20,min=15,pre1={731},nx=942,rwc={[8]=3},si=4654,ot="Take the mysterious fossil to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus.",st="So the prospector wants to send the mysterious fossil to the Explorers' League in Darnassus? I don't feel right leaving Darkshore without him.$b$bHere, $n, deliver the mysterious fossil to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus."},[783]={t="A Threat Within",lv=1,min=1,nx=7,ot="Speak with Marshal McBride.",st="I hope you strapped your belt on tight, young $c, because there is work to do here in Northshire.$B$BAnd I don't mean farming.$B$BThe Stormwind guards are hard pressed to keep the peace here, with so many of us in distant lands and so many threats pressing close.  And so we're enlisting the aid of anyone willing to defend their home.  And their alliance.$B$BIf you're here to answer the call, then speak with my superior, Marshal McBride.  He's inside the abbey behind me."},[865]={t="Raptor Horns",lv=18,min=13,nx=1491,ot="Gather 5 Intact Raptor Horns from Sunscale Scytheclaws, and bring them to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",st="The raptors of the Barrens are smarter than raptors in other lands.  And I think all that smarts is hiding in their horns!  If so, then I could grind their horns into powder and use it to make \"smart drinks.\"  I could sell them for a fortune!!!$B$BAnd you can help me.  Find me intact raptor horns from sunscale scytheclaws.  They roam in the southern Barrens, and in the northern Barrens near the border of Ashenvale Forest.",how={{"loot",5055,{3256}}}},[916]={t="Webwood Venom",lv=4,min=3,nx=917,ot="Bring 10 Webwood Venom Sacs to Gilshalan Windwalker at Aldrassil.",st="I came to Shadowglen to observe the webwood spiders that dwell in the Shadowthread Cave.  They are cousin to a much smaller variety of spider; I believe the world tree has had a profound effect on them, and I would like specimens to study to confirm this.$B$BFirst, I would like some of their venom.  Gather Webwood venom sacs from the spiders in and around the Shadowthread Cave, to the north.  I can then examine them for similarities with their smaller cousin's venom.",how={{"loot",5166,{1986}}}},[917]={t="Webwood Egg",lv=5,min=1,pre1={916},nx=920,ot="Bring a Webwood Egg to Gilshalan in Aldrassil.",st="Now that I have the spiders' venom, I'd like some live specimens to study.  Unfortunately, capturing a living, giant spider is more than I can ask of you, young $c.  And a giant spider is more than I could handle myself!$B$BBut if you can find an unhatched egg, then delivering specimens will be much easier, and I can then arrange for the unhatched spiders to be contained.$B$BThere must be a nest deep in the Shadowthread Cave.  Please, search for an egg in the nest and return it to me.",how={{"open",5167,{4406}}}},[918]={t="Timberling Seeds",lv=7,min=4,nx=922,ot="Bring 8 Timberling Seeds to Denelan at Lake Al'Ameth.",st="The timberlings of Teldrassil are elementals of nature.  In some ways they reflect the natural order of plants and animals on our great tree.$B$BSo it is disturbing to see how angry the timberlings have become.$B$BI believe it has something to do with the soil.  I have been working on different methods of nurturing plants and would like to try them on timberling seeds.  Please, can you gather seeds from timberlings around Lake Al'Ameth and bring them to me?",how={{"loot",5168,{2022}}}},[919]={t="Timberling Sprouts",lv=7,min=4,ot="Bring 12 Timberling Sprouts to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.",st="Small timberlings are sprouting around the waters of Lake Al'Ameth.  I'm afraid these sprouts are beyond help -- we should try to clear them from the land before they grow large enough to cause trouble.$B$BWhen you're wandering the lake, if you see any timberling sprouts please take them.  Help keep our land clean!",how={{"open",5169,{4608}}}},[920]={t="Tenaron's Summons",lv=5,min=1,pre1={917},nx=921,ot="Speak with Tenaron Stormgrip atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",st="$n, is it? I heard that Tenaron has been asking for you. You'll find him in the highest room atop Aldrassil.$b$bWe may live long lives, but it's best you not keep him waiting too long."},[921]={t="Crown of the Earth",lv=5,min=1,pre1={920},nx=928,si=5185,ot="Fill the Crystal Phial and bring it back to Tenaron Stormgrip atop Aldrassil.",st="It is time for you to set out to seek your destiny, $n. But before you are ready to set out into the world beyond our enchanted forests, there is much you must learn about our recent history.$b$bMuch has changed with our people since the Battle of Mount Hyjal. Nordrassil lies a pale shadow of what it once was, its power used to defeat Archimonde and drive back the Burning Legion...$b$bThere is a task you must perform. Go to the moonwell north of Aldrassil and return me a phial of its water.",how={{"open",5184,{19549}}}},[922]={t="Rellian Greenspyre",lv=7,min=4,pre1={918},nx=923,si=5168,ot="Bring a Timberling Seed to Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus.",st="$n, can you take one of the seeds you brought me to my friend, Rellian Greenspyre?  He is a druid in Darnassus, and when last we spoke he revealed his interest in my work with the Timberlings.  He had some ideas himself, and he will appreciate a specimen seed to work with.$B$BThank you, $n.  You have been a great help to me.  I hope that, some day, you will see the fruit of my labors.$B$BYou will usually find Rellian walking the pathways of the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus."},[923]={t="Tumors",lv=9,min=4,pre1={922},nx=2498,ot="Bring 5 Mossy Tumors to Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus.",st="There is a malevolence growing in the timberlings.  We are trying to find the source, but until we do...in order to keep Teldrassil safe we must cut down the timberlings who are beyond help.  Those that wander Wellspring Lake in northern Teldrassil are the most tainted.  They must be removed!$B$BDestroy the Timberlings you find there, and gather the mossy tumors growing upon them.  Bring the tumors to me so that they may be burned.",how={{"loot",5170,{2029,2030,2027}}}},[927]={t="The Moss-twined Heart",lv=12,min=5,nx=941,si=5179,ot="Bring the Moss-twined Heart to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.",st="The heart of Blackmoss the Fetid is covered with a dark, oily moss.  In fact, the only way to tell this is a heart is from its slow, rhythmic beat... A beat that continues even now.$B$BPerhaps Denalan will want to see this heart."},[928]={t="Crown of the Earth",lv=5,min=1,pre1={921},nx=929,si=5186,ot="Bring the Partially Filled Vessel to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",st="While there is more I could speak to you of the moonwells and of Teldrassil, I must send you along. Corithras Moonrage will be expecting you. I have poured the phial of water you brought to me into this vessel to bring to him.$b$bSeek out Corithras. You will find him at the moonwell in Dolanaar. Follow the road south from Aldrassil out of Shadowglen, and continue to follow the cobblestones as the road turns west.$b$bMind you stay on the road though, $n. There are dangerous beasts in the forests of late."},[929]={t="Crown of the Earth",lv=5,min=1,pre1={928},nx=933,si=5619,ot="Fill the Jade Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",st="First, let me tell you more of the task you must complete. The druids in Darnassus use the water of the moonwells of Teldrassil, and their moonwell must be replenished from time to time. Using these specially crafted phials, you can collect the water of the moonwells.$b$bTake this vessel to the moonwell outside of Starbreeze Village to the east, and fill it with some of its waters, then return to me. When you have completed your task, I shall continue the story where Tenaron left off...",how={{"open",5639,{19550}}}},[930]={t="The Glowing Fruit",lv=10,min=4,pre1={918},si=5189,ot="Bring the glowing fruit to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.",st="Hanging from beneath its fronds of this glowing plant is a large, round fruit.$B$BDenalan would want to study this fruit, you are certain."},[931]={t="The Shimmering Frond",lv=10,min=4,pre1={918},nx=2399,si=5190,ot="Bring a Shimmering Frond to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth",st="The fronds on this plant shimmer in the forest light, giving it a twisting, pulsing aura.$B$BYou believe that Denalan would want a specimen of this."},[932]={t="Twisted Hatred",lv=8,min=4,nx=98403,ot="Kill Lord Melenas and bring his head to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.",st="I must warn you, $n, this matter must stay between us. The satyr are enough of an embarrassment to us already, and this one is much too close to home.$B$BHe is called Lord Melenas. He resides in the nearby cave of Fel Rock where he has gathered a large group of grell warriors. His heart is black as night, and he plots something most foul.$B$BYou must find him within his nearby cave just to the north of here, and bring me his head.",how={{"loot",5221,{2038}}}},[933]={t="Crown of the Earth",lv=9,min=1,pre1={929},nx=7383,si=5621,ot="Fill the Tourmaline Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",st="There is another moonwell southeast of the entrance to Darnassus, on the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien. The Sentinels are having problems patrolling the area because of attacks and the growing ill-temperedness of the Gnarlpine furbolgs.$b$bBe wary as you seek out the well, and keep your weapons close at hand.",how={{"open",5645,{19551}}}},[935]={t="Crown of the Earth",lv=11,min=1,pre1={7383},nx=98046,si=5188,ot="Bring the Filled Vessel to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",st="Without the blessings of Alexstrasza the Life-Binder and Nozdormu the Timeless, Teldrassil's growth has not been without flaw. Strange beasts have been reported arising from the very ground of the tree, and crazed furbolgs attack passing travelers.$b$bI can only hope that the solution the Arch Druid is looking for will be found quickly. I will pour all the phials you brought into this vessel, for you to deliver to Darnassus.$b$bBring it to Fandral Staghelm, you will find him in the druid grove."},[937]={t="The Enchanted Glade",lv=11,min=6,nx=98392,ot="Acquire 6 Bloodfeather Belts and bring them to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade.",st="I was dispatched with a small group of Sentinels here to protect the Oracle Tree from the harpies that have made nests all around the glade. Little by little we are trying to push them back.$b$bWhen the Oracle Tree attempted to send a runner to Darnassus with a report, the messenger was attacked and killed by a group of the harpies.$b$bIf you feel up to the task, go to their nests, slay them, and return their belts to me as proof of your deeds.",how={{"loot",5204,{2020,2019,2021}}}},[938]={t="Mist",lv=12,min=7,ne=1,ot="Escort Mist to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak at the moon well near the Oracle Tree.",st="The sabercat's fur is a distinctive gray color, blending into the surrounding forest. As she lays there, you observe that she is badly wounded, with deep lacerations across her back and stomach.$b$bShe raises her head and gazes at you, bright intelligence shining in blue eyes. She seems to wish to follow you."},[940]={t="Teldrassil",lv=11,min=6,pre1={98398},pre={98398},nx=952,si=5219,ot="Deliver the Inscribed Bark to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",st="The forest whispers of your feats of valor, $n. As I felt the harpies forced from their nests, a greater calm spread across the forest, its creatures once again feeling safe. I have feared sending another messenger to the Arch Druid, but I know that you will see my message safely to him.$b$bDeliver this to him and know that the forest will see you safely along its paths to the forest of stone."},[941]={t="Planting the Heart",lv=12,min=9,pre1={927},si=5217,ot="Plant the Tainted Heart in Denalan's Planter.",st="I have removed that foul moss from the heart, but it remains tainted...$B$BTry placing the heart in my planter.  It is filled with a nutritive soil that may cleanse and heal the heart."},[942]={t="The Absent Minded Prospector",lv=20,min=15,pre1={741},nx=943,si=4654,ot="Take the mysterious fossil to Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor.",st="This fossil bears a striking resemblance to one I once saw in Ironforge. An archaeologist by the name of Flagongut brought it to our annual Explorers' League conference. He believed the fossil had a power which could be unlocked somehow.$b$bLast I heard Flagongut had holed up in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, awaiting escort to the Whelgar Excavation Site. Seek him out and show him Remtravel's fossil. Perhaps he can reveal the secrets of the past.$b$bThe ship to Menethil departs from Auberdine."},[943]={t="The Absent Minded Prospector",lv=24,min=15,pre1={942},ot="Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor wants you to bring him the Stone of Relu and Flagongut's Fossil.",st="Prospector Whelgar now holds the original fossil at his site in the Wetlands. When I discovered the Stone of Relu, I believed it to be the key to unlocking the mystery of the fossil.$b$bWhile I traveled on the road to meet Whelgar, I was attacked by raptors and the relic was lost. I don't know which one of the mottled beasts swallowed the relic but if you can retrieve it, I can unleash the power of these artifacts.$B$BBring me both the Stone of Relu, and the original fossil he holds.",how={{"loot",5233,{1022,1023,1020}},{"open",5234,{9630}}}},[944]={t="The Master's Glaive",lv=17,min=12,pre1={948},nx=949,si=5251,ui={13536},ot="Gather information, then use the Phial of Scrying to create a Scrying Bowl.  Use the bowl to speak with Onu.",st="It is strange that the naga are here, in Darkshore.  But stranger still...are the Twilight's Hammer.  That cult worships the old, old lords of the earth.  Lords defeated long ago.$B$BThe Master's Glaive, to the south, is a place where such an old lord fell.$B$BGo there and look for more Twilight's Hammer cultists.$B$BTake this phial of scrying.  Use it to create a scrying bowl after searching the Master's Glaive.  Then speak to me through the bowl."},[945]={t="Therylune's Escape",lv=18,min=10,ne=1,si=13536,ot="Help Therylune escape, then tell Therysil at the Shrine of Aessina that her sister is safe.",st="Help!$B$BI was wandering around the Master's Glaive, and these dirty cultists surrounded me.  Lucky I'm good at hiding!!$B$BCan you help me out of here?  And I need to send word to my sister Therysil that I'm all right.  She's in Ashenvale to the south, at the Shrine of Aessina."},[947]={t="Cave Mushrooms",lv=17,min=12,nx=948,ot="Bring 5 Scaber Stalks and 1 Death Cap to Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine.",st="I am devising a potion that requires rare mushrooms, mushrooms that grow only in a certain cave.  The cave lies behind Cliffspring Falls, to the east and slightly north along the mountains.$B$BI would go there myself, but I was advised by the Grove of the Ancients to stay away from that place.  Our venerable allies sense that the cave is the hiding place for a new evil in Darkshore.$B$BPlease, $n, gather the mushrooms for me.  And while doing so, scout the cave to confirm the Ancients' fears.",how={{"open",5271,{11714}},{"open",5270,{11713}}}},[948]={t="Onu",lv=17,min=12,pre1={947},nx=944,ot="Speak with Onu at the Grove of the Ancients.",st="Onu, an Ancient of Lore at the Grove of the Ancients, knows of your journey to Cliffwater Falls and wishes to speak with you.  The grove lies to the south, nestled near the mountains.$B$BThe Ancients are patient and wise, $n.  But if Onu seeks your counsel concerning what you saw in the falls, then I fear it is urgent."},[949]={t="The Twilight Camp",lv=17,min=12,pre1={944},nx=950,ot="Find a clue in the Twilight's Hammer camp at the Master's Glaive.",st="The Twilight's Hammer's purpose at the Master's Glaive is not known.  But it must be dark.$B$BSearch through their camp at the Glaive... Search for some thing that may teach us their intentions.$B$BFor we must learn their intentions before a plan is made."},[950]={t="Return to Onu",lv=17,min=12,pre1={949},nx=951,si=5272,ot="Bring Onu the recovered Insane Scribbles.",st="Peering into the Twilight Tome is maddening.  Text begins to swim and dance after only a moment's glance, and once beautiful scrollwork twists into grotesque shapes.$B$BTearing away one page of insane scribbles is all that is possible before a swoon overtakes you."},[951]={t="Mathystra Relics",lv=20,min=12,pre1={950},ot="Bring 6 Mathystra Relics to Onu at the Grove of the Ancients.",st="The parchment you found at the Master's Glaive is a page from an ancient text...written by elves!  It is heavily cursed and tainted by the corruption of the Twilight's Hammer, but it seems the cult is using ancient elven magic to bring their old masters back to our world.$B$BTravel to the ruins of Mathystra to the northeast, and search for ancient relics among the grass and broken stones.  Through their study, we may divine how the Twilight's Hammer intends to exploit the magic of the elves.",how={{"open",5273,{13872,12654,13360}}}},[952]={t="Grove of the Ancients",lv=17,min=6,pre1={940},si=5390,ot="Deliver Fandral's message to Onu in the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore, south of Auberdine.",st="If you had enough time to run messages for the Oracle Tree, then I'm sure that I can press you into service to deliver a message to the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore, due south of Auberdine.$b$bYou will most likely have to secure transport on a hippogryph, but I have faith enough in you that you can manage that. Take this to Onu, the Ancient of Lore. He has been awaiting word from me, even as I waited for news from the Oracle Glade."},[953]={t="The Fall of Ameth'Aran",lv=12,min=9,ot="Study the tablets which tell of Ameth'Aran and of its fall, then return to Sentinel Tysha Moonblade in Darkshore.",st="To the east you will find the ruins of Ameth'Aran. It is now inhabited by the restless spirits of the Highborne that once dwelt within its walls, but once it was a place where the servants of Azshara freely practiced their powerful magics.$b$bI was sent to explore the ruins and came across two large tablets, scrawled with the stories of Ameth'Aran and its fall. While I read the runes, I was accosted by the spirits, and fled.$b$bPlease, if you can, venture to the ruins and decipher the tablets in my place.",how={{"click",17188},{"click",17189}}},[954]={t="Bashal'Aran",lv=12,min=7,nx=955,ot="Find the source of the strange blue aura in the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",st="The ruins of Bashal'Aran to the east are overrun with demonic minions. The sprites and satyrs that have taken up residence in the area feed upon the magical energies of the area, their powers growing from continued exposure.$b$bEven with that, I have noticed that there is one shrine they will not approach. On the western side of the ruins, atop a small bluff, a strange blue aura permeates... There must be an explanation to the demons' reluctance.$b$bI would like you to investigate it."},[955]={t="Bashal'Aran",lv=12,min=7,pre1={954},nx=956,ot="Acquire 8 Grell Earrings for Asterion in Bashal'Aran.",st="If I were to relate the story of my life, I have no doubt it would surpass the limits of your patience. Let us say that mine has been a long and painful life, and this spectral form is perhaps the worst torment of all.$b$bI am held here by the means of magic. Though my words may seem disingenuous, I assure you I would be grateful beyond words if you would help me find the means of my imprisonment. A seal binds me, and by examining the earpieces of the sprites and grells, I may find a trace of it.",how={{"loot",5336,{2189,2190}}}},[956]={t="Bashal'Aran",lv=13,min=7,pre1={955},nx=957,ot="Obtain the Ancient Moonstone Seal and bring it to Asterion in Bashal'Aran.",st="If the grells have come into close contact with the seal that binds my eternal prison, I suspect I know the cause. No doubt the seal has come into the possession of the satyr that lead them.$b$bI feel strongly that this must be true, $n. One of the satyr must surely possess it. If you can obtain it, you would bring me so close to passing the bars of my prison that tears would come to my eyes.",how={{"loot",5338,{2212}}}},[957]={t="Bashal'Aran",lv=13,min=7,pre1={956},rwc={[8]=3},si=5338,ot="Destroy the Ancient Moonstone Seal at the ancient flame in Ameth'Aran, then return to Asterion in Bashal'Aran.",st="It was the craft of one of the most powerful of the Highborne that created the seal that formed my prison. In Ameth'Aran, the ruins to the south that are twin to these, persists even today an ancient flame, blue in color. In this flame this seal could be destroyed.$b$bBe wary in the ruins, $n...",how={{"click",16393}}},[958]={t="Tools of the Highborne",lv=12,min=9,ot="Retrieve 7 Highborne Relics for Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.",st="$C. A task I would ask of you.$b$bHave you seen the ruins of Ameth'Aran? If not, you will find them on the eastern side of the main road, some ways to the south. Once they were the home of many powerful Highborne, now they are a testament to the destruction their dabblings produced.$b$bI have been told by the Sentinels that the spirits of the Highborne persist, and that they wield their ancient magical implements. Those relics must be appropriated, so that we might destroy them.",how={{"loot",5360,{2176,2178,2177}}}},[959]={t="Trouble at the Docks",lv=18,min=14,ot="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz in Ratchet wants you to retrieve the bottle of 99-Year-Old Port from Mad Magglish who is hiding in the Wailing Caverns.",st="Oops!$b$bHad a little mishap, as you can see! The morning cargo shipment from Booty Bay was huge. Huge I say! Never seen so many crates. Well, I was trying to expedite things so I started unloading a bit more than I could handle. That's when everything came tumbling down.$b$bBefore I knew what was going on, I saw that menace, Mad Magglish, go running off with a bottle of 99-year-old port. Chased him all the way to Wailing Caverns. No way I was going in there.$b$bMaybe you're brave enough to find him?",how={{"loot",5334,{3655}}}},[963]={t="For Love Eternal",lv=16,min=11,ot="Free the spirit of Anaya Dawnrunner and bring her pendant back to Cerellean Whiteclaw in Auberdine.",st="In the aftermath of the battles at the Well of Eternity, I heard that Ameth'Aran had been destroyed, its people dead, including my love, Anaya.$b$bI would never have thought, thousands of years later, that memories of Anaya would still haunt my dreams. Wandering the woods of Darkshore in a stupor, I found myself in the ruins of Ameth'Aran... where I saw the haunted spirit of my beloved.$b$bShe must be freed, but I lack the heart to do it. Her spirit must be destroyed.",how={{"loot",5382,{3667}}}},[965]={t="The Tower of Althalaxx",lv=18,min=13,nx=966,ot="Find Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore.",st="Hail, young $r. I am Elissa Starbreeze, and it is my charge to protect Auberdine from harm.$b$bTo this end, I sent Balthule Shadowstrike to observe the strange happenings around the Tower of Althalaxx to the northeast.$b$bIt is past time that he should have returned. I worry that he has encountered some unforeseen danger in the forest. I would be most appreciative if you would find him and see that he is doing well."},[966]={t="The Tower of Althalaxx",lv=18,min=13,pre1={965},nx=967,ot="Collect 4 Worn Parchments for Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx.",st="A group of warlocks has taken up residence around and inside the tower. I would have returned to Auberdine to report to Elissa earlier, but I was afraid that I might miss something while I was away.$b$bDelgren suspected such a company might be gathering at the tower, but did not know why.$b$bA few scraps of parchment that the warlocks carry have found their way to my hands, but I need more to complete the puzzle. I warn you not to venture into the tower, however, the warlocks there are much more powerful!",how={{"loot",5348,{2336}}}},[967]={t="The Tower of Althalaxx",lv=18,min=13,pre1={966},nx=970,si=5354,ot="Deliver Balthule's letter to Delgren the Purifier in Ashenvale Forest.",st="My master, Delgren the Purifier, is a paladin who has graciously offered his assistance in defending our forests from the forces of the demons and undead. He has taught me much about the Holy Light and the art of battle.$b$bDelgren must know of the cult's operations immediately.$b$bYou will find him far south of here at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale Forest. Be swift, I fear the Dark Strand's threat grows with each passing hour."},[968]={t="The Powers Below",lv=18,min=10,si=5352,ot="Bring the Book: The Powers Below to Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern, Ironforge.",st="Although terribly worn and scratched, the title of this book can still be read upon its cover:$B$BThe Powers Below$B$BInside the book is a listing of unpronounceable names with foreboding titles, methods of worship, and preferred sacrifices...many of which include living, humanoid creatures.$B$BOn the inside cover of the book are the words: \"Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms, The Forlorn Cavern, Ironforge.  Proprietor: Gerrig Bonegrip.\"$B$BIf Bonegrip sells books like this, perhaps he'll buy this one back.",how={{"kill",2338},{"kill",2339}}},[970]={t="The Tower of Althalaxx",lv=21,min=13,pre1={967},nx=973,ot="Collect a Glowing Soul Gem and return it to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.",st="Balthule's letter is dire. This Cult of the Dark Strand is a thorn in my side that must be removed. I have been dealing with some of the Dark Strand scum northeast of here at Ordil'Aran. One of their number possesses a soul gem that I believe holds the secret to the cult's power.$b$bBring it to me, and I will be able to decipher the secrets held within.",how={{"loot",5366,{3730,3725,3727}}}},[971]={t="Knowledge in the Deeps",lv=23,min=18,ot="Bring the Lorgalis Manuscript to Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern in Ironforge.",st="As you might know, I collect lore.  Old lore.  Powerful lore.  Lore that opens doorways, and lore that can awaken Those Who Sleep.$B$BThere are rumors of an old piece of lore, the Lorgalis Manuscript, at the bottom of Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale.  That place is the old dwelling of long-dead elves.  Elves who held great knowledge before their city fell to ruin.$B$BSearch Blackfathom Deeps for the manuscript.  Do this, and I will not forget it.  Not even after ... the end days.",how={{"open",5359,{13949}}}},[973]={t="The Tower of Althalaxx",lv=24,min=13,pre1={970},nx=1140,ot="Bring Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.",st="Ilkrud Magthrull. Yes, I have knowledge of him. He is a powerful orc warlock that makes his residence at the Fire Scar Shrine,  a place of great evil in southwestern Ashenvale.$b$bHe had been little more than an annoyance until now, and I had not dealt with him, but it seems that his time has come.",how={{"loot",5533,{3664}}}},[982]={t="Deep Ocean, Vast Sea",lv=17,min=13,rwc={[8]=2},ot="Recover the Silver Dawning's Lockbox and the Mist Veil's Lockbox for Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine. Both items should be found aboard the wreckage of the ships to the north of the village.",st="Off the coast of Darkshore to our north are two wrecked ships - the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil. Some time ago, both ships ran afoul of the blasted murlocs as they sailed across the vast sea into Auberdine. They now lie at the bottom of the ocean as trophies for those fiends.$B$BBoth captains didn't make it out that night, and their logs and other effects are still below in lockboxes. I'd like for you to recover them for us; it would mean a lot to the crew members still around these parts.",how={{"open",12191,{175165}},{"open",12192,{175166}}}},[983]={t="Buzzbox 827",lv=10,min=7,nx=1001,ot="Collect 6 Crawler Legs and place them in Buzzbox 827.",st="Hey! Help me with my latest invention, the buzzbox. You can talk to people far away!$B$BMaybe you've already seen them, they're boxes with levers on them. The only problem is they need constant maintenance.$B$BEach one suffers from a different problem, but I made a really smart decision. I placed each one near creatures that have the proper parts to fix that particular machine. Right now Buzzbox 827 is on the fritz. It's just south of Auberdine, real close. It takes 6 Crawler Legs to fix it. I'll pay ya...",how={{"loot",5385,{2231}}}},[984]={t="How Big a Threat?",lv=14,min=10,nx=985,ot="Find a corrupt furbolg camp in Darkshore and return to Terenthis in Auberdine.",st="Some of my brethren were rescued from a corrupt furbolg in Teldrassil, and I've vowed to stop any more atrocities before more of our kind are injured... or worse.$B$BI have seen a couple hints of corruption in Darkshore already, but I have yet to find any widespread signs. I think it would be logical if the investigation continued with the furbolgs. Would you find one of their camps, and return to me if you see any signs of corruption?"},[985]={t="How Big a Threat?",lv=14,min=10,pre1={984},nx=986,ot="Kill 8 Blackwood Pathfinders and 5 Windtalkers and return to Terenthis in Auberdine.",st="You've already proven adept at scouting our enemy, $n. Do you have what it takes to fight them as well?$B$BNot all adventurers prefer straightforward combat to the art of stealth and evasion.$B$BIf you think you're up for the task, then the furbolg camp south of Auberdine is currently the biggest threat to our people. You'll find some of the Blackwood tribe there. Kill 8 pathfinders and 5 windtalkers, and return to me here.",how={{"kill",2167},{"kill",2324}}},[986]={t="A Lost Master",lv=20,min=10,pre1={985},nx=993,si=13536,ot="Find 5 Fine Moonstalker Pelts and return them to Terenthis in Auberdine.",st="$n, your skills have already helped me in my endeavor. Could I impose on you again to help Grimclaw and his master Volcor? In addition, I can craft you a magical cloak that will allow you to walk unhindered by Darkshore's creatures while you look for him.$B$BTo create the cloak, I'll need five fine moonstalker pelts from a moonstalker sire or matriarch to have enough material. The cats can be found near Wildbend River to the south, or even farther south near Ashenvale.",how={{"loot",5386,{2071,2237}}}},[990]={t="Trek to Ashenvale",lv=19,min=15,pre1={994,995},ot="Find Raene Wolfrunner in Ashenvale.",st="$n, my mistress, Raene Wolfrunner, awaits you in the city of Astranaar within Ashenvale. With your help, perhaps we can at least ease some of the corruption that's taken hold there.$B$BHead south from here and stay close to the road--you'll find your way there without issue if you follow those directions."},[991]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=19,min=18,nx=1023,ot="Find Teronis in Ashenvale.",st="$n, a longtime friend of mine is also aiding the Sentinels here in Ashenvale, but he has yet to return.$B$BHe had leads on finding an item that he thought could slow the furbolg attacks on our people--a rod created by a now-dead, evil wizard.$B$BBefore he left here, he mentioned seeking out a gem for the rod.$B$BHe mentioned the gem possibly being hidden at the shrine in Lake Falathim at the base of the mountain to the west. The gem was being held there before it was overrun.$B$BFind my friend, $n, please."},[993]={t="A Lost Master",lv=20,min=10,pre1={986},si=5387,ot="Find Volcor in Darkshore and give him the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak.",st="The cloak is complete, $n. The time has come to find Volcor. I can only hope we are in time.$B$BThe cloak's magic, once invoked, will not last long; perhaps five minutes. It will be up to you to know when to use it: I would suggest waiting until you find Grimclaw.$B$BIf what he has told me is true, you will find his master in a cave south of here. Grimclaw will be alongside the road waiting for you. Signal to him by waving when you see him, and he'll point the way towards his master."},[995]={t="Escape Through Stealth",lv=20,min=10,pre1={993},ex={994},nx=990,ne=1,ot="Escape the Furbolg cave and meet Terenthis in Auberdine.",st="All right then... if you're sure, we'll sneak out of here. Let us leave when you're ready.$B$BRemember, after you've escaped, meet Terenthis back in Auberdine. I'll head there on my own since I'll probably be moving faster than you."},[997]={t="Denalan's Earth",lv=5,min=4,si=5391,ot="Bring the package of Rare Earth to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.",st="Are you heading to the south?  To Lake Al'Ameth?  If so, then I have a task I might ask of you...$B$BMy colleague Denalan has a camp along the eastern end of the lake, where he is studying and experimenting on the plant life of Teldrassil.  He requested a package of rare earths from Darnassus and it was late, only recently arriving here in Dolanaar.$B$BCan you take the package to him?"},[1001]={t="Buzzbox 411",lv=12,min=7,pre1={983},nx=1002,ot="Collect 3 Thresher Eyes from Darkshore Threshers in the deep sea near Buzzbox 411.",st="A tiny voice crackles from deep within the machine.$B$B\"Wizbang here! The next Buzzbox is north of Auberdine, on the beach$B$BSo, that Buzzbox is number 411 and it needs 3 Thresher Eyes for its repairs. They're just off the coast! The darkshore threshers... *Hic*... Sorry about that...$B$BJust like last time, when you give the Buzzbox the goods, it'll spit out your reward. *Hic*... What? No, I'm fine!\"",how={{"loot",5412,{2185}}}},[1002]={t="Buzzbox 323",lv=14,min=7,pre1={1001},nx=1003,ot="Collect 6 Moonstalker Fangs and place them in Buzzbox 323.",st="The Buzzbox gives a burst of static as you hear Wizbang begin to speak.$B$B\"The next Buzzbox is number 323. Ish north of Auberdine but... where's the ale? Wha? Oh, ish on the road sho ya shouldn't have trouble finding it near the bridge.\"$B$BWizbang mumbles something incoherent before you hear a loud gulping sound.$B$B\"Thish one needs Moonstalker Fangs... 6 of 'em.\"",how={{"loot",5413,{2069}}}},[1003]={t="Buzzbox 525",lv=16,min=7,pre1={1002},si=13536,ot="Collect 4 Grizzled Scalps from Grizzled Thistle Bears to the south of Auberdine and place them in Buzzbox 525.",st="Over the boiling noises and dripping sounds coming from the machine, you hear Wizbang's wavering voice call out.$B$B\"Nexsht onesh far south down the road. Shouldn't be hard to find... jusht off to the shide... near a fensh. I think I hid it in shum bushesh... Bushessh. Hehehe... Yesh, Buzzbox 525 takes grizzled scalps from thoshe grizzled thistle bears. Boy thash a mouthful. Grizzshled... Hehehe...\"$B$BYou hear more gulping sounds as the machine cuts out. Then, suddenly, it bursts back to life.$B$B\"4!\"",how={{"loot",5414,{2165}}}},[1007]={t="The Ancient Statuette",lv=20,min=19,nx=1009,ot="Bring the Ancient Statuette to Talen, in his camp near the Zoram Strand.",st="I would charge you with a task, $n.$B$BI was on my small vessel, skimming over the submerged ruins of Zoram, when naga attacked me, surging from the water and tearing at me with their claws!  I fled, carrying what supplies I could to make this meager camp.$B$BBut when I reached the shore and ran... my prized possession was lost.$B$BPlease, $n, find the site of my ambush, along the coast to the north, and search for an ancient statuette.  It is the reason I have braved the dangers of the Zoram Strand.",how={{"open",5424,{17783}}}},[1008]={t="The Zoram Strand",lv=19,min=14,nx=1134,ot="Bring 20 Wrathtail Heads to Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar.",st="There is evil lurking on our northwestern coast, known as the Zoram Strand.$B$BIt is the resting place of the doomed city of Zoram, destroyed during the Sundering and submerged beneath the seas.  It has been lost to the night elves for ages.  Lost, and nearly forgotten.$B$BNow, the naga have returned, and for what reason we do not know.  But reason matters little; we must slay these fiends and throw them back to the depths!$B$BReturn to me when your mission is complete.",how={{"loot",5490,{3715,3711,3944}}}},[1009]={t="Ruuzel",lv=25,min=20,pre1={1007},ot="Bring the Ring of Zoram to Talen near the Zoram Strand.",st="I fear the ancient statuette's secrets will remain forever hidden unless you find the key to its ancient lock.$B$BThat key is a ring, the Ring of Zoram.  It belonged to the rulers of this city before the waves of the Sundering drowned it.$B$BFor years the ring was lost, but the naga have recently found it.$B$BTheir leader, Ruuzel, dwells on an isle on the northern edge of Zoram.  Please, $n, retrieve the ring for me!",how={{"loot",5445,{3943}}}},[1010]={t="Bathran's Hair",lv=20,min=20,nx=1020,ot="Bring 5 Bathran's Hair to Orendil Broadleaf in Ashenvale.",st="There is a plant that once grew in the old ruins of Bathran's Haunt to the north.  The plant was called Bathran's Hair and was known to cure ailments of the spirit.$B$BThere is a sick child in the village, and I believe it is more than just a physical illness.  Will you go to Bathran's Haunt and search it for Bathran's Hair?  I may need it to properly treat the child.$B$BBathran's Haunt lies north of Maestra's Post and just south of the border to Darkshore.",how={{"open",5437,{17282}}}},[1011]={t="Forsaken Diseases",lv=29,min=24,nx=1012,ot="Bring a Bottle of Disease to Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song.",st="The Forsaken, the undead arm of the Horde, have crept into Ashenvale, lurking at our ruins and our barrows.  We believe their goal is to spread disease amongst the lands of the night elves.  We must confirm this!$B$BThe Forsaken have a camp south of here, near the Dor'Danil Barrow Den, where they create poisons and diseases and place them in bottles.  Fight your way into that camp and steal a bottle of disease.  Return with such a bottle.  I will test it and find its purpose.",how={{"open",5440,{18036}}}},[1016]={t="Elemental Bracers",lv=24,min=20,nx=1017,si=5456,ui={5996},ot="Collect 5 Intact Elemental Bracers and use the Divining Scroll on them. Afterwards, bring the Divined Scroll to Sentinel Velene Starstrike at the Silverwind Refuge.",st="Take this divining scroll--it can determine the creator of these elementals. But you will need something from them to use as a reagent to focus scroll's magic--their bracers should do nicely.$B$BA few intact bracers from the creatures should be enough. The other bracers will be useless for our purposes, but they may be worth something to a merchant if you wish to sell them. Once you have the intact bracers attempt to use the scroll. Return to me with the results and we shall proceed from there.",how={{"loot",5455}}},[1017]={t="Mage Summoner",lv=25,min=20,pre1={1016},ot="Slay Sarilus Foulborne and bring his head to Sentinel Velene Starstrike in Silverwind Refuge.",st="There's only one undead mage in the Barrens capable of defiling this many water elementals. He's also the only one foolish enough to try. Sarilus Foulborne is probably sitting at the top of Dreadmist Peak, laughing at me.$B$B$n, you must go into enemy territory and destroy this miscreant. I have had enough of his idiocy and we must show him what happens to those who annoy the Sentinels.$B$BDestroy him and bring me his head. Be wary though, the Horde may be watching for you.",how={{"loot",5537,{3986}}}},[1020]={t="Orendil's Cure",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1010},nx=1033,si=5460,ot="Bring Orendil's Cure to Pelturas Whitemoon in Astranaar.",st="$n, I have created a cure that I believe will help the afflicted child.  Take it to Astranaar and give it to the child's parent, Pelturas Whitemoon.$B$BTo reach Astranaar, follow the road south, then east."},[1021]={t="Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger!",lv=32,min=26,nx=1031,ot="Find Anilia in Xavian.",st="Listen, I don't know who you are, but I need your help. My sisters went to take back the Branch of Cenarius from the satyr. They said they'd be back soon, but it's been two whole days!$B$B$n, you have to find them! They were looking for the ruins of a night elf temple in Xavian to the northeast. I don't know what to think. Look for Anilia, she was leading them on the search."},[1022]={t="The Howling Vale",lv=30,min=25,nx=1037,ot="Go to the Howling Vale and study the Tome of Mel'Thandris, then return to Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow at the Shrine of Aessina.",st="Though we have put many resources and much effort into driving the remaining demons from the Felwood to the north, our successes have been few. We have been able to keep much of the demonic presence from Ashenvale.$b$bTo the north, near the Felwood border, the ruined shrine of Mel'Thandris has been overtaken by mysterious wolf-men. Their chilling calls have led the area to be known as the Howling Vale. The Tome of Mel'Thandris kept at the shrine may shed some light on why these wolf-men have come.",how={{"click",19027}}},[1023]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=21,min=18,pre1={991},nx=1024,si=5505,ot="Find the Glowing Gem and return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar with Teronis' Journal.",st="As you rummage through Teronis' belongings, you find a journal that is still in good condition.$B$BYou take the journal and leave Teronis' corpse as is.$B$BThe only thing left to do is find the gem Teronis was seeking. Raene mentioned it being in the area. Perhaps the murlocs have it...",how={{"loot",5463,{3742,3740,3737}}}},[1024]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=21,min=18,pre1={1023},nx=1026,si=5463,ot="Find Shael'dryn at the moonwell to the northeast.",st="You'll have to do the research yourself, but from what notes Teronis has made, it sounds like your next course of action is to find the other pieces of the rod Dartol created. I would start by heading to the moonwell east of Iris Lake. When you're ready, follow the road and turn north when you reach a small sitting area on your left.$B$BA dryad there named Shael'dryn is better suited to guide you. Seek her out.$B$BKeep the gem with you--Shael'dryn will need it if she's to help you recreate the rod."},[1025]={t="An Aggressive Defense",lv=24,min=18,pre1={1023},ot="Kill 1 Den Watcher, 2 Ursas, 10 Totemics, and 12 Warriors of the Foulweald tribe, and then return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.",st="Before you travel to the moonwell I have another task that will aid the people of Ashenvale if you would like to test your skills.$B$BAlong the road heading east before the Falfarren River, furbolgs have been attacking travelers. Their tortured minds feeding upon fear, and their appetites satiated by the blood of innocents.$B$BAid the Sentinels in protecting the lands by showing those monsters the same mercy they have shown our kind.$B$BI believe their camps are south of the road... be careful.",how={{"kill",3746},{"kill",3749},{"kill",3750},{"kill",3743}}},[1026]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=27,min=18,pre1={1024},nx=1027,ot="Find the Wooden Key and a piece of Dartol's Rod before returning to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.",st="I wish your tidings were better.$B$BRaene is correct, I know about Dartol's creation and the treants in the area--at least I did once. They've become corrupted now, their nature twisted.$B$BIf your goal is to find the next piece of the rod, then you'll have to find the key to open the chest it's in.$B$BThe wooden key is on one of the treants northeast of here, near Felwood. Once you have it, look for a small glade west of the road near the Felwood border... the chest should be hidden around there.",how={{"open",5464,{19022}}}},[1027]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=28,min=18,pre1={1026},nx=1028,ot="Find the final piece of Dartol's Rod and return to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.",st="The final piece of the rod was given to the druids of Dor'danil for safekeeping. I have no idea where they hid it. I'm sorry I can't help you more than that.$B$BAll I can tell you is to follow the road that leads towards the Barrens. The druids took shelter to the east of that road, but they won't be of much help to you: they were killed recently... it's something I don't like to think about much.$B$BWhen you find the final piece, bring it to me and I will help you reconstruct the rod.",how={{"open",5519,{19021}}}},[1028]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=28,min=18,pre1={1027},nx=1055,si=5547,ot="Find the hidden shrine and re-enchant Dartol's Rod.",st="Here is the completed rod, $n. Reconstructing it was simple... it's finding the shrine that has the power to recharge it that will be the hard part.$B$BWith some focus and effort it shouldn't be too hard for someone like you, who's already accomplished so much.$B$BHead southeast of here--there are very few paths, so be careful--and keep your eyes to the north. The shrine is hidden within the mountains that surround this glade.$B$BOnce there, place the rod within the shrine... the rest is magic. Hehe."},[1029]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=28,min=18,pre1={1055},nx=1030,si=5462,ot="Return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.",st="I suggest you find Raene and let her know the rod is finished. I'm sure she'll know what your next course should be.$B$BGood luck, $n."},[1030]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=28,min=18,pre1={1029},nx=1045,si=5462,ot="Find an uncorrupted furbolg, and using the power of Dartol's Rod of Transformation, speak to him.",st="Alas, I'm not completely certain what he had in mind next.$B$BIf what he said was true about the rod's power, then it will allow you to take on another form altogether. Which form, I do not know.$B$BPerhaps he meant to use its powers to get closer to the tainted furbolgs, but even the uncorrupted creatures would slaughter him were he not careful. Transformed by the rod, Dartol would have to speak to a furbolg who was safe from the effects of Fel Moss.$B$BI would start your search southeast of Mystral Lake."},[1031]={t="The Branch of Cenarius",lv=32,min=26,pre1={1021},nx=1032,ot="Kill Geltharis and return the Branch of Cenarius to Illiyana at the Shrine of Aessina.",st="Anilia puts her hands on your shoulders and draws you close. Gasping, she points towards the arch to the north, before her eyes close and her last wheezing breath leaves her body. \"He has taken it... Geltharis...\" You know in your heart that Anilia's dying wish is to see the Branch of Cenarius back in dryad hands.",how={{"loot",5461,{4619}}}},[1032]={t="Satyr Slaying!",lv=32,min=26,pre1={1031},ot="Bring 16 Satyr Horns to Illiyana in the Shrine of Aessina.",st="I can't believe that Anilia is gone... We used to play together in the forests all the time. I almost feel... sad.$B$BI know something that might make me feel better. Please, slay the satyrs that took Anilia from me! Bring me their horns as proof of your actions and you will forever have my gratitude.",how={{"loot",5481,{3767,3770,3765,3771}}}},[1033]={t="Elune's Tear",lv=22,min=20,pre1={1020},nx=1034,ot="Bring Elune's Tear to Pelturas in Astranaar.",st="I had hoped Orendil's cure would save Relara, but I fear it only slowed the disease running through my child.  We must find more powerful medicine!  Thankfully, Orendil spoke to me of further remedies to try should his first one fail.$B$BElune's Tear is a type of stone that rests in only one place: the isle on Iris Lake, east of Astranaar.  Orendil said the stone will wash away corruption... please, $n, bring me Elune's Tear and pray it will end my child's sickness!",how={{"open",5493,{19015}}}},[1034]={t="The Ruins of Stardust",lv=23,min=20,pre1={1033},nx=1035,ot="Bring 5 Handfuls of Stardust to Pelturas in Astranaar.",st="Elune's Tear washed clear some of my daughter's sickness.  Her nightmares are lessened and I thank the goddess for her blessing.  But ... fever still rages within her.$B$BOrendil told me of a frosted dust found among the Ruins of Stardust.  Perhaps it will abate Relara's fever.  Gather some of the dust, then please return to me.$B$BThe Ruins of Stardust lie to the south, $n.  May Elune speed your journey.",how={{"open",5494,{19016}}}},[1035]={t="Fallen Sky Lake",lv=30,min=20,pre1={1034},ot="Retrieve a Fallen Moonstone from the Shadethicket Oracle, then bring it to Pelturas in Astranaar.",st="Relara's fever has passed, but she is still very weak.  I do not believe time alone will give her back the strength she has lost.  I believe it will take the power of a moonstone.$B$BWe used to gather moonstones at Fallen Sky Lake to the southeast... until the Shadethickets came.$B$BTheir leader, a Shadethicket Oracle, gathered up all the fallen moonstones and hoards them.  Now, you must retrieve a moonstone from the Oracle.$B$BAnd to do that, I fear that you must slay him.",how={{"loot",5508,{3931}}}},[1037]={t="Velinde Starsong",lv=30,min=25,pre1={1022},nx=1038,ot="Speak with Thyn'tel Bladeweaver at the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus.",st="Velinde Starsong was my predecessor here in Ashenvale Forest. At first it seemed she had the situation in Felwood under control, but little by little her efforts faltered. One day, she simply disappeared.$b$bI was sent here to continue her work. I'm afraid I know nothing of the priestess, however. Perhaps Thyn'tel Bladeweaver, one of the commanders of the Sentinels, knows further details of her disappearance that I was not a party to.$b$bSurely she will understand the import of such information."},[1038]={t="Velinde's Effects",lv=30,min=25,pre1={1037},nx=1039,si=5521,ot="Search through Velinde's chest for her journal, then return it along with the key to Thyn'tel Bladeweaver in Darnassus.",st="The Tome of Mel'Thandris showed you this? I suppose there would be little harm in allowing you to examine her belongings. This key will allow you to open the chest where we stored her things in the Sentinels' bunkhouse. She kept a journal of her duties, if there is anything to be learned, it will be from that.$b$bI should tell you, the Sentinels believe that she had her own reasons for leaving, and expect that she could return at any time. The priestess has done much in the past to earn our trust.",how={{"open",5520,{19877}}}},[1039]={t="The Barrens Port",lv=30,min=25,pre1={1038},nx=1040,ot="Speak with Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.",st="Ratchet is the only port in the Barrens. Most likely Velinde found a trading vessel in Ratchet to take her to Blackwater Cove in Azeroth. We've had limited dealings with the goblins that run the port, but the master of the dock should have information about the comings and goings of ship passengers.$b$bFollow the road southeast through Ashenvale and you will find yourself in the Barrens. Watch your step, $n, warriors of the Horde patrol the land. You will be safe at the port, though."},[1045]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=30,min=18,pre1={1030},nx=1046,si=5462,ot="Kill 4 Bloodtooth Guards and retrieve Ran Bloodtooth's Skull for Krolg near Lake Mystral.",st="The night elves are as old as time, but their arrogance destroys their very world. And now it destroys our lives too. But that can no longer be controlled...$B$BI blame the elves for much, but we are still responsible for our actions. Even beyond the corruption, we are capable of great evil.$B$BRan Bloodtooth is one such evil. Power hungry, lusting... the corruption has only made him stronger. My hatred for the elves burns, but I do not wish ill upon their children, so we must police our own.",how={{"kill",3696},{"kill",3932}}},[1046]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=30,min=18,pre1={1045},ot="Bring Ran Bloodtooth's Skull and Dartol's Rod of Transformation to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.",st="Return to your own tribe and let them know of your victory here.$B$BShow them your trophy, and bask in the glory...",how={{"loot",5388,{3696}},{"loot",5462}}},[1054]={t="Culling the Threat",lv=25,min=18,ot="Bring Dal Bloodclaw's Skull to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.",st="Directly to the north of Astranaar are the Thistlefur furbolg. My scouts report that their numbers have grown greatly over the past few months. If they grow too great, they may find the courage to attack Astranaar directly.$B$BKill as many of their kind as you can, but bring me their chieftain's skull as proof that their efforts have been stifled... for now.$B$BI shall remain here in Astranaar and await word from you. Elune be with you.",how={{"loot",5544,{3987}}}},[1055]={t="Raene's Cleansing",lv=28,min=18,pre1={1028},nx=1029,ot="Return to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.",st="The rod, now complete, lies in your hands. Shael'dryn will want to hear of your success."},[1056]={t="Journey to Stonetalon Peak",lv=18,min=18,nx=1057,bc=1057,ot="Travel to Keeper Albagorm on Stonetalon Peak.",st="The forest spirits tell me you are brave and willing to travel.$b$bTo the south, not far from Mystral Lake, there lies a tunnel named The Talondeep Path. Through this tunnel you will come to an area known as Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Once there, journey to the southwest past Cragpool Lake and then north, up the steep slope until you reach Stonetalon Peak.$b$bThere awaits Keeper Albagorm. Heed his bidding, $r.$b$bThe journey will be perilous."},[1057]={t="Reclaiming the Charred Vale",lv=27,min=20,nx=1059,ot="Keeper Albagorm on Stonetalon Peak wants you to slay 6 Bloodfury Harpies, 6 Bloodfury Ambushers, 6 Bloodfury Slayers and 6 Bloodfury Roguefeathers.",st="As a protector of the forest spirits you can undoubtedly guess why I am alarmed.$b$bYou have traveled through these mountains to reach this peak. Surely you have seen the travesty which has befallen the land. Greed has led to the destruction of these sacred hills.$b$bThe Charred Vale to the south was set afire by the greedy mechanized army of industrialists. Worse yet, the Bloodfuries that have encroached on the land refuse us passage in to begin regrowth.$b$bDrive the wretched harpies out, $n!",how={{"kill",4022},{"kill",4025},{"kill",4024},{"kill",4023}}},[1070]={t="On Guard in Stonetalon",lv=21,min=17,nx=1085,bc=1085,ot="Find Kaela Shadowspear overlooking the valley entering Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",st="Hello, $n.$B$BYou seem to be full of wanderlust by the looks of you. Have you been to the Stonetalon Mountains? It is a land plagued by the Venture Co. and other enemies of the night elves.$B$BRecently, Sentinel Wolfrunner sent my friend Kaela Shadowspear there to investigate what's happening to the land, but I have yet to hear word back from her. I'm even more concerned because the Alliance sent a gnome mage along with her... a sign of trouble for sure.$B$BWould you find her and report back to me?"},[1071]={t="A Gnome's Respite",lv=21,min=17,pre1={1085},ot="Kill 10 Venture Co. Loggers, and 10 Venture Co. Deforesters and return to Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon.",st="You see, $n, I'm a member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, and it's my goal... nay, my DUTY! to show the night elves that a blend of magic, mixtures, and mechanisms can help save their forests.$B$BBut it's a hard fought war, and the goblins reproduce like rabbits it seems. I haven't even had time to build my newest inventions!$B$BI need some time to plan and organize. But to do that, I need your help keeping the goblins at bay in Windshear Crag to the east...",how={{"kill",3989},{"kill",3991}}},[1072]={t="An Old Colleague",lv=21,min=17,pre1={1071},nx=1073,ot="Speak to Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge.",st="The device I'm thinking about is my most advanced version to date. But we'll need a special potion if it's to work. I'm thinking we might as well get the good stuff since this mission could be your last.$B$BAnd for that, we're going to need some potent explosives: Nitromirglyceronium.$B$BThe only person who can make NG-5 is an old friend of mine: Lomac Gearstrip. Look for him in Tinker Town.$B$BYou talk him into making us some NG-5, I'll get to work on placement for my devices."},[1073]={t="Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun",lv=21,min=17,pre1={1072},nx=1074,ot="Bring 4 Minor Mana Potions and 2 Elixirs of Minor Fortitude to Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge.",st="Hahaha... you need Nitromirglyceronium to stop goblins from destroying a forest?!$B$BI don't care if you know Gaxim or not... I'll give you the stuff just to see you or them explode into itty bitty pieces.$B$BThere's a problem though: I'm all out.$B$BBut I'll tell you what, you bring me the correct potions, and I'll make some up for you right away.$B$BThe least you can do is prove you've got some skill as an alchemist before I just give you a sample of my greatest creation.",how={{"loot",2455,{95}},{"loot",2458}}},[1075]={t="A Scroll from Mauren",lv=21,min=17,pre1={1071},nx=1076,ot="Find Collin Mauren in Stormwind.",st="Okay, now for the remote detonation part of my plan... oh, I haven't explained that yet, have I?$B$BOkay, so the short of it is this: with a little magic, I can make it so the explosives go off while you're not around. I'm putting together a device that'll allow you to push just one button and have the NG-5 explode when you're ready.$B$BBut I need a spell from a friend in Stormwind--Collin Mauren is his name. You can find him in the mage quarter there. He's human, so he shouldn't be hard to miss."},[1076]={t="Devils in Westfall",lv=21,min=17,pre1={1075},nx=1077,ot="Bring Dust Devil Debris to Collin Mauren in Stormwind.",st="Ah, I think I have it. A messaging spell... I believe that's the effect he's looking for.$B$BI'll have to create a scroll with the spell impressed upon it. To do that I'll need debris from a dust devil.$B$BWhile I gather the rest of the components, why don't you head to Westfall and find one of the foul creatures? They are dangerous, but I'm sure it's nothing you can't handle if you're willing to subject yourself to one of Gaxim's experiments.$B$BI'll be here when you return.",how={{"loot",5669,{832}}}},[1078]={t="Retrieval for Mauren",lv=26,min=17,ot="Bring 8 Crystalized Scales to Collin Mauren in Stormwind.",st="Travelers keep asking me about the Stonetalon Mountains. It seems to be a popular place for adventure--it doesn't matter if you're seeking wyvern, elementals, or you have business with the Venture Co.$B$BWithin the Charred Vale, deep in Stonetalon, there used to be a species of basilisks whose scales, when ground to dust, made a wonderful reagent for some spells I've created.$B$BIf those basilisks still live, I would love to have a few of their scales.$B$BTake your time, it is no rush, but I can pay well.",how={{"loot",5675,{4042,4044,4041}}}},[1085]={t="On Guard in Stonetalon",lv=21,min=17,nx=1071,ot="Speak to Gaxim.",st="The situation here in Stonetalon is obviously grave for a night elf and gnome to be working together.$B$BThe Venture Co. has devastated these lands and I've spent most of my time putting an end to the destruction.$B$BDo not judge Gaxim prematurely; he understands the need for us to work together.$B$BIf you wish to aid us, then start by speaking to Gaxim.$B$BI'm sorry I cannot send you back to Tara with good news yet. Perhaps soon."},[1090]={t="Gerenzo's Orders",lv=22,min=17,nx=1092,ne=1,ot="Get the mysterious ore from Piznik after he finishes mining it.",st="You know, I was once the second most important person here at this site. That all changed when Gerenzo took over. Fired my boss, Ziz Fizziks, and sent me down to work in the mines. Ziz told me to stay here and gather information, though. His new boss will pay us well if we can find out what Gerenzo's plans are.$b$bAnyways, what I do know is that Gerenzo has ordered large amounts of this gold-green ore to be mined. I can get you a sample to bring to Ziz, but you'll have to watch for patrols while I get it.",how={{"kill",3998}}},[1092]={t="Gerenzo's Orders",lv=22,min=17,pre1={1090},si=5733,ot="Deliver the Unidentified Ore to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",st="I guess I'd better think about getting out of here, also. It won't take long for word of what happened here to spread to the higher ups, and I'm sure they wouldn't take too kindly to meeting me again.$b$bI'll sneak out and meet with Ziz. Hopefully, he'll be able to find me a new job!$b$bI'll try and clean up this mess a little, but you should take the ore sample to Ziz right away. He told me that he'd set up camp somewhere on the western side of Windshear Crag. Good luck."},[1093]={t="Super Reaper 6000",lv=21,min=16,nx=1094,ot="Get the Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints for Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",st="Terrible what the Venture Company has done here, eh? What were they thinking? Goblin company hiring a gnome!$b$bLucky for me, Sputtervalve knows a genius when he sees one. Hired me just after I'd been kicked out!$b$bTells me they built some enormous woodcutting machine, and Sput' wants me to steal the plans for him. Unfortunately, Gerenzo--bloody gnome--wants me dead on sight... maybe you could steal the plans for me? You should be able to find them on one of their operators.",how={{"loot",5734,{3988}}}},[1097]={t="Elmore's Task",lv=15,min=9,nx=353,bc=353,ot="Speak with Grimand Elmore.",st="There's a dwarven weaponsmith in Stormwind, Grimand Elmore, who sent word that he needs help with a delivery.  I believe he wants a package sent to his homeland in the north.$B$BYou have a sturdy pair on you!  So if you're interested in some legwork then speak with Grimand.  We could use you down here, but we must also keep our ties strong with the dwarves.$B$BYou can find Grimand Elmore at the weapon shop in the Dwarven District of Stormwind, in the northeast section of town."},[1100]={t="Lonebrow's Journal",lv=34,min=29,nx=1101,si=5790,ot="Read Henrig Lonebrow's Journal.",st="You slowly open the weathered journal of Henrig Lonebrow...."},[1101]={t="The Crone of the Kraul",lv=34,min=29,pre1={1100},ot="Bring Razorflank's Medallion to Falfindel Waywarder in Thalanaar.",st="Poor Heralath! And this dwarf... Lonebrow. What a brave soul he was.$b$bWe must not let their valiance go for naught. This crone... Charlga Razorflank ... must be stopped.$b$bSurely, infiltrating the Kraul will be perilous. There isn't time to send word to Darnassus. $n, assemble a party to slay the crone.$b$bBring me Razorflank's Medallion as proof of demise.",how={{"loot",5792,{4421}}}},[1134]={t="Pridewings of Stonetalon",lv=21,min=18,pre1={1008},ot="Bring 12 Pridewing Venom Sacs to Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar.",st="We are not in open war with the Horde, but our peace is fragile.  We often find their agents moving against us, but they do so covertly.$B$BOne such advance was revealed to us from hidden sources in Theramore, claiming that the orcs collect venom from the pridewings near Mirkfallon Lake, in the Stonetalon Mountains to the south.  Orc assassins then use the venom on their secret death raids against the Alliance!$B$BIf this is true, then we must stop them, $n.  We must deny them their source of venom.",how={{"loot",5808,{4013,4015,4014}}}},[1138]={t="Fruit of the Sea",lv=17,min=15,rwc={[8]=2},ot="Collect 6 Fine Crab Chunks for Gubber Blump in Auberdine.",st="I love crab.  Crabs are the fruit of the sea!  You can bake it, barbecue it, boil it, and broil it.  They're pan fried, deep fried, and stir fried.  There's crab salad, crab soup, crab stew, pepper crab, lemon crab, whipper root crab, and Ironforge surprise crab.  That's... that's about it.$B$BI'm here fishing right now, so I can't get any fine crab chunks.  You can pick them out of reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers.  You can make a lot with it.  You can bake it, barbecue it, boil it...",how={{"loot",12237,{2235,2233}}}},[1140]={t="The Tower of Althalaxx",lv=28,min=13,pre1={973},nx=1167,ot="Free the trapped Highborne souls in Night Run and Satyrnaar, then return to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.",st="The writing of the orcs is little better than the scribblings of a child. Many of my order scoffed when I chose to learn their tongue, but I have found it beneficial to gain further understanding of my enemies.$b$bFrom Ilkrud's scribblings, it appears that Athrikus still possesses two soulgems, and they are being held in Night Run and Satyrnaar, satyr-held areas in northeast Ashenvale.$b$bBe careful out there, $n, the satyrs' blood-soaked temples can be unsettling even for a seasoned $c such as yourself.",how={{"click",19901},{"click",20352}}},[1141]={t="The Family and the Fishing Pole",lv=14,min=10,ot="Catch 6 Darkshore Grouper for Gubber Blump in Auberdine.",st="I love fishing.  The Blump family is known for fishing.  My name is Gubber Blump; I fish.$B$BThere's a kind of fish I like to catch around these parts called Darkshore grouper.  I used to go out on a boat to fish for grouper, but no boats have been going out since them mean ol' murlocs moved in.  I bet they been eating up all the grouper too.$B$BSay, you wanna help me catch Darkshore grouper?  I'd give you a bona fide Blump Family Fishing Pole if you did!  It's a real good pole to catch fish with.",how={{"loot",12238}}},[1142]={t="Mortality Wanes",lv=30,min=25,ot="Find and return Treshala's Pendant to Treshala Fallowbrook in Darnassus.",st="I have not long to live... so... so... weak.$b$b...the b-b-brave dwarf, Lonebrow, has been sent to w-w-warn Falfindel...$b$bBut before I... d-d-die...$b$b...my wife, Treshala... her pendant of bonding to me... stolen... by one of the f-f-foul aggressors...$b$bFind it p-p-please... and return it to Treshala in Darnassus...$b$b...along with w-w-word of my lonely... death.",how={{"loot",5825,{4420,4421,4424}}}},[1144]={t="Willix the Importer",lv=30,min=22,ne=1,ot="Escort Willix the Importer out of Razorfen Kraul.",st="At last, help has arrived!$b$bYou have no clue how long I've been held prisoner here. I can't remember the last time I saw the outside of this place.$b$bYou see, I am an entrepreneur. Always out for a copper, as they say. I caught wind that Mebok Mizzyrix was paying well for Redleaf Tuber from this here pig pen. I figured it would be an easy in, easy out kind of affair. As you can see, I was a bit wrong!$b$bAnyway, if you'd be so kind as to help me get out of here, I'll make it worth your while."},[1167]={t="The Tower of Althalaxx",lv=28,min=13,pre1={1140},nx=1143,ot="Speak with Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx.",st="Before confronting Athrikus, it would probably be wise for you to consult with Balthule. I have no doubt he has been vigilant in his watch of the Tower, and he may have information about recent developments."},[1198]={t="In Search of Thaelrid",lv=24,min=18,nx=1200,ot="Seek out Argent Guard Thaelrid in Blackfathom Deeps.",st="Many rumors circulate these days about the union of the Twilight's Hammer and the naga in Blackfathom Deeps on the coasts of Ashenvale.$b$bMy role here with the Argent Dawn is to collect as much information as I can, so we know when and where help is needed.$b$bIt has been weeks now since I sent a scout to check on the activity at Blackfathom Deeps. Argent Guard Thaelrid has not yet reported back.$b$bMy other scouts are preoccupied with pressing matters.$b$bSeek out and aid Thaelrid for me, $n."},[1199]={t="Twilight Falls",lv=25,min=20,ot="Bring 10 Twilight Pendants to Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus.",st="Empowered by the ancient rites of the chaotic Old Gods the members of the Twilight's Hammer strive to bring about the return of their dark patrons and spread death and terror across the world.$b$bWe believe that the Twilight's Hammer has allied with the naga and are amassing in Blackfathom Deeps on the coast of Ashenvale.$b$bWhatever evil plan brews in the depths of the old temple must be thwarted.$b$bWage war on the Hammer and bring back proof of your deeds. Your efforts will be rewarded handsomely.",how={{"loot",5879,{4809,4810,4811}}}},[1200]={t="Blackfathom Villainy",lv=27,min=18,ot="Bring the head of Twilight Lord Kelris to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus.",st="Strength has left me. Your help is needed!$b$bLong ago this site was a great temple of Elune. But misfortune led to ruin when the corruption of an Old God seeped up from beneath the earth and tainted the sacred Moon Well.$b$bAku'Mai, servant of the Old God, rose from the waters.$b$bThe Twilight's Hammer cultists have allied with the naga to occupy these grounds. The cultists, led by Kelris, sacrifice innocents to Aku'Mai for power.$b$bSlay Kelris and bring his head to Selgorm in Darnassus, $n, please.",how={{"loot",5881,{4832}}}},[1221]={t="Blueleaf Tubers",lv=26,min=20,si=6684,ui={5880},ot="Grab a Crate with Holes.$BGrab a Snufflenose Command Stick.$BGrab and read the Snufflenose Owner's Manual.$B$BIn Razorfen Kraul, use the Crate with Holes to summon a Snufflenose Gopher, and use the Command Stick on the gopher to make it search for Tubers.$B$BBring 6 Blueleaf Tubers, the Snufflenose Command Stick and the Crate with Holes to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",st="Blueleaf tubers are a delicacy around the world!  But they're rare, very rare.  The only place to find them is here in the Barrens, deep in the earth, in Razorfen Kraul.$B$BAnd even then, they're impossible to find unless you know just where to look!  That's why I've trained these snufflenose gophers to find them for me.  They have great noses and can smell a tuber from fifty paces away.$B$BIt won't be easy, but if you get me some tubers I'll pay you handsomely.",how={{"open",5876,{20920}},{"open",5880,{21277}},{"open",5897,{21530}},{"open",6684,{68865}}}},[1275]={t="Researching the Corruption",lv=24,min=18,ot="Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine wants 8 Corrupt Brain stems.",st="Foolish blood elves toil with demonic magic. Have they not witnessed what happened with the naga and with the satyrs of Kalimdor?$b$bI fear that the blood elves will meet a similar deformation. Azeroth cannot afford to give birth to another vile race of monsters.$b$bI wish to study the brain stems of the satyr and naga so that I might deduce what fate the elves are headed toward. In Blackfathom Deeps, on the coast of Ashenvale, you will find both satyr and naga.$b$b'Tis a long journey, $n.",how={{"loot",5952,{4802,4788,4803}}}},[1338]={t="Stormpike's Order",lv=14,min=9,si=5998,ot="Bring Stormpike's Request to Furen Longbeard in Stormwind.",st="There is a dwarven armorsmith whose work I admire greatly.  His name is Furen Longbeard, and his skill is unmatched.  I need a new shield, and I must have one of his!$B$BThe problem is... Furen is far to the south, in the dwarven district within Stormwind.  In human lands!  I can't imagine why he would live there, so far from Ironforge.  The humans must pay him a king's ransom to keep him there!$B$BSo, if you want to travel and don't mind making some money, then will you send Furen my request for a shield?"},[1339]={t="Mountaineer Stormpike's Task",lv=15,min=9,nx=1338,bc=1338,ot="Speak with Mountaineer Stormpike.",st="I hear Mountaineer Stormpike is looking for a runner.  Someone to do a little traveling for him.  How about it?  Are you the $r for the job?$B$BIf so, then you'll find Stormpike at the top of the northern guard tower."},[1442]={t="Seeking the Kor Gem",lv=22,min=20,ot="Bring a Kor Gem to Thundris Windweaver in Darkshore.",st="Greetings, $n. What can I do for one who follows a holy path?$B$BAh, yes, Stilwell, the blacksmith... from long ago. I remember him well, though, I have not heard his name in some time.$B$BHe never struck me as an impudent man, so I can only assume his desire for a Kor gem is noble.$B$BIf you truly wish for one of the gems, then you must head to the northwest of Ashenvale. You will find Blackfathom Deeps there within some ancient ruins. The naga who still use the gems are down below. Do not go alone, $c.",how={{"loot",6995,{4803,4802,4805}}}},[1486]={t="Deviate Hides",lv=17,min=13,ot="Nalpak in the Wailing Caverns wants 20 Deviate Hides.",st="As Naralex descended deeper into his nightmare, a strange breed of beasts arose from beneath the Barrens into the Wailing Caverns.$b$bThese deviate creatures have strange, otherworldly properties. While evil in nature, it is my opinion that some good can come from their existence here in Kalimdor. I believe their hides will be of particular use in the ways of leatherworking.$b$bIf you feel up to the task, venture into the caves below and retrieve some deviate hides.",how={{"loot",6443,{3631,3633,3630}}}},[1487]={t="Deviate Eradication",lv=21,min=15,ot="Ebru in the Wailing Caverns wants you to kill 7 Deviate Ravagers, 7 Deviate Vipers, 7 Deviate Shamblers and 7 Deviate Dreadfangs.",st="Naralex had a noble goal.$b$bOur great leader aspired to enter the Emerald Dream and help regrow these harsh lands back into the lush forest it once was. But something went terribly wrong.$b$bNaralex's dream turned into a nightmare and corrupt creatures began to inhabit the caverns.$b$bWhile some Disciples of Naralex seek to awake our master, my concern is with ridding these caves of the evil beasts.$b$bBrave the caverns, $n, and eradicate the deviate spawn.",how={{"kill",3636},{"kill",5755},{"kill",5761},{"kill",5056}}},[1491]={t="Smart Drinks",lv=18,min=13,pre1={865},ot="Bring 6 portions of Wailing Essence to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",st="Ok, so the raptor horns didn't work so well.  But that's all right -- no one got rich on their first try!  And besides, I think I found something that'll work even better in my smart drinks!$B$BThere is a substance called Wailing Essence, and I think it is the cause of the strange plants and animals in the Barrens.  Get me some and I'll try it in my drink!$B$BI heard the essence gathers in ectoplasmic creatures in the Wailing Caverns to the west.  Hunt those creatures and gather the essence.",how={{"loot",6464,{3638,3640,5763}}}},[1578]={t="Supplying the Front",lv=12,min=1,ot="Bring 6 Copper Axes and 6 Copper Chain Belts to Thorvald in the southern guard tower of Loch Modan",st="The mountaineers of Loch Modan are fighting troggs, and having a busy time of it!  They need constant supplies of new armor and weapons if we're ever to get a handle on those troggs.$B$BThat's why my colleague Thorvald is there, trying to keep the mountaineers in good gear.  So if you were to make some copper axes and copper chain belts and bring them to Thorvald, he would be obliged.  He might even share his knowledge with you.$B$BThorvald is in Loch Modan's southern guard tower.",how={{"loot",2845},{"loot",2851}}},[1579]={t="Gaffer Jacks",lv=12,min=10,nx=1580,ot="Bring 8 Gaffer Jacks to Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine.",st="I came to Auberdine because of the quiet.  I want to invent my inventions where it's quiet, because after a night of drinking I don't like all the noise of Ironforge!$B$BSo I took a ship to Auberdine and had a little too much to drink on the way.  I dropped my box of gaffer jacks overboard!  I need my gaffer jacks!$B$BI don't know exactly where I dropped them, but if you fish for them in the ocean you might get lucky...",how={{"loot",6717}}},[1580]={t="Electropellers",lv=12,min=10,pre1={1579},ot="Bring 12 Electropellers to Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine.",st="We know you're lucky, but... just how lucky are you, $n?$B$BOne night I was wandering the roads of Darkshore.  I was looking for a good river or lake to try my new self-propelled, exploding duck decoy and I think I was a little tipsy... because I passed out and awoke hours later in Auberdine.  My hair was singed and my bag of electropellers was gone!  I must have dropped them in the water!$B$BI need those electropellers!  Maybe you can fish them out of some lake or stream in Darkshore...",how={{"loot",6718}}},[1581]={t="Elixirs for the Bladeleafs",lv=8,min=4,ot="Bring 6 Elixirs of Lion's Strength and 2 Elixirs of Minor Defense to Syral Bladeleaf in Dolanaar.",st="Our herb and alchemy shop is booming, but my husband spends so much time mixing potions that we never have time for each other.$B$BCan you help us?$B$BIf you can bring me a supply of pre-made elixirs, then I would be happy to trade with you.  I have some rare herbs that you might find useful.",how={{"loot",2454},{"loot",5997}}},[1598]={t="The Stolen Tome",lv=4,min=1,ex={1599},ot="Retrieve the Powers of the Void for Drusilla La Salle.",st="You there! $n, right?$b$bI hope you're sure about becoming a warlock, because if you can't hold your own, you're likely to get pulled under.$b$bI'm to teach you, but I need to make sure you're strong enough first.$b$bThere was a novice studying at the Abbey who ran off to join the Defias Brotherhood. Why do I care? Well, he stole some important books.$b$bOne of those happens to be a book I've wanted for myself, the Powers of the Void. Steal it for me, they have it hidden at their tent in the Vineyards.",how={{"open",6785,{83763}}}},[1599]={t="Beginnings",lv=4,min=1,ex={1598},ot="Bring 3 Feather Charms to Alamar Grimm in Anvilmar.",st="You must be the new warlock everyone's been whispering about. Must be someone's taken a liking to you if they've asked me to take time away from my research to start your training.$b$bDon't worry, I won't hold it against you.$b$bThe simplest of the summoning spells you will learn is that of the imp. Before I impart this to you, however, you must prove that you have the necessary magical and physical ability.$b$bBring me three feather charms from the frostmane novices from the cave to the southwest.",how={{"loot",6753,{946}}}},[1618]={t="Gearing Redridge",lv=16,min=1,ot="Tormus Deepforge  wants you to bring 4 Runed Copper Belts and 4 Heavy Copper Mauls to Verner Osgood in Redridge.",st="We dwarves aren't the only ones fighting.  Our human allies have their hands full too!$B$BRedridge is under periodic attack from blackrock orcs, and their supply of equipment is always low.  If you were to help them out, I'm sure their resident blacksmith, Verner Osgood, would teach you a trick or two.",how={{"loot",2857},{"loot",6214}}},[1638]={t="A Warrior's Training",lv=10,min=10,ex={1678,1683,1639},ot="Speak with Harry Burlguard.",st="You've shown yourself to be a competent warrior, $n.  But you're still young and have a lot to learn.$B$BSpeak with Harry Burlguard--he's usually in the Pig and Whistle tavern, in the Old Town of Stormwind.  Harry is an old veteran and a good teacher.  He can show you a few moves that'll keep you breathing longer."},[1639]={t="Bartleby the Drunk",lv=10,min=10,ex={1678,1683},nx=1640,ot="Speak with Bartleby.",st="Yeah, I can teach you.  But first I wanna see what moves you have already.$B$BSee that drunk over there at the end of the bar?  Bartleby?  I want you to get his mug.$B$BHah, and if you know Bartleby then you know he won't just give it to you."},[1640]={t="Beat Bartleby",lv=10,min=10,pre1={1639,1678,1683},nx=1665,ne=1,ot="Beat Bartleby, then talk to him.",st="You want what??  You're crazy!$B$BThe only way you'll get this mug is if you pry it from my cold, dead fingers...",how={{"talk",6090}}},[1641]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre={2998},nx=1642},[1642]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre={1641},nx=1643,ot="Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.",st="In all things, a paladin must reflect the Light which supplements our strength. To strive to be divine for one of our kind does not mean we strive for godhood--we strive to be good in all actions.$B$BAlthough called upon to smite evil in these harsh times, you must always remember that it's aiding others that will truly set you apart from the citizens of Azeroth. Compassion, patience, bravery--these things mean as much to a paladin as strength in battle.$B$BKnow this well, and never forget it."},[1643]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre1={1642},nx=1644,ot="Search the Trade District of Stormwind for Stephanie Turner.",st="Your task then, $n, is to find someone here in Stormwind that is in need of aid. Someone who is pure of heart and motive. Perhaps someone helping others. Perhaps someone in need of a guide. Regardless, the person must have noble intent and be relying on your kindness.$B$BDo this, and return to me when you are finished. Then, we shall discuss more of your path and what it means to be a paladin of the Light."},[1644]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1643},nx=1780,ot="Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Stephanie Turner in Stormwind.",st="Bless their hearts, most of them have no families because of the Scourge attacks in the last decade.$B$BMy husband John collects the materials for me to make the shirts and pants for the children, but I haven't even had time to do that. I've been too focused on keeping food on their plates, and a roof over their heads.$B$BWhat's that? You'd be willing to help? Oh, thank the Light, and thank you, $n.$B$BIf you could bring me some linen cloth so I can sew clothes for the kids, that would help me out so much.",how={{"open",2589,{106318,106319,2039}}}},[1645]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre={2999},nx=1646},[1646]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre={1645},nx=1647,ot="Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.",st="In all things, a paladin must reflect the Light which supplements our strength. To strive to be divine for one of our kind does not mean we strive for godhood--we strive to be good in all actions.$B$BAlthough called upon to smite evil in these harsh times, you must always remember that it's aiding others that will truly set you apart from the citizens of Azeroth. Compassion, patience, bravery--these things mean as much to a paladin as strength in battle.$B$BKnow this well, and never forget it."},[1647]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre1={1646},nx=1648,ot="Search the outer ring of Ironforge for John Turner.",st="Your task then, $n, is to find someone here in Ironforge that is in need of aid. Someone who is pure of heart and motive. Perhaps someone helping others. Perhaps someone in need of a guide. Regardless, the person must have noble intent and be relying on your kindness.$B$BDo this, and return to me when you are finished. Then, we shall discuss more of your path and what it means to be a paladin of the Light. I will remain here in the temple for your return. Other paladins will need my guidance also."},[1648]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1647},nx=1778,ot="Bring 10 Linen Cloth to John Turner in Ironforge.",st="My wife and I run an orphanage in Stormwind, mostly for children who have lost parents due to the attacks by the Scourge in the last decade. I come to Ironforge every month or so to see about collecting more supplies from the citizens here, and talk to the various groups to see if they can do anything to help.$B$BThis trip's been agonizingly slow, and not very productive.$B$BIf I could just get some more linen for my wife to make some clothes, I could finally send a shipment home.",how={{"open",2589,{106318,106319,2039}}}},[1649]={t="The Tome of Valor",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1793,1794},nx=1650,ot="Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.",st="Valor, and all the virtues that go along with it, are like rare minerals: you must cherish them when you find them because of their value, but you must also take time to harvest them... refine them. When mixed together properly, a strong alloy is formed, sometimes unbreakable by even the most powerful blows.$B$BThis strength, your faith, your bravery, must be tested. You must learn to never lose faith and realize that with the power of the Light, you can overcome things that most others cannot."},[1650]={t="The Tome of Valor",lv=23,min=20,pre1={1649},nx=1651,ot="Find Daphne Stilwell in Westfall.",st="Good! Your lack of hesitation is a sure sign that you are prepared and eager to test yourself. So be it.$B$BAt the very ends of Westfall's Longshore, a small house overlooks the ocean. There, a couple lives, the Stilwells. Jordan is an incredible smith, and he's gone to Ironforge to meet with the dwarves for a while. But this has left Daphne, his wife, alone and unprotected.$B$BReports suggest that the Defias have all but taken over the area, Daphne may need some protection from the villains. Go there."},[1651]={t="The Tome of Valor",lv=25,min=20,pre1={1650},nx=1652,ne=1,ot="Defend Daphne Stilwell from the Defias attack.$B$BNeither of your spirits must be released from their mortal coils if you wish to succeed.$B$BAfter you are successful, speak to Daphne Stilwell again.",st="Now, they'll be coming again soon, I'd wager, so get yourself ready.$B$BI've got myself a gun in the house. I'll grab it and be ready to help you out, but for the most part, you're on your own.$B$BI've no idea how many they'll send, but I'm sure it'll be more than the few they sent earlier.$B$BAsk the Light for whatever blessings you can because... did you hear that? I think they're coming.$B$BWe make our stand near the house!"},[1652]={t="The Tome of Valor",lv=25,min=20,pre1={1651},nx=1653,ot="Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.",st="Please, return to Duthorian and let him know that I'm safe for now. I have you and the Church to thank for that.$B$BHe'll send word to Ironforge to let my Jordan know that he has nothing to fear.$B$BOh, how I miss my husband. I can't wait till he returns."},[1653]={t="The Test of Righteousness",lv=21,min=20,pre1={1652},nx=1654,ot="Speak to Jordan Stilwell in Ironforge",st="Actually, I have no doubt that Jordan himself would like to thank you, and seeing as I need a messenger to send word that his wife is safe, I think you'd be a perfect choice.$B$BJordan was to be a paladin of the Light before his dedication to his father's craft took him on another path--he's intimately familiar with our way of life and is considered among our most faithful.$B$BHe should still be in Ironforge--he likes to work outside the gates during the day, something about the cool mountain air."},[1654]={t="The Test of Righteousness",lv=22,min=20,pre1={1653},nx=1806,si=6996,ot="Using Jordan's Weapon Notes, find some Whitestone Oak Lumber, Bailor's Refined Ore Shipment, Jordan's Smithing Hammer, and a Kor Gem, and return them to Jordan Stilwell in Ironforge.",st="I'd like to reward you if you'd be willing to accept such a thing? Don't misunderstand me, my generosity is dependent on how much help you can be, but I see us both benefiting greatly from such an alliance.$B$BI will craft for you a weapon worthy of what you've accomplished, a symbol of paladinhood and the Light, but you must gather the items I need to craft it. I've already started taking notes on the items, it just requires someone brave and skilled enough to recover them. What do you say, $c?",how={{"loot",6994,{641}},{"loot",6993,{6241}},{"open",6895,{91138}},{"loot",7083,{3649}}}},[1665]={t="Bartleby's Mug",lv=10,min=10,pre1={1640},nx=1666,si=6781,ot="Bring Bartleby's Mug to Burlguard",st="Ok, here's my mug.  Wait!  Let me finish what's in it first... there we go."},[1680]={t="Tormus Deepforge",lv=11,min=10,pre1={1683,1678,1639},nx=1681,bc=1681,ot="Speak with Tormus Deepforge.",st="Now that you've learned some moves, it's time to get you a decent weapon.  Speak with Tormus Deepforge.  He can make you a weapon I'm sure you'll like.$B$BYou'll find Tormus here in Ironforge, at the Great Forge."},[1683]={t="Vorlus Vilehoof",lv=10,min=10,ex={1639,1678},nx=1686,ot="Bring the Horn of Vorlus to Elanaria in Darnassus.",st="Before I can teach you, you must show me your resolve.$B$BThe satyr Vorlus Vilehoof has found one of our remote moonwells, southeast of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.  He now splashes within it, defiling its pure waters with his filth.$B$BFind Vorlus at the moonwell and destroy him.  Bring me his horn as proof and I will begin your advanced training as a warrior.$B$BThe path to the moonwell is hidden well, $n, but stay focused and alert and you will find it.",how={{"loot",6805,{6128}}}},[1684]={t="Elanaria",lv=10,min=10,ex={1639,1678,1683},ot="Speak with Elanaria.",st="Greetings, warrior.  Your skill grows, but there is more to your profession than you may believe.  To further progress, you must soon find a teacher.$B$BThe warrior Elanaria dwells in Darnassus, at the Warrior's Terrace.  She can instruct you."},[1685]={t="Gakin's Summons",lv=10,min=10,nx=1688,bc=1688,ot="Report to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.",st="Isn't that how it always works? Was looking for you all day and couldn't find you, now when I'm not expecting it, you come and walk right up to me.$b$bI've wasted enough time trying to find you, so I won't delay you any longer. Master Gakin's summoned you for additional training. Seems to me you should seek him out as soon as possible.$b$bYou'll find him in the basement of the Slaughtered Lamb tavern. By the way, you might want to keep that particular location quiet. Don't want word spreading about it."},[1688]={t="Surena Caledon",lv=10,min=10,nx=1689,ot="Retrieve Surena's Choker for Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind.",st="I had a student named Surena Caledon. She stood where you stand now, eager to learn of warlock magic, and possessing no small bit of talent. More than that she was young and pleasing to the eye. Had I seen it then, the traitorous trollop!$b$bThe thieving wench ran off with one of the Defias, Erlan Drudgemoor. While her loss is of little importance, I gifted her a bloodstone choker that I must have.$b$bHer life means nothing to me now. You will find her at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch. Retrieve what is mine.",how={{"loot",6810,{881}}}},[1689]={t="The Binding",lv=10,min=10,pre1={1688},si=6928,ot="Using the Bloodstone Choker, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Bloodstone Choker to Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind.",st="By retrieving my choker and besting Surena, you've proven that you're at least as capable as she was.$b$bWith that said, I can tell you're direly in need of training. You can manage the flows of magic, yes, but being a warlock is much more than that.$b$bI will show you how to command a voidwalker, but before I can, you must call one forth at a summoning circle and subdue it using whatever weapons--physical and magical--you have at your disposal. Use the magic of this choker at the summoning circle below.",how={{"kill",5676}}},[1699]={t="The Rethban Gauntlet",lv=22,min=20,nx=1702,ot="Enter the Rethban Caverns, reach the first fork, and return to Yorus Barleybrew within the time allowed.$B$BYou must not die and release your spirit.",st="I call my challenge the Rethban Gauntlet.  To pass the trial, all you must do is enter the Rethban Caverns, to the first fork, then return here.  Easy!  Except there are a few wrinkles...$B$BYou have to return within an hour.$B$BThere are whole heaps of Redridge Gnolls in the way.$B$BBefore you start, you have to take a swig of my family's signature drink: Barleybrew Scalder!$B$BSo what do you say?  The Rethban Caverns are in the foothills north of Lakeshire.  Are you ready to run the Rethban Gauntlet?"},[1701]={t="Fire Hardened Mail",lv=28,min=20,pre1={1702},nx=1782,si=6842,ot="Gather the materials Furen Longbeard requires, and bring them to him in Stormwind.",st="So I gave you a nice shield, but we don't have to stop there.  I know the secrets to make extremely hard mail armor.  It's not easy and it takes very rare materials, but if you're willing to do the legwork then I'll make a piece for you.$B$BWhat do you say, $n?  If you're up for the challenge, then I'll give you a list of what to get and where to get them.",how={{"loot",6838,{4040,1111,211967}},{"loot",6839,{4031,4032}},{"loot",6840,{6167}},{"loot",6841,{6168}}}},[1702]={t="The Shieldsmith",lv=22,min=20,pre1={1699},nx=1701,si=6843,ot="Bring the Cask of Scalder to Furen Longbeard.",st="You really showed what you were made of when you ran the Rethban Gauntlet, $n.  And I'm true to my word.  I'll get you the reward I promised...$B$BExcept it's in Stormwind.$B$BTalk to my friend, Furen Longbeard, in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.  He's the best shieldsmith you'll ever meet, and he owes me a big favor.$B$BHere, take Furen this cask of Barleybrew Scalder and ask him for a shield.  He'll give you a nice one."},[1716]={t="Devourer of Souls",lv=20,min=20,nx=1738,ot="Speak with Takar the Seer in the Barrens.",st="A sayaad is a devourer of souls, dominator of wills, and tempter of hearts. It knows nothing but evil.\r\n\r\nSalacious tales refer to the demon by its common name: succubus for females, incubus for males.\r\n\r\nA stimulus is required to beckon the creature. With a symbol of love as bait, it will surely answer your call. Defeat it, and make it your tool.\r\n\r\nIt will be hard to find a thing of this nature, though. You should speak with Takar the Seer. You will find him in the Barrens of Kalimdor near Camp Taurajo."},[1738]={t="Heartswood",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1716},nx=1739,ot="Retrieve the Heartswood from Ashenvale and bring it to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.",st="In preparation for your coming, I used my sight to look over the world and through the mists of time. I have found what it is you seek.$b$bIn the War of the Ancients, two lovers fell together in battle. Where they took their last breaths, a tree known as the heartswood grew, a symbol of their undying love.$b$bThat should be enough to tempt a succubus. You will find it in the ruins of Ordil'Aran in the northwestern part of the forest of Ashenvale.",how={{"open",6912,{93192}}}},[1739]={t="The Binding",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1738},si=6913,ui={190186},ot="Using the Heartswood Core, summon and subdue a succubus, then return the Heartswood Core to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Slaughtered Lamb.",st="Using the heartswood core, you will be able to cast a spell at the summoning circle in the crypt below to open a portal for the succubus to pass through.$b$bBe careful, $n, succubi have overrun even the strongest of minds.$b$bOnce you have bested and returned it to the void, return to me and I will show you how to call and control it.",how={{"kill",5677}}},[1740]={t="The Orb of Soran'ruk",lv=25,min=20,ot="Find 3 Soran'ruk Fragments and 1 Large Soran'ruk Fragment and return them to Doan Karhan in the Barrens.",st="When demons of the Legion fall out of favor, their spirits are imprisoned within orbs and distributed to their mages and warlocks.$b$bMany were carried by their servants in Azeroth. Even fragmented, they still possess the powers of the demons trapped inside.$b$bThe orb of Soran'ruk was broken into two pieces, one was further broken to be used by the acolytes of the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. The other, larger piece, was possessed by a wizard in Shadowfang Keep. Find them and I can reform it.",how={{"loot",6914,{4809}},{"loot",6915,{3855}}}},[1778]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1648},nx=1779,ot="Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.",st="I'm going to see about making plans to return home soon. Hopefully, Stephanie is doing well back in Stormwind. I can't wait to see her again. Till next we meet, $c."},[1779]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1778},nx=1783,si=6866,ot="Take the Symbol of Life and speak to Muiredon Battleforge in Ironforge.",st="I want you to take this, $n. It is called the Symbol of Life.$B$BYou've proven charitable and patient, and now I want you to prove just how adept you've become in both combat, and power.$B$BMy husband Muiredon returned recently from an encounter with some Dark Iron dwarves, and he barely escaped with his life--he's over there having his wounds healed by one of our priests.$B$BTake the Symbol and speak to him. If you can help him, then we will speak again soon. May the Light shine upon you."},[1780]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1644},nx=1781,ot="Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.",st="I'll take these to the children this very day. Please be safe, good $c. It is not often $G men:women; of your character show their faces in the city, but you've proven that the paladins here in Stormwind shall never turn their backs on those in need.$B$BFarewell."},[1781]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1780},nx=1786,si=6866,ot="Take the Symbol of Life to Gazin Tenorm in Stormwind.",st="Take this, $n. It is called the Symbol of Life.$B$BYou've proven charitable and patient, and now the time has come to see if you're powerful enough to focus one of the Light's greatest gifts.$B$BMy friend Gazin returned recently from an encounter with some Defias in Elwynn near Heroes' Vigil--he barely escaped with his life. He's near the altar having his wounds healed by our priests.$B$BTake the Symbol and speak to him. If you can help him, then we will speak again soon. May you bask in the Light's glory."},[1783]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1779},nx=1784,ot="Take the Symbol of Life and resurrect Narm Faulk in Dun Morogh.",st="We was spyin' on some of the Dark Iron dwarves that've bunkered down south of Helm's Bed Lake. We knew they was up to no good, so Narm an' me thought we'd take a closer look--got ta see their leader given orders to some o' his men.$B$BNarm an' me took the chance to kill a few of 'em, but they proved tougher than we thought, an' more of 'em got the jump on us. Narm tol' me to run an' get support, so 'ere I am.$B$BNarm needs help, an' I'll not rest till he gets it.$B$BC'n ya help, $n?"},[1784]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1783},nx=1785,si=6866,ot="Retrieve a Dark Iron Script from the Dark Iron dwarves near Helm's Bed, and return to Muiredon Battleforge in Ironforge.",st="Before I fell in battle, Muiredon and I had almost defeated one of the Dark Iron spies near that small house. We witnessed their captain passing orders to them, and sought to kill him and take the orders.$B$BSome of the council in Ironforge do not yet believe the presence of Dark Iron dwarves exists in Dun Morogh. By attaining one of those scripts, we'll not only have proof of their movements, but possibly an idea of what they're planning.$B$BGet one of those scripts and take it back to Muiredon, $n.",how={{"loot",6847,{6123}}}},[1785]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1784},ot="Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.",st="I c'n see me wife's o'er there beamin' wit pride already. Ya better get yer tuchus o'er there pronto. I be thinkin' she'd have some words wit ya.$B$BLight be witcha, mighty $c. I'll be lookin' fer ya on the battlefield against the Scourge and dem Dark Irons when the time comes."},[1786]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1781},nx=1787,si=6866,ot="Take the Symbol of Life and resurrect Henze Faulk in Elwynn.",st="Henze and I had made it to Heroes' Vigil, an island in the middle of Stone Cairn Lake in northeastern Elwynn. We'd heard the Defias had infiltrated our borders and we wanted proof to take to the king's advisors.$B$BWe caught sight of a couple of the scum going over some documents, and we attacked. Unfortunately, we were quickly overwhelmed by more of the mages.$B$BHenze held them off for me while I escaped... the daft fool, going and being brave.$B$BHe's out there now, Henze is. Can you help us, $n?"},[1787]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1786},nx=1788,ot="Retrieve a Defias Script from the Defias Rogue Wizards in Elwynn, and return to Gazin Tenorm in Stormwind.",st="We'll have time to talk more about the Symbol at a later time. What's important now is to get those papers we saw the Defias going over. If we can get our hands on them, we'll be able to prove the Defias have infiltrated Elwynn and hopefully gain some insight into what their plans are.$B$BI'm in no shape for battle as of now, $n. Do you think you're strong enough to get those papers from the Defias here on the island?$B$BIf you're able to get them, bring them back to Gazin and let him know I'm all right.",how={{"loot",6846,{474,6866}}}},[1788]={t="The Tome of Divinity",lv=13,min=12,pre1={1787},ot="Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.",st="I'll take the script to the King's advisors after Duthorian's taken a look at them, but in the meantime, you should go speak to Duthorian now. He'll be wanting to pat you on the back for sure!$B$BThank you again, $n. I hope we meet again. You're surely an ally I'm proud to call friend."},[1793]={t="The Tome of Valor",lv=20,min=20,nx=1649},[1860]={t="Speak with Jennea",lv=10,min=10,ex={1880},nx=1861,bc=1861,ot="Speak with Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.",st="We mages have a task that needs doing.  One that is vital to the safety of Stormwind and Elwynn forest.$B$BJennea Cannon has the details.  She studies in the wizard's sanctum, in the mage district of Stormwind.  You should make your way to her with haste."},[1879]={t="Speak with Bink",lv=10,min=10,ex={1861},nx=1880,bc=1880,ot="Speak with Bink in Ironforge.",st="$n!  Bink, my gnome colleague in Ironforge, sends word.  She has a task that needs doing and won't rely on anyone but a mage to do it!  Are you that mage, $n?$B$BIf so, then speak with Bink.  She spends her time in the Hall of Mysteries in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge."},[1919]={t="Report to Jennea",lv=15,min=15,nx=1920,bc=1920,ot="Speak with Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.",st="Your knowledge of the craft grows, young $n.  Are you now ready to begin your true lessons?  Are you ready to take your place in the secret war we wage?$B$BIf so, then speak with Jennea Cannon, in the wizard's sanctum in the mage district of Stormwind.  She has a task for you which will open your first window into the invisible world."},[1920]={t="Investigate the Blue Recluse",lv=16,min=15,nx=1921,ot="Obtain a Cantation of Manifestation and a Chest of Containment coffers from behind Jennea Cannon.  Bring 3 Filled Containment Coffers to Jennea at the Wizard's Sanctum.",st="A disturbance has been reported at the Blue Recluse tavern in the Mage Quarter.  Strange, invisible creatures now wander the tavern, and I fear a mana rift has formed there.$B$BI want you to investigate the tavern and capture those creatures.  Use the cantation of manifestation in the tavern to make the creatures visible, subdue them then use a containment coffer to capture them.  When you have enough, return to me with your filled coffers, your empty coffers and the cantation.",how={{"open",7292,{103574}},{"open",7247,{105174}},{"open",7308,{105175}}}},[2038]={t="Bingles' Missing Supplies",lv=15,min=12,ot="Find and return Bingles' supplies:$B$BBingles' Wrench, Bingles' Screwdriver, Bingles' Hammer, and Bingles' Blastencapper.",st="As if crashing into the Loch wasn't bad enough, troggs from the nearby island attacked me and stole my tools and special Blastenheimer Blastencapper explosives. With no gyrocopter and no explosives, the movement has no chance!$B$BGet my tools back and find my Blastencapper explosives, $n. For Gnomeregan!",how={{"open",7343,{104564}},{"open",7345,{104569}},{"open",7346,{104574}},{"open",7376,{104575}}}},[2039]={t="Find Bingles",lv=15,min=12,nx=2038,bc=2038,ot="Find Bingles Blastenheimer in Loch Modan.",st="We've lost contact with Bingles! He was sent on a reconnaissance mission over Gnomeregan and hasn't reported back in over a week. I just know he's gone and blown himself up.$B$BHe was last seen flying over the Loch. Perhaps you can investigate, $n."},[2040]={t="Underground Assault",lv=20,min=15,ot="Retrieve the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket from the Deadmines and return it to Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind.",st="Gnomeregan has fallen under the control of those dastardly troggs! The situation is grave but perhaps you can help, $n.$B$BDeep in the Deadmines is a functional goblin shredder. Find that shredder and bring back the intact power supply. With the shredder's power supply, we can give our gyrodrillmatic excavationators the power they need to break through the rocky underground borders of Gnomeregan, opening the way for a gnomish assault!",how={{"loot",7365,{642}}}},[2041]={t="Speak with Shoni",lv=15,min=15,nx=2040,bc=2040,ot="Speak with Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind.",st="Perhaps... Perhaps you can help us in the battle for Gnomeregan.$B$BIn Stormwind you will find the commander of our underground assault crew, Shoni the Shilent. Shoni needs assistance with her gyrodrillmatic excavationators.$B$BYou will probably find her amongst the dwarves in Stormwind.$B$BGood luck, $n."},[2078]={t="Gyromast's Revenge",lv=20,min=14,pre1={2098},si=7442,ot="Find Gelkak's First Mate, the Threshwackonator 4100, and lead it back to Gelkak.",st="Landlubber, ye needs to find me first mate.$B$BTake this'n key, puts it in his gulliver an' bring him back here to serve the Cap'n.$B$BThem murlocs an' their chief ain't gonna be too happy once me first mate gets a hold of em!",how={{"talk",6669}}},[2098]={t="Gyromast's Retrieval",lv=20,min=14,nx=2078,ot="Find and return the three pieces of Gelkak's Key to Gelkak Gyromast.",st="A pirate's life ain't an easy one, landlubber. It ain't all about plunderin' and booze! Alas, me ship be sunk just off shore thanks to them pesky Threshadons.$B$BWhat I be needin' is me first mate back in workin' order!$B$BWhen I washed up'n shore, the key for me first mate broke on the rocks and was pilfered by the beasties of Darkshore. Out of the corner of me eyes I saw some of them Ragin' Crawlers, Ferocious Foreststrider, and murloc rummaging through the wreckage....",how={{"loot",7498,{2323}},{"loot",7499,{2207,2208,2205}},{"loot",7500,{2236,2233}}}},[2118]={t="Plagued Lands",lv=14,min=10,nx=2138,si=7586,ot="Capture a living Rabid Thistle Bear and bring it back to Tharnariun.$B$BShould you fail to capture a Rabid Thistle Bear and lose your trap, return to Tharnariun Treetender and request another trap.",st="A sickness spreads across the Darkshore, gripping the minds and bodies of all it touches.$B$BThe Thistle Bears have been hit the hardest by this plague. The once noble beasts are now an instrument of destruction - rabid and frenzied. I may have a cure for this ailment.$B$BTake this trap to the forest and lay it on the ground. Any Rabid Thistle Bear that crosses the light shall become docile for a short time. Once the bear is docile, it shall follow you. Lead it back here, $n.",how={{"kill",2164}}},[2138]={t="Cleansing of the Infected",lv=16,min=10,pre1={2118},nx=2139,ot="Cleanse the forest of 20 Rabid Thistle Bears and return to Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore.",st="As I had feared, the cure does not work.$B$BIt saddens me greatly to order the death of any of nature's beasts, but the sick and tainted thistle bears must be put down.$B$BReturn to the forest and destroy 20 rabid thistle bears, $n. It will most certainly not put a stop to the plague but it will slow down the damage the animals are doing to our forest and its inhabitants for a short time.",how={{"kill",2164}}},[2139]={t="Tharnariun's Hope",lv=18,min=10,pre1={2138},rwc={[8]=1},ot="Find and kill the Den Mother.",st="The survival of our people and lands comes at unfortunate costs, $n.\r\n\r\nYou have spilled the blood of nature's servants; many sick animals you have felled. The people of Auberdine are indebted to you, for the forest's pain is eased--even if only for a moment.\r\n\r\nI have one final task for you, but be warned, you will have to kill again. It is my hope that this will be the last time I call upon you, $n.\r\n\r\nIn a cave to the northeast, near Bashal'Aran, resides the Den Mother. Slay her.",how={{"kill",6788}}},[2158]={t="Rest and Relaxation",lv=5,min=1,rwc={[1]=1,[2]=2,[3]=2,[4]=1,[5]=2,[8]=2,[9]=2},ot="Speak with Innkeeper Farley at the Lion's Pride Inn.",st="Every adventurer should rest when exhaustion sets in - and there is no finer place to get rest and relaxation than at the Lion's Pride Inn!$B$BMy best friend, Innkeeper Farley, runs the Lion's Pride. If you tell him I sent you, he may give you the special discounted rates on food and drink.$B$BTo find the Lion's Pride Inn, travel south along the road from here -- you can't miss it!"},[2159]={t="Dolanaar Delivery",lv=5,min=1,rwc={[3]=2},si=7627,ot="Bring the Dolanaar Delivery to Innkeeper Keldamyr.",st="Greetings, young $c.  Can you offer me aid?  I have a package of herbs that I must deliver to the town of Dolanaar.  But I still have business with the druids of Shadowglen and cannot yet leave.$B$BCan you deliver this package for me?  It must be sent to Innkeeper Keldamyr, at the Dolanaar inn.  It lies along the road, to the south."},[2160]={t="Supplies to Tannok",lv=5,min=1,rwc={[1]=1,[2]=2,[3]=2,[4]=1,[5]=2,[7]=2,[8]=2,[9]=2},si=7646,ot="Deliver the Crate of Inn Supplies to Tannok Frosthammer in Kharanos.",st="Hey! You look like a hearty adventurer. If you're planning on braving the pass, do you suppose you could bring a package to the inn in Kharanos?$b$bYou were planning on stopping at the inn, right? If you make it through the pass, you'll definitely want to take a breather there.$b$bAnyways, bring this to Tannok Frosthammer, the innkeeper's assistant. I can't get through the pass myself, and it'll be days until a Mountaineer escort comes through!"},[2178]={t="Easy Strider Living",lv=12,min=9,ot="Bring back 5 Strider Meat to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine.",st="Do you smell that delicious aroma? It's my secret recipe, $n--fresh strider stew. Delicious!$B$BPerhaps you would be interested in learning the recipe?$B$BBefore I teach you the recipe, you will need to prove that you can handle the beasts.$B$BNow, I don't expect you to go out and tame one and ride it back to me, but if you can kill a few and bring back some of their succulent meat, I may be persuaded to show you the ways of strider stew.",how={{"loot",5469,{2321}}}},[2205]={t="Seek out SI: 7",lv=10,min=10,nx=2206,si=7674,ot="Deliver Keryn Sylvius's package to Master Mathias Shaw at the Stormwind Barracks.",st="The badge? Oh, it's nothing, fish - nothing you could handle anyhow. By the looks of you, I'd say Mathias is likely to mistake you for the cheese delivery $g boy:girl; instead of a proper rogue. Regardless, I've been assigned a job and I've made a promise to deliver on that job.$B$BSpeaking of which, deliver this package to Mathias and he may give you a small task or two.$B$BGet cracking."},[2218]={t="Road to Salvation",lv=10,min=10,nx=2238,ot="Speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge.",st="Another lost soul looking for guidance, eh? I suppose you want to find a purpose - your purpose. I've seen it a thousand times, another hero looking for work.$B$BWell, today's your lucky day, friend. Hogral's got the cure for your ailment.$B$BHere's what you do: Take this road here up to Ironforge and make your way to the Forlorn Cavern. Once there, locate the thieves' guild and speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard. He'll put you on the road to salvation."},[2241]={t="The Apple Falls",lv=10,min=10,nx=2242,si=7735,ot="Take Jannok's Rose to Syurna in Darnassus.",st="They say I'm 'lovestruck,' whatever that means.$B$BSure, I spend my every waking moment thinking about Syurna. Sure, my home is full of paintings and drawings of Syurna. Sure, I often go days without eating, sleeping, or drinking, while I lament about the love we could have had. Is that so wrong?$B$BNow she won't see me! ME! I've tried sending her messages but she won't even talk to another person unless they are a rogue.$B$BCould you deliver this flower to her? Don't forget to tell her it's from Jannok."},[2242]={t="Destiny Calls",lv=10,min=10,pre1={2241},ot="Find Sethir the Ancient and bring back any clues that you may discover to Syurna.",st="We believe there is one being that may be able to help us understand what is happening to the forests of Teldrassil. Unfortunately, getting the creature to cooperate has proven disastrous.$B$BHe hides on a branch at the outskirts of the Oracle Glade. All who have so far approached the satyr, whether through force or diplomacy, have met with doom. Perhaps stealth is the answer, $n.$B$BFind what Sethir the Ancient carries in his packs and report back to me.",how={{"loot",7737,{6909}}}},[2281]={t="Redridge Rendezvous",lv=16,min=16,nx=2282,ot="Venture forth to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains and speak with Lucius.",st="Sending you out in the field now would be suicide. Renzik doesn't need another dead rogue on his hands. Don't fret, though, $n - Renzik is going to get you up to speed.$B$BMake your way to the Redridge Mountains and speak with an associate of SI:7 named Lucius. You will find him hanging around the docks of Lakeshire with the other shady good-for-nothings."},[2282]={t="Alther's Mill",lv=20,min=16,pre1={2281},si=5060,ot="Open Lucius's Lockbox, recover the Token of Thievery and return it to Lucius in Lakeshire.",st="We've been training thieves here for years! After all, not every rapscallion is born with the grace and finesse of old Lucius.$B$BUp off the road here you'll find Alther's Mill. I got a chest up there with something important inside. Go get it for me! Bring back that token and you'll receive your Certificate of Thievery!",how={{"open",7871,{121264}}}},[2298]={t="Kingly Shakedown",lv=16,min=16,ot="Travel to Stormwind and seek out Renzik \"The Shiv.\"",st="So there we were, about to start plottin' out phase III when a couple o' Magni's blockheads come bargin' in here talkin' bout some kind o' heist and arresting some o' the Hidden Circle.$B$BWell nobody puts the iron on old Blackbeard! The argumentations got heavy and thick and somehow yer name weres blurted out!$B$BMe advice? Take the first Gryphon out o' Ironforge and get to Stormwind. Get yerself to Old Town and once there, talk to an old friend o' mine named Renzik \"The Shiv.\""},[2359]={t="Klaven's Tower",lv=24,min=20,pre1={2360},nx=2607,si=8046,ot="Steal the Defias Tower Key, break into the Defias Tower and uncover the contents of the Duskwood Chest. Take whatever information you find back to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind. Read Kearnen's Journal to gain insight about the tower.",st="I've been staking out this tower for weeks, $n. Recently a major shipment came through from Duskwood, and along with it came those guards.$B$BWhat are they? Your guess is as good as mine. I can tell you one thing - they aren't human.$B$BAnyhow, the shipment had a chest - which is what I assume those abominations are guarding. The zombie with the spikes holds a key we'll need.$B$BGet that key, get in the tower, and uncover whatever is in that chest. Take your findings back to Mathias.",how={{"open",7908,{123214}},{"loot",7923,{7051}}}},[2360]={t="Mathias and the Defias",lv=20,min=20,nx=2359,ot="Travel to Westfall and find Agent Kearnen for your debriefing.",st="Not a moment too soon, $n. SI:7 reconnaissance is reporting unusually heavy Defias activity in Westfall.$B$BIt would seem that the Defias have taken over an abandoned Alliance watch tower southeast of Sentinel Hill and are using it as a base of operations to smuggle in goods from the Redridge supply route.$B$BGet to Westfall and contact Agent Kearnen for your debriefing. You will find her hidden near the tower.$B$B...and $n, should you be discovered, SI:7 will disavow all knowledge of your existence."},[2399]={t="The Sprouted Fronds",lv=10,min=4,pre1={931}},[2438]={t="The Emerald Dreamcatcher",lv=6,min=1,nx=2459,ot="Bring the Emerald Dreamcatcher to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.",st="I was once given an emerald dreamcatcher from Gaerolas Talvethen, the warden of the druids in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. This powerful amulet is able to siphon energy from the Emerald Dream, bestowing luck upon those who carry it.$B$BSadly, I have not been able to retrieve it from my dresser in Starbreeze Village... Although Starbreeze was once a tranquil place, it has now succumbed to the corruption of the furbolg that reside there.$B$BPerhaps you would be willing to recover my dreamcatcher, $c?",how={{"open",8048,{126158}}}},[2459]={t="Ferocitas the Dream Eater",lv=8,min=1,pre1={2438},si=8049,ot="Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar wants you to kill 7 Gnarlpine Mystics and find the Missing Jewel.",st="The emerald... It is missing! My dreamcatcher has been damaged!$B$BThere is a band of Gnarlpine mystics located to the north of Starbreeze. I have heard reports that their leader, Ferocitas the Dream Eater has been wearing a necklace that glows green in the night. Now seeing my dreamcatcher, I am sure that he has stolen my emerald... He would never realize that its power is useless to him.$B$BFind this missing jewel, $n. And, while you're there, clear out some of the corrupted mystics as well.",how={{"kill",7235},{"loot",8050}}},[2498]={t="Return to Denalan",lv=9,min=4,pre1={923},nx=2499,ot="Rellian Greenspyre wants you to speak with Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.",st="I have just received word that  Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth has discovered what may be the cause of the tumors that plague the timberlings. Please speak with him, and tell him I sent you.$B$BMake haste, $n; he needs our help."},[2499]={t="Oakenscowl",lv=9,min=4,pre1={2498},ot="Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth wants you to collect the Gargantuan Tumor from Oakenscowl.",st="In a cave along the southern bank of the lake, a timberling named Oakenscowl is spreading corruption to all the creatures that make Lake Al'Ameth their home.$B$BI dared not get too close, but even from a distance, it is obvious: Oakenscowl is being poisoned by the largest tumor I have ever seen...  I would call it gargantuan, even.$B$B$n, you have already done much to aid my efforts, but I ask of you one more task. Hunt down Oakenscowl and collect the tumor; remove this source of corruption from my home.",how={{"loot",8136,{2166}}}},[2518]={t="Tears of the Moon",lv=12,min=5,nx=2520,ot="Priestess A'moora in the Temple of the Moon at Darnassus wants you to bring her Lady Sathrah's Silvery Spinnerets.",st="Lady Sathrah was once beloved of Elune. Graceful and pure, the spider spun her silver threads through the moonlight, catching the evening mist. The silvery dew had strong healing powers and was kept here in the temple.$B$BBut of late, Sathrah has descended into madness. Her future generations are now threatened as well.$B$BFind Lady Sathrah, $n, and end her suffering. She dwells along the northern borders of Teldrassil, near Wellspring Lake. Gather her silvery spinnerets and bring them back to me.",how={{"loot",8344,{7319}}}},[2519]={t="The Temple of the Moon",lv=10,min=5,nx=2518,bc=2518,ot="Sister Aquinne wants you to speak with Priestess A'moora in the Temple of the Moon.",st="A once great creature of the forest is in need of help, $r.$B$BThere is a difficult task that must be done.$B$BPlease seek out Priestess A'moora; she will explain things to you. Find her to the southeast of here, inside the Temple of the Moon."},[2520]={t="Sathrah's Sacrifice",lv=12,min=5,pre1={2518},si=8155,ot="Priestess A'moora wants you to place Lady Sathrah's silvery spinnerets at the fountain inside the temple, and then return to her.",st="Now you must finish the task to which you have been appointed. Take the spinnerets and offer Lady Sathrah's sacrifice to Elune; lay the great spider to rest.$B$BInside this temple, find the central fountain. There is where you may leave the sacrifice.  The holy waters will purify and cleanse the corruption that drove Sathrah mad.$B$BWhen you have completed this, return to me.",how={{"click",138498}}},[2541]={t="The Sleeping Druid",lv=8,min=3,nx=2561,ot="Bring a Shaman Voodoo Charm to Oben Rageclaw in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",st="The Gnarlpine shaman that inhabit this place have discovered a way of separating a sleeping druid's spirit from the physical body. The furbolg have animated my physical form and are using it to attack anyone that attempts to explore the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. I am now trapped in the Emerald Dream, powerless to stop this.$B$BYou must help me. The Gnarlpine shaman carry a strange charm which is used to perform this ritual, and I'd like to examine it. Please, $n, bring one to me.",how={{"loot",8363,{2009}}}},[2561]={t="Druid of the Claw",lv=10,min=3,pre1={2541},si=8149,ot="Oben Rageclaw wants you to kill his soulless body, and then use the Voodoo Charm.",st="After examining this charm, $n, I see now what must be done. Please take it, and do as I ask.$B$BYou are to explore the deepest areas of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. There, you will find my soulless body... Although I regret what I am about to tell you, I see no other way to free myself from the control of the Gnarlpine.$B$BIn order for me to escape them, you must kill my physical form.  Once that is done, use the voodoo charm on my fallen body. After you have completed this task, please return to me.",how={{"kill",7318}}},[2607]={t="The Touch of Zanzil",lv=20,min=20,pre1={2359},nx=2608,ot="Speak with Doc Mixilpixil in the cellar of the Barracks.",st="It appears as if you've brought back more information than even I expected. This certainly is a strange turn of events, $n.$B$BA cure? Hrm... Go down to the cellar and speak with Doc Mixilpixil - he may be able to help."},[2608]={t="The Touch of Zanzil",lv=20,min=20,pre1={2607},nx=2609,ot="/Lay down to be examined by Doc Mixilpixil. How can he find the cure if he can't find the cause?",st="Oh my, you look like death. Correction - I've seen death, you look worse than death. You, $g sir:miss;, would be what death coughed up at his last physical.$B$BHah! You hear that Noarm? Write that one down!$B$B*Cough* Hrm yes, in order for me to help you, I'll need to draw some blood. Don't worry, it only hurts the first few... fifty times or so... /lay down when you're ready for the treatment, $n."},[2609]={t="The Touch of Zanzil",lv=20,min=20,pre1={2608},ot="Bring Doc Mixilpixil one bundle of Simple Wildflowers, one Leaded Vial, one Bronze Tube, and one Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread. The 'itis' doesn't cure itself, young $g fella:lady;.",st="It's unanimous, $n. You've got the 'itis.'$B$BLuckily, I have a cure for the 'itis.'$B$BHere's what I need: One bundle of simple wildflowers, one leaded vial, one bronze tube, and last but certainly not least, one spool of light chartreuse silk thread. Ol' Emma left a spool of it for me at 'The Finest Thread.' You can find the shop along the canals.$B$BHurry along now, $n, and try not to touch anyone until you're cured. Oh, and Dr. Montgomery says you need a shower -- his words, not mine.",how={{"buy",3421,{1303,1302,3014}},{"buy",3372,{1286,1257,1326}},{"open",4371,{19019,19020}},{"open",8431,{140911}}}},[2745]={t="Infiltrating the Castle",lv=31,min=16,pre1={350},nx=2746,ot="Speak to Tyrion in Stormwind Castle.",st="Hmm, an interesting tale, and not one to be taken lightly. Yeah, I can help you, but what you need to do is divvy out a form of justice that's not... legal, if you're to see this through to the end.$B$BLescovar and Marzon need to be dealt with, and swiftly. Do you think you're capable of such a thing?$B$BYou decide. If so, then make haste to the castle and find an old friend of mine, a gnome named Tyrion. He's been watching Lescovar now for a couple weeks. He should be able to help you end this."},[2746]={t="Items of Some Consequence",lv=31,min=16,pre1={2745},nx=434,ot="Bring 3 Silk Cloth and 2 of Clara's Fresh Apples to Tyrion in Stormwind.",st="Trias wants the timetable pushed up some, huh? Okay, we can do that, but I'm not ready. And know this, I'm doing the hard part, but you're the one that's going to get $g his:her; hands dirty, understand? Good.$B$BOkay, I'll need you to get me a few things before I can put my plan into effect. I got the perfect disguise that'll get Spybot past those guards.$B$BBring me some silk and a couple apples. The silk's up to you, but Clara's little farm right outside the city has the perfect sized apples.",how={{"open",4306,{2850,2852,2849}},{"open",8683,{142076}}}},[2904]={t="A Fine Mess",lv=30,min=20,ne=1,ot="Escort Kernobee to the Clockwerk Run exit and then report to Scooty in Booty Bay.",st="<Kernobee groans.> Wha.. What happened?$B$BThe last thing I remember is being captured by a group of dark iron dwarves, beaten to within an inch of my life and then thrown in here with these filthy troggs.$B$BGet me out of here, $n!$B$BHere's the plan: Lead me to the exit; if we make it out alive, you go to Booty Bay and let Scooty know that I went to Ratchet to warn Tinkerwiz of the dark iron's involvement in the making of that super rig.$B$BLet's get going!"},[2922]={t="Save Techbot's Brain!",lv=26,min=20,rwc={[1]=1,[2]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[5]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[9]=1,[11]=1},ot="Bring Techbot's Memory Core to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.",st="When our beloved city Gnomeregan fell, a rogue spark must have jolted my poor creation, Techbot.  It once aided me and my associates with its countless gizmos and limitless store of information, but its positronic brain has polarized.  Now it's negatronic... and Techbot's behaviors are reversed.  It roams Gnomeregan in a frenzy!$B$BBut perhaps it can be salvaged.  Perhaps, if you can retrieve Techbot's memory core and bring it to me, I can discover the cause of the polarization and fix my poor Techbot.$B$B",how={{"loot",9277,{6231}}}},[2923]={t="Tinkmaster Overspark",lv=26,min=20,nx=2922,bc=2922,ot="Speak with Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.",st="Tinkmaster Overspark is very upset with the fate of his mechanical creation, Techbot.  I remember Techbot as a kind and helpful tool for the gnomes, but Overspark tells me it's malfunctioned.$B$BVery sad.  But with luck perhaps he can be fixed!$B$BSpeak with Tinkmaster Overspark, in Tinker Town in Ironforge.  He would welcome your help."},[2924]={t="Essential Artificials",lv=30,min=24,rwc={[1]=1,[2]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[5]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[9]=1,[11]=1},ot="Bring 12 Essential Artificials to Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge.",st="A nigh-universal mechanical component--the essential artificial--was of great use to the tinkers and smiths of Gnomeregan.  But during the frantic exodus from our city, no one remembered to take any of these devices with them!  And I need a large supply of them for work I will soon undertake.$B$BPlease, go into Gnomeregan and get me some essential artificials.  You'll find them in the deeper areas of our city, held in containers called artificial extrapolators.$B$BThank you, $n, and please hurry!",how={{"open",9278,{142344}}}},[2926]={t="Gnogaine",lv=27,min=20,nx=2962,si=9283,ot="Use the Empty Leaden Collection Phial on Irradiated Invaders or Irradiated Pillagers to collect radioactive fallout. Once it is full, take it back to Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos.",st="Since the accident, all Gnoarn thinks about or talks about is cleansing Gnomeregan of the trogg infestation and finding a cure for the sickness that plagues it, $n.$B$BLuckily, Razzle and I are close to some kind of cure - either that or the recipe for a really powerful rum. We won't know until we test! Naturally, in order to test our theory, we're going to need a few things; namely, fallout from the irradiated troggs in Gnomeregan. Fill up this phial with the green glow and bring it back!",how={{"loot",9284,{6213,6329}}}},[2927]={t="The Day After",lv=27,min=20,nx=2926,bc=2926,ot="Speak with Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos.",st="You don't think I was always bald, do you? No $g sir:ma'am;! It was the radiation leak in Gnomeregan that caused this tragic hair loss. Before that day, I had the only gnomefro in all of Azeroth.$B$B<Gnoarn shakes his fist in the air.>$B$BDamn those damned dirty troggs - damn them all!!$B$BPerhaps it's not too late, $n. We may still be able to save it - the city I mean! Speak to Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos. He and his partner Razzle are working on a solution."},[2928]={t="Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators",lv=30,min=20,ot="Bring twenty-four Robo-mechanical Guts to Shoni in Stormwind.",st="It's terrible, $n. We are not going to have enough parts to get our fleet of gyrodrillmatic excavationators to Dun Morogh.$B$BWhat we need are spare parts, $n. What better place to get the spare parts for our vehicles than Gnomeregan? I hear that bots and mechs roam around that place like cattle on an open range.$B$BWhat I need you to do is go to Gnomeregan and tear apart those robots. Bring me back their robot guts. Two dozen should be sufficient.",how={{"loot",9309,{6213,6208,6231}}}},[2929]={t="The Grand Betrayal",lv=35,min=25,rwc={[1]=1,[2]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[5]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[9]=1,[11]=1},ot="Venture to Gnomeregan and kill Mekgineer Thermaplugg. Return to High Tinker Mekkatorque when the task is complete.",st="I trusted Thermaplugg, $r. Never did I expect that he would betray me and the entire gnomish people. And for what? Power? Wealth? All things that he would have had in time. Now we have been displaced from our home and that madman is in charge. The king of nothing....$B$BWe will retake Gnomeregan, $n. We will not stop until the city is back in our control. If you wish to join in our fight, a simple task I ask of you: Kill the betrayer. Destroy Mekgineer Thermaplugg.",how={{"kill",7800}}},[2930]={t="Data Rescue",lv=30,min=25,rwc={[1]=1,[2]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[5]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[9]=1,[11]=1},ot="Bring a Prismatic Punch Card to Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge.",st="When we fled Gnomeregan, we left so much data behind!  Vitally important data!$B$BI need the data on a prismatic punch card, from a Matrix Punchograph 3005-D high security terminal, deep in Gnomeregan.  You must access the terminal, but to do that you first need clearance... and to get that you must access lower security terminals-- models -A, -B and -C.  And to do THAT you need security punch cards, starting with white... and we left all the punch cards in the city.$B$BIt's a catastrophe!  Can you help?",how={{"open",9316,{142696}}}},[2945]={t="Grime-Encrusted Ring",lv=34,min=28,si=9326,ot="Figure out a way to remove the grime from the Grime-Encrusted Ring.",st="You have uncovered what appears to be a ring from the corpse of one of the Dark Iron dwarves.  It is difficult to tell what kind of ring it is, however; dirt and hardened residue cake the item completely, making wearing it impossible.  You think you can make out the slight luster of precious metal and maybe even the glint of a gem under the residue.$B$BIf you are going to make use of this ring, you are going to need to find something to get the hardened residue off of it."},[2947]={t="Return of the Ring",lv=34,min=28,pre1={2945},nx=2948,si=9362,ot="You may either keep the ring, or you may find the person responsible for the imprint and engravings on the inside of the band.",st="Opening the box produced by the Sparklematic 5200 reveals what you had suspected - a shiny ring!  Wearing the ring, you feel magic power surge through you body.$B$BInside the band is a small but nonetheless discernable imprint of the seal of Ironforge.  Next to that, three small initials are engraved: \"TdK\".  This may signify either the initials of the previous owner, or perhaps the initials of the ring's crafter.  Keep the ring... or return it to this person.  Decisions, decisions..."},[2948]={t="Gnome Improvement",lv=35,min=28,pre1={2947},rwc={[1]=2948,[2]=2948,[3]=2948,[4]=2948,[5]=2948,[7]=2948,[8]=2948,[9]=2948,[11]=2948},si=9362,ot="Bring the Brilliant Gold Ring, a Silver Bar, a Moss Agate, and 30 silver coins to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.",st="Listen $n, that ring is yours, sure... but I can make you a better one!  That design, like I said, is really simple.  I am a lot more skilled now, and for the mere fee of thirty silver coins I'll spruce it up for you!  Well, a little more than thirty, actually...$B$BI'm in a tight spot right now; all my material stock is all dried up.  If you bring me a bar of silver and a moss agate, I'll add a silver and agate lattice to the ring that will give it a little more pizzazz!$B$BTrust me!",how={{"open",2842,{106319}},{"open",1206,{1732,1733,179486}}}},[2951]={t="The Sparklematic 5200!",lv=30,min=25,ex={4601,4602},ot="Insert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.",st="This contraption stands out amongst the gnomes holding out against the madness outside the room.  A small plaque on the device reads \"The Sparklematic 5200\", followed by some text:$B$B\"Grime and residue ruining your sparklies?  The Sparklematic 5200 puts the shine back in shine-tastic!  Insert the item you wish to clean and deposit three silver coins in the coin slot.  Give the Sparklematic 5200 a moment for operation, and voila!  Your valuables will emerge clean and shiny!\"",how={{"loot",9308,{6213,6209,6210}}}},[2952]={t="The Sparklematic 5200!",lv=30,min=25,pre1={2951,4601,4602},ex={4605,4606}},[2962]={t="The Only Cure is More Green Glow",lv=30,min=20,pre1={2926},si=9364,ot="Travel to Gnomeregan and bring back High Potency Radioactive Fallout. Be warned, the fallout is unstable and will collapse rather quickly.$B$BOzzie will also require your Heavy Leaden Collection Phial when the task is complete.",st="Not only was your sample insufficient in quantity, it was also impure.$B$BWhat we require is more green glow. The troggs are obviously not irradiated sufficiently to fulfill our needs. You will have to go into Gnomeregan and bring back some radioactive fallout, straight from the tap. I am speaking of the irradiated slimes, lurkers and horrors. Be warned, the containment of this type of fallout is difficult. You may need to make several attempts with the phial until a suitable sampling is recovered.",how={{"loot",9365,{6218,6219,6220}}}},[2998]={t="Tome of Divinity",lv=12,min=12,ex={3681},nx=1642,bc=1642,ot="Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.",st="Greetings, $Gbrother:sister;. Duthorian Rall, one of our most influential paladins, was speaking about you recently. I overheard him talking about how it was time you be put to the test some... along with some very complimentary things about how well you've performed thus far.$B$BIf I were you, I'd head to Stormwind and speak to him when you have time. I'm sure he's in the Cathedral of Light--that's where he spends most of his time."},[2999]={t="Tome of Divinity",lv=12,min=12,ex={2997,3000},nx=1646,bc=1646,ot="Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge",st="Hello, $n. I know you're busy helping out the people of Dun Morogh, but when you have the time, you should go upstairs and speak to one of our most respected ilk: Tiza Battleforge. She's the one the younger paladins go to when it's time they learn more about the Light and what's expected of ya."},[3100]={t="Simple Letter",lv=1,min=1,pre1={7},si=9542,ot="Read the Simple Letter and speak to Llane Beshere in Northshire Abbey.",st="I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Llane, our local warrior trainer. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey."},[3101]={t="Consecrated Letter",lv=1,min=1,pre1={7},si=9570,ot="Read the Consecrated Letter and speak to Brother Sammuel in Northshire Abbey.",st="I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Brother Sammuel, our local paladin trainer. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey."},[3102]={t="Encrypted Letter",lv=1,min=1,pre1={7},si=9555,ot="Read the Encrypted Letter and speak to Jorik Kerridan in the stable behind Northshire Abbey.",st="I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Jorik, one of our local trainers. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey."},[3103]={t="Hallowed Letter",lv=1,min=1,pre1={7},si=9548,ot="Read the Hallowed Letter and speak to Priestess Anetta in Northshire Abbey.",st="I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Priestess Anetta, our local priest trainer. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey."},[3104]={t="Glyphic Letter",lv=1,min=1,pre1={7},si=9571,ot="Read the Glyphic Letter and speak to Khelden Bremen inside Northshire Abbey.",st="I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Khelden, our local mage trainer. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey."},[3105]={t="Tainted Letter",lv=1,min=1,pre1={7},si=9576,ot="Read the Tainted Letter and speak to Drusilla La Salle next to Northshire Abbey.",st="I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Drusilla, one of our local trainers. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey."},[3106]={t="Simple Rune",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9543,ot="Read the Simple Rune and speak to Thran Khorman in Coldridge Valley.",st="While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the warrior trainer Thran. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[3107]={t="Consecrated Rune",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9563,ot="Read the Consecrated Rune and speak to Bromos Grummner in Coldridge Valley.",st="While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the paladin trainer Bromos. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[3108]={t="Etched Rune",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9566,ot="Read the Etched Rune and speak to Thorgas Grimson in Coldridge Valley.",st="While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the hunter trainer Thorgas. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[3109]={t="Encrypted Rune",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9550,ot="Read the Encrypted Rune and speak to Solm Hargrin in Coldridge Valley.",st="While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the rogue trainer Solm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[3110]={t="Hallowed Rune",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9556,ot="Read the Hallowed Rune and speak to Branstock Khalder in Anvilmar.",st="While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the priest trainer Branstock. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[3112]={t="Simple Memorandum",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9544,ot="Read the Simple Memorandum and speak to Thran Khorman in Coldridge Valley.",st="While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the warrior trainer Thran. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[3113]={t="Encrypted Memorandum",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9558,ot="Read the Encrypted Memorandum and speak to Solm Hargrin in Coldridge Valley.",st="While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the rogue trainer Solm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[3114]={t="Glyphic Memorandum",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9573,ot="Read the Glyphic Memorandum and speak to Marryk Nurribit inside Anvilmar above Coldridge Valley.",st="While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the mage trainer Marryk. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[3115]={t="Tainted Memorandum",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=9577,ot="Read the Tainted Memorandum and speak to Alamar Grimm inside Anvilmar above Coldridge Valley.",st="While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the warlock trainer Alamar. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.$B$BAnd watch yerself, $n, your kind ain't too trusted 'round these parts."},[3116]={t="Simple Sigil",lv=1,min=1,pre1={456},si=9545,ot="Read the Simple Sigil and speak to Alyissia in Shadowglen.",st="This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our warrior trainer, Alyissia. It seems Alyissia would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to her afterwards."},[3117]={t="Etched Sigil",lv=1,min=1,pre1={456},si=9567,ot="Read the Etched Sigil and speak to Ayanna Everstride at the top of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",st="This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our hunter trainer, Ayanna. It seems Ayanna would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to her afterwards."},[3118]={t="Encrypted Sigil",lv=1,min=1,pre1={456},si=9551,ot="Read the Encrypted Sigil and speak to Frahun Shadewhisper in Shadowglen.",st="This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our rogue trainer, Frahun. It seems Frahun would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to him afterwards."},[3119]={t="Hallowed Sigil",lv=1,min=1,pre1={456},si=9557,ot="Read the Hallowed Sigil and speak to Shanda in Aldrassil.",st="This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our priest trainer, Shanda. It seems Shanda would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to her afterwards."},[3120]={t="Verdant Sigil",lv=1,min=1,pre1={456},si=9580,ot="Read the Verdant Sigil and speak to Mardant Strongoak, in the tree Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",st="This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our druid trainer, Mardant. It seems Mardant would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to him afterwards."},[3361]={t="A Refugee's Quandary",lv=3,min=3,ot="Bring Felix's Box, Felix's Chest and Felix's Bucket of Bolts to Felix Whindlebolt in Anvilmar.",st="We drove the troggs out of Gnomeregan, but then it all went so horribly wrong!  Now our home is completely irradiated, and we gnomes have been scattered all over Dun Morogh.$B$BIn my haste to get away from the radiation, I lost all my personal belongings and tools.  It was the trolls that got them.  They stole my chest, my box, and my bucket of bolts!  They took them back to their camps southwest of Anvilmar.$B$BI'm no adventurer - could you find my things and bring them here to me, please?",how={{"open",10438,{148499}},{"open",16313,{178084}},{"open",16314,{178085}}}},[3364]={t="Scalding Mornbrew Delivery",lv=5,min=4,nx=3365,si=10439,ot="Take a Scalding Mornbrew to Durnan Furcutter inside Anvilmar before it gets cold in five minutes!",st="Gah!  I was supposed to get this delicious scalding mornbrew to Durnan Furcutter inside Anvilmar a while ago now, but I had to deliver one to Grelin here first.  I'll never make it to Anvilmar before the brew runs cold!$B$BYou look fast.  Maybe you can make it.  This cup will only stay hot for five more minutes, and Durnan didn't order \"chilly\" mornbrew, so get going.  Anvilmar is to the northeast, a settlement dug into the mountain.$B$BThanks, $n, and don't forget to bring me back my mug!"},[3365]={t="Bring Back the Mug",lv=5,min=4,pre1={3364},si=10440,ot="Return Nori's Mug to Nori Pridedrift.",st="Now that hit the spot!  Nothing like a piping hot - nay, SCALDING mornbrew on a cold winter's day to warm your cackles of yer soul.$B$BHere ya go $n - be a pal and take this empty mug back to Nori for me, would ya now."},[3370]={t="In Nightmares",lv=25,min=10,pre1={6981},si=10649,ot="Bring the Nightmare Shard to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus.",st="This shard holds great secrets; it is the pure essence of the Emerald Dream. However, what I see in this shard is not a dream; one would call this sort of a vision a nightmare.$B$BI do not wish to alarm you, $n, but I think it is best if you deliver this shard into the hands of a wise druid as soon as you can... $B$BMathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Circle is who you need to find. Head to Darnassus. I cannot say more."},[3519]={t="A Friend in Need",lv=4,min=2,pre1={4495},nx=3521,ot="Speak to Dirania Silvershine in Shadowglen.",st="Ughhh... I was bitten very badly by a spider named Githyiss the Vile while exploring the spider cave very close to here. I am sure I have been seriously poisoned; you must help me.$B$BPlease tell Dirania Silvershine. She will be able to help me.$B$BHurry... I'm so dizzy..."},[3521]={t="Iverron's Antidote",lv=4,min=2,pre1={3519},nx=3522,ot="Collect 7 Hyacinth Mushrooms, 4 Moonpetal Lilies, and 1 Webwood Ichor for Dirania Silveshine in Shadowglen.",st="We may be able to help Iverron, as I know of an antidote that should help with the poison. It requires some ingredients, though, before I can make it.$B$BI'll need Hyacinth mushrooms. You can find these growing under trees, or you may collect them from the grell south of here; they seem to have taken a liking to them. I'll also need Moonpetal lilies, which only grow around watery pools.$B$BThe last ingredient may prove the most difficult. From the very spiders that poisoned Iverron, collect Webwood ichor.",how={{"loot",10639,{1988,1989}},{"open",10641,{152095}},{"loot",10640,{1986}}}},[3522]={t="Iverron's Antidote",lv=4,min=2,pre1={3521},si=10642,ot="Bring Iverron's Antidote to Iverron before the time limit is up. Iverron can be found by the cave to the north.",st="The antidote is ready, $n. Please see that Iverron drinks it.$B$BThere is something that you should know -- the antidote -- it will only remain viable for 5 minutes. You must get it to him in time.$B$BSpeed be with you, $n."},[3524]={t="Washed Ashore",lv=13,min=11,nx=4681,ot="Recover Sea Creature Bones from the beached sea creature just south of Auberdine, and then return with it to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="Majestic sea creatures are known to launch themselves at the Darkshore coastline, beached there until they die. Lately, these beasts have been washing ashore in ever-increasing numbers.  I've been sent here by the Temple of the Moon to investigate, but the presence of murlocs along the water has made my research difficult.$B$BThere is a giant creature washed ashore just south of Auberdine that is ringed by the foul Greymist murlocs.  Could you go there and retrieve bones from the creature for our study?",how={{"open",12242,{175207}}}},[3741]={t="Hilary's Necklace",lv=15,min=12,ot="Find Hilary's Necklace, and return it to Hilary in Lakeshire.",st="My friend Hilary lost her necklace, and we can't find it.  We've been fishing all day right here, and we looked around here already.  The only thing I can think of is that it fell into the lake.  Our parents don't want us to swim in the lake... my mom says there's some mean things underwater, but you look like you aren't scared of mean things.$B$BCould you find it for her, please?",how={{"open",10958,{154357}}}},[3765]={t="The Corruption Abroad",lv=24,min=18,nx=1275,bc=1275,ot="Travel to Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine.",st="Stormwind -- such a bustling hub of activity.$b$bI have traveled from afar to seek help. Often it is heard that brave adventurers roam these city streets.$b$bMy brother, Gershala, requires assistance in Darkshore. He resides in the seaside town of Auberdine.$b$bThe journey is a long and epic one. It is for this reason that I ask the help of a seasoned $c such as yourself."},[3903]={t="Milly Osworth",lv=4,min=2,pre1={18},nx=3904,bc=3904,ot="Speak with Milly Osworth.",st="You've shown yourself a dependable $c, $n.  Dependable, and not afraid to get your hands dirty, eh?$B$BI have a friend, Milly Osworth, who's in some trouble.  She's over with her wagon on the other side of the abbey, near the stable.  I'm sure she could use a pair of hands like yours."},[3904]={t="Milly's Harvest",lv=4,min=2,pre1={18},nx=3905,ot="Bring 8 crates of Milly's Harvest to Milly Osworth at Northshire Abbey.",st="A gang of brigands, the Defias, moved into the Northshire Vineyards while I was harvesting!  I reported it to the Northshire guards and they assured me they'd take care of things, but... I'm afraid for my crop of grapes!  If the Defias don't steal them then I fear our guards will trample them when they chase away the thugs.$B$BPlease, you must help me!  I gathered most of my grapes into buckets, but I left them in the vineyards to the southeast.$B$BBring me those crates!  Save my harvest!",how={{"open",11119,{161557}}}},[3905]={t="Grape Manifest",lv=4,min=2,pre1={3904},rwc={[5]=1,[8]=1},si=11125,ot="Bring the Grape Manifest to Brother Neals in Northshire Abbey.",st="Now that my crop is saved, take this Grape Manifest to Brother Neals.  He manages the store of food and drink in Northshire, and I'm sure he'll be delighted to hear that he has fresh grapes.$B$BYou'll find Brother Neals in the abbey, in the bell tower... where he likes to taste his wine."},[4161]={t="Recipe of the Kaldorei",lv=7,min=1,ot="Collect 7 Small Spider Legs for Zarrin in Dolanaar.",st="Long ago, the night elves were called the kaldorei, a name that means \"children of the stars.\" Learning of the past is an important step in your path as a $c, $n, so listen well to what I have to tell you.$B$BThe kaldorei have always taken much pride in their harmonious relationship with nature. This means that we only take from nature what is necessary, and that we return in kind. This balance has afforded us much, $n.$B$BGo out and collect seven small spider legs -- no more than that, and return to me.",how={{"loot",5465,{1998,1999,272096}}}},[4495]={t="A Good Friend",lv=4,min=2,nx=3519,ot="Find Iverron by the cave to the north.",st="A friend of mine named Iverron usually visits me at the same time every day. The strange thing is that he hasn't been by today at all -- he's several hours late, in fact.$B$BI admit, I am a little worried, $n. Iverron spends a lot of time over by the cave to the north, and I'm sure you know how dangerous it is there -- spiders, everywhere!$B$BIf you happen to be going that way, though, will you keep an eye out for him?"},[4581]={t="Kayneth Stillwind",lv=29,min=24,si=12060,ot="Take Shindrell's Note to Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song.",st="The druid Kayneth Stillwind sent word to me.  He would like a report of the happenings along our coast and in the forests surrounding Astranaar.  He fears there is a corruption moving through Ashenvale... and he may be right.$B$BHere, take my report to him.  You will find him in the shrine of Forest Song, in the Nightsong Woods to the east."},[4681]={t="Washed Ashore",lv=14,min=11,pre1={3524},rwc={[8]=1},ot="Recover the Sea Turtle Remains from the Skeletal Sea Turtle in the waters west of Auberdine, and then speak with Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde back in Auberdine.",st="That beached creature is not an isolated incident here in Darkshore.  There are more along the coastline and even in the water.  I would like for you to investigate another one that we know of; this one was reported to be in the water due west of Auberdine, close to a sunken vessel.  Return to me with anything that you may recover that would aid our research.$B$BAlso, in your travels you may find other creatures.  By all means, if you should discover anything then please bring it to our attention!",how={{"open",12289,{176189}}}},[4722]={t="Beached Sea Turtle",lv=13,min=11,pre1={4681},si=12289,ot="Take the Sea Turtle Remains to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="You find a corpse of a sea turtle that had beached itself on the coast of Darkshore some time ago.  It has been scavenged by the murlocs who have encamped themselves around the creature's remains.  Still, there appear to be some suitable samples left on the creature's remains that Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine might be able to make use of."},[4723]={t="Beached Sea Creature",lv=13,min=11,pre1={4681},si=12242,ot="Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="The remains of a giant thresher - much larger than one you'd expect to find in Darkshore - lie beached on the coast of the Mist's Edge.  How this creature came to be here is unknown; the group of murlocs that now feast off the carcass of it seem to be much too weak, even in large numbers, to have brought down the beast. $B$BWhile some of it has been picked clean, enough of it remains to take a sample for Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine to study."},[4725]={t="Beached Sea Turtle",lv=15,min=12,pre1={4681},si=12292,ot="Take the Strangely Marked Box to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="More sea turtle remains lie beached along the coastline.  This particular set has an abandoned carriage attached to the turtle's shell.  Perhaps this creature was driven to the shoreline by unknown beings rather than beaching itself as some of the other remains suggested.  Greymist murlocs now make the remains of this creature their home, feasting off the carrion.$B$BIn the carriage, you find a box with strange markings on it; perhaps Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine can make sense of it."},[4727]={t="Beached Sea Turtle",lv=15,min=12,pre1={4681},si=12289,ot="Take the Sea Turtle Remains to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="The skeletal remains of a sea turtle lie in the sand of the northern Darkshore beaches.  The Greymist murlocs have either not found this carcass, or perhaps they have and are shying away from it for some unknown reason.  Regardless, there is enough of the turtle left to take a sample back to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine for the Temple of the Moon to study."},[4728]={t="Beached Sea Creature",lv=14,min=12,pre1={4681},si=12242,ot="Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="The corpse of what appears to be some sort of giant sea mammal lies partially gutted on the beach.  A wheelbarrow and various tools lie abandoned by this enormous beached sea creature, as though an attempt to study it had been made previously.  Though murlocs have scavenged this beast, enough of it remains to gather a suitable sample for Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine."},[4730]={t="Beached Sea Creature",lv=16,min=12,pre1={4681},si=12242,ot="Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="The half-devoured corpse of what might have been a giant sea mammal lies on the beach.  A band of murlocs, stronger than those found closer to Auberdine, have taken up residence around the fallen creature.  Enough of the creature remains that a suitable sample of its bones could be delivered to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine."},[4731]={t="Beached Sea Turtle",lv=19,min=13,pre1={4681},si=12292,ot="Take the Strangely Marked Box to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="Another set of sea turtle remains lie beached on the coastline.  This set of remains has an abandoned carriage half buckled to the turtle's shell.  Perhaps this creature was driven to the shoreline by unknown beings rather than beaching itself as some of the other remains suggested.  Powerful Greymist murlocs have made the carcass of this creature their current home.$B$BIn the carriage, you find a box with strange markings on it; perhaps Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine can make sense of it."},[4732]={t="Beached Sea Turtle",lv=19,min=13,pre1={4681},si=12289,ot="Take the Sea Turtle Remains to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="You find a corpse of a sea turtle that had beached itself on the coast of Darkshore some time ago.  It has been picked nearly clean by Greymist murlocs, the very ones who now have encamped themselves around the creature's remains.  Still, there appear to be some suitable samples left on the creature's remains that Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine might be able to make use of."},[4733]={t="Beached Sea Creature",lv=19,min=13,pre1={4681},si=12242,ot="Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.",st="The remains of what appear to be a giant thresher have washed ashore on the rocky inlet of the Twilight Shore.  The thresher is several times larger than any of the other threshers spotted in these parts.  Wherever it came from, this creature would not seem to have been native to Darkshore.$B$BThough the creature has been picked apart in places, enough of it remains to gather a suitable sample for Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine."},[4740]={t="WANTED: Murkdeep!",lv=18,min=15,ot="Find and slay the murloc known as Murkdeep.  The creature is thought to be defending the murloc huts south of Auberdine along the water.$B$BReport the death of Murkdeep to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.",st="Attention!$B$BA reward is being offered for the death of the murloc \"Murkdeep\".  This foul beast is known to be responsible for the death of at least one Sentinel, and is suspected of causing the sinking of at least two cargo vessels in the waters off Darkshore!$B$BMurkdeep was last spotted at a hutted murloc camp south of Auberdine, and is thought to be protecting the huts there.  Reward claims for this bounty should be claimed with Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.$B$BThe Auberdine Village Council",how={{"kill",10323}}},[4761]={t="Thundris Windweaver",lv=15,min=11,pre1={984},nx=4762,ot="Speak with Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.",st="Your scouting of the furbolg camp is information that Thundris Windweaver should be made aware of.  He graciously serves as the elder of Auberdine, offering sage and just stewardship of the day to day affairs of the village.  Please - share with him your findings to date on the furbolg situation.$B$BI believe he has some ideas of his own on the reasons behind their corruption.  Perhaps you can work with him to enact a plan to restore the balance of nature here!"},[4762]={t="The Cliffspring River",lv=15,min=11,pre1={4761},nx=4763,si=12350,ot="Travel north of Auberdine to the first waterfall along the Cliffspring River and draw a sample from the pool there.$B$BReturn to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine with the Cliffspring River Sample.",st="The Cliffspring River has begun turning foul and corrupted.  It empties into the Mist's Edge, and I fear the wash will affect Auberdine soon.  I suspect the Blackwood furbolgs up-river are the cause of the taint, but I also suspect that they aren't the true root of it.$B$BTake this sampling tube and go to the mouth of the river to our north.  Proceed inland to the first waterfall and draw a sample from the pool there.  You'll see a bridge overhead.  Once you have a sample, return to me in Auberdine.",how={{"open",12349,{175371}}}},[4763]={t="The Blackwood Corrupted",lv=18,min=15,pre1={4762},rwc={[8]=1},si=12346,ui={12347,14338},ot="Fill the Empty Cleansing Bowl at the Auberdine Moonwell.$B$BGather a sample of fruit, nut, and grain from the northern Blackwood furbolg camps.$B$BMix the bowl and place it near the bonfire closest to the Cliffspring River at the northern camp, thus summoning the satyr corruptor.$B$BTake the Talisman of Corruption and bring it to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.",st="We've learned that a source of furbolg corruption is from the satyr.  They hold sway via talismans that they channel magic through.  If the furbolg have a chance at salvation, we must lure out the satyr corruptor and take that talisman!$B$BFill this bowl at our moonwell and take samples of the furbolgs' food from their northern camp.  Mix them and place it near the bonfire by the river; any furbolgs who eat will be cleansed just long enough to lure out the satyr corruptor... who then you must slay!",how={{"open",12355,{177624}}}},[4811]={t="The Red Crystal",lv=14,min=12,nx=4812,ot="Travel east of Auberdine and look for a large, red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain range.  Report back what you find to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.",st="Hostile moonkin roam in ever increasing numbers to our east.  They once were thought to be gentle, almost mystical creatures.  While some continue to hold reverence for them, the safety of Auberdine forces me to keep a more realistic view.$B$BI've received reports that moonkin are being drawn to a large red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain range.  No one has any idea what that crystal is, or even if it really exists.  I want you to locate it over there and report back to me what you find.",how={{"click",175524}}},[4812]={t="As Water Cascades",lv=14,min=12,pre1={4811},nx=4813,si=14338,ui={12346},ot="Fill the Empty Water Tube at the Auberdine moonwell, and then investigate the red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain wall.",st="Use this empty vial and fill up on some moonwell water here in Auberdine.  Such potent magic should provide a clue as to the composition of the crystal.  To do that, you'll pour the liquid over the crystal; it should take care of the rest.$B$BWhile I don't anticipate anything bad happening to you, I still want you to be careful.  Above us to the east is Felwood; if that crystal is tied to that place as I suspect it is, then it could prove to be very dangerous.",how={{"open",14339,{174795}}}},[4813]={t="The Fragments Within",lv=14,min=12,pre1={4812},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[5]=3,[8]=2,[11]=3},ot="Report back what you have found to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.",st="The moonwell water has revealed that embedded inside the crystal are a few small fragments of bone, as well as half of a jawbone.  The jawbone appears to be from a humanoid, but it is unclear without breaking open the crystal - a feat that even the strongest of magic would find near impossible.$B$BWith the task at hand complete, all that remains is to report back to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine."},[5061]={t="Aquatic Form",lv=16,min=16,pre1={272},si=15885,ot="Return to Darnassus and show Mathrengyl Bearwalker the Pendant of the Sea Lion.",st="You have completed the necessary lessons all young druids are taught before they can adopt an aquatic aspect.  Go now back to your trainer, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, in Darnassus.  Show him your pendant and prove to him you are ready to learn what he has to teach you.  He will complete your training, allowing you to become one with the water.$B$BGoodbye, young druid.  We shall speak again."},[5261]={t="Eagan Peltskinner",lv=2,min=1,pre1={783},nx=33,bc=33,ot="Speak with Eagan Peltskinner.",st="Eagan Peltskinner is looking for someone to hunt wolves for him.  That's good news, because we're seeing a lot more wolves in Northshire Valley lately.$B$BIf you're interested then speak with Eagan.  He's around the side of the abbey, to the left."},[5321]={t="The Sleeper Has Awakened",lv=20,min=17,ne=1,rwc={[8]=1},si=13536,ot="Escort Kerlonian Evershade to Liladris Moonriver south along the road to find his bag in Darkshore.",st="I was on my way to Maestra's Post to meet Liladris Moonriver, but I decided to stop here and take a short nap. Ever since I awoke from the emerald dream, I have been so sleepy...\r\n\r\n<yawn>\r\n\r\nAnd I can't find my things anywhere! Would you mind helping me find them?\r\n\r\nI understand that Maestra's Post is south of here, along the road in Ashenvale. I had come from that way...\r\n\r\nLastly, I may fall asleep so if you ever need to wake me, please use my horn. You'll find it in the chest here."},[5541]={t="Ammo for Rumbleshot",lv=6,min=5,ot="Bring Rumbleshot's Ammo to Hegnar Rumbleshot in Dun Morogh.",st="Hegnar Rumbleshot sells guns off the road to Anvilmar.  Riflemen and mortar teams spend a lot of time practicing out near his shop, and he's always needing fresh ammunition.$B$BBut... the last crate of ammo I sent him got lost along the way.  My courier said he was camped near the Grizzled Den when wendigo chased him away... and the fool left Rumbleshot's ammo behind!$B$B$n, can you get that ammo and take it to Rumbleshot?  He's been waiting on it and I'm sure he's running low.",how={{"open",13850,{176785}}}},[5545]={t="A Bundle of Trouble",lv=9,min=5,ot="Bring 8 Bundles of Wood to Raelen at the Eastvale Logging Camp.",st="I've got a real problem on my hands. I have a deadline looming for an order of lumber, and I'm running out of time. The wolves and bears north of here have chased my workers away from the bundles of wood that they've already chopped.$B$BI've already talked to Deputy Rainer about clearing the animals, but I need someone to go collect the wood for me. If you could collect eight bundles of wood for me I might just make my deadline.",how={{"open",13872,{176793}}}},[5621]={t="Garments of the Moon",lv=4,min=5,ot="Find Sentinel Shaya and heal her wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant her Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Laurna Morninglight in Dolanaar.",st="I need your help, $n. I am needed here to train the other students, but you, you can help one of our injured Sentinels just south of Dolanaar. She was hurt patrolling the town and could use our aid. Her name is Shaya.$B$BWhen you find her, heal her wounds, and then fortify her body with your spells. This will at least protect her from harm longer if she finds trouble. Return to me here after you've done your duty to Elune.",how={{"talk",12429}}},[5622]={t="In Favor of Elune",lv=4,min=5,nx=5621,bc=5621,ot="Speak to Laurna Morninglight in Teldrassil.",st="$n, you must travel to Dolanaar when your business here in Shadowglen is done. There, you will find Laurna Morninglight. She will instruct you further in the ways of Elune, and it is with her that you will earn your first garments denoting your station as a $gpriest:priestess; of Elune.$B$BTake care, and may you be protected in your journeys."},[5623]={t="In Favor of the Light",lv=4,min=5,nx=5624,bc=5624,ot="Speak to Priestess Josetta in Elwynn Forest.",st="Hello again, young $gpriest:priestess;. The time has come for you to learn more about our religion. After you've completed whatever tasks you have here in Northshire, please seek out Priestess Josetta in Goldshire. She has more to teach you and has heard that you are growing strong in the ways of the Light. She looks forward to tutoring you more."},[5624]={t="Garments of the Light",lv=4,min=5,ot="Find Guard Roberts and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Priestess Josetta in Goldshire.",st="Normally I put forth a small challenge to followers of the Light to test their skill. I want to see if they are worthy of wearing their first robes--a sign that the church outwardly approves of the $gpriest:priestess; and supports $ghim:her;.$B$BBut this situation is a bit different. One of Goldshire's citizens saw an injured guard near the lake to the east of here. His name is Roberts. Find him, heal him, fortify his body and return here. If you can do that for me, then I will consider your test complete.",how={{"talk",12423}}},[5625]={t="Garments of the Light",lv=4,min=5,ot="Find Mountaineer Dolf and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Maxan Anvol in Kharanos.",st="It's usually about this time that one of your power is tested to see if they're worthy of wearing robes denoting their place in the church. But to be honest, I got more pressing matters to look into. Citizen of Kharanos' just came in here and told me 'bout a hurt mountaineer just outside town to the south--name's Dolf.$B$BYou heal Dolf and give him Fortitude, and I'll consider you done with proving yourself. How's that sound?",how={{"talk",12427}}},[5626]={t="In Favor of the Light",lv=4,min=5,nx=5625,bc=5625,ot="Speak to Maxan Anvol in Dun Morogh.",st="Hey! $n! Got a minute?!$B$BYa been following the Light now for long enough that you find your way to Maxan Anvol in Kharanos. He'll teach ya more about the path yer following, and if you prove worthy, give ya yer first set of robes to denote your station as a $gpriest:priestess;.$B$BNow get goin'! As soon as yer done here, head through the tunnel--he'll be waitin' for ya."},[5629]={t="Returning Home",lv=10,min=10,ex={5627,5628,5630,5631,5632,5633},ot="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",st="Hello again, $n. I know you've been busy aiding our people, but you must take some time for yourself also. Priestess Alathea sent someone here looking for you. It seems that you've caught the attention of our elders and they feel you are prepared for greater things. Head to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus and look for Alathea there. She will be waiting. Good luck, and may Elune be with you."},[5634]={t="Desperate Prayer",lv=10,min=10,ex={5635,5636,5637,5638,5639,5640},ot="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.",st="A priest recently visited our halls seeking you out, young $r. He said that he was on a mission to find you and that you should return to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. When you arrive, seek out High Priest Rohan--he will tell you more.$B$BThe Light be with you, $n."},[5641]={t="Chastise",lv=20,min=20,ex={5645,5647}},[5672]={t="Elune's Grace",lv=20,min=20,ex={5673,5674,5675}},[5676]={t="Arcane Feedback",lv=20,min=20,ex={5677,5678}},[5713]={t="One Shot. One Kill.",lv=15,min=10,ne=1,ot="Protect Sentinel Aynasha, then speak with Onaeya at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.",st="I was traveling to Auberdine with an important message when I was attacked by the furbolg Marosh and his trackers. During the attack I was poisoned, leaving me barely able to stand. I can make an antidote, but it will take time before it is ready.$B$BI would ask that you defend me until I can apply the antidote. I will aid you with my bow as best I can.$B$BShould we survive, I will be able deliver my message to Auberdine, while you speak with Onaeya at Maestra's Post to inform her of this incident."},[5921]={t="Moonglade",lv=10,min=10,nx=5929,ot="Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade.  When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.",st="All druids are welcome in the sacred lands of Moonglade, regardless of the current tensions in the Cenarion Circle between Arch Druid Staghelm and Keeper Remulos - Moonglade's guardian.  Now that you're learning the ways of the Claw, I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there.  Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.$B$BAs for your first lesson, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on.  Good luck, young druid."},[5923]={t="Heeding the Call",lv=10,min=10,ex={5924,5925},nx=5921,bc=5921,ot="Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.",st="Excuse me, friend...$B$BIt has come to my attention that Mathrengyl Bearwalker has put out word that he wishes to speak with you.  It seems that your training as a druid is about to take on a new life, and he will be training you personally.  Mathrengyl is the direct assistant to the Arch Druid himself, and is one of the most sage and august druids you'll find in Teldrassil.$B$BHe is located in the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus, on the second floor of Fandral Staghelm's tree."},[5929]={t="Great Bear Spirit",lv=10,min=10,pre1={5921},nx=5931,ot="Seek out the Great Bear Spirit in northwestern Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the bear.  When finished, return to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven, Moonglade.",st="In the northwest part of Moonglade resides the home of a wise and noble being we call the Great Bear Spirit.  For all druids, it has served as a tutor and mentor into the first true natural understanding of the bear.  All druids at one point seek the spirit's wisdom, and you shall be no exception.$B$BGo to the Great Bear Spirit now and learn what it will teach.  When it is satisfied with you, return to me here in Nighthaven.  We will then see if you have truly taken account of the lessons it teaches.",how={{"talk",11956}}},[5931]={t="Back to Darnassus",lv=10,min=10,pre1={5929},nx=6001,ot="Return to Darnassus and speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave.",st="The time has come for us to part ways, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to whom that sent you to me.  Mathrengyl Bearwalker walks truly in balance with nature, even as he dwells precariously close to where the balance has faltered.  Listen to his instructions, and you will soon complete your first lessons into your role as a protector of balance.$B$BGo now, young one.  We shall meet again."},[6001]={t="Body and Heart",lv=10,min=10,pre1={5931},si=15208,ot="Use the Cenarion Moondust on the Moonkin Stone of Auberdine to bring forth Lunaclaw.  From there, you must face Lunaclaw and earn the strength of body and heart it possesses.$B$BSpeak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus when you are done.",st="Directly east of Auberdine lay many moonkin caves.  The one closest to Auberdine has a Moonkin Stone inside it.  Lunaclaw, the defender of the stone, will face you only when Cenarion Moondust is applied to it.  Lunaclaw possesses within it a strength that you must use as one of the Claw.$B$BYou've earned the right to use this Cenarion Moondust, $n... now show me that you've earned the right to possess the strength of body and the strength of heart needed as a druid!",how={{"talk",12144}}},[6063]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,nx=6101,si=15921,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Webwood Lurker. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Dazalar in Dolanaar.",st="As a hunter, it is important to remember the responsibility you hold in your hands. Nature is not a power that can be bent to obey our desires; it is one that is to be respected and acknowledged as something stronger than your very existence.$B$B$n, you must prove your understanding of this before you will gain the ability to tame an animal to be your companion.$B$BYour first task is to take this taming rod. With it, you will be able to tame a webwood lurker. Tame it, and practice your skills as a hunter.",how={{"kill",1998}}},[6064]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,nx=6084,si=15911,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Large Crag Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.",st="Hi there, $Glad:lass;! So, you'd be wanting to know how you can gain a pet of your own?$B$BWell, let's get started. There's nothing more important than yer equipment when it comes to hunting, but we can chat about my new Shrapnel Blaster some other time. Fer now, let's focus on something I'm sure you're quite interested in: a pet!$B$BThe best way to learn is for you to try out several creatures as companions and see what ya like. So, find a large crag boar, then use the taming rod to tame it.",how={{"kill",1126}}},[6084]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6064},nx=6085,si=15913,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Snow Leopard. Practice your skills, then return to Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.",st="Those crag boars are quite burly; maybe you'd like something with a little more finesse? Alright then, I've got jus' the thing. South and east of here, you'll find large white cats called snow leopards. Just like an elegantly-carved rifle, behind their beautiful exterior lies a powerful fighter, capable of doing extreme damage. You'll find them to be much more agile an' swift than the boar you tamed.$B$BTake this taming rod and see how you like the snow leopard.",how={{"kill",1201}}},[6085]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6084},nx=6086,si=15908,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame an Ice Claw Bear. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.",st="Perhaps you'd like a creature that possesses little more than brute strength. The ice claw bear is an excellent companion for a fledgling hunter like yourself, and can be found east of Kharanos. Here is the taming rod; try this animal as a pet and see if ya like it!$B$BWhen you return, I'll give ya the skills you will need to tame an animal of your choosing; this creature will face the challenges you face, and gain experience alongside you. I will also show you how to call it and dismiss it as ya like.",how={{"kill",1196}}},[6086]={t="Training the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6085},ot="Speak with Belia Thundergranite in Ironforge.",st="$n, ya now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills ta train it.$B$BTravel to Ironforge and find the Hall of Arms. There you must speak to one of our most revered animal trainers, Belia Thundergranite. She'll give ya the power to train your new pet, so get goin', $Glad:lass;!$B$BBelia is a friendly sort; you should have no problems gaining her approval. Good luck, $n."},[6101]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6063},nx=6102,si=15922,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Nightsaber Stalker. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Dazalar in Dolanaar.",st="The variance of nature is something that can be relied upon, $n. It is predictable in the way that it never remains the same; it is always changing.$B$BThe tasks I give to you will help you to see and appreciate the vast differences of the creatures you may choose as your companion.$B$BTake this taming rod and use it to tame a nightsaber stalker, found to the south. Practice your skills as a hunter. Then you will begin to understand the similarities and differences of nature.",how={{"kill",2043}}},[6102]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6101},nx=6103,si=15923,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Strigid Screecher. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Dazalar in Dolanaar.",st="You have tamed two creatures that inhabit the land, now you must tame one that soars the skies. Use the taming rod to tame a strigid screecher, found west of here. Practice your skills with this mighty owl at your side.$B$BWhen you return, I will bestow you with the skills you will need to tame an animal of your choosing to be your companion; this creature will face the challenges you face, and gain experience alongside you. I will also show you how to call it and dismiss it as you wish.",how={{"kill",1996}}},[6103]={t="Training the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6102},ot="Speak to Jocaste in the Cenarion Enclave, in Darnassus.",st="You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it.$B$BTravel to Darnassus. There you must speak to one of our most revered hunters, Jocaste. She will give you the ability to train your new pet, so make haste.$B$BWhile Jocaste may seem stern, she is always pleased to see another hunter rising through the ranks. Treat her with respect and she will return in kind. Good luck, $n."},[6121]={t="Lessons Anew",lv=14,min=14,nx=6122,ot="Travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.",st="You're now ready to learn about poison and the power we as druids have over it, $n.  Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to purge even the most foul of poisons with but a mere incantation.  This gift is not to be taken lightly... and to ensure you learn this lesson, you'll work to address the effects of poisonings as a layman would.$B$BTravel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze; he awaits your arrival to begin your lesson."},[6122]={t="The Principal Source",lv=14,min=14,pre1={6121},nx=6123,si=15844,ot="Use the Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler to draw a sample of water from the mouth of the cave by the falls.$B$BDeliver the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, Darkshore.",st="The Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore serves as the principal source of drinking water for the region, and now I suspect it is the principal source of the poison that is harming the local fauna - deer specifically.  Use this sampler to draw some water from the mouth of the cave; be careful, as dangerous naga now reside in a cave by the falls.$B$BOnce filled, deliver it to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine.  She is the one that requested our aid, and you will work with her to address this malady.",how={{"open",15845,{19463}}}},[6123]={t="Gathering the Cure",lv=14,min=14,pre1={6122},nx=6124,ot="Bring 5 Earthroot and 12 Lunar Funguses to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine so she may make a curative salve.",st="The water will serve as the base of the curative salve I'll make for the deer.  For curative properties, I need some earthroot.  Herbalists know how to find it, so if we're unlucky and you aren't one then you'll need to find one to help us out.$B$BFinally for potency, I need some lunar fungus.  Finding lunar fungal blooms is easy enough; they're all over the place in caves just to the east of here.  Moonkin reside in the caves and they're irritable as of late, so be careful.",how={{"loot",2449,{2022}},{"open",15851,{177750}}}},[6124]={t="Curing the Sick",lv=14,min=14,pre1={6123},nx=6125,si=15826,ot="Use the Curative Animal Salve on 10 Sickly Deer that are located throughout Darkshore; doing so should cure them.  Sickly Deer have been reported starting south of the Cliffspring River to the north of Auberdine and extending all the way into southern Darkshore where the edge of Ashenvale begins.",st="The amount of salve made out of the reagents you brought me is good enough for ten doses, $n.  While I work with the village to try and make some more salve, I'd like for you to help us get a head start.  All around Darkshore are sickly deer; use the salve on them and cure their malaise.$B$BDendrite Starblaze in Moonglade will want to talk to you when you're done, I'm sure.  Please extend Auberdine's thanks to the Cenarion Circle there... and let me say thanks to you directly for the help you've given!",how={{"kill",12298}}},[6125]={t="Power over Poison",lv=14,min=14,pre1={6124},ot="Return to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.",st="You've learned what it means to cure poison without the benefit of spiritual aid.  Remember what others must endure in fighting poisonous afflictions as you soon embrace your newfound power over poison.$B$BYou should now return to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus, $n.  He, no doubt, has a very important spell to teach you now that the student understands the lesson given unto $g him : her;.$B$BFarewell, young druid.  We shall speak again."},[6181]={t="A Swift Message",lv=10,min=10,nx=6281,si=15998,ot="Bring Lewis' Note to Thor the gryphon master.",st="Although we don't get much aid from Stormwind directly, I do have a contact in the city who helps supply us with armor.  His name is Osric Strang.  His shop, Limited Immunity, is in the Old Town of Stormwind.$B$BOur supply of armor dwindles, and I must contact Osric for more.  Can you take him this note?$B$BThe fastest way to Stormwind is through Thor, our gryphon master.  He's just down the hill; bring him my note, and then take a gryphon to Stormwind."},[6261]={t="Dungar Longdrink",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6281},nx=6285,si=16115,ot="Bring Osric's Crate to Dungar Longdrink the gryphon master.",st="$n, I gathered into this crate everything Lewis asked for.  Can you take it to him?$B$BIf you've already spoken to Thor in Westfall, then you can take a gryphon back to him.  Dungar Longdrink is our gryphon master, over in the trade district.$B$BSpeak with Dungar, then get this crate to Lewis as fast as you can.  We don't want our fighting men and women in Westfall to go without fresh equipment!"},[6281]={t="Continue to Stormwind",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6181},nx=6261,si=15998,ot="Buy a gryphon ride from the gryphon master Thor, then bring Lewis' Note to Osric Strang, in the shop Limited Immunity, in the Old Town of Stormwind.",st="For a small fee, you can take a gryphon to Stormwind, so you can deliver Lewis' note to Osric.  You won't get there faster any other way.$B$BIf that sounds acceptable, then just speak to me again when you're ready for the ride.  I'll charge you a little, but trust me; it'll be worth it!"},[6285]={t="Return to Lewis",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6261},si=16115,ot="Buy a gryphon ride to Sentinel Hill from the gryphon master Dungar Longdrink, then take Osric's Crate to Lewis at Sentinel Hill.",st="The gryphon master in Westfall is Thor.  If you've spoken to him before, then you can take one of my gryphons to him.$B$BThat's a good lesson to know: gryphons are always trained to fly to their capital city, but they'll only take you to a remote gryphon master after you've already been there.$B$BYou've already been to Thor, so just speak with me again when you're ready to take a gryphon to Westfall.  Once there, you can deliver Osric's Crate to Quartermaster Lewis."},[6341]={t="The Bounty of Teldrassil",lv=10,min=10,nx=6342,si=16262,ot="Bring Nessa's Collection to Vesprystus.",st="The fishermen of Rut'theran village do very well, for the fish here are extremely large and abundant.  I would like to compare the bounty here with that of the mainland.$B$BI have a collection of fish bones and scales that I would like taken to a colleague of mine in Darkshore.  His name is Laird, he is a fish vendor in the village of Auberdine.$B$BBring my collection to our hippogryph master, Vesprystus, and speak to him about traveling to Auberdine."},[6342]={t="Flight to Auberdine",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6341},nx=6343,si=16262,ot="Ride a hippogryph to Auberdine from the hippogryph master Vesprystus, then bring Nessa's Collection to Laird.",st="From Rut'theran, there are two methods of travel to Auberdine: by ferry and by hippogryph.  Both are quick and reliable, but if you have not yet flown to Auberdine by hippogryph, then I suggest you do.$B$BIt is sound advice to speak with the hippogryph master in every town that has one.  Once you speak to the master, you can then fly there from other towns.$B$BHere is Nessa's collection.  Speak with me again when you are ready to fly to Auberdine and deliver Nessa's collection to Laird."},[6343]={t="Return to Nessa",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6342},si=16263,ot="Bring Laird's Response to Nessa Shadowsong.",st="I must send a response to Nessa.  She'll be very interested to know how different the fish here are from those along Teldrassil's coastline.  We can only guess the cause, but it is my suspicion that the world tree itself is affecting the wildlife around it!$B$BPlease, take this response to Nessa.  If you wish to take a hippogryph back to Rut'theran then speak with the hippogryph master Caylais Moonfeather.  If you wish to take the ferry, then one regularly departs from the dock to the northwest."},[6344]={t="Nessa Shadowsong",lv=10,min=10,nx=6341,bc=6341,ot="Speak with Nessa Shadowsong.",st="A friend of mine, Nessa Shadowsong, is a fishing merchant in Rut'theran Village.  She needs a parcel taken to Darkshore, and is looking for someone to help her.$B$BIf you're interested, then to reach Nessa you must take the portal in Darnassus to Rut'theran Village.  You will find the portal west of the Temple Gardens."},[6387]={t="Honor Students",lv=10,min=10,nx=6391,si=16310,ot="Bring Brock's List to Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar.",st="I see a lot of young dwarves at my door, eager to learn the trade of mining.  And if there's one thing a miner needs more than anything, it's a pick!$B$BI have a list of mining students who scored high in their lessons and earned an honorary pick.  Take my list to Golnir Bouldertoe in Ironforge.  He'll get the picks ready.$B$BThe fastest way to Ironforge is on a gryphon, so bring the list to our gryphon master, Thorgrum Borrelson, and speak with him about transport to Ironforge."},[6388]={t="Gryth Thurden",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6391},nx=6392,si=16311,ot="Bring the Honorary Picks to Gryth Thurden in Ironforge.",st="Here are the honorary picks for Brock's students.  If you've already been to Thelsamar, then you should fly a gryphon back there!$B$BTake the picks to our gryphon master, Gryth Thurden, and speak with him about a ride back to Thelsamar."},[6391]={t="Ride to Ironforge",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6387},nx=6388,si=16310,ot="Buy a gryphon to Ironforge from the gryphon master Thorgrum Borrelson, then bring Brock's List to Golnir Bouldertoe in Ironforge.",st="For just a few coins, one of my gryphons will take you to Ironforge.  From there, deliver Brock's list to Golnir Bouldertoe.  You'll find him in the Deep Mountain Mining Guild.  That's in the Great Forge District of Ironforge, which is right where my gryphon will drop you off!$B$BSpeak to me again when you're ready for the journey."},[6392]={t="Return to Brock",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6388},si=16311,ot="Buy a gryphon to Thelsamar from the gryphon master Gryth Thurden, then bring the Honorary Picks to Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar.",st="For a small fee you can buy a gryphon ride to Thelsamar... as long as you've already been there.  Gryphons will only fly you to places you've already been, so be sure to speak with every gryphon master you see so you can fly to him later.$B$BYou've already been to Thorgrum, the gryphon master of Thelsamar, so now you can return to him.  And once in Thelsamar, you can deliver the picks to Brock Stoneseeker.$B$BSpeak with me when you're ready to go."},[6607]={t="Nat Pagle, Angler Extreme",lv=45,min=35,ot="Nat Pagle wants you to catch the following fish:  Misty Reed Mahi Mahi from the Misty Reed Strand in the Swamp of Sorrows.  A Sar'theris Striker from the Sar'theris Strand in Desolace.  Feralas Ahi from the Verdantis River of Feralas.  Savage Coast Blue Sailfin from the Savage Coast of Stranglethorn Vale.  Return to Nat Pagle when you have reeled them all in!",how={{"open",16967,{400006}},{"open",16970,{400007}},{"open",16968,{400008}},{"open",16969,{400009}}}},[6661]={t="Deeprun Rat Roundup",lv=12,min=10,nx=6662,si=17117,ot="Capture 5 Deeprun Rats by using the Rat Catcher's Flute. Lead the rats back to Monty. Don't forget to turn in the flute when you're finished.",st="Avast ye scallywag. Arrrr... Arrrr ye looking fer work? We gots a serious rat problem down here an' not enough hands on the poop deck.$B$BWhat do ye say? All ye needs to do is take this here rat catchin' flute and play the melody around the vermin. They'll follow ye to the ends of the world!$B$BJust capture five of the little buggers and bring em back here. We needs em alive.$B$BArrrrr...",how={{"kill",13016}}},[6662]={t="Me Brother, Nipsy",lv=12,min=10,pre1={6661},si=17118,ot="Take the Carton of Mystery Meat to Nipsy at the Stormwind Deeprun Tram Depot.",st="Me brother, Nipsy, runs a rat kabob operation on the other side of Deeprun. Ye needs to take this here crate o' rats to him before they go bad. Get a move on!$B$BYe have ridden a tram before, aye? It's easy. Just step aboard when she arrives and enjoy the ride. An' keep yer arms and legs inside durin' the ride, lest ye be peglegged fer life."},[6981]={t="The Glowing Shard",lv=26,min=15,si=10441,ot="Travel to Ratchet to find someone that can tell you more about the glowing shard.$B$BThen, deliver the shard as you are directed.",st="The shard is a brilliant green, and although solid, what looks like smoke swirls just below the surface. You can't help staring into the depths of the crystal; at the same time, you know there is something very disturbing about it.$B$BMaybe you should see if anyone in Ratchet can tell you more about this strange shard.",how={{"talk",3442}}},[7383]={t="Crown of the Earth",lv=11,min=1,pre1={933},nx=935,si=18152,ot="Fill the Amethyst Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",st="All was not well with Teldrassil, however. Staghelm's carefully made plans for the new World Tree had borne out as he had hoped, but there was one small problem, a problem to which many of the troubles on Teldrassil may be attributed.$b$bHowever, I will not get into that yet. You must visit the last moonwell, to the northwest in the Oracle Glade. Under the boughs of the Oracle Tree lies the first and most powerful of our wells. Retrieve a phial of its water and return to me.",how={{"open",18151,{19552}}}},[65602]={t="What Is Love?",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1716},nx=65603,si=190307,ot="Retrieve the Wooden Figurine and bring it to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.",st="You will need a powerful reagent to tempt an incubus -- an object that represents great devotion and love.\r\n\r\nWith my scrying, I have located a small figurine that should be suitable for your ritual.\r\n\r\nThousands of years ago, the figurine belonged to a young couple. The original owners are no more, but their keepsake has survived to the present day.\r\n\r\nFollow the road north into Ashenvale, then west and past Maestra's Post. You will see a house nestled amongst the trees. There you will find what you seek.",how={{"open",190309,{375544}}}},[65603]={t="The Binding",lv=20,min=20,pre1={65602},ot="Using the Wooden Figurine, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Wooden Figurine to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Slaughtered Lamb.",st="The time has come. Take the figurine and descend into the crypts below. A summoning circle has been prepared, and you must place the figurine at its center.\r\n\r\nThen the gateway will open, and the incubus will cross into our world.\r\n\r\nA sayaad is not to be underestimated. The demon will not hesitate to attack when it realizes your ruse. You must draw upon all you have been taught to defeat it.\r\n\r\nIf you succeed, return to me and I shall bind the creature to your will. Fail, and your soul is forfeit.",how={{"kill",185335}}},[79008]={t="... and that note you found",lv=22,min=14,nx=79192,ot="Charred remains of the note serve as your only guide."},[86574]={t="Stonetalon Supply Run",lv=24,min=20,si=277915,ot="Collect $1oa Stonetalon Supplies from Pridewing Wyverns and deliver them to Innkeeper Faralia.",st="<The unfortunate body here bears the marks of many strikes from the Pridewing wyverns. The pack nearby is rumpled and discarded, with its contents missing, and only a small note clutched in the courier's hand to indicate what was lost: a shipment meant for Innkeeper Faralia at Stonetalon Peak.>\r\n\r\n<The wyverns have probably carried off the supply bundles to line their nests.>",how={{"loot",277917,{4013,4015,4014}}}},[86585]={t="Banner of the Fallen",lv=17,min=10,si=253247,ot="Raise the standard of Ironforge, call out the trogg Headsplitter and kill it, then report to Captain Rugelfuss.",st="The fallen mountaineer bears a standard of Ironforge. Perhaps she was scouting, or making a doomed charge. Either way, the standard has been cast down and trampled. The mountaineer was hit on the head so hard that her helm was knocked off and she was killed outright by a trogg, likely with a spiked club.\r\n\r\nThe trogg that killed her is probably still nearby, and likely remembers the banner. Raising the banner of Ironforge once more may call it out.",how={{"kill",269185}}},[86613]={t="Excavation Tools",lv=18,min=13,si=278398,ot="Return $1oa Excavation Tools to Magmar Fellhew.",st="The excavation's tools, left behind when the dwarves fled from the troggs, seem mostly untouched. Returning them to the excavators will surely aid their work.",how={{"open",278398,{665282}}}},[86614]={t="Silver of the Waves",lv=20,min=13,si=278051,ot="Return the Monogrammed Silver Hair clip to its owner.",st="<Among the fishing knickknacks in the debris are some rusty hooks, broken spools of wire, and a slightly corroded but ornate silver hair clip with the monogram \"K.D.\">"},[86667]={t="Snowbound",lv=10,min=10,si=279380,ot="Deliver a Jar of Snow to Norric Lochthane at his house on the northwest coast of the Loch.",st="My old mentor, Norric, sent a minor elemental with an odd request. He needs a jar of snow for some of his shamanic workings! I don't know what he's going to do with that, but I learned a long time ago not to question his ways with respect to magic.\r\n\r\nI'm busy learning about the local elementals, so I can't leave to help him. Go to the tunnel entrance at South Gate Pass where there's snow year-round. Scoop some up in this ceramic jar and bring it to him before it melts. The jar should keep it cold.",how={{"loot",279379}}},[86758]={t="Twisting the Knife",lv=16,min=12,ot="Find and defeat the crocolisk Daggerfang and bring back Marek's knife.",st="Did I ever tell you how I almost lost me hand to a crocolisk? Managed to jam me knife into its jaw, and scrambled out real quick. I thought I had the knife around here somewhere, but I can't seem to find it.\r\n\r\nAnyway, that croc is probably still out there hunting along the edge of the lake. That nasty brute probably needs to go, for the safety of the other hunters, if nothing else.\r\n\r\nI've taken to calling it Daggerfang. If you see it, give it a friendly hello from me! And by \"hello\" I mean \"stab.\"",how={{"loot",279591,{270693}}}},[87288]={t="Soft Saber Pelts",lv=7,min=4,ot="Bring $1oa Soft Nightsaber Pelts to Aldria.",st="Hello, traveler! I hope you are enjoying your visit to our village. I like Dolanaar because it is small and rustic and everyone is friendly.\r\n\r\nI'm a local trader, and I bring in all sorts of tools and trinkets that might be useful to you in your travels. Indeed, if you are interested in a trade, I find myself in need of some nightsaber pelts. While these majestic creatures are beautiful, the local ones are rather aggressive, so don't feel too bad about defending yourself.",how={{"loot",280087,{2042}}}},[87760]={t="Holy Diver",lv=20,min=15,pre={4722,4723,4725,4727,4728,4730,4731,4732,4733},ot="Find a Stormscale Beastmistress, slay her, and bring back her Rod of Deep Dominion.",st="I have received word back from Darnassus, $n!\r\n\r\nFrom the animal samples, we learned that the naga dominated these sea creatures to use as unwilling mounts and beasts of burden. The ones that were too obstinate, or too old or badly injured, they drove out for sport. Monstrous!\r\n\r\nIt is our sacred duty to put a stop to this!\r\n\r\nThe naga have forces in the Ruins of Mathystra, and they must be seizing threshers from off the shore. Find their beastmistress, slay her, and bring back her tools of domination!",how={{"loot",280686,{271903}}}},[91723]={t="Delicate Instruments",lv=8,min=6,nx=91724,ot="Kill 8 Kobold Geomancers in Jasperlode Mine, then return to Hamish Bergwort in the Tower of Azora.",st="Blast it! Every time I try to calibrate these sensitive arcane instruments, they get thrown off again by a surge of energy.\r\nThe surges seem to be coming from the north, where those primitive Kobolds have been practicing their crude magic. Could you clear some of them out, so I can continue my work?",how={{"kill",476}}},[91724]={t="Delicate Instruments",lv=10,min=6,pre1={91723},ot="Kill $1oa Defias Rogue Wizards at Stone Cairn Lake, then return to Hamish Bergwort in the Tower of Azora.",st="Almost there, and... By the Nether! Something is still disrupting my instruments.\r\n\r\nThis is most frustrating, $n. I have heard rumors that the local bandits have been practicing spells near Stone Cairn Lake. Maybe if you stop them, these disruptions will finally cease and I can get some work done?",how={{"kill",474}}},[91725]={t="Stolen Enchanting Supplies",lv=10,min=7,ot="Collect 5 Stolen Enchanting Supplies from gnoll camps around Stone Cairn Lake, then return to Blixie Fitzwink near the Tower of Azora.",st="I was sent by Master Theocritus to pick up some enchanting supplies from the trading post, but on the way back I was ambushed by a pack of gnolls!\r\n\r\nI dropped the package and escaped, but if I return without it, I'll be cleaning up after the polymorph experiments for weeks as punishment! Do you think you could find the supplies for me?",how={{"open",247805,{561159}}}},[91732]={t="Good Steel",lv=7,min=6,ot="Collect 4 Mining Tools from Jasperlode Mine, then return to Hagar Lowe in Eastvale Logging Camp.",st="Good steel is in short supply after the war, and our tools have suffered for it. The Jasperlode miners used finely-crafted picks, and I imagine some of them are still there in the depths of the mine. Could you retrieve some for me, and I'll see if I can repurpose the steel?",how={{"open",247816,{562114}}}},[91733]={t="Downstream",lv=10,min=7,ot="Collect the Waterlogged Axe, Waterlogged Saw, and Waterlogged Toolbox that have washed downstream from Eastvale Logging Camp, then return to Ormin Pelford.",st="I was bringing back a supply shipment from the trading post, but my wagon tipped over and the supplies fell in the river! Before I could catch them, they had already washed downstream.\r\n\r\nBetween the murlocs and wolves down there, I don't stand a chance of retrieving the supplies on my own. You seem like the hardy sort. Do you think you could find them for me?",how={{"open",247817,{562105}},{"open",247813,{562103}},{"open",247818,{562106}}}},[91740]={t="Croaky's Head",lv=11,min=7,si=247826,ot="Deliver Croaky's Head to Merell Ross at Ridgepoint Tower.",st="This murloc has no doubt been terrorizing the local roads for some time. You suspect the nearby watch guards will want to know of its demise."},[91741]={t="Nibbled-On Book",lv=2,min=1,nx=92124,si=247857,ot="Return the book to Brother Paxton.",st="<One of the kobolds dropped this book. It looks like the kobold might have tried to eat it.\r\n\r\nBrother Paxton inside the abbey has a small library he maintains. The book must have come from there.>"},[91743]={t="Rascally Rodents",lv=2,min=1,pre1={92124},nx=91745,ot="Retrieve $1oa Stolen Books from kobolds in Northshire Valley and return them to Brother Paxton.",st="Those awful kobolds are eating my books! You have to get them back before they devour my whole library.",how={{"loot",247839,{257,6}}}},[91745]={t="Mining Consultant",lv=3,min=1,pre1={91743},nx=91752,ot="Talk to Kelsey Fargo outside the Echo Ridge Mine in Northshire Valley.",st="Go talk to the new mining apprentice, Kelsey Fargo. She works right outside the mine and has probably seen what the kobolds are up to. Maybe she can teach you a thing or two about mining while you're at it."},[91746]={t="Elmpaw's Head",lv=12,min=7,si=247862,ot="Deliver Elmpaw's Head to Helene Peltskinner near Goldshire.",st="The trophy serves as an impressive reminder of your victory over Elmpaw. A local hunter or skinner might be interested to hear the story."},[91751]={t="Rough Wolf Pelts",lv=8,min=5,ot="Skin wolves around Elwynn Forest to obtain $1oa Rough Wolf Pelts, then deliver them to Helene Peltskinner near Goldshire.",st="Are you looking for an opportunity to practice skinning? My husband usually helps with hunting wolves, but he's busy up by the abbey. I could use a hand collecting more pelts to finish the orders I'm working on.",how={{"loot",247877,{118}}}},[91752]={t="The Big Picture",lv=3,min=1,pre1={91745},nx=91758,ot="Retrieve a Sack of \"Picture\" Books from Shinyfinder Narf. Bring the sack to Marshal McBride just inside Northshire's Abbey.",st="Every once in a while, a kobold comes through yelling \"Picture for Narf!\" I don't know who Narf is. Maybe one of the head kobolds at the back of the mine? I bet he has a whole sack of books by now.\r\n\r\nGo get those books and bring them to our local law enforcement, Marshal McBride. You should find a friend to help. Those kobolds inside the mine are a lot meaner.",how={{"loot",247886,{248362}}}},[91753]={t="An Enchanting Lesson",lv=7,min=5,ot="Kitta Firewind in the Tower of Azora wants you to collect 3 Luminous Residue.\r\n\r\nLuminous Residue can be obtained by disenchanting Crude Wax Effigies dropped by Kobold Geomancers.",st="Academic rigor is of course essential to the enchanter's craft, but a practical foundation can pay dividends. Consider, as an example, the lowly Kobold. Lacking formal education, they nevertheless demonstrate a sort of innate aptitude for simple cantrips and enchantments.\r\n\r\nObtain some of their wax effigies and deconstruct the enchantments bound within them. You may find it elucidating.",how={{"kill",476}}},[91758]={t="Follow That Kobold!",lv=4,min=1,pre1={91752},nx=91772,ot="Speak to Tordrin Sternblade near the stable behind Northshire's Abbey.",st="You're not done with those kobolds yet. We just got word from Kelsey that a kobold left the mine carrying a large sack of books. I need you to track down this kobold so we can retrieve the books for Brother Paxton.\r\n\r\nGo talk to Tordrin Sternblade. He's the new Hunter trainer that just arrived from Ironforge. You can find him behind the abbey, near the stable. He can help you track this kobold thief."},[91772]={t="Shhh! We're Hunting Kobolds",lv=4,min=1,pre1={91758},nx=91775,si=247970,ot="Follow the kobold tracks and report to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire with your findings and the Kobold Tracking Kit.",st="Alright. Take this kobold tracking kit. It'll let ye' track the kobold that Marshal McBride is concerned with.\r\n\r\nFollow the tracks and bring what ye' find to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.\r\n\r\nI have a feelin' these varmints are up to somethin' outside Northshire. So ye'll be needin' Dughan's help.",how={{"click",563442}}},[91775]={t="Book Return",lv=6,min=1,pre1={91772},nx=91777,si=279935,ot="Find 6 Lost Books and \"Fun with Elementals\" and return them to Marshal Dughan.",st="While you're investigating the Fargodeep Mine, see if you can find any of Brother Paxton's books to return. In particular, Paxton is very concerned about a book titled, \"Fun with Elementals\". He thinks even a kobold could use it to summon an elemental servant. Be warned, the depths of the mine are fairly dangerous. You should bring friends.\r\n\r\nTake this book bag to protect the books when you find them!",how={{"loot",248002,{248464}},{"loot",248001,{475}}}},[91777]={t="Rare Books",lv=7,min=1,pre1={91775},ot="Recover \"Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards\" and \"Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words\" and return them to Brother Paxton inside Northshire's Abbey.",st="There are just two books left missing on Brother Paxton's list: \"Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards\" and \"Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words\".\r\n\r\nThe kobolds must have taken them to the Jasperlode Mine. Please track down those two books and bring them back to Brother Paxton.\r\n\r\nBut I'm afraid it will be quite dangerous. If the \"apprentice\" kobold was summoning an elemental, who knows what the master can do. I'd bring some friends if I were you.",how={{"loot",248003,{248474}},{"loot",248004,{471}}}},[92109]={t="My First Alchemy Set",lv=10,min=10,nx=92110,ot="Bring 5 Empty Vials, 5 Silverleaf, and 5 Peacebloom to the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.",st="Erm... 'Ello, $Gmister:miss;. I'm not supposed to talk to strangers, but... Hey, what are those shiny bottles sticking out of your backpack for? Are you an alchemist? That's so cool!\r\n\r\nWhen I grow up, I want to be an alchemist too. Daddy won't let me play with any of his herbs; too dangerous, he says.\r\n\r\nWell, I want to start learning now. Could you maybe get some supplies for me, pretty please?",how={{"buy",3371,{843,8934,2481}},{"loot",2447,{2022}},{"loot",765,{2022,275703}}}},[92110]={t="My First Real Potion",lv=10,min=10,pre1={92109},ot="Gather 3 Murloc Eyes for the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.",st="Wow, my very first potion! Did you know that mixing those two herbs together would change the potion to a bright red color when you first started?\r\n\r\nThat was fun, but mixing a few flowers doesn't seem like the kind of alchemy Daddy does. He uses other ingredients too.\r\n\r\nI don't know what else to use, so let's try the first thing that comes to mind! Let's see... maybe murloc eyes? That sounds so gross, but I bet something will happen.",how={{"loot",730,{456,126,515}}}},[92124]={t="Book Inventory",lv=2,min=1,pre1={91741},nx=91743,ot="Speak to Daniel, Brother Paxton's assistant in the library.",st="We need to take stock of how many books are missing!\r\n\r\nGo talk to my useless assistant, Daniel. He can do a quick inventory and let us know how serious the problem is.\r\n\r\nHe's obsessed with the various trade professions in Elwynn Forest. The boy keeps focusing on those instead of his important work helping me.\r\n\r\nDon't let him prattle on about tradeskills, and find out what's happened to my books!"},[92415]={t="Remember That I Love You",lv=22,min=15,nx=95161,si=251522,ot="Bring the Blood-Stained Letter to Orphan Matron Nightingale in Stormwind City.",st="<A torn and stained bundle of parchment has barely survived the undead trodden grounds of the graveyard. It mentions a missing child of the Heartweaver family. Perhaps the orphan matron in Stormwind City will know more.>"},[92432]={t="An Alarming Request",lv=33,min=30,ot="Report to the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.",st="I bring ill tidings from Dalaran. Something has disrupted our leylines, causing erratic and destructive behavior from our constructs in the city.\r\n\r\nWe know not yet what is causing this mayhem. The high council has ordered us to keep this matter private so as to not bring shame to our order. But we cannot keep up this charade forever. The city is being overrun as we speak!\r\n\r\nArchmage Modera has dispatched me to solicit outside aid. Seek her image out near Dalaran beside Lordamere Lake."},[92456]={t="A Green Sample",lv=33,min=24,ot="Collect a Fel Infused Blossom from the City of Dalaran for Shylamiir in Stormwind City.",st="If you're going to bother me you can at least make yourself useful. I have an errand I need run.\r\n\r\nFor a city of mages, Dalaran has a surprising interest in botany. The Kirin Tor keep to themselves, but I would love a sample of their mana-infused vegetation.\r\n\r\nYou're clearly someone who is comfortable being where people don't want you, maybe you could find a way into the city. If you do, bring me back whatever is growing in their central garden.",how={{"open",251983,{553757}}}},[92457]={t="Starving Arcane",lv=33,min=24,ot="Defeat $1oa Seeking Remnants, $2oa Saturated Remnants, and $3oa Mana Echoes inside the City of Dalaran for Archmage Modera outside of Dalaran.",st="The breach has affected many of our factotums and enchantments throughout the city, including many that are seeing to our defenses. This fragmented arcane energy has spoken to rogue elementals who seek to saturate themselves in this free flowing magic.\r\n\r\nWhile we are busy tending to the wards and other major incidents, it would be a favor to the Kirin Tor if you could cull this elemental throng.",how={{"kill",247003},{"kill",247001},{"kill",246600}}},[92458]={t="Heart of Disruption",lv=33,min=24,pre={92432},si=277507,ot="Collect the Arcane Mote for the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.",st="Whatever disturbed the leylines, it started at the top of the Violet Citadel. A thunderous crash rang out from the parlors above, and now we are overrun with rampant arcane power. It's taking all we have just to keep the wards in place.\r\n\r\nWe cannot afford to stall any longer. We need help.\r\n\r\nThe Kirin Tor are busy inside, but you will still need a less public approach to gain entry. Take this key and meet me in the citadel once you've made your way into the city. We must put an end to this disruption.",how={{"loot",251961,{246020,250657}}}},[92460]={t="Coming of Age",lv=1,min=1,nx=92461,ot="Speak with Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.",st="Look at you, bright eyed and ready for adventure! We need all the help we can get here in Thendal Village and your arrival is most welcome. I imagine you are brimming with nerves for what is to come. After all, you only get to come of age once in a lifetime.\r\n\r\nGo, seek out our village leader Rorian the Dayseeker at the entrance to the greatfather tree just west of here. He will get you started on your journey."},[92461]={t="Harmony in Balance",lv=1,min=1,pre1={92460},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Slay 8 Vuldren Juveniles in Thendal Grove.",st="We live in times of great uncertainty for our people. We face unprecedented challenges that may require bold solutions, but we also must contend with the ordinary and mundane here in Thendal Grove. Take, for example, the recent unsustainable rise in the vuldren population.\r\n\r\nThe vuldren are a vital part of our ecosystem. However, imbalances must be corrected to maintain the delicate harmony that all creatures in Thendal Grove share.\r\n\r\nHead east and cull some of the vuldren there.",how={{"kill",250873}}},[92462]={t="Infestation Investigation",lv=2,min=1,pre1={92460},nx=92463,ot="Slay 8 Pesky Cirrusflies in Thendal Grove.",st="One of our rangers recently reported an infestation of cirrusflies here in Thendal Grove. \r\n\r\nCirrusflies can be dangerous if the swarm is allowed to grow too large, so please head to the eastern end of the Grove and exterminate as many as you can.",how={{"kill",251169}}},[92463]={t="The Cirrusfly Queen",lv=3,min=2,pre1={92462},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Destroy the Cirrusfly Queen in Thendal Grove.",st="If the forest is as thick with these insects as it sounds, simply killing the workers won't be enough.\r\n\r\nGo deeper into the forest and find the queen. She'll be close to the hive and surrounded by bigger and more aggressive soldiers, so be careful.\r\n\r\nPut her down and return here when it's done. That'll be one less problem to think about around here.",how={{"kill",251404}}},[92464]={t="Elemental Unrest",lv=3,min=2,pre={92461},ot="Speak to Yala Windwatcher in Thendal Grove.",st="Ever since our elemental benefactors left us, it seems that we are simply moving from one unrest to another. The problem we face now is that the manifestations of the winds near the standing stones to the northeast are agitated.\r\n\r\nNot truly self-aware like the sentient wind spirits that once lived here, these simple sprites respond in kind to forces, emotions, and intentions of the creatures around them. \r\n\r\nMy apprentice Yala Windwatcher went to observe them. Seek her out and discover what she's learned."},[92465]={t="Agitators",lv=3,min=2,pre={92464},nx=92469,ot="Slay $2oa Roiling Winds and $1oa Al'Aketh Converts in Thendal Grove.",st="The Al'Aketh cult is a blight upon this island. These cultists are surely the ones responsible for agitating the simple wind sprites that reside here and turning them violent.\r\n\r\nRegrettably, we'll need to disperse these roiling winds here before they harm someone. We also need to send a clear message to the cult that they are not welcome in the grove.\r\n\r\nWill you lend me your aid, $c?",how={{"kill",251160},{"kill",251143}}},[92469]={t="Return to Rorian",lv=4,min=3,pre1={92465},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Bring word of the Al'Aketh to Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.",st="You've done enough here, $c. I'll stay and clean up any stragglers down there.\r\n\r\nHead back to the Village and tell Rorian about the cult's presence. He will not be pleased."},[92470]={t="Foul Matriarch",lv=5,min=2,pre1={92471},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=4,[7]=2,[8]=3,[11]=2},ot="Slay 8 Ursera Scavengers and collect the head of the den mother, Urs'anah in Thendal Grove.",st="Rorian informed you that I've been watching you. I now offer you a test of resolve. However, be warned--it will send you into great danger.\r\n\r\nGo to the caves to the west. Thin out the ursera's numbers there, and find their matriarch, one the rangers call \"Urs'anah\". Put her down and bring me proof of her demise. Once you have done that, you will have taken an important step on your path.",how={{"kill",250937},{"loot",252665,{251115}}}},[92471]={t="Aetheen of the Gales",lv=4,min=4,pre={92469},ot="Speak with Aetheen of the Gales in Thendal Grove.",st="You may not realize this but everything you've done has been a trial of sorts. A test for what is to come for you. It's a big island out there, and Zephras needs spirited young adventurers such as yourself if we are to survive the trials our people face.\r\n\r\nThe one called Aetheen of the Gales is one of the leaders of our people here on Zephras Isle, and she has been watching you. She has a task that you must complete. Speak with her to learn more."},[92472]={t="The Next Step",lv=5,min=3,pre1={92470},ot="Report to Constable Aonda in Shen'dar Village.",st="One of the most pervasive threats on Zephras Isle is the Al'Aketh Cult. They are religious zealots devoted to the worship of the supposed elemental ruler of Skywall, Al'Akir the Windlord. They are brutal, single-minded, and their power and ambitions are growing more deadly by the day.\r\n\r\nYour path will soon take you to Shen'dar Village to the south. Present yourself to Constable Aonda when you arrive. The cult threatens Shen'dar and they are in need of aid. Tell Aonda that I sent you."},[92473]={t="Aggressive Encroachment",lv=4,min=3,pre1={92471},pre={92471},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Collect 6 Scrawny Ursera Claws from Scrawny Ursera in Thendal Grove.",st="The ursera den to the southwest is rapidly becoming a problem. Just last week the rangers had to kill an adolescent ursera who wandered too close to the village and attempted to attack a boy playing near the base of the elder tree in the center of the village.\r\n\r\nWe were fortunate that the boy escaped with his life. Hunger and desperation makes these beasts too dangerous to be left unchecked. Go south and put the scrawniest among the ursera down. Bring me their claws as proof when it is done.",how={{"loot",251918,{250926}}}},[92474]={t="Falling With Style",lv=2,min=2,ot="Jump from the top of the watchtower in Thendal Grove and use your Walk on Air ability to slow your fall.",st="Well hello there, $n! Want to play a game?\r\n\r\nAll you've got to do is step up on that ledge... then jump! Use your innate ability to walk on the air to slow your fall and see how far forward you can float.\r\n\r\nThe rules are made up and the points don't matter, but you get bonus points if you can land right in front of Rorian the Dayseeker and startle him! He won't like it but I'll certainly get a good laugh if you can get him all worked up! Hah!"},[92479]={t="A Scribbled Letter",lv=1,min=1,pre1={7},pre={7},si=251941,ot="Read the Scribbled Letter and speak to Tordrin Stemblade in Northshire Abbey.",st="I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the mark of Tordrin Stemblade, our local hunter trainer. Take a moment to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey."},[92481]={t="A Student of the Arcane",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282416,ot="Examine the Glowing Recall Crystal, then speak with Dorii Brightwhisper in Thendal Grove.",st="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident mage trainer--Dorii Brightwhisper--left this recall crystal for you. It contains some sort of message for you, so give it a look. Afterwards, you can find Dorii in the structure just behind me."},[92482]={t="The Way of the Hunter",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282421,ot="Read the Scribbled Note and then speak with Tai'ree Farsight in Thendal Grove.",st="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident hunter trainer--Tai'ree Farsight--left this note for you. You can find her just over yonder near the center of the village. Read the note then seek her out."},[92483]={t="At Home in the Shadows",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282422,ot="Read the Simple Note then speak with Akeri Duskblade within the watchtower in Thendal Grove.",st="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident rogue trainer--Akeri Duskblade--has requested to speak with you. He left this note, so read that first, then seek him out inside the watchtower, here in the village.\r\n\r\nHe's a shady fellow, but then again, so are you. I think you'll get along well."},[92485]={t="A Student of Nature",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282420,ot="Read the Folded Parchment then speak with Xyton Silverwind in Thendal Grove.",st="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident druid trainer--Xyton Silverwind--left this note for you. Read it as soon as you can, and then seek out Silverwind on the ground floor of this great tree just behind me.\r\n\r\nHeed his words and his counsel, he can teach you much."},[92489]={t="Power Overwhelming",lv=33,min=24,ot="Slay the Mana Elemental in the City of Dalaran for High Sorcerer Andromath in Stormwind City.",st="The Kirin Tor have long been allies of the Alliance. With the destruction of their city at the hands of the arch demon Archimonde, the once proud city of mages has now become reclusive and distrusting of outsiders.\r\n\r\nIn recent years they have begun reconstruction efforts to bring the city of Dalaran back to its former glory. However, reports show they are struggling to contain an outbreak of wayward arcane energies.\r\n\r\nWe must help them disperse these attacks lest we lose one of our most powerful allies.",how={{"kill",246016}}},[92515]={t="The Problem With Prideclaws",lv=6,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Collect 10 Prideclaw Pelts from the Prideclaws in Shen'dar Highlands.",st="As if bandits and mad cultists weren't enough, the hills are thick with prideclaws as well right now. They are starting to encroach on the village borders and growing bolder by the day. It's only a matter of time before someone's pet or child is taken. It would be a mercy for us to cull their numbers now rather than after some tragedy occurs.\r\n\r\nBring me a dozen or so of their pelts. I can turn them into all sorts of goods that will be of aid to the village.",how={{"loot",252670,{251245}}}},[92516]={t="Hippogryph Harassment",lv=7,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Slay 8 Hippogryph Youths, 6 Hippogryph Protectors and a Hippogryph Matriarch in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="A flock of Hippogryph have recently established nesting grounds southeast of Shen'dar Village and they've been wreaking havoc on travelers on the road. I need someone to head down there and thin them out for us.",how={{"kill",251291},{"kill",251284},{"kill",251261}}},[92517]={t="The Criminal Element",lv=7,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},nx=93036,rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Kill 10 Highlands Bandits and their leader, \"Badwind\" Bennic in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="There's a cave not far to the north, hidden behind a waterfall. It's well known to me that there's a group of bandits that are operating out of that cave. They were a problem for us before the cult arrived, but now they are a real terror. I can't spare the people to go and clear them out, unfortunately.\r\n\r\nI need you to go there and take care of them for me. Kill as many as you can, and if possible, take out their leader, the one they call \"Badwind\" Bennic. That cave is dangerous, so be careful.",how={{"kill",251918},{"kill",255534}}},[92528]={t="Among the Faithful",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92529},rwc={[1]=2,[3]=3,[4]=2,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Look around Falaath Village to learn about the cult's intentions in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="The faithful of Al'Akir grow ever stronger with each eager new recruit like yourself. As you can see, our strength gives form to the storm itself!\r\n\r\nNormally I'd send you straight to Skypriest Aanders for assessment, but he is occupied at present receiving a guest at the inn on the north side of town. Please avoid that place for now. An unshaven recruit like yourself in the presence of such a guest would be inappropriate.\r\n\r\nFor now, just don't get in anyone's way.",how={{"kill",254128}}},[92529]={t="Falaath Village",lv=8,min=5,pre1={93036},nx=92528,ot="Report to Missionary Jasaan near the entrance to Falaath Village.\r\n\r\nIf you lose your Mark of Akir, speak with Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village to regain the effect.",st="It gladdens my heart that you wish to serve Al'Akir. Our current trials as a people stem from our own complacency. We grew prideful and took the bounty of the winds for granted. The stagnation that followed is the reason the spirits of the wind abandoned us.\r\n\r\nOnly through acts of contrition may we feel the wind's caress once more. If you seek the fellowship of like-minded shen'dorei, go to Falaath Village and find Missionary Jasaan there. I will mark you so that the faithful will know you as a recruit."},[92532]={t="The Warrior's Path",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282419,ot="Read the Crumpled Note you've been given, then seek out Blademaster Ren inside the Thendal Village watchtower.",st="While you were gone our warrior trainer--Blademaster Ren--requested that we send you their way when you returned. She dropped this note off for you as well.\r\n\r\nGive it a read, then find Blademaster Ren inside the village watchtower."},[92544]={t="Al'Aketh Thugs",lv=5,min=2,ot="Slay 6 Al'Aketh Brutes, 4 Al'Aketh Neophytes, and Malduko Cloudcrush in Thendal Grove.",st="A band of Al'Aketh cult ruffians have taken up residence near the temple ruins just southwest of here, led by a real monster called Malduko Cloudcrush. This rabble has no doubt been dispatched here by High Priestess Lorthuna at the Shrine of Akir to attack travelers and coerce our people into joining the cult.\r\n\r\nI need to stay here at my post to alert travelers leaving the grove of the danger, but I would be grateful if you could do something about those cultists and their leader for me.",how={{"kill",251145},{"kill",251448},{"kill",256935}}},[92550]={t="Havoc in the Highlands",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92528},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Travel to the ruins of Falaath Village and slay 6 Al'Aketh Stormcallers, 4 Living Lightning and take the head of Commander Cyclas.",st="Our best defense here might just be a strong offense. The advantage we now have is that we expect an attack is coming. What they won't expect is for us to hit them first.\r\n\r\nI've already asked a lot of you, but please head back over to Falaath Village. Kill as many cultists as you can and if you can get close enough, kill the commander and bring me his head. I'll stay here and organize the citizens and our few peacekeepers to prepare a defense... just in case you don't return.",how={{"kill",252068},{"kill",251662},{"loot",252661,{251966}}}},[92551]={t="Stolen Supplies",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92528},ot="Collect 10 packs of Stolen Shen'dar Supplies from Falaath Village in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="I overheard you might be going to Falaath Village? While you are there, please keep an eye out for our stolen supply caches.\r\n\r\nThe Al'Aketh have been raiding our supply caravans carrying various goods such as food and windstones to and from the lowlands for months. They've been blaming the bandits, of course, but we all know that it all ends up in the same place. If there's any of that stuff left in Falaath, it would be a huge help if you could recover it.",how={{"loot",252760,{252068}}}},[92553]={t="Restocking the Larders",lv=6,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Collect $1oa Small Eggs and $2oa Strider Meat from creatures found throughout the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="Up for a bit of work? I could use a bit of muscle from a strong adventuring-type such as yourself. With how dangerous things are getting around here, no one's had much time to hunt or forage of late, and I need someone to get out there and source me fresh eggs and strider meat to keep this village fed.\r\n\r\nI'd be happy to teach you one of my famous recipes if you can bring me what I need. What do you say?",how={{"loot",6889,{251661}},{"loot",5469,{251661}}}},[92596]={t="The High Order",lv=6,min=4,nx=94413,ot="Have a seat and speak with Rathiril Sunlance.",st="The aura of arcane energy that surrounds you is strong, even though you are not initiated as a mage. I am quite sure that you are going to be a capable adventurer, and your connection with our ancient magic will only ever be a boon to you even if you were to never utter a single word of power in spellcasting.\r\n\r\nCome, let us sit and speak some on my order, the nature of the arcane here on Zephras, and the plight of our people."},[92597]={t="Reading the Leylines",lv=4,min=2,pre1={92461},ot="Use your Read Leyline racial ability at the leyline in Thendal Grove.",st="Here in the elemental plane, we derive much of our arcane strength from leylines that still run through the ground under our feet. Of late, these leylines have begun to pierce the surface, giving us more direct and powerful access to these latent arcane energies.\r\n\r\nGo to the standing stones to the northeast. There is a leyline there. Tap into your birthright and draw in its energy.",how={{"click",460002}}},[92640]={t="Desperate Times",lv=11,min=6,pre1={94568},nx=93065,rwc={[1]=2,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=3,[11]=1},ot="Speak with Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar and follow her instructions.",st="Since engaging the cult in the open is not viable, our best chance is going to be to use this opportunity to attack the shrine itself. We can take Lorthuna herself off the board before she can finish her part of this scheme.\r\n\r\nIt so happens that Valennia has been preparing a strategy for a potential assault on the Shrine for some time now. The only problem is, we will need help. \r\n\r\nSpeak with Valennia for the details.",how={{"kill",252383},{"kill",251968},{"talk",252475}}},[92642]={t="Disrupting Logistics",lv=11,min=6,pre1={93320},ot="Slay 4 Al'Aketh Healers and 8 Al'Aketh Brawlers in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="Valennia only sent one person to help repel a full-scale assault... by the winds.\r\n\r\nYou don't look like much but I'll take what I can get. We need to inflict as much damage as possible to stop this soon. My people can't hold out much longer.\r\n\r\nGo down the hill and disrupt their logistics. Their healers are keeping the attackers coming, if we take them out we might be able to rally and push them back. Any other cultists you kill while you are out there are helpful as well.",how={{"kill",254596},{"kill",270201}}},[92643]={t="The Turncoat",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92881},nx=92644,ot="Find the cultist turncoat at the house just inside the highlands northwest of Valanaar.",st="There is a turncoat amongst the Al'Aketh. They claim to know the cult's true intentions for the island and want to come in, but will only do so with assurances of protection.\r\n\r\nThis defector is hiding at a secluded residence just northwest of Valanaar inside the highlands. I need someone who can discreetly go there, find the traitor, and escort him back to us. This might be a trap, but if this information is as important as this traitor claims, it's worth some risk.",how={{"kill",255013},{"kill",253372}}},[92644]={t="Unfortunate News",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92643},nx=94568,rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},si=273852,ot="Deliver the glowing crystal to Talanaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",st="<You reach beneath the still-warm body of the turncoat cultist and recover a small, glowing blue crystal. It appears to be damaged, but it may still be important. High Elder Shadowsong may be interested in this.>"},[92645]={t="Breaking the Breaker",lv=11,min=6,pre1={93320},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Slay Commander Belguilos in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="This attack is going to be hard to repel unless we can take out the cult commander. Belguilos \"the Breaker\" they call her, and she's a veritable terror. She used to be a peacekeeper before the cult got out of control, and even then she was... off. As a cultist I can only imagine how much worse she could be now.\r\n\r\nI might just be sending you to your death, but someone needs to take Belguilos out if we are going to survive here. You can find her at the villa at the hill's base. Good luck, $c.",how={{"kill",252666}}},[92679]={t="Blood Tithe",lv=9,min=5,ot="Listen to what Alvarion Windfield has to say and find Aamelia Windfield at the Windfield Orchard.",st="H--Hello, stranger. You have the look of a capable adventurer about you. I...\r\n\r\n<The Skyborne man winces, clearly suffering terrible pain>\r\n\r\n...I was wondering if you were seeking employment? I came here to Valanaar to recruit fighters to help save my farm. If you are interested, please go find my wife Aamelia Windfield at our orchard to the west of Valanaar, in the lowlands.",how={{"kill",252800},{"kill",252448}}},[92682]={t="Make Yourself Useful",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92679},ot="Gather 10 Ripe Stormapples and slay 5 Hungry Bandits at the Windfield Orchard.",st="Oh, so you've got more courage than sense, then? Fine, I won't argue.\r\n\r\nFerauu and his goons aren't due to pick up their take of the harvest just yet, so I'm going to put you to work for your meals until they arrive.\r\n\r\nHead outside and gather today's batch of stormapples for me. Oh, and the bandits lurking around the stormapple trees... They think they are sneaky. They aren't. Kill them for me. \r\n\r\nLet's see what you've got in a fight.",how={{"open",253591,{578937}},{"kill",252802}}},[92683]={t="Flutterfly Dust",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92679},si=253666,ot="Gather 5 Flutterfly Dust from the Flutterflies around the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="I'm sure you've noticed the giant flutterflies out in the outer fields near the orchard? They are pleasant to look at, but they also have other benefits; namely their wing dust. It can be a mess, but if you can gather it up in large amounts, it has useful household applications.\r\n\r\nTake this Flutterfly Swatter and give the big bugs a good swat for me. They'll usually just get scared and flee, but sometimes they'll take some offense. Either way, they'll give their rumps a shake and drop a pile of dust.",how={{"open",253595,{578959}}}},[92684]={t="Ornery Ornery Galestriders",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92679},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Gather 7 Lowlands Galestrider Tenderloins from the Ornery Galestriders found throughout the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="As if the harvest wasn't light enough this year already, the galestriders in the area have been getting into the orchard and stealing my stormapples. Think you can head out to the fields and cull them for me?\r\n\r\nTake care though stranger, these lowlands galestriders are bigger and angrier than the highlands variety. Watch yourself. A well-timed kick is all it takes to put you down for good if you aren't paying attention.\r\n\r\nBring me some of their meat and I can make us a hot meal with it as well.",how={{"loot",253597,{251707}}}},[92685]={t="The Hills Have Eyes",lv=9,min=5,pre={92682,92683,92684},nx=92693,si=263329,ot="Loot 7 Blood-Stained Bandit Masks from Highwayman Bandits in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="The bandits have camps all over and there's a small one in the hills just north of here. Head up there and start cracking skulls. If we can catch them off guard and take them out before they come for us, we might just even the odds enough to stand a chance.\r\n\r\nBring me their masks. The bloodier the better.",how={{"loot",253596,{252820}}}},[92693]={t="Standing Our Ground",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92685},nx=92703,si=279981,ot="Speak with Aamelia Windfield when you are ready to confront the bandit leader.",st="You've done a lot to give us a fighting chance. Even if we die today, we'll at least know we gave it our best shot.\r\n\r\nThis is your last chance, stranger. If you want to head back to Valanaar and live another day, I wouldn't blame you.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, if you really have a thing for lost causes just let me know when you are ready to go. We'll walk out there with our heads held high and whatever happens, happens.",how={{"kill",252800},{"kill",252863}}},[92698]={t="What Is My Purpose?",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92679},ot="Speak with Aamelia Windfield about the Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct.",st="<You lean in close to try and hear the words coming from beneath the giant construct's armor plates.>\r\n\r\n...Function error...\r\n\r\n...Question...\r\n\r\n...What is....\r\n\r\n...Function...\r\n\r\n<These fragmented words and phrases seem to just repeat. Maybe someone nearby knows more about this construct?>"},[92699]={t="The Supreme Magister",lv=9,min=4,pre1={92701},ot="Find Elaadrin Evengale in Valanaar.",st="Now that you've arrived in Valanaar, you'll likely want to check in with the other members of the High Order here. The current Supreme Magister, Elaadrin Evengale and his people operate out of the lodge on the far southeastern part of Valanaar.\r\n\r\nYou should also take care, the High Order and Windshapers don't get along very well here. Be careful and give the Windshapers a good, wide berth. We've got enough to worry about with the cult, I won't tolerate faction violence in the streets of Valanaar."},[92701]={t="To Valanaar",lv=9,min=6,pre={92550,93927},nx=92699,si=253152,ot="Deliver Aonda's Written Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.",st="For now it seems the pylon and the village are safe, so I'd like you to deliver this report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, at the southeastern edge of the island. Valennia is the leader of the peacekeepers on the island and she needs to know what happened here.\r\n\r\nThe cult is expanding rapidly and the peacekeepers have avoided direct conflict until now, but those days are over. Valanaar will need to be ready for a fight.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, thank you. You'll always have friends in Shen'dar, $n."},[92703]={t="Deliver the News",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92693},rwc={[1]=1,[4]=3,[7]=1,[11]=2},ot="Speak with Alvarion Windfield in Valanaar.",st="I guess it doesn't feel quite right to keep calling you stranger after all of this so... thank you, $n. \r\n\r\nIf you wouldn't mind and are back out that way, please let Alvarion know what happened here. Also, tell him that once he's up on his feet he needs to bring a windshaper back here to look at that construct for us to make sure it's safe to have around our... our family.\r\n\r\n<Aamelia touches her belly gently.>\r\n\r\nHe doesn't know about this part. Let's just keep that bit between us for now."},[92709]={t="A Grand Adventure",lv=12,min=7,pre1={92699},ot="Listen to what Elaadrin Evengale in Valanaar has to say.",st="Your highborne lineage shines as clearly in your eyes as the sky above. You are one of us, and it's youths like yourself that will help us save our home. But first, let me tell you more of our mission and plans here on Zephras... and beyond."},[92727]={t="The Missing Scholar",lv=10,min=4,pre1={92699},nx=92849,ot="Discover what became of Fillion Flamebreeze.",st="Seeking knowledge is the primary mandate of the High Order, but this work has never been more dangerous than it is now on Zephras.\r\n\r\nOne of our scholars--Fillion Flamebreeze--was en route to the Shen'dar Highlands to gather data on the windborne magic that congregates in some areas there. Regrettably, he has not returned and we fear that something may have befallen him on the road.\r\n\r\nIf you can, please locate him for us. He was last seen on the road leading west from Valanaar towards Shen'dar Highlands."},[92741]={t="Unwelcome Visitors",lv=13,min=8,pre1={92699},ot="Travel to Shadowgale Forest and collect 8 Shriekling Talons for Iaadaria Bitterwind in Valanaar.",st="The Shadowgale Forest is incredibly dangerous and is usually off limits to normal adventurers. In recent months there's been an explosion in the shriekling population and they've started to expand their territory outside the woods, which is a potential problem. I have an interest in the alchemical properties of shriekling talons, so a much-needed culling also presents an opportunity for scholarly gain.\r\n\r\nTravel to Shadowgale Forest and hunt the beasts. Bring me as many of their talons as you can.",how={{"loot",254378,{256092,251247}}}},[92742]={t="Testing the Wells",lv=12,min=9,si=254545,ot="Use the Well Water Sample Kit to collect samples from the wells at the Jansen Stead and the Molsen Farm.",st="We must determine the source and nature of the poison corrupting this land. Let us begin with the groundwater under the farms in the area.\r\n\r\nGo to the Jansen Stead in the north and the Molsen Farm northwest of here, and collect samples from the wells there.",how={{"open",254546,{460005}},{"open",254547,{460006}}}},[92744]={t="Murloc Gills",lv=12,min=9,ot="Alba Fairmoon wants you to collect 7 Longshore Murloc Gills along the shoreline of Westfall.",st="The corruption affecting Westfall's crops may have seeped into the ocean as well. If the local fish are affected too, it could doom Stormwind to famine.\r\nCollect gills from the murlocs along the shoreline and bring them to me. Murlocs are quite hardy, but their physiology is extremely sensitive to contaminants. Any toxins in the seawater will be readily apparent in the gills you find.",how={{"loot",254548,{126,515}}}},[92745]={t="The State of the Mines",lv=14,min=9,pre={92742,92744},nx=92747,ot="Slay 4 Kobold Diggers in the Jangolode Mine and 6 Riverpaw Miners in the Gold Coast Quarry.",st="The well samples you collected contain toxic metals! If we do not put an end to this corruption quickly, it will be decades before crops can grow in this soil again.\r\nThe Defias have seized the mines of Westfall and use creatures as labor to strip their resources. Disrupt them by slaying their miners in the Jangolode Mine to the north, and the Gold Coast Quarry to the west.",how={{"kill",1236},{"kill",1426}}},[92747]={t="Moonbrook Espionage",lv=15,min=9,pre1={92745},nx=92748,ot="Collect 8 Suspicious Industrial Supplies from Moonbrook.",st="Strange - the poison does not seem to originate from the mines you investigated.\r\n\r\nI am told the Deadmines under the town of Moonbrook are the largest, deepest mines of Westfall, but they have been abandoned since the First War. Could the Deadmines be active again?\r\n\r\nPlease travel to Moonbrook, $n, and look for evidence of mining or industrial activity. This is the last lead we have!",how={{"open",254676,{581777}}}},[92748]={t="Explosive Consultation",lv=16,min=9,pre1={92747},ot="Travel to the Dwarven District in Stormwind and find an engineer who can help.",st="The supplies you found point to a massive industrial operation somewhere in the Deadmines. There's no question that this is the source of the toxins plaguing the farmland of Westfall. We need to stop it, quickly.\r\n\r\nWhatever's down there will be difficult to destroy. Go to the Dwarven District of Stormwind, and find an engineer who can supply us with some explosives."},[92749]={t="A Dynamite Plan",lv=16,min=9,pre1={92748},ot="Obtain $1oa Rough Dynamite from crafting, trading, or the auction house, then return to Sprite Jumpsprocket in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.",st="Industrial sabotage? You've got my attention!\r\nWe'll start with some dynamite...",how={{"loot",4358}}},[92750]={t="Detonation at a Distance",lv=16,min=9,pre1={92748},nx=92751,ot="Talk to someone in Stormwind Intelligence about acquiring a remote detonator.",st="I assume you want a \"controlled\" explosion? Not as much fun, but a good choice if you want to keep all your limbs.\r\nI'm afraid I don't have a remote detonator--why don't you go check with the sneaky folks down at Stormwind Intelligence? They should be able to find us something."},[92751]={t="Detonation at a Distance",lv=16,min=9,pre1={92750},si=254552,ot="Bring the Remote Detonator Kit to Sprite Jumpsprocket in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.",st="You need something destroyed? Would this have anything to do with your activities in Moonbrook? Don't look surprised. SI:7 stays apprised of all that goes on in Stormwind's lands.\r\n\r\nIf you're planning to set off an explosion in the caves below Westfall, you'll want to be well outside beforehand. Take this remote detonator--it's a recent prototype from our own engineers.\r\n\r\nOh--and it would be best if you didn't mention my involvement to your elf friend."},[92752]={t="Explosive Consultation",lv=16,min=9,pre={92749,92751},nx=92753,si=254553,ot="Return to Alba Fairmoon in Westfall.",st="That's it--the bomb's ready to go! Careful with that detonator, now."},[92753]={t="Destruction in Deadmines",lv=18,min=9,pre1={92752},nx=92819,si=254553,ot="Find the forge hidden in the Deadmines, and plant the Extra-Destructive Explosives nearby. Then, meet up with Alba Fairmoon at the Deadmines exit.",st="The source of the poison is likely a large metallurgical forge of some kind. Find a way into the Deadmines and locate the forge, then place the explosives.\r\nI will wait for you in the hills behind Moonbrook. Once you return, we can detonate the explosives. Hopefully, with the forge gone, the land can begin to heal.",how={{"kill",253370}}},[92819]={t="Destruction in Deadmines",lv=18,min=9,pre1={92753},pre={92753},ot="Use the detonator.",st="We are almost finished. Use the detonator, and end this.",how={{"click",581792}}},[92834]={t="Avenged Tenfold",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92840},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Collect 10 Al'Aketh Windstone Charms from Al'Aketh cultists found north of Valanaar at the Gustberry Fields or Shrine of Akir.",st="When the cult began their campaign of violence, the Peacekeepers and Windshapers responded with posturing. I saw this as foolish escalation so I advocated for peaceful dialogue. Yesterday I dispatched my friend Belathaan Brightwish to the Shrine of Akir, hoping to establish that dialogue.\r\n\r\nA box just arrived containing Belathaan's tongue, dipped in silver pigment. \r\n\r\nIt's clear to me now that there is no reasoning with the cult. Kill any cultists you see, and bring me the prayer charms that they carry.",how={{"loot",255658,{252664,252665,252767}}}},[92840]={t="Catching Wind",lv=11,min=5,pre1={99260},si=254584,ot="Take the Index Esoteria to the Overlook Standing Stones in Shen'dar Highlands and use it on the Windstone Formations in the area to gather data.",st="Fillion was sent to the Overlook Standing Stones with a special device used to measure and study the elemental energy there.\r\n\r\nTake this--an Index Esoteria--and use it to extract data from the massive windstone formations that form there. Be on your guard however, as the Windshapers are likely to be jealously guarding this site now.\r\n\r\nShould any attempt to obstruct you, well... do what you need to do. I have no more patience for their interference.",how={{"click",697118}}},[92849]={t="The Missing Scholar",lv=10,min=4,pre1={92727},nx=92850,ot="Keep searching for Fillion Flamebreeze.",st="<Judging by what you've just found, it's very likely that Fillion befell some misfortune here. He may still be nearby, and he might be in need of aid. You notice a cave just to the north of your current location. You should continue searching for him there.>",how={{"talk",253002},{"click",581820}}},[92850]={t="The Missing Scholar",lv=10,min=4,pre1={92849},nx=99260,ot="Slay the Shriekling Matriarch in the Shriekling Den then return its head to Fillion Flamebreeze in Valanaar.",st="I am feeling much better already. I have some skill with the arcane arts and we are but a short distance from Valanaar. I can make it on my own. More important than my safety, however, is how close to Valanaar these shrieklings have nested and the danger they pose. If you would be so kind, please head back inside and take the head of that beast!\r\n\r\nAfter it's done, you'll find me back in Valanaar. I need to report to the Supreme Magister what occurred here and the status of my mission.",how={{"loot",257107,{253283}}}},[92860]={t="In Service of Zephras",lv=12,min=6,pre1={92840},nx=93320,ot="Report to Valennia Stormfist and let her know that the High Order is with them in their fight against the Al'Aketh.",st="The High Order have done our best to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but that is clearly no longer an option. Their hostility has been clearly demonstrated, and now there are rumors of larger-scale cult movements around the island. They are clearly gearing up for something and whatever it is can't be good for the people of Zephras.\r\n\r\nReport to Valennia Stormfist and inform her that the High Order offers our full support in Valanaar's efforts against the Al'Aketh, should the need arise."},[92880]={t="Return to Valanaar",lv=11,min=6,pre={92642,92645},nx=92881,rwc={[1]=1,[3]=3,[4]=2,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Bring Yorna's Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.",st="I suspect it will take a bit of time for us to mop up what's left of the attackers, but our chances are far better now. Head back to Valanaar and let them know that we are stable here now.\r\n\r\nI can't thank you enough for your help. We'd be in much worse shape without you. I asked for reinforcements and it seems that I got a burgeoning hero instead. I'll take that.\r\n\r\nMay the four winds bless you, $c."},[92881]={t="The High Elder's Request",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92880},nx=92643,ot="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",st="The attacks on both the western and eastern watchtowers are not a coincidence. Based on what you told us about what occurred at the western watchtower with that skypriest, our best guess is that the cult is trying to do something to the anchor pylons.\r\n\r\nPlease speak with High Elder Shadowsong. He will tell you about a lead that could prove to be promising."},[92909]={t="Harvesting the Harvesters",lv=15,min=8,ot="Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm wants you to bring him 14 Golem Isosprings and 5 Harvester Gyrostabilizers.",st="Oh no... I'm in for it now!\r\n\r\nI heard about the harvesters terrorizing the fields of Westfall, so I traveled all the way from Ironforge to see if I could recalibrate them. But they're far more aggressive than my calculations anticipated, and they chased me into this stable!\r\n\r\nIf I had some isosprings and gyrostabilizers from the harvesters, I could build a device to cover my escape. Could you gather the parts for me?",how={{"loot",255007,{114,36,480}},{"loot",255010,{114,36}}}},[92910]={t="Harvesting the Harvesters",lv=15,min=8,nx=92911,si=255155,ot="Bring the Precessive Autocognition Assembly to Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm.",st="The part you managed to salvage from the harvester appears mostly intact. Someone interested in harvest golems may want to see it."},[92911]={t="Harvesting the Harvesters",lv=15,min=8,pre1={92910},ot="Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm wants you to bring him 8 Golem Isosprings, 4 Copper Modulators, and a Crude Scope.",st="I see... this gives me some insight into what makes those monsters tick. I have an idea how we could override their systems, at least momentarily.\r\n\r\nI'll continue tinkering with the assembly you brought me. In the meantime, could you scrounge up some parts for the device?",how={{"loot",255007,{114,36,480}},{"loot",4363,{114,36,480}},{"loot",4405,{513,590,589}}}},[92947]={t="Making Our Move",lv=12,min=7,pre1={93065},nx=93958,ot="Slay $1oa Al'Aketh Guardians, $2oa Al'Aketh Spiritcallers, and $3oa Al'Aketh Blademasters, then report to Hyusaa Quickbreeze at the Shrine of Akir.",st="Everyone is here, good. I've just sent a few of my best fighters in through the front of the shrine to cause a bit of trouble and serve as a distraction, while I lead the the bulk of our forces in from the flank.\r\n\r\nIf all goes well, we should be able to punch through quickly and take out the High Priestess. As for you, get in there and start cracking skulls. Meet my second, Hyusaa Quickbreeze, near the steps to the shrine after you've caused some trouble.\r\n\r\nWinds guide you, $c.",how={{"kill",252762},{"kill",252763},{"kill",252765},{"kill",253576}}},[93036]={t="Infiltrating the Cult",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92517},nx=92529,ot="Speak with Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village.",st="You may or may not be aware of this, but Sania Silverstream over there is a \"missionary\" for the Al'Aketh. They like to play at being a normal religious order and send non-threatening emissaries around to recruit. We've tolerated Sania so far to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but it's obvious the illusion of peace won't last much longer.\r\n\r\nYou are new here and unknown to most, so I'd like to see if you can use Sania to get close to the cult and find out what their plans are for the village."},[93065]={t="Prepare for Battle",lv=12,min=7,pre1={92640},nx=92947,ot="Speak with Valennia Stormfist in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="The Peacekeepers are mobilizing and we are all gearing up to head out. Make whatever preparations you need to make and meet us at the eastern road leading north out of town. We'll have one final check-in with everyone before we move out."},[93089]={t="What Comes Next",lv=13,min=7,pre1={94369},pre={93835},nx=94946,ot="Speak with Elaadrin Evengale when you are prepared to leave Zephras Isle.",st="Please extend my thanks to Elaadrin for all that the High Order and your new friends from this \"Kirin Tor\" have done for Zephras Isle. I'm aware of the High Order's plans to leave the island, and your order has my blessing and well-wishes in this expedition.\r\n\r\nI can only hope that whatever arcane solution the High Order finds can truly provide us with the stability we've lacked these past years. If you plan to go with them... well, this mission will be all the stronger for it.\r\n\r\nWinds be with you, $n."},[93159]={t="The Strange Hermit",lv=13,min=8,ot="Speak with the Strange Hermit in the Shadowgale Forest and learn more about him.",st="Uh, um... h-hello, I mean to say, hi! Greetings, even! I'm sorry... it's um, been so long since I've actually spoken to another person. I'm afraid I'm a bit rusty at this.\r\n\r\n<The strange hooded figure shifts uncomfortably before you.>\r\n\r\nSo er, um... how is your day going?"},[93160]={t="The Forest's Bounty",lv=13,min=8,pre1={93159},ot="Gather $1oa Shadowgale Acorns in Shadowgale Forest.",st="I do appreciate you stopping by to talk with me! I-If you do want to help out, I could use a bit of help gathering up acorns from the forest floor. I've gathered most of the ones close by but there sure are a lot of raptor-bird things in the forest. It's dangerous out there and I'd rather not become a giant bird's lunch!\r\n\r\nSo if you want, you could maybe gather them for me? I'll make us something tasty if you do!",how={{"open",257128,{613238}}}},[93165]={t="Mercy Falls on Deaf Ears",lv=13,min=8,pre1={94484,94493},nx=93459,rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Collect $1oa Al'Aketh Cultist's Ears from the Al'Aketh cultists in Shadowgale Forest, the Shrine of Akir, or Gustberry Lowlands.",st="The Al'Aketh have visited great tragedy upon our enclave, and blood must be repaid with blood.\r\n\r\nI have an offer for you, stranger. Should you find conflict with these accursed cultists, bring me the ears of those you kill. I will reward you for each that you return with in both coin and, in time, access to the Nightclaw's secrets should you prove yourself to be a true friend.",how={{"loot",258771,{257196,252762,252763}}}},[93172]={t="Free the Hollows",lv=13,min=8,pre1={93159},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Destroy 10 Wind Hollows in Shadowgale Forest.",st="Most of the elves on this island seem to think that these woods are haunted, and they aren't wrong.\r\n\r\nAt the old ruins to the northeast, a strange type of ghost-like spirits gather. Some nights, you can almost hear them \"singing\". It's not like any song I've heard before, but it's definitely a song and it's... just so sad.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why, but I think something terrible happened there at some point, and the spirits are trapped there somehow. If you are feeling brave, maybe you can help set them free?",how={{"kill",251676}}},[93317]={t="Crab Season",lv=9,min=4,ot="Collect 6 pieces of Windsong Crawler Meat.",st="Are you familiar with Windsong Crawlers? You see, these crabs are native only to Windsong Lake here on Zephras, and they are only able to be harvested a few weeks of the year.\r\n\r\nWith all of the cult activity of late, I've not been able to get out to the lake to harvest them, and our window is rapidly closing. I'd be appreciative if you could go and gather some for me. They can generally be found along the shorelines around the lake and in rivers.\r\n\r\nDo be careful though, they are meaner than they look!",how={{"loot",257941,{254588}}}},[93318]={t="WANTED: Vulgara the Insatiable",lv=9,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Kill Vulgara the Insatiable in the Shen'dar Highlands and bring her head to Danarii Bellowveil.",st="By order of Constable Aonda of the Peacekeepers, a bounty is hereby placed upon the scourge of the highlands, Vulgara the Insatiable. Last spotted on a hilltop rise just southwest of Shen'dar Village, the winged vuldren terror is highly dangerous and should be approached with caution.\r\n\r\nDeliver the beast's head to Danarii Bellowveil to receive your reward.",how={{"loot",257942,{254589}}}},[93319]={t="Pilfered Windstones",lv=7,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Collect 10 Pilfered Windstones from the Highlands Bandits in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="We are relying on windstones more and more for day-to-day living here on Zephras so we try and maintain a cache of them in reserve for emergencies. Lately I've noticed some go missing from our stores.\r\n\r\nWe've found windstones on bandits we've captured recently, and I suspect they are behind our shortages.\r\n\r\nIf you find yourself near the bandit cave to the north, mind knocking a few heads together and reclaiming some of our pilfered windstones for me?",how={{"loot",257945,{251918}}}},[93320]={t="Tower Defense",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92860,92871},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Report to Yorana Windyreed at the eastern watchtower in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="I've just received word that the cult is attacking the pylon watchtower just outside of town! I've sent the few extra peacekeepers we have here to try and break through the enemy back line to relieve the defenders, but any additional help could mean the difference between our people there living or dying.\r\n\r\nPlease leave immediately for the east watchtower and provide whatever aid you can.\r\n\r\nMy lieutenant Yorana Windyreed led the relief force. If she still lives she can tell you how best to help."},[93461]={t="Welcome to Shen'dar Village",lv=6,min=4,pre={92472},ot="Speak with Rathiril Sunlance and Coriella Calmbreeze in Shen'dar Village.",st="You've got that \"High Order\" look to you. Those with Highborne ancestry always seem to have a slight twinkle in their eyes that gives it away. Before I properly put you to work around here, you should check in with our resident High Order elder Rathiril Sunlance. You can find him here in the main lodge, just around the corner from me.\r\n\r\nOh, and check in with Coriella Calmbreeze as well, she runs the local inn and can provide lodging and supplies, should you need them.",how={{"talk",251903},{"kill",254089}}},[93552]={t="Harvesting Windstones",lv=4,min=2,pre1={92461},ot="Collect 15 Windstone Clusters from Raw Windstones in Thendal Grove.",st="Windstones are a critical resource on Zephras Isle as they contain the raw, concentrated energy of the winds themselves. The wind elementals who used to live here on Zephras with us vanished a number of years ago, and since then, the magic that sustains this island is slowly fading. Not without limitations, the windstones are still a reliable energy source, and are incredibly valuable to us.\r\n\r\nYou'll find raw windstones scattered around the grove. Think you can help me harvest them?",how={{"open",258772,{613286}}}},[93791]={t="Speak with Belann",lv=10,min=10,nx=93797,ot="Speak with Belann Windwood in Valanaar.",st="$n, it is clear your skill with magic is growing and I believe it is time for you to partake in one of the High Order's oldest traditions for young and aspiring mages. It is time for you to craft a spell focus of your own.\r\n\r\nSeek out Belann Windwood in Valanaar. He has been crafting staves and wands for the High Order for over a century, so you will be in good hands."},[93797]={t="Boughs in the Wind",lv=10,min=10,pre1={93791},ot="Bring a Wind-Infused Bough to Belann Windwood in Valanaar.",st="It is a time-honored tradition for young mages to create their own spell focus when they have shown a certain degree of magical proficiency. This is typically done by gathering a fallen branch from our oldest trees, as they have some lingering traces of elemental wind.\r\n\r\nI have found the most ideal ones to be near the wind shrine, just south of Falaath Village. Go and bring me back a large branch and I will teach you about the traditions as we create your spell focus.",how={{"open",262668,{616860}}}},[93835]={t="Confront Lorthuna",lv=12,min=7,pre1={93958},nx=94369,ot="Take the portal to the Rohashi Spires overhead and join Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger in their confrontation with High Priestess Lorthuna.",st="Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.\r\n\r\nI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Elaadrin and help them stop Lorthuna.\r\n\r\nUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, $c."},[93926]={t="The Western Watch",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92528},nx=93927,ot="Find Peacekeeper Vaaniel at the western watchtower.",st="Whatever reason the cult has for attacking the tower, it's not worth losing our people over.\r\n\r\nI'd like for you to head to the southwest and check in on that watchtower for us. Find the peacekeepers there and tell them to head back to the village. Holding that tower is not worth the lives it would cost and I'd rather concentrate the defenders we do have here to protect our citizens.\r\n\r\nPeacekeeper Vaaniel is in charge; let him know to head back here as quickly as possible. Hurry!"},[93927]={t="A Last Request",lv=8,min=5,pre1={93926},ot="Collect the note you found near the dead peacekeeper and read it to determine your next steps.",st="<As you inspect the body of the dead peacekeeper, a bloody note falls free of his hands. Picking it up and reading it may give you a clue as to how to proceed from here.>",how={{"kill",256966},{"open",254871,{617704}},{"open",263415,{617675}},{"open",263418,{617674}}}},[93948]={t="Deliver the Signet",lv=9,min=6,pre={92550,93927},nx=93949,si=263491,ot="Deliver the Shadowsong Family Signet to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",st="Since you are going to Valanaar anyway, please deliver the signet ring you recovered from the tower to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar. \r\n\r\nHe will want this back, and more importantly, he will want to learn the fate of his nephew. Talaanis is the High Elder of Zephras Isle and more importantly, he is a good man who is well loved by the people, despite our current hardships. It pains me to think of how he will react to this news. Please express my condolences for his loss."},[93949]={t="Bugged",lv=8,min=6,pre1={93948},ot="Kill Skyhoppers in Valanaar until you've eliminated $1oa Enchanted Skyhoppers.",st="We've been bugged.\r\n\r\nIt's skyhopper season in the lowlands, which means the pests are everywhere. One of the High Order mages reported that one of the insects that they killed had an enchantment of some kind placed upon it. When we inspected it closely it seems to be some sort of listening spell.\r\n\r\nWe suspect that the cult is using these enchanted insects as spies. Go and exterminate them for us. You won't be able to tell which are enchanted by looking at them, so you'll just have to kill them all.",how={{"kill",251727}}},[93951]={t="A Little Beauty",lv=7,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Collect 8 Hippogryph Down feathers in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="The hippogryphs that have taken up residence southwest of the village can be a nuisance, but they also present a rather unique opportunity to obtain their feathers. Many skyborne love to adorn their hair with vibrant plumes and the down feathers of a hippogryph are exceptionally vibrant and, more importantly, silky soft.\r\n\r\nIf you are heading that way, try and gather as many of the fallen feathers as you can from around their nesting grounds. Do be careful, as wild hippogryph are not tolerant of guests.",how={{"open",263493,{617839}}}},[93958]={t="The Inner Sanctum",lv=12,min=7,pre1={92947},ot="Speak with Valennia Stormfist inside the inner sanctum at the Shrine of Akir.",st="Valennia's forces just breached the inner sanctum. The fighting was thick in there at first, but it's grown... unsettlingly quiet. Go in there and do your best to link up with Valennia and her forces... if any of them are left.\r\n\r\nI'll stay here and watch your back."},[94003]={t="The Skybreaker Bulwark",lv=10,min=10,ot="Reclaim the Skybreaker Bulwark from Zaal Stormshield at the Shrine of Akir.",st="I am all that remains of the line of Skybreakers here on Zephras Isle. The rest were murdered by the Al'Aketh.\r\n\r\nThe only thing that outweighs my sorrow is my shame. My family's ancestral shield--the Skybreaker Bulwark--is now in the hands of a cultist named Zaal Stormshield. Family lore holds no harm may befall a worthy wielder of this shield.\r\n\r\nZaal is not worthy, of that I am sure. Find this man at the Shrine of Akir and reclaim my shield from him. Do this and I will teach you the Skybreaker Defense.",how={{"loot",263993,{257196}}}},[94006]={t="The Great Ursera Spirit",lv=10,min=10,nx=94638,ot="Speak with Urs'endris near the falls northeast of Valanaar.",st="Greetings, $n. You have progressed in your druidic studies far enough that I think it is time for you to meet one of the great spirits that reside here on Zephras. Urs'endris is a wise and noble spirit, who has taught druids how to take on the ursera shape for generations. Unfortunately his domain has begun to wither and fall into the sky like many other areas of Zephras.\r\n\r\nTo find him, travel northeast near the waterfall in the shadow of the Shrine of Akir. He should be able to instruct you further."},[94013]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94979},nx=94050,si=264163,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Vuldren Alpha in the Gustberry Lowlands. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",st="You've returned triumphant from taming two beasts. It's time now for your last trial. The winds of Zephras whisper of greater challenges ahead. \r\n\r\nTake this Taming Rod and journey to the Gustberry Lowlands. There, tame a Vuldren Alpha and prove your mastery. \r\n\r\nComplete this lesson and you'll be ready to learn the deeper ways of the hunter.",how={{"kill",250874}}},[94050]={t="Training the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94013},ot="Speak to Quel'dora Quickgale in Valanaar.",st="You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than my sister, Quel'dora. She will give you the ability to train your new pet. \r\n\r\nGo with the winds, young $c."},[94369]={t="The Fate of Zephras",lv=12,min=7,nx=93089,ot="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",st="Ansirem has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir now that the wards that have hidden Zephras are down. If the Windlord chooses to attack us, we stand no chance to defend ourselves while we are here in his domain.\r\n\r\nHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it."},[94373]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,pre={98581},nx=94374,ot="Bring 2 Frostmane Bear Pendants to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.",st="Aye, the time's come, young shaman. Ye've grown stout and sturdy, like the stone beneath our boots. Takin' up the shaman's path shows ye've got the wisdom o' the mountain, even before ye've proven yerself. Ye've the grit of stone to walk the earth's path.\r\n\r\nBut to earn its favor, ye must face it proper. South o' here, the Frostmane trolls live in a cave.\r\n\r\nBring me two of the necklaces they wear, crafted from the Iceclaw bears. Then we'll speak more of yer future.",how={{"loot",264356,{706,946}}}},[94374]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,pre1={94373},nx=94375,si=6635,ot="Find the Spirit Stone and drink the Earth Sapta.",st="Aye, sapta's a brew forged with magic, bindin' our spirit to the elements. Only a few shaman know the recipe, and it's nae for the weak-willed. Drink it, and ye will see what others can't. Hold true--it's only to be drunk in a sacred place.\r\n\r\nHead north to the Spirit Stone, tucked at the end of a hidden path up the mountain. Drink it there... see what the earth has to show ye."},[94375]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,pre1={94374},si=6656,ot="Bring the Rough Quartz to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.",st="Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Teo Hammerstorm as proof o' our meeting. He will craft a totem for ye, and this pebble will be the heart o' it. As small as it may seem, ye will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest o' things can outlast many others.\r\n\r\nBe patient, $n. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks o' ye. In the end, ye shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect ye."},[94413]={t="A Magical Affront",lv=6,min=4,pre1={92596},ot="Slay 6 Windshaper Novice Seers in Shen'dar Highlands.",st="The recent emergence of the leylines on the surface of Zephras has been profound for our order. We have more direct and tangible access to the energies that permeate this place and it has increased our understanding of said magic greatly.\r\n\r\nThe Windshapers, however, view these emergences as scars on the land that must be \"healed\". This is an affront to our order and is something we simply cannot abide.\r\n\r\nGo to the leyline in the forest to the southwest and drive off the Windshapers you find there.",how={{"kill",257532}}},[94414]={t="The Anchors of Zephras",lv=2,min=2,ot="Speak with Halaan Hawk-Eye and borrow his gift to view the anchor pylon in the distance.",st="Greetings, young $n. I oftentimes come here to look upon the ancient anchor pylon. Gifts from the spirits of the winds, they bind and sustain our island. Of late however, their magic has grown unstable and inconsistent.\r\n\r\nThey suffer no distress I can see. Their splendor has not changed.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like, I can lend you my gift to look upon them yourself."},[94449]={t="Call of Fire",lv=10,min=10,ot="Find Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.",st="It's been long since ye were last tested, $n. Ye've shown patience, aye -- but now it's time ye learned of chaos... of destruction. Fire's call is loud, and if ye're ready to pay its price, it'll speak to ye. \r\n\r\nSeek out Bruegs Kindleborn, far east in the mountains. He dwells in a cave above South Gate Outpost. He'll know if ye're truly ready."},[94465]={t="Call of Fire",lv=11,min=10,pre={94449},nx=94466,si=6653,ot="Bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.",st="Aye, ye've the strength to bear the totem o' fire, lad--but strength alone won't make ye ready.\r\n\r\nBeyond the Valley o' Kings, in the crags of Loch Modan, lies a hidden path to one o' our sacred peaks. There, Braldir Ashmantle guards the Shrine o' the Dormant Flame. \r\n\r\nTake this torch to him--it shows yer intent. Return it burnin' by the shrine's brazier, and I'll see ye earn the totem proper."},[94466]={t="Call of Fire",lv=14,min=10,pre1={94465},nx=94467,ot="Bring 1 Fire Tar and 1 Reagent Pouch to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.",st="Bah, ye didn't trek all this way for tales, did ye, $n? Ye seek the Eternal Flame and the fire totem.\r\n\r\nFirst, ye'll need a sapta to bind yer spirit to the flame.\r\n\r\nI'll craft it--but I'll need two things: fire tar from Tunnel Rat Geomancers in the kobold caves up north, and a reagent pouch from a Stonesplinter Seer lurkin' in the southern hills. Dangerous work, but worthy of the flame.",how={{"loot",5026,{1174}},{"loot",6652,{1166}}}},[94467]={t="Call of Fire",lv=14,min=10,pre1={94466},nx=94468,si=6653,ui={6636},ot="Defeat the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and place the Glowing Ember in the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",st="The fire sapta's ready, $n. Now ye face the flame. Use it at the shrine, then climb to the peak. There, ye'll see the spirit--he'll not strike 'til ye do, but he'll know ye see him.$B$BStrike fast, lad. The longer ye wait, the stronger he burns. When he falls, take his glowing embers and place 'em in the brazier. Light the torch and earn the fire's favor.",how={{"loot",6655,{5893,268763}}}},[94468]={t="Call of Fire",lv=14,min=10,pre1={94467},si=6654,ot="Bring the Torch of Eternal Flame to Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.",st="Torch firmly in hand, you turn away from the brazier and look out over Loch Modan. You feel an excitement tugging at your spirit as the wind picks up and forces the flame to dance violently.$B$BYou start off down the path back to Dun Morogh in search of Bruegs Kindleborn."},[94484]={t="Unnerving Silence",lv=11,min=8,ex={94493},ot="Find and speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.",st="A moment if you will, $n. Are you headed towards Shadowgale Forest? There is a druid conclave there in a cave to the northeast. I have been waiting on word from them but their correspondence is long overdue.\r\n\r\nWith Ban'aethall in ruins and all the unrest lately I worry something dire may have happened. Please, if you are able, go seek out Elegael Thornpaw and put my mind at ease."},[94485]={t="Tears of the Lady",lv=12,min=8,pre1={94484,94493},ot="Collect $1oa Lady's Tear Moss.",st="If we are to save my fellows in the Nightclaw Den, I am going to need some ingredients for a poultice. The first and most important is a spindly moss called Lady's Tear. It typically grows on the base of the trees here in Shadowgale.\r\n\r\nThis moss secretes a sticky substance that acts as an antiseptic and is perfect for binding open wounds. I have gathered what little I can reach but I know there is more in this forest.\r\n\r\nGo and be swift. We are going to need a lot if the injured I left behind still live.",how={{"open",265105,{619450}}}},[94486]={t="Feathers for Binding",lv=11,min=8,pre1={94484,94493},ot="Collect $1oa feathers from the Shadowgale Shrieklings in Shadowgale Forest.",st="The other ingredient I need for the poultice is feathers from the Shadowgale shrieklings that roam this forest. In their juvenile form, the shrieklings have insulative feathers which would be ideal to put over the moss. These feathers will prevent the antiseptic sap from drying out and will provide at least some protection against the elements.\r\n\r\nBe warned, the shrieklings are normally docile but they have been incredibly hostile of late. Their large talons can easily disembowel you if you aren't careful.",how={{"loot",265140,{256092}}}},[94487]={t="Unwanted and Unworthy",lv=11,min=8,pre1={94484,94493},ot="Collect $1oa Bloodied Heirlooms from Al'Aketh Footsoldiers and Al'Aketh Stormchasers in the Shadowgale Forest.",st="The Al'Aketh Cultists ambushed us with no warning, though their motives remain a mystery to me. I knew these cultists had clouds between their ears, but I never imagined they would upset the delicate balance here on Zephras with such brutality. Go, slay as many as you can and take their heirlooms if they wear any.\r\n\r\n<Elegael spits.>\r\n\r\nThese storm-cursed cultists don't deserve to be called shen'dorei. The beasts of the forest can have their bodies. Their ashes don't deserve the winds.",how={{"loot",265141,{252664,252665}}}},[94488]={t="The Ties That Bind",lv=11,min=8,pre={94485,94486,94487},ot="Kill Commander Haalien and bring his head to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.",st="The reason for cultists' presence here still baffles me, but I smell a familiar scent over the bloodshed.\r\n\r\nOne of our circle druids, Haalien, disappeared months back. It appears he's thrown his sorry hide in with the cultists.\r\n\r\nShow him what happens when he spills the blood of his kin! Take his head and return it to me.",how={{"loot",265475,{253622}}}},[94489]={t="The Wounds of Betrayal",lv=12,min=8,pre={94485,94486,94487},ot="Enter the Nightfang Den and heal $1oa druids and find Jorel Windsinger in Shadowgale Forest.",st="I have finished the poultices. Quickly, take them to the druids in the cave, north just across the clearing. I know my brethren are in much more dire condition than I. They are likely too injured to heal their own wounds. There are so few of us shen'dorei druids that every life is precious.\r\n\r\nBefore you go, I have a selfish request. My mate, Jorel Windsinger was in dire condition when I left. Please, see to his wounds if he still lives.",how={{"kill",258130},{"kill",258134},{"kill",258137},{"kill",258138},{"kill",258275},{"kill",258277},{"kill",258288},{"kill",258289}}},[94490]={t="Ripped Missive",lv=12,min=9,pre={94485,94486,94487},nx=94491,si=265476,ot="Bring the Ripped Missive to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.",st="<Tucked behind one of Haalien's bracers is a note that's been slightly torn and bloodstained in your fight. It looks like it contains useful information about the cultist motivations for the attack on the druid den. Elegael would be interested in this intel.>"},[94491]={t="The Fate of the Den",lv=12,min=8,pre1={94490},si=265782,ot="Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valanaar and tell him what has transpired.",st="It would appear that there is a correspondent hiding somewhere in Valanaar feeding information to the cult. I am clearly in no shape to make the journey, but Lotheluum needs to know what transpired here.\r\n\r\nHe should also know the fate of those who are no longer with us. Thanks to your help I think we can handle the rest of the situation from here, though the damage has been done.\r\n\r\nPlease go swiftly, $n. I hope our paths will cross again someday. Until then, I have cultists to slay."},[94494]={t="Call of Water",lv=20,min=20,nx=94495,ot="Find Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.",st="Long has it been since ye were last tested, $n. Ye have shown patience thus far in yer studies, but the time has come for ye to learn about the purity of water.\r\n\r\nSeek out Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan. He is along the north western edge o' the lake, south of Stonewrought Dam. Ye will find him there at his burrow hut. Good luck to ye, $n."},[94495]={t="Call of Water",lv=22,min=20,pre1={94494},pre={94494},nx=94497,ot="Find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.",st="If there's one truth ye need to learn about water, it's this: water means rebirth. It carves stone, cleanses filth, and heals the weary -- but only when it's pure. Taint it, and it'll ruin all it touches.\r\n\r\nIf ye seek the water sapta, find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands. Her family dwells in a cave beneath the southern falls.\r\n\r\nGo on then, don't let the river outrun ye."},[94497]={t="Call of Water",lv=22,min=20,pre1={94495},pre={94495},nx=94499,si=265732,ot="Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the bottom of the waterfalls below Hervdana's cave and return it to her in the Wetlands.",st="Ah, so ye've come seekin' the sapta, have ye? Well then, listen close, love. To find understandin' and earn the sapta, ye must seek water in its various forms. As ye gather the samples, keep yer eyes open. Watch the beasts that guard it, the land it nourishes, and how it changes lives.\r\n\r\nWe'll start simple: fill this skin at the base o' the falls, where the fresh meets the brackish. Go on now, and mind the marsh.",how={{"loot",265734}}},[94499]={t="Call of Water",lv=22,min=20,pre1={94497},nx=94500,si=265747,ot="Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at Stonewatch Falls near the Nightcrawler Murlocs and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.",st="Aye, Redridge drinks deep from Lake Everstill, but by the time the waters tumble down Stonewatch Falls, somethin' has seeped in. The murlocs down there are big, twisted brutes. Not like the ones ye find here or in the Loch. Lucky for the townsfolk they keep to the base o' the falls.\r\n\r\nBring a sampling to me. I've a mind to find out if it's magic, venom, or somethin' worse that's taintin' the waters near that old fort.",how={{"loot",265748}}},[94500]={t="Call of Water",lv=23,min=20,pre1={94499},nx=94501,si=265772,ot="Fill the Unfilled Blue Waterskin at the waters of Astranaar in Ashenvale and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.",st="Take this waterskin and journey deep into the emerald shade o' Ashenvale. Astranaar rests cradled by waters untouched by corruption. Ruins litter the bed o' the lake, hinting at a bygone era. Bring back a sample from the lake. Pure, ancient, and possibly enchanted water.\r\n\r\nIt's the last liquid I need before I send ye back to Norric.\r\n\r\nBoard the boat in Menethil to Auberdine. It stops in Southshore on the way over.\r\n\r\nAnd mind yerself... the forest's got eyes, and they don't blink.",how={{"loot",265773}}},[94568]={t="The Cult's True Plans",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92644},nx=92640,ot="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong and observe the conversation.",st="The turncoat clearly was afraid of what the cult had planned, enough so to defect and seek our aid. It's truly unfortunate that he is dead and took his secrets to the grave with him.\r\n\r\nWe must discuss this further to determine our next steps."},[94638]={t="Strength and Mercy",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94006},ot="Find and kill Ur'endra in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="You have come to me in hopes of learning to take a shape of strength. I have a task for you, though it lies heavy on my heart.\r\n\r\nMy mate, Ur'endra, has lost herself to madness and has begun to attack her own kin. Without the magic of the winds, many creatures have begun to lose themselves... Ur'endra included. She makes her lair in a cave to the west of here, in the bluffs along the border between the Shen'dar Highlands and the Gustberry Lowlands.\r\n\r\nEnd her suffering and I shall grant you my blessing.",how={{"kill",258443}}},[94774]={t="Divine Grace",lv=10,min=10,ex={94773,94775,94776,94777,94778,94779},ot="Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.",st="You've caught the attention of our superiors, $n. They've asked you to travel to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Laurena. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you."},[94792]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,nx=94863,si=266158,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Rockhide Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.",st="Many hunters prefer to travel with animal companions. With a beast at your side, you will find that you can survive even the most dangerous of circumstances. As they say, everything is easier with a friend. However, obtaining an animal companion is something that must be done with care. The balance of nature is delicate, and must always be respected.\r\n\r\nTake this Taming Rod with you to the forest. With it, you will be able to tame a Rockhide Boar and practice your skills as a hunter.",how={{"kill",524}}},[94793]={t="Training the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94864},ot="Speak to Isaac Chan in Goldshire.",st="You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than Isaac Chan, a lifelong woodsman. He will give you the ability to train your new pet.\r\n\r\nGo with the winds, young $c."},[94818]={t="Contingency Plan",lv=20,min=20,ex={94819,94820}},[94824]={t="Confounding Flash",lv=10,min=10,ex={94817,94821,94822,94823,94825,94826},ot="Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.",st="Time's come for you to head to Ironforge, $n. High Priestess Mims in the Hall of Mysteries commands you to come speak with her. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.$B$BBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can."},[94863]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94792},nx=94864,si=266253,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Gray Forest Wolf. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.",st="You've already mastered taming a boar. Now it's time for the next lesson. The forest holds fiercer companions, and with care, you can earn their trust.\r\n\r\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Gray Forest Wolf. Remember, nature's balance must be respected. Prove your skill as a hunter once more.",how={{"kill",1922}}},[94864]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94863},nx=94793,si=266254,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Young Forest Bear. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.",st="You've proven yourself by taming a boar and a wolf. Now it's time for your final challenge. Elwynn's balance depends on respect and skill. Take this Taming Rod and seek out a Young Forest Bear. Show that you can earn the trust of even the mightiest companion. \r\n\r\nCompleting this lesson will deepen your attunement to beasts.",how={{"kill",822}}},[94896]={t="Aid For The Refugees",lv=11,min=8,ot="Collect $1oa Abandoned Belongings from the ruins of Ban'aethal.",st="You look like a capable adventurer. Do you happen to be headed towards Shadowgale Forest? Ban'aethal lies deep in the forest; that's where we're all from.\r\n\r\n<Ealaane gestures to the other refugees.>\r\n\r\nWe've recently had to evacuate Ban'aethal, as it began to fall into the sky. It was sudden and in the middle of the night. If you are headed that way, would you please look for any belongings left behind? The forest and village are far too dangerous for us to return to now.",how={{"open",266433,{623295}}}},[94897]={t="The Fate of a Loved One",lv=11,min=8,ot="Find Resaan in the Ruins of Ban'aethal.",st="If you are traveling to Ban'aethal, I have a selfish request. My love, Resaan... I believe is no longer a part of this world. He had tried to go back to get supplies even though I begged him to stay. It has been over a week already and I fear the worst.\r\n\r\nPlease, if you find him, bring him home. If he has perished then I beg you to please bring me his heirloom.",how={{"loot",266434,{259013}}}},[94912]={t="Child of Nature",lv=10,min=10,ot="Speak with Sheldras Moontree in Stormwind.",st="Greetings, young $c. \r\n\r\nHave you heard of the Cenarion Circle? I'd expect not. They are an ancient order of naturalists and practitioners of the druidic arts, much like yourself. In the city of Stormwind you'll find a night elf by the name of Sheldras Moontree. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, a place called Moonglade.\r\n\r\nGo now. You have much to learn if you wish to save your home."},[94946]={t="The Magical City of Dalaran",lv=13,min=7,pre1={93089},ot="Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Dalaran City and speak with Danaaris Stargale when you arrive.",st="I had intended to be the first of us to step foot onto Azeroth, but recent events with the cult have changed my plans. As a result, I will be remaining here in Valanaar for a time. Fret not though, we have several mages awaiting our people's arrival in Dalaran. I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we set our affairs in order here. We will call upon agents such as yourself when you are needed.\r\n\r\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there."},[94947]={t="Welcome to Azeroth",lv=13,min=7,nx=93963,ot="Take the Skyborne Portal to Stormwind and report to Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.",st="It's a big world down here, and we need our people to start branching out to explore it. That's where you come in.\r\n\r\nThe Kirin Tor is a member of an \"Alliance\" of like-minded nations. The de-facto heart of this alliance is the city of Stormwind to the south. Elaadrin has asked me to find someone to travel to Stormwind and meet with the regent lord there, a human named Bolvar Fordragon.\r\n\r\nWhen you are ready, the Kirin Tor mages have set up a special portal for the High Order to use to access Stormwind.",how={{"click",631299}}},[94978]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,nx=94979,si=267272,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Windsong Crawler found near bodies of water. \r\nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",st="Every hunter begins by learning the bond between beast and master. This is your first challenge. In time, you'll tame creatures from every corner of the world, but for now, start with our rivers and lakes on Zephras. \r\n\r\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Windsong Crawler.\r\n\r\nShow that you can earn its trust, and begin your path toward true mastery.",how={{"kill",254588}}},[94979]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94978},nx=94013,si=267298,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame an Ornery Galestrider in the Gustberry Lowlands. \r\nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",st="You've proven you can tame the river's crawler. Now it's time to test your skill on open ground. The plains of Zephras echo with the cries of the galestrider, a proud, winged hunter that runs like the wind.\r\n\r\nTake this Taming Rod and seek one out. Travel to the lowlands and earn its trust.\r\n\r\nShow you're ready for the trials yet to come.",how={{"kill",251707}}},[95065]={t="Fishin' Time",lv=12,min=7,ot="Bring $1oa Shiny Bauble and $2oa Nightcrawlers to Gilbert Gray at the harbor in Stormwind.",st="What a view... Best an old man can ask for.\r\n\r\nThe fish sure are bitin' now, though I'm down to my last bait. I don't suppose you have any spare fishing supplies on you? Of course not, forgive me. I get so excited at the thought of casting another line it didn't dawn on me I may be one of the few carrying supplies everywhere I go.\r\n\r\nWould you be able to help refresh my stock? Catherine Leland has an assortment of fishing goods just west of the Trade District along the canals. Tell her old Gray sent you.",how={{"buy",6529,{5494,66,8934}},{"buy",6530,{5494,1286,8934}}}},[95161]={t="Remember That I Love You",lv=22,min=15,pre1={92415},pre={92415},si=251522,ot="Deliver the Blood-Stained Letter to Avette Fellwood in Duskwood.",st="If you're looking for Jeremy Heartweaver, your best bet is to talk to his newly adopted mother, Avette Fellwood out in Duskwood. Sweet woman. Likely needs another pair of hands for her work, but it beats staying in the orphanage.\r\n\r\nIf you see little Jeremy, do be sure to tell him we're all thinking of him, won't you?"},[95189]={t="Crest of Lordaeron",lv=22,min=16,si=268579,ot="Return the Crest of Lordaeron to Lady Dena Kennedy in Stormwind City.",st="<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in Stormwind would be very keen to get their hands on this.>"},[95195]={t="Bloodied Insignia",lv=22,min=16,si=268540,ot="Collect $1oa Bloodied Insignias and take them to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind City.",st="<The old Alliance insignia appears to have belonged to a soldier of Lordaeron. These ruins are likely filled with similar medals that living relatives would be grateful to have returned to them.>",how={{"loot",268540,{250618,250621,250622}}}},[95212]={t="Never Saddle on Quality",lv=10,min=7,ot="Collect 6 Pristine Leopard Pelts and deliver them to Amberstill Ranch.",st="We're getting ready to send a team of rams to reinforce the Alterac expedition, but we've run out of material to make their saddles.\r\n\r\nCollect pelts from the largest, fiercest leopards to the east and bring them to me. It's biting cold up there and our forces deserve nothing but the finest pelts to keep them warm!",how={{"loot",267414,{260157}}}},[95213]={t="Stolen Blasting Powder",lv=10,min=7,nx=95214,ot="Bring the Empty Powder Keg to Quarrymaster Thesten at Gol'Bolar Quarry.",st="The keg is stamped:\r\n\r\nBLASTING POWDER - DANGER - DO NOT HANDLE - DANGER - QUARRYMASTER AUTHORIZATION ONLY - DANGER\r\n\r\nYou get a sinking feeling that the troggs shouldn't have this. It would be best to report this to the quarry sooner rather than later.",how={{"loot",268548,{1115,1117}}}},[95214]={t="Stolen Blasting Powder",lv=10,min=7,pre1={95213},ot="Recover $1oa Stolen Blasting Powder from the troggs east of Gol'Bolar Quarry, then return to Quarrymaster Thesten.",st="This keg held enough powder to turn King Magni's throne room into an open air courtyard. We've got to get it back from the troggs before they work out how to ignite it.",how={{"loot",267415,{1116,1118}}}},[95217]={t="The Quarry's Smith",lv=10,min=7,ot="Collect 12 Copper Bars and 4 Toughened Boar Hides and deliver them to Frast Dokner.",st="So you're looking to learn the blacksmith's trade? Maybe we can help each other.\r\n\r\nThe supply shipment's late, and I need materials for some repairs around the camp. If you get me what I need, I'll teach you some of my techniques. Sound fair?",how={{"loot",2840},{"loot",267416,{1689}}}},[95250]={t="Abominable Creatures",lv=21,min=16,ot="Collect the Head of the Baron in the Ruins of Lordaeron and bring it back to Captain Truman.",st="What do you want, $r? Can't you see there is a war to be won?\r\n\r\nMy master has already charged into the fray and has ordered me to maintain my post. It has been quite some time, however.\r\n\r\nI doubt you'll survive ten minutes in combat, but if it keeps your simple mind busy, why don't you seek out the Grand Marshal. He is the tallest, most statuesque hero you've ever laid eyes on. You'll know him when you see him.",how={{"loot",268518,{250660}}}},[95646]={t="Horrors in the Highland",lv=31,min=24,pre={275},ot="Kill a Highland Horror within Excavation Sites and bring its root core to Rethiel the Greenwarden in the Wetlands.",st="These brackish wetlands hold a greater well of unsalted southern waters. It pains me, yet within my roots I sense a corruption seeping through that mountain gully.\r\n\r\nThe creatures, like those in our lowlands, react more bitterly to the taint. Lacking the sea's hardening salt since life's dawn, they have little strength against such evil.\r\n\r\nGo to those highlands, and bring me the Highland Horror's root core.",how={{"loot",270180,{260808}}}},[95647]={t="Lost in the Thicket Things",lv=31,min=24,ot="Find Ardin Grassman in the Excavation Sites.",st="My husband, Ardin, has a rare gift for sensing nature. He'll scale any peak to gather the herbs and flowers I need for my alchemy, keeping our shelves and pantry stocked.\r\n\r\nBut I fear he's wandered into trouble. An excavation crew passed through seeking supplies. They spoke, among other things, of towering grasses unlike anything they'd ever seen. Those were what he told me he had to go see for himself. He's been gone too long!\r\n\r\nIf you learn anything of him, I'd be grateful."},[95772]={t="Songblade Search",lv=31,min=24,ot="Look for Dorin Songblade's brother, Daewyn, in Whelgar's Excavation Site.",st="Me brother tried draggin' me off tae the Wetlands with some diggin' crew out o' Loch Modan. Said they were headin' into hills no dwarf's ever set boot in for some sort o' excavation.\r\n\r\nAye, I'd 'ave gone, if I wasn't already behind on this pile o' girdles I've got to refit.\r\n\r\nDaewyn normally writes after he sends off, though. Haven't heard a thing, gives me a strange feelin' this time.\r\n\r\nIf yer marchin' that way, mind checking in on me brother?"},[95795]={t="Fallen in the Fen",lv=31,min=24,pre={95772},ot="Return to Dorin Songblade.",st="<You cover the dwarf's body with his cloak.>\r\n\r\nTravel to Lakeshire and personally inform Dorin Songblade what became of his brother within the Excavation Sites."},[95809]={t="Heartwoven",lv=31,min=24,pre={95647},si=270901,ot="Return to Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.",st="I need a moment to rest before I find my own way out.\r\n\r\n<He pulls some reeds from his pack and quickly braids and bends them into a heart.>\r\n\r\nTake this, and bring it back to Caitlin. Let her know I'll be home soon! Now that we have a path cleared out thanks to you, I'll gather my bushels and follow your trail.\r\n\r\nThank you."},[95810]={t="Lost Relic Carry",lv=31,min=24,ot="Bring the Titan Relic to Prospector Whelgar in the Wetlands excavation site.",st="You pick up a fractured piece of the rock-mech automaton. It has a texture unlike anything you've touched before, a composite material of unknown makeup. This is certainly bound to be more 'device' than 'debris.'\r\n\r\nProspector Whelgar himself at his excavation site might have something useful to share about the relic.",how={{"loot",270865,{260326}}}},[95998]={t="The Great Outdoors",lv=6,min=4,pre={96627},ex={96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ot="Sit near Sam's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",st="Well howdy there, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. Good for you. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\r\n\r\nIt's a big wide world out there and you'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful. Not sure how your outdoorsman skills are but I reckon I could teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\r\n\r\nHave a seat near the fire, get comfy. I'll walk you through it.",how={{"click",460003},{"click",460003}}},[95999]={t="WANTED: Incinerator Gar'im",lv=25,min=16,ot="Deliver the Broken Staff of Incinerator Gar'im to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.",st="Wanted! Incinerator Gar'im, Leader of an orc incursion in Render's Valley. Purported to be working with the Blackrock of Stonewatch Keep.\r\n\r\nBeware of Incinerator Gar'im. He and his Shadowcasters are extremely dangerous. A handsome reward will be given to any brave soul that can deliver proof of Incinerator Gar'im's demise to Magistrate Solomon.",how={{"loot",271872,{214519}}}},[96031]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97906,97922,97934,97946,97958,97969},ot="Speak with Gretta Finespindle in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[96044]={t="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97900,97916,97928,97939,97952,97964},ot="Speak with Tognus Flintfire in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons."},[96045]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97899,97915,97927,97938,97951,97963},ot="Speak with Vosur Brakthel in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Now that you've taken up Alchemy, I can also teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp once you've learned a bit. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste."},[96046]={t="Camping 101: Mining",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97907,97923,97935,97948,97959,97970},ot="Speak with Yarr Hammerstone in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess."},[96047]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97903,97919,97931,97942,97955,97965},ot="Speak with Thamner Pol in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[96050]={t="Camping 101: Fishing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97904,97920,97932,97943,97956,97967},ot="Speak with Paxton Ganter near Iceflow Lake in Dun Morogh to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that."},[96055]={t="Camping 101: Herbalism",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97905,97921,97933,97944,97957,97968},ot="Speak with Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate."},[96056]={t="Camping 101: Skinning",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97908,97924,97936,97949,97960,97971},ot="Speak with Balthus Stoneflayer in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up."},[96057]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96102,97925,97937,97950,97961,97972,97973},ot="Speak with Uthrar Threx in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[96058]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97902,97918,97930,97941,97954,98285,98287},ot="Speak with Bronk Guzzlegear in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells."},[96059]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97901,97917,97929,97940,97953,98284,98286},ot="Speak with Thonys Pillarstone in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Now that you've begun your journey into being an enchanter, I reckon I can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp once you've learned the ropes.\r\n\r\nIt's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[96101]={t="The Great Outdoors",lv=6,min=4,pre={96638},ex={95998,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ot="Sit near Raan's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",st="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\r\n\r\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\r\n\r\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",how={{"click",460003},{"click",460003}}},[96102]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,97925,97937,97950,97961,97972,97973},ot="Speak with Snang in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[96137]={t="Ira's Dagger",lv=25,min=18,si=281143,ot="Defeat $1oa Young Black Ravagers and $2oa Black Ravagers then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.",st="A small dagger belonging to the self-appointed ranger, Ira, who kept the forests safe by preventing the beasts within from attacking travelers.\r\n\r\nWith Ira's spirit still wandering the woods, perhaps her unfinished business was to clear out the worg that continue to claim victims throughout the forest.",how={{"kill",923},{"kill",628}}},[96139]={t="The Valor Family",lv=23,min=18,ot="Search Raven Hill for anything of interest and return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.",st="In dark times like these, it's important we remember our heroes as much as our foes. Darkshire would not still be standing if it weren't for the bravery of folk like the good Lady Althea or those who lost their lives at Raven Hill.\r\n\r\nHave you read much on Raven Hill? No, of course not. Its history was wiped out along with its people. My library, impressive as it is, has little on the subject.\r\n\r\nIf you happen to find anything, I'd appreciate it if you brought it here. Those folk deserve to be remembered.",how={{"open",281046,{673515}}}},[96390]={t="Nip 'Em in the Bud",lv=13,min=9,pre1={96392},si=274268,ot="Slay $1oa Dark Iron Spies in Dun Morogh.",st="Dark Iron spies have infiltrated Dun Morogh. To what end I canna' be sure, but this is a problem we need to nip in the bud before it is allowed to grow.\r\n\r\nHead eastward to Ironband's Compound and kill the Dark Iron spies that you find there.",how={{"kill",6123}}},[96391]={t="Underground Map",lv=15,min=9,si=274268,ot="Deliver the Dark Iron Map to Earthseer Farsen in Dun Morogh.",st="The map you are holding seems to show a complex series of underground tunnels and highways that all seem to converge on a point underneath Ironforge itself.\r\n\r\nYou can't be sure what the runes say as they are written in the ugly jagged rune language of the Dark Iron dwarves, but you can guess at the purpose of these tunnels. As you are reading the map, a gust of wind washes over you and you can faintly hear a dwarven voice carried on it. Earthseer Farsen needs to see this."},[96392]={t="Farsen's Watch",lv=13,min=9,nx=96390,ot="Speak with Earthseer Farsen and ask him to lend you his far sight to observe the Dark Iron threat.",st="Greetings to ye, friend. My name is Earthseer Farsen and I'm visiting Dun Morogh from Aerie Peak. As I was travelin', I couldn't help but notice that we have, well... a bit o' a Dark Iron Dwarf problem.\r\n\r\nIf ye have a moment, I can show ye what I mean. I've got a bit o' magic that should do the trick."},[96393]={t="Old Ironforge Incursion",lv=16,min=9,pre1={96391},ot="Enter the Hall of Thanes beneath Old Ironforge and claim the Head of Durgen Dirgehammer.",st="Gather some allies and head down into the caverns beneath Old Ironforge. Enter the Hall of Thanes there and push to the lower vaults. \r\n\r\nMy Dark Iron is a bit rusty, but I can make out a name--one Durgen Dirgehammer. It's likely that he's the commander. Take his head and deliver it to King Magni Bronzebeard. \r\n\r\nOh, and when you do, tell him his old friend Farsen sends his regards!",how={{"loot",274286,{261319}}}},[96394]={t="The Restless Dead",lv=15,min=10,ot="Kill $1oa Enraged Apparitions, $2oa Tormented Souls and put the spirit of Anvilmar to rest.",st="Something has disturbed the tombs down in the Hall of Thanes, and strange noises have been heard coming from deep within the vaults. The spirits of the dead are light sleepers, and whatever is going on down there seems to have startled them.\r\n\r\nHead down there and see what you can do about that for us. If any of the dead are awake--well, put them back down!",how={{"kill",263389},{"kill",263390}}},[96395]={t="An Ancient Grudge",lv=15,min=10,ot="Put the spirit of Faldrim Anvilmar to rest and then return to the Ghostly Attendant in the Hall of Thanes.",st="The... Thane... my mighty... Thane... he... needs to... rest.\r\n\r\nPlease... help him... help him... rest...\r\n\r\nConsumed... by... ancient... grudge... No... rest...",how={{"kill",261306}}},[96403]={t="Important Heirlooms",lv=15,min=10,ot="Collect $1oa Dwarven Heirlooms from the Hall of Thanes.",st="You there, adventurer... I could really use your aid.\r\n\r\nI was sneaking--uh... 'patrolling' in the vaults when a force of Dark Iron dwarves emerged from the depths in mole machines! I don't know what they are here for, but there is priceless loot--uh or, rather... I mean, 'important cultural heirlooms' down there! Please, recover any such relics you see and return them here.\r\n\r\nI assure you that anything you recover will be catalogued and returned to its proper place of honor.",how={{"open",274289,{457387,652227,652228}}}},[96408]={t="A Visitor to Dun Morogh",lv=13,min=9,nx=96392,bc=96392,ot="Investigate the campsite overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.",st="Last night one of our mountaineers spotted a campfire on a hillside to the east. It looks to be pretty high up, overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.\r\n\r\nIt's probably nothing, but I'd like you to go check on that camp. If they are friendly, no harm done. If they aren't friendly... well, you know what to do."},[96606]={t="The Great Outdoors",lv=6,min=4,pre={96630},ex={95998,96101,96604,96605,96607,96608},ot="Sit near Lyreena's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",st="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\r\n\r\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\r\n\r\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",how={{"click",460003},{"click",460003}}},[96608]={t="The Great Outdoors",lv=6,min=4,pre={96628},ex={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607},ot="Sit near Eric's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",st="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\r\n\r\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\r\n\r\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",how={{"click",460003},{"click",460003}}},[96626]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96629,96634,96646,96655,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Tomas in Goldshire to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96627]={t="The Adventurer",lv=6,min=4,pre1={21},ex={96628,96630,96638,96652,96656,96659},nx=95998,bc=95998,ot="Speak to Sam Sarsparilla near Goldshire.",st="$n, you have proven your competence as a protector thus far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.\r\n\r\nI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Goldshire. Go and see what he's doing."},[96628]={t="The Adventurer",lv=6,min=4,pre1={282},ex={96627,96630,96638,96652,96656,96659},nx=96608,bc=96608,si=275019,ot="Deliver the Supply Bundle to Eric Brighthammer near Kharanos.",st="Wait, $n. I have another ask of you, before you brave that tunnel.\r\n\r\nMy mountaineers have reported an adventurer that's shown up just outside of Kharanos. Could you deliver these supplies to him?"},[96629]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96634,96646,96655,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Gremlock Pilsnor in Kharanos to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96630]={t="The Adventurer",lv=6,min=4,pre1={921},ex={96627,96628,96638,96652,96656,96659},nx=96606,bc=96606,si=275022,ot="Bring the journal to Lyreena Duskblade near Dolanaar.",st="<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.\r\n\r\nThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>"},[96634]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96646,96655,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Zarrin in Dolanaar to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96638]={t="The Adventurer",lv=6,min=4,pre1={92470},ex={96627,96628,96630,96652,96656,96659},nx=96101,bc=96101,ot="Speak to Raan Wildwind near Shen'dar Village.",st="More and more adventurers like yourself have been seeking glory and fortune outside of the safety of Thendal Grove. There's one such adventurer who has made a camp outside of Shen'dar Village, along the road leading southwest out of Thendal Grove.\r\n\r\nSeek him out and see what you can learn from him that may help you in your own travels."},[96646]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96634,96655,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Zerril Softbreeze in Shen'dar Village to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96655]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96634,96646,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Cook Torka in Razor Hill to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96658]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96634,96646,96655,96661},ot="Speak with William Pickman in Brill to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96661]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96634,96646,96655,96658},ot="Speak with Pyall Silentstride in Bloodhoof Village to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[97220]={t="Philmor's Favor",lv=15,min=9,nx=97222,si=277119,ot="Bring the Gatehouse Shipment to the stockroom entrance located in Trias' Cheese shop in the Trade District.",st="Every day this week we've been short dockhands.\r\n\r\nCare to ease the stress on our cargo schedule?\r\n\r\nTake this package to the stockroom entrance of the Gatehouse. You'll find it inside Trias' Cheese shop on the second floor. The mistress, Elaine, will be quite familiar with the deliveries. The Gatehouse often has shipments arriving with more discretion to allow for ceremonial surprises on behalf of the guard's officers."},[97222]={t="Gatehouse Goods",lv=15,min=9,pre1={97220},si=277198,ot="Carry the Gatehouse Shipment up the stairs in Trias' shop and leave it outside the door.",st="Yes, it's only a flight of stairs, but if it's such a small ask, it should be no problem for you to finish the delivery yourself! \r\n\r\nTrias' Cheese isn't part of the Gatehouse or their stocking inventory, but our buildings share a floor.\r\n\r\nPlace the crate outside their stockroom door--the guard will send someone for a regular pickup. They will see the package arrival and carry it inside as they return to post.",how={{"click",460004}}},[97234]={t="Reading Room",lv=18,min=13,nx=97237,si=277158,ot="Bring the wrapped reading material to the Stormwind library.",st="Are you here to discuss the deeper meanings of our storied legends? No?\r\n\r\nWell, after you're done looking around, can you carry this to the library for me? We're exchanging some of our less popular bodies of work for some more modern writing. I have a list of tomes I'm quite sure the librarian will be able to procure for us within our existing arrangement.\r\n\r\nComplimentary club refreshments on us, if you help us out."},[97236]={t="Fang of Githyiss",lv=5,min=1,ot="Deliver the Fang of Githyiss to someone interested in the study of spiders in Aldrassil.",st="A fresh specimen from a beast of this size is quite a find. Perhaps someone in Aldrassil familiar with the study of spiders would be interested in the fang."},[97237]={t="Shelf Picked",lv=18,min=13,pre1={97234},ot="Find each of the reading materials located somewhere in the library and then return to Roy Lewells in Stormwind's Park.",st="I've checked our inventory and all of the selections Mr. Lewells has listed are currently available.\r\n\r\nYou will, however, need to procure them off the shelves yourself. Part of our librarian duty is vigilance, and for that, I will resume supervisory bookkeeping.\r\n\r\nReturning with the material to Roy on his behalf will not mark yourself accountable for their return; as with his note you're serving as the book club's official courier. Their establishment shall carry that burden.\r\n\r\nGood day, $n.",how={{"open",277196,{660731}},{"open",277194,{660730}},{"open",277195,{660729}},{"open",277197,{660732}}}},[97277]={t="Grund and Gozwin",lv=6,min=4,ot="Find Grund and Gozwin's camp in the hills to the northwest. Recover Gozwin's Mechanic's Log and kill the Snow Leopard Prowler.",st="Oi, had me back turned gettin' the boar roast ready when I heard me pal Gozwin screamin' fer his life!\r\n\r\nWicked fangs and a blur are all I saw when I turned. Such huge paws! A snow leopard was draggin' its gnomish catch away. I grabbed me shotgun and fired above the beast. It dropped him and sprinted off.\r\n\r\nLuckily, it hadn't done more than give ol' Goz some deep scratches.\r\n\r\nHead back to camp in the northwestern hills and retrieve Gozwin's Mechanic's Log. Kill that snow leopard too if you see it!",how={{"open",277976,{664122}},{"kill",269075}}},[97899]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96045,97915,97927,97938,97951,97963},ot="Speak with Whuut in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste."},[97900]={t="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96044,97916,97928,97939,97952,97964},ot="Speak with Dwukk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons."},[97901]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97917,97929,97940,97953,98284,98286},ot="Speak with Jhag in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[97902]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96058,97918,97930,97941,97954,98285,98287},ot="Speak with Mukdrak in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells."},[97903]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96047,97919,97931,97942,97955,97965},ot="Speak with Rawrk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[97906]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96031,97922,97934,97946,97958,97969},ot="Speak with Karolek in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[97914]={t="Expanding Horizons",lv=17,min=13,pre={958},nx=97926,si=279045,ot="Bring Thundris' Letter to Baros Alexston in Stormwind.\r\n\r\nThundris mentioned a boat in Auberdine that can take you there.",st="Auberdine is a humble place, $c. You won't hear its name spoken in the boughs of Darnassus. Most reference only what the Sundering took from us--the thriving cities of Ameth'Aran, Bashal'Aran, and... Lathar'Lazal.\r\n\r\nYet Auberdine remains in their shadow.\r\n\r\nI would see our work here recognized. A new vessel connects us to the kingdom of Stormwind, bringing life and supplies to our shores. I beseech you to join its next voyage, and bring this letter to a human called Baros Alexston.\r\n\r\nMake our home known."},[97915]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96045,97899,97927,97938,97951,97963},ot="Speak with Alchemist Mallory in Elwynn Forest near Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste."},[97916]={t="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96044,97900,97928,97939,97952,97964},ot="Speak with Smith Argus in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons."},[97917]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97901,97929,97940,97953,98284,98286},ot="Speak with Betty Quin in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[97918]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96058,97902,97930,97941,97954,98285,98287},ot="Speak with Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells."},[97919]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96047,97903,97931,97942,97955,97965},ot="Speak with Michelle Belle in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[97920]={t="Camping 101: Fishing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96050,97904,97932,97943,97956,97967},ot="Speak with Lee Brown near Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that."},[97921]={t="Camping 101: Herbalism",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96055,97905,97933,97944,97957,97968},ot="Speak with Herbalist Pomeroy in Elwynn Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate."},[97922]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96031,97906,97934,97946,97958,97969},ot="Speak with Adele Fielder in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[97923]={t="Camping 101: Mining",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96046,97907,97935,97948,97959,97970},ot="Speak with Gelman Stonehand in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess."},[97924]={t="Camping 101: Skinning",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96056,97908,97936,97949,97960,97971},ot="Speak with Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up."},[97925]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,96102,97937,97950,97961,97972,97973},ot="Speak with Eldrin in the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[97927]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96045,97899,97915,97938,97951,97963},ot="Speak with Kray in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste."},[97928]={t="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96044,97900,97916,97939,97952,97964},ot="Speak with Thrag Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons."},[97929]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97901,97917,97940,97953,98284,98286},ot="Speak with Mot Dawnstrider in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[97930]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96058,97902,97918,97941,97954,98285,98287},ot="Speak with Twizwick Sprocketgrind in the Venture Co. Mine in Mulgore to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells."},[97931]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96047,97903,97919,97942,97955,97965},ot="Speak with Vira Younghoof in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[97934]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96031,97906,97922,97946,97958,97969},ot="Speak with Chaw Stronghide in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession 