termend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[97967]={t="Camping 101: Fishing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96050,97904,97920,97932,97943,97956},ot="Speak with Fenn Fairweather in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that."},[97968]={t="Camping 101: Herbalism",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96055,97905,97921,97933,97944,97957},ot="Speak with Syriel Nightrain in Valanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.",how={{"kill",254345}}},[97969]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96031,97906,97922,97934,97946,97958},ot="Speak with Indari Sunseam in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[97970]={t="Camping 101: Mining",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96046,97907,97923,97935,97948,97959},ot="Speak with Messana Crestwind in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess."},[97971]={t="Camping 101: Skinning",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96056,97908,97924,97936,97949,97960},ot="Speak with Mendalass Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up."},[97972]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,96102,97925,97937,97950,97961,97973},ot="Speak with Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[97973]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,96102,97925,97937,97950,97961,97972},ot="Speak with Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[97977]={t="Nature's Call",lv=3,min=1,pre1={458},ot="Collect $1oa Gnarlpine Totems and bring them to Tarindrella.",st="The Gnarlpine furbolg would not turn on their ancient allies so readily. We must learn more of their plight.\r\n\r\nSearch their abandoned homes for totems. If any survived the chaos of their departure, their engravings may tell us more of what happened here.\r\n\r\nYou'll find their camps along the western edge of the glen, though the grell and grellkin may have scattered them beyond.",how={{"open",279082,{668493,668482}}}},[97979]={t="The Goddess Provides",lv=1,min=1,pre1={456},ot="Cast Elune's Light and Shadowmeld.",st="You are born kaldorei--the children of the stars--and have inherited a birthright unlike any other in this world. Elune's grace may illuminate our strengths, helping our strikes hit true, or it may help conceal us just as the moon may eclipse the sun.\r\n\r\nOur Long Vigil after the defense of Mount Hyjal has ended, and we have joined an Alliance of others--which you will meet in due time. For now, you are nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil.\r\n\r\nDemonstrate Mother Moon's gifts, and bask in her blessings."},[98013]={t="Swelling Forces",lv=20,min=12,ot="Eliminate $1oa Stormscale Myrmidons, $2oa Stormscale Sorceresses, and $3oa Stormscale Warriors for Arbal at the Grove of the Ancients.",st="Steel yourself for your time in the ruins, young one... you will not be granted free passage there.\r\n\r\nScores of cursed Highborne, now known as naga, roam the once great city. Travel northeast and dispatch them from this land.\r\n\r\nWhat they once were... is no more. If they aid the Twilight's Hammer, they can bring only further pain to the forests that once gave them shelter.\r\n\r\nWar is what they seek, $c. War... is what we will bring.",how={{"kill",2181},{"kill",2182},{"kill",2183}}},[98021]={t="Journey to Sentinel Hill",lv=13,min=7,pre1={94947},ot="Report To Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill in Westfall.",st="If you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, I'd recommend reporting to a man named Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall to the south, at the settlement known as Sentinel Hill. His people are in need of aid.\r\n\r\nAfter journeying here from another plane of existence, the problems our lands face may seem small. I assure you, the aid you provide to those impacted by such problems means everything to them, and you will grow stronger for your labors.\r\n\r\nGood luck out there, adventurer!"},[98025]={t="WANTED: Jai'vhanel",lv=13,min=10,ot="Find and slay the owl known as Jai'vhanel and take one of her feathers. The black owl was last seen north of the Ameth'Aran ruins near the mountain base. Report the death of Jai'vhanel to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.",st="Attention!\r\n\r\nA reward is being offered for the death of the owl \"Jai'vhanel\" also known as \"Swordfeather\".\r\n\r\nUnfortunately this owl has gone mad and has begun to attack travelers as they journey along the road near Auberdine.\r\n\r\nJai'vhanel was last seen north of the Ameth'Aran ruins near the mountain base. Bring back one of her jet black feathers as proof of her death.\r\n\r\nReward claims for this bounty should be claimed with Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\r\n\r\nThe Auberdine Village Council",how={{"loot",281038,{270196}}}},[98027]={t="Gleaming Crescent Necklace",lv=26,min=22,si=279274,ot="Deliver the Crescent Necklace to Maliynn in Astranaar.",st="<The silver necklace in your hands gleams gently as you examine it. The small crescent moon shape seems similar to other night elf symbols you've seen before.\r\n\r\nUpon flipping the necklace over there is a small inscription: \"Alor'lormah, Maliynn\". Perhaps it belongs to Maliynn in Astranaar?>"},[98042]={t="It's All Fun and Games Until...",lv=17,min=12,ot="Obtain a Peerless Eye from a Twilight Disciple or Thug at the Master's Glaive in Darkshore and find someone in Auberdine who is willing to take it.",st="<As you tear away the single page from the Twilight Tome, a foreboding voice floods your mind, uninvited.>\r\n\r\nThey have failed.\r\n\r\nYou will be forgotten.\r\n\r\nThey will lose the eye they gained.",how={{"loot",279279,{2339,2338}}}},[98046]={t="Crown of the Earth",lv=11,min=1,pre1={935},nx=98065,si=279291,ot="Bring the Drained Vessel to Lariia in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",st="<Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm's gaze narrows.>\r\n\r\nYou're still here?\r\n\r\nTake the phial and get out of my sight, $c. It is clear my answers do not lie in the waters, just as they did not before. \r\n\r\nPerhaps one of the priestesses in the Temple of the Moon to the south will dispose of it.\r\n\r\n<Fandral looks away, no longer speaking to you.>\r\n\r\nI must look elsewhere if this is to work..."},[98065]={t="Crown of the Earth",lv=11,min=1,pre1={98046},si=279331,ot="Bring the Moonwell Remnants to Tyrande Whisperwind in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",st="You must bring this to Tyrande at once! I will transfer it to a more ceremonial container for you.\r\n\r\nDo not be afraid. The High Priestess of Elune is firm, but kind. She protects all who enter Darnassus, and carries our goddess' light to all.\r\n\r\nShe will be glad to receive this sacred water. You will find her directly above us."},[98067]={t="Eyes of the Sentinels",lv=11,min=1,si=279378,ot="Place Sentinel Owls at the entrance to the Cenarion Hold depths, the Darnassus Bank, the Craftsman's Terrace Inn, and the City Gate for Sentinel Dalia Sunblade in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",st="General Feathermoon ensures all sentinels have time to pray to Elune. A proper huntress wields not blade alone, but gifts of the goddess to overcome our enemies.\r\n\r\nYou may help with my daily duties. Place sentinels around the city--start with the tunnels leading beneath Cenarion Hold to the north, the bank at the center of town, the inn in the Craftsman's Terrace to the northeast, and the city gates. The guards can assist you.\r\n\r\nSomething is amiss in Teldrassil--we must remain vigilant.",how={{"spot",270418},{"spot",270419},{"spot",270420},{"spot",270421}}},[98189]={t="Return the Statuette",lv=25,min=20,pre1={286},nx=98190,si=279589,ot="Bring the Menethil Statuette to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep.",st="My goodness, it's--it's beautiful!\r\n\r\nThe Blind Princess was to deliver this to Menethil Harbor before tragedy struck. We were so close!\r\n\r\nI believe it was to be signed for by Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep just behind us. Why don't you do the honors of finishing the job?"},[98190]={t="A Friend of the Family",lv=25,min=20,pre1={98189},pre={98189},nx=98191,si=279595,ot="Bring the Menethil Statuette to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.",st="You'll want to take this to Stormwind right away. Proud as I am that this keep and harbor bears King Terenas Menethil II's name, we are a calm harbor in a very nasty storm of enemies. It's just not safe here.\r\n\r\nThe Dragonmaw in particular would sacrifice much to loot something like this... and I shudder to think of what they'd do with it.\r\n\r\nDon't bother going up the chain of command on this one, $Glad:lass;. Go straight to Highlord Fordragon with this. He'll know where it will be best kept."},[98191]={t="A Friend of the Family",lv=25,min=20,pre1={98190},si=279598,ot="Bring the Menethil Statuette to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral of Light.",st="King Terenas was a good man. A devout man. Beloved by his people, and truly the reason we have this Alliance at all.\r\n\r\nThe irony is he was humble--he hated these sorts of memorials, and so precious few exist. And of those, few survived Lordaeron's fall.\r\n\r\nIt seems the Light has coalesced in this statuette. It would be best kept in the Cathedral of the Light in Cathedral Square, in the center of the city. Bring it to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker for safekeeping."},[98197]={t="Spoils of War",lv=22,min=18,ot="Recover $1oa Khaz Modan Timber and $2oa Khaz Modan Iron from Menethil Harbor for Valstag Ironjaw.",st="This harbor was first built by the Old Horde as a staging ground for their naval invasion of Hillsbrad. Completely circumvented Lordaeron's defenses!\r\n\r\nSo many lives lost...\r\n\r\nWhat's worse is that fleet was built with the very resources they stole from Khaz Modan!\r\n\r\nPlenty of it remains in the harbor after Admiral Proudmoore routed the brutes and built this place for the Alliance. We'll need it to bolster the town's defenses with the Dragonmaw on the move.",how={{"open",279821,{670773,670771}},{"open",279822,{670774}}}},[98219]={t="The Shamed Lieutenant",lv=30,min=20,ot="Speak to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills.",st="Thank you again for delivering the statuette safely, $n.\r\n\r\nI could use your help with something else. There's a member of the city guard who was reassigned to duty in Southshore out in the Hillsbrad Foothills.\r\n\r\nHis father was a friend of mine, and while I don't disagree that he could use the lesson... I'd still like to see him succeed. He would really benefit from someone like you helping him out.\r\n\r\nThere is a boat that can take you that way from Menethil Harbor, if you are passing back through."},[98245]={t="Razormaw Needling",lv=29,min=21,ot="Collect $1oa Razormaw Incisors for Howin Kindfeather.",st="I don't know who I hate more: the bloody Dark Irons, the Dragonmaw, or the drakes they rode.\r\n\r\n<Howin spits.>\r\n\r\nI aim tae make things right. But we're gonna need some supplies.\r\n\r\nThese whelp scales will protect against dragonfire a good bit, but they're a pain in the arse tae weave together.\r\n\r\nThe Razormaw raptors up in Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest are so named for their pointy chompers--they oughta break through the scales.\r\n\r\nBring me a handful of the incisors.",how={{"loot",280103,{1018,1019}}}},[98246]={t="Trying Times",lv=29,min=21,ot="Gather $1oa Perfect Razormaw Eggs for Howin Kindfeather.",st="I'll need some eggs if my plan is going tae work. Bassbeak needs a nice an' full belly--I ain't in the business of hoppin' on the back of a surly gryphon.\r\n\r\nThey need to be perfect--no cracks or anything.\r\n\r\nTake some from the Razormaw raptors--they're known for having yolks the size of a gnome's noggin. You can find 'em in Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest.\r\n\r\nLet's make it a nice even dozen, just to be safe.",how={{"open",280132,{671892,671931}}}},[98282]={t="Alchemical Hazards",lv=22,min=20,ot="Collect an Unruptured Stalker Gland from Thelgen Rock for Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.",st="Certain alchemical recipes require ingredients sourced from, well, very dangerous places. And those are often just the base herbs! The other ingredients are even worse!\r\n\r\nI need to make more antivenom before I can leave again. I swear everything in this marsh is venomous. It's like it runs through the land itself!\r\n\r\nCan you help me? I'll need a venom gland from the spiders in Thelgen Rock to the far southeast. But it has to be unruptured, or too much venom will spill out before you can get here. Sorry!",how={{"loot",280319,{4040,1111,211967}}}},[98284]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97901,97917,97929,97940,97953,98286},ot="Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[98285]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96058,97902,97918,97930,97941,97954,98287},ot="Speak with the Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="An engineer is ever-resourceful, and if you are in the wilds alone, it's always good to be able to put your trade to use. No good camp is complete without a few helpful constructs!\r\n\r\nYes, come back and see me when you've gained a little bit of experience as an engineer and I can show you how to make something special!"},[98286]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97901,97917,97929,97940,97953,98284},ot="Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[98319]={t="Secure the Mountain",lv=8,min=4,pre1={98322},nx=98323,ot="Find Mountaineer Cornelius in the Grizzled Den for Mountaineer Gretchen.",st="It's bad enough havin' a troll problem, but the mountains are filled tae the brim with wendigos! They normally keep to their own caves, but they seem tae be spreadin' like bunnies. Now they've filled the Grizzled Den north of here.\r\n\r\nIf we want Whitebeard's report, we're gonna need to find my partner Cornelius. The blockhead got a little too excited and charged in head first. Brave, but stupid.\r\n\r\nHead into the cave and see where he is. And feel free to take out some of the beasts while yer at it.",how={{"talk",278166}}},[98321]={t="Flintfire's Shipment",lv=7,min=4,ot="Collect $1oa Flintfire Shipments from the Grizzled Den for Tongus Flintfire in Kharanos.",st="Hoha! Good to see a $r who's not afraid to get their hands dirty.\r\n\r\nIf yer lookin' fer work, I'm afraid I'm a little short on supplies at the moment. Our most reliable source of ore has been overrun by wendigo and now the cave has been abandoned. The miners had to drop everything when they fled!\r\n\r\nSay, why don't ye poke yer head around the Grizzled Den to the west and see if you can find some of our missing shipments. It would save us a great deal o' trouble.",how={{"open",280413,{672508,7983211}}}},[98322]={t="Secure the Mountain",lv=8,min=4,pre={420},nx=98319,ot="Check in on Mountaineer Gretchen west of Kharanos.",st="Spelunking dark caves is adventurer business. My job's just to make reports and send them over to Ironforge.\r\n\r\nTrouble is, one of my reports hasn't... well, reported back. I asked a few mountaineers to learn more about the wendigo problem we have out here, but I haven't heard from them.\r\n\r\nIf you're already going to be out and about, what say you check in with Mountaineer Gretchen just west of town. I'm late enough as it is!"},[98323]={t="Secure the Mountain",lv=8,min=4,pre1={98319},si=280430,ot="Deliver Mountaineer Gretchen's Report back to Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.",st="Hopefully ye put down a fair number of the mongrels while you were in there. Shame about Cornelius, though.\r\n\r\nFrom what you described, there's not much to report other than the cave is a lost cause. Whitebeard's not gonna like that answer, but I'm not darin' sendin' anybody else into that death trap.\r\n\r\nFeel free tae pass along the message, $n. I'm not leavin' this spot till the mountain's secure."},[98326]={t="Frosthowl",lv=9,min=5,ot="Slay Frosthowl and collect the Sack of Fish for Gretta Ganter in Brewnall Village.",st="Do ye know how hard it is to fish on a frozen lake? My poor husband, Paxton, has been out in the middle of it for days and we barely have a single sack to show fer it.\r\n\r\nWell, we DID have a sack to show fer it. Until the thrice-damned wendigo attacked me and made off with our haul. It'll take us weeks to fish all that back up! If that loudmouth Frosthowl didn't scare 'em all off, anyway.\r\n\r\nDo us a favor and get it back, aye? Drooling brute is hiding somewhere deep in the Grizzled Den to the southeast.",how={{"loot",280426,{271587}}}},[98341]={t="The Great Windborne Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre1={98340,98393},ot="Seek out the Avatar of Saeyleenan in the southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the windborne cat.",st="A spirit of your homeland has recently appeared here and has asked me to guide you to it. This windborne cat spirit has come to tutor and mentor you so that you may take the feline shape of the spirit on Zephras.\r\n\r\nAll druids eventually seek this wisdom, though it seems your homeland has a slightly different shape than our traditional one. If you desire to take this spirit's feline form, you will need to undergo our trial.\r\n\r\nIt can be found in the southern part of Moonglade, south of the twin bridges."},[98386]={t="Alther's Mill",lv=21,min=15,pre1={89},pre={89},ot="Slay $1oa Greater Tarantulas and destroy $2oa Tarantula Eggs in Alther's Mill for Foreman Oslow in Redridge.",st="Orcs, gnolls, murlocs. Everything seems to be out to stop me from getting this bridge done on time. Now we have word there's an infestation of tarantulas at our lumber mill!\r\n\r\nIf you're up to earn a bit more coin, would you head over to Alther's Mill to the east and clear out their spider problem? Place is as good as useless to me if I can't safely send workers to collect shipments.\r\n\r\nOh, and if you see ol' Alther, tell him he owes me for cleaning up his mess.",how={{"click",673101},{"kill",505},{"kill",271898},{"kill",271988}}},[98387]={t="Blackrock Blockade",lv=21,min=18,ot="Bring $1oa Stolen Weapons and $2oa Blackrock Supplies to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.",st="You can't fight a war without weapons.\r\n\r\nThough the Blackrock orcs have encroached upon these lands, their brazen efforts are not without certain vulnerabilities.\r\n\r\nHead southeast below Stonewatch Keep, seek out their encampments, and target their weapons and supplies.\r\n\r\nWe'll see just how much of a threat they are without their tools of war.",how={{"open",280841,{673399,673390}},{"open",280839,{673385,673376,673384}}}},[98391]={t="The Sisterhood of Elune",lv=10,min=5,nx=2519,bc=2519,ot="Speak to Sister Aquinne in Darnassus.",st="Blessings to you, $c. The Sisterhood of Elune has stood as a pillar of kaldorei society for thousands of years.\r\n\r\nBefore the Great Sundering, before the War of the Ancients, through the Long Vigil, we have guided and healed our people through the darkness. Such is our charge, and such is the demand of the peerless Mother Moon.\r\n\r\nWe now require your aid in a matter of great importance. Sister Aquinne awaits your arrival in Darnassus."},[98392]={t="Darkness in the Glade",lv=12,min=6,pre1={937},nx=98398,ot="Collect Hatescreech's Amulet, Windmistress Gaedress' Amulet, and Witchmother Arysa's Amulet for Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade.",st="These belts... look closely at the leather, $n. Do you see the taint running through the fibers?\r\n\r\nI have a suspicion as to its origin, but we will need further proof to be sure.\r\n\r\nVenture back out into the harpies' nests to the west and take out their leaders. If their necklaces carry the same darkness as these belts, we'll have our answer.",how={{"loot",280831,{272034}},{"loot",280832,{272044}},{"loot",280834,{272046}}}},[98393]={t="The Great Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,ot="Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.",st="It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.\r\n\r\nYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training."},[98394]={t="The Great Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98393},ot="Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.",st="In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.\r\n\r\nMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.\r\n\r\nGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you."},[98396]={t="The Great Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98394},ot="Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Great Cat Spirit.",st="To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\r\n\r\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\r\n\r\nReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.",how={{"open",280502,{672821}},{"open",280679,{673093}},{"open",280680,{673094}}}},[98397]={t="To Darnassus",lv=20,min=20,pre1={98731,98738},ot="Return to Darnassus and speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave.",st="The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to the one who sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.\r\n\r\nGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again."},[98398]={t="The Oracle Tree",lv=12,min=6,pre1={98392},nx=940,ot="Find the Oracle Tree Bark nearby to receive its message.",st="I am impressed by what you have accomplished here in so short a time, $n. Would that I could ask you to remain here to assist me with my duties... but I know in my heart that greater tasks lie ahead for you.$b$bI have noticed the Oracle Tree has just shed a piece of its bark. No doubt it has a task that it wishes completed. You should speak with it."},[98403]={t="Twisted Hatred",lv=12,min=4,pre1={932},ot="Kill $1oa Befouled Webwoods and bring Xethorr the Wicked's Mature Fel Moss to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.",st="Lord Melenas did not act alone; he was at the behest of another. The one you seek is Xethorr the Wicked. It seems he has twisted the spiders that call Teldrassil home, intending their venom for some foul plan.\r\n\r\nHe has taken residence deep in the forest, in the area to the northwest of here known as the Cleft. Take caution, and bring allies, for Xethorr is not an opponent to be trifled with.\r\n\r\nDispatch his brood, and bring me anything that may tell us more of the satyr's work here.",how={{"kill",272096},{"loot",281023,{272116}}}},[98404]={t="The Great Windborne Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98341},ot="Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Avatar of Saeyleenan.",st="In order to draw upon my spirit, you will need to undergo a trial. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\r\n\r\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\r\n\r\nReturn these relics to me to pass the druidic trial of these lands.",how={{"open",280502,{672821}},{"open",280679,{673093}},{"open",280680,{673094}}}},[98407]={t="Show of Force",lv=17,min=11,ot="Collect $1oa Spiked Collars from Redridge Thrashers for Deputy Feldon near Lakeshire.",st="If the gnolls are growing so bold they are willing to camp this close to humans, there's no telling how much further they'll go. We need to deter them.\r\n\r\nThe beasts are hardly organized, but they seem to respect strength above all else. If we can slay the worst of them, maybe claim some of their trophies, we can remind these gnolls why they should stay in the hills where they belong.\r\n\r\nShould you see any of their thrashers, bring me their collars. That should put the fear of the Alliance back into them.",how={{"loot",280911,{712}}}},[98417]={t="Vengeful Trail",lv=28,min=23,ot="Maseara Autumnmoon wants you to search west of Forest Song, amongst the Satyrnaar demons. Report any signs of her husband Kurothel upon your return.",st="At the moment our fates bound us most vulnerable, tragedy fell upon our villages. Satyrs defiled our temples, their profane touch staining sacred boughs, and they slaughtered the innocent without mercy.\r\n\r\nKurothel was consumed by wrath. The druids are taking the fight to the satyr, and he has followed.\r\n\r\nOur bond endures. I feel my husband, west, within these woods. Please, return to me with news of his fate.",how={{"open",281014,{673431}}}},[98418]={t="Shared Fury",lv=30,min=23,pre={98417},ot="Kill $1oa Xavian Rogues, $2oa Felsworn, $3oa Betrayers, and $4oa Hellcallers.\r\nReturn to Maseara Autumnmoon in Forest Song afterwards.",st="Kurothel mentioned sightings of what they say are wolf-men. Those of the pack now lurking in greater numbers in our forest. Last we had spoken, druids were pursuing communication with those of the beast heart who displayed measured control of their animal instincts.\r\n\r\nHis written words show a darker struggle. If there is anything we can do to help see HIM again, surely quelling the demon threat that is driving him to this burning transformation will be of aid to his anguished soul.\r\n\r\nSlay the Xavian, $n.",how={{"kill",3754},{"kill",3755},{"kill",3757},{"kill",3752}}},[98423]={t="The Treaty of Understanding",lv=16,min=9,si=281030,ot="Deliver the Treaty of Understanding to Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.",st="Inside of the vault you find a tablet detailing the terms of a peace treaty between the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarf clans. It appears to date back to the time period just after the War of the Three Hammers, and is very likely a notable piece of dwarven history. The king of Ironforge would no doubt be interested in this artifact."},[98461]={t="Unrequited Love",lv=21,min=18,si=281243,ot="Deliver Hollee's Note to Tarrel Rockweaver near Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",st="If you're heading out of Auberdine, I could use your help!\r\n\r\nMy dear friend Tarrel and I were classmates in school. Oh, he was such a quickfire on all things excavation! We got split up after graduation--him to Wetlands, and me to here in Darkshore.\r\n\r\n<Hollee sighs, then her brow furrows slightly.>\r\n\r\nSorry, and his wife... Merrin.\r\n\r\nIt doesn't matter. If you go to the Wetlands, could you make sure he's alright? And maybe give him this? He's probably near Menethil Harbor. There's a boat straight there."},[98512]={t="Al'Aketh Assassins",lv=11,min=6,ot="Kill 10 Al'Aketh Assassins in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="You there, stranger. Get low and keep quiet. We are not alone here.\r\n\r\nI was on patrol near the border and noticed that there are a number of Al'Aketh skulking around the house just up the hill there to the north. I don't know what they are doing here, but it can't be good.\r\n\r\nIf you want to make yourself useful, get in there and take them out. I'll wait here and watch your back.",how={{"kill",254626}}},[98574]={t="Hallowed Memorandum",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=282338,ot="Read the Hallowed Memorandum and speak to Branstock Khalder in Anvilmar.",st="While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the priest trainer Branstock. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[98581]={t="Archaic Rune",lv=1,min=1,pre1={179},si=282400,ot="Read the Archaic Rune and speak to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.",st="While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. Based on the Wildhammer style to these inscriptions, I'm guessin' this came from the shaman trainer Teo Hammerstorm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance."},[98731]={t="Blessings of the Great Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98396},ot="Speak to Dendrite.",st="Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further. I do hope we meet again someday.\r\n\r\nMay the shadows forever hide you and your foes easily fall prey to your claws, young one."},[98738]={t="Blessings of the Great Windborne Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98404},ot="Speak to Dendrite.",st="Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately I have little left to teach you for the moment. I do hope you come and visit me in Zephras again someday. I sense promise in you, young shen'dorei.\r\n\r\nMay the shadows forever hide you, your foes easily fall prey to your claws, and the winds guide your steps."},[98815]={t="Highland Hides",lv=28,min=24,pre={484},ot="Return $1oa Thicket Raptor Hides to James Halloran, the tanner, in Menethil Harbor.",st="The Highlands are host to ruins of some sort, secrets now being explored by an expedition team. What I know is that they've got their own wildlife and beasts lurking in that mountain marshland. How about you take a foray in there with some well-equipped friends, and we work a trade?\r\n\r\nI don't care if they're hiding, I want their hides! Bring me the skins from four of the Thicket Raptors, I'll have a trade worked out for you to make it worth it.",how={{"loot",284845,{260325,260800,260801}}}},[98824]={t="Prehistoric Prism",lv=31,min=24,pre={95810},si=287959,ot="Bring the Titan Relic to High Explorer Magellas in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.",st="With titan-like inscriptions like that on its facets, nothing less than Ironforge's Hall of Explorers is the right place to bring it.\r\n\r\nI'd like to think that you'll be noted in the history for it in the catalogue -- \"Recovered by $n! Authenticated by Prospector Whelgar...\" Ah, I'm gettin' meself carried away.\r\n\r\nHigh Explorer Magellas will receive you, and given the exquisite nature of what you carry, will surely be most generously appreciative should you donate it to the museum.\r\n\r\nGood find!"},[99046]={t="The Lost Runner",lv=9,min=4,nx=99047,bc=99047,ot="Search for Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow on the road leading to the Oracle Glade.",st="The Council of the Forest sent a small group of sentinels to the Oracle Tree some time ago. The tree sends messages to our elders, and it falls to us to deliver them to Darnassus safely.\r\n\r\nI received word that our most recent runner has not yet arrived. The Oracle's messages vary in frequency, but it has been abnormally long.\r\n\r\nPlease head towards the Oracle Glade along the road to the west and check on her. It would have been Eralya Leafshadow's turn, and she is still in training. Elune guide you."},[99047]={t="Not Dead Yet",lv=9,min=4,pre={99046},nx=99050,ot="Seek aid from Byancie in Dolanaar for Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow.",st="My sisters and I... were dispatched... Oracle Tree...\r\n\r\nTree... message. I... harpies... everywhere...\r\n\r\n<Eralya coughs up blood, grimacing through the pain.>\r\n\r\nI may not have long... no one coming. Please... Byancie... in Dolanaar..."},[99050]={t="The Great Tree Provides",lv=10,min=4,pre1={99047},nx=99073,ot="Collect $1oa Dewy Lasher Fronds, an Empty Vial, and a Refreshing Spring Water for Byancie in Dolanaar.",st="I will need your help acquiring the ingredients I need to stop the affliction long enough for Eralya to make it back here for further treatment.\r\n\r\nThankfully, our living home is still bountiful and will provide in our time of need.\r\n\r\nThe core ingredient is dewy lasher fronds. You'll find them around Lake Al'Ameth directly south of here, or Wellspring Lake and its river to the northwest.\r\n\r\nIn addition, I'll need an empty vial and some spring water. Both can be bought here in town, or traded for.",how={{"loot",286017,{275703}},{"buy",3371,{3614,4229,4216}},{"buy",159,{4265,6736,3608}}}},[99053]={t="Escaping Ban'ethil",lv=10,min=4,pre={2561},ne=1,ot="Help Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom escape Ban'ethil Barrow Den, and report her safety to Sentinel Kyra Starsong in Dolanaar.",st="My prayers have been answered! I am thankful that you have fought your way down here.\r\n\r\nI was sent here by the Oracle Tree to deliver a message to the slumbering druids here only to find it completely overrun by furbolg! They ambushed me before I could turn back and brought me down here--I fear for their next meal.\r\n\r\nI don't know about you, but I loathe this place. Under the earth is no place for the kaldorei."},[99073]={t="Easing Suffering",lv=10,min=4,pre1={99050},si=286069,ot="Take the Lashwater Salve to Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow on the road to the Oracle Tree.",st="The salve is ready. Take it to Eralya swiftly.\r\n\r\nI do not know if it will truly cure her. The rot festers quickly, and grows in strength as it spreads.\r\n\r\nIt will, if nothing else, ease her suffering. And that is still worth your haste."},[99127]={t="A Net Disaster",lv=7,min=4,nx=99128,ot="Check the fishing traps in Crystal Lake.",st="The fish just ain't biting today, and there's something wrong going on with them. It's not just empty hooks. I haven't seen a single minnow up in the water at all.\r\n\r\nLee here set up some traps overnight. Go check to see if we've at least got some stock there. If you find anything weird, make sure to show me.",how={{"open",286205,{694772}}}},[99128]={t="Slimy Menace",lv=7,min=4,pre1={99127},nx=99129,ot="Kill $1oa Murlocs and $2oa Murloc Streamrunner at Crystal Lake, then return to Jason Mathers.",st="This can only be the work of those murlocs on the other side of the lake. They're disgusting little things, with a vicious temper and teeth to match. \r\n\r\nIf we let this continue, there won't be any fish to speak of anywhere in this lake. If you could clear them out a bit, it would help me a ton.",how={{"kill",285},{"kill",735}}},[99129]={t="A Man About a Murloc",lv=7,min=4,pre1={99128},nx=99130,ot="Speak with Remy \"Two Times\" about Jason's murloc problems.",st="Remy mentioned murlocs the other day... I'm pretty sure he hates the little buggers as much as I do. \r\n\r\nHe might have some ideas on how to keep them away from my fish in the future. I'd like to ask you to go chat with him and see if there's anything he can think of."},[99130]={t="An Enticing Offer",lv=7,min=4,pre1={99129},pre={99129},nx=99131,ot="Collect $1oa Vials of Animal Blood and $2oa Duskweed Petals for murloc bait, then return to Remy \"Two Times\" in Goldshire.",st="I've got a few ideas on how to deal with murlocs. And one of those also helps some others in the process.\r\n\r\nThere's a weed often found on farms in the area called duskweed, and in large quantities the petals are toxic to most animals. If we make some murloc bait with the plant, hopefully that can train those creatures to stay away.\r\n\r\nAnd some farmers get their fields cleared in the process. Truly a win-win... truly a win-win.",how={{"loot",286215,{113}},{"open",286214,{694855}}}},[99131]={t="Baited for Success",lv=7,min=4,pre1={99130},pre={99130},ot="Return to Jason Mathers.",st="Tell Mathers he can come pick up the bait later today. I'll give him the rundown on the proper usage.\r\n\r\nHopefully he'll be able to sell his fish again soon. And we'll have less murlocs in this world."},[99143]={t="Bottles and Baubles",lv=7,min=4,ot="Collect $1oa pieces of shiny junk from the nearby Murloc camp.",st="Those fish men must think like actual fish, right? Which means anything they like, fish will like!\r\n\r\nIf you rummage through some of their junk and return to me with anything that seems like it would make good bait, I'll reward you.",how={{"open",286209,{694785}}}},[99158]={t="Dawn in the Mountains",lv=8,min=5,nx=99159,bc=99159,si=286355,ot="Bring the crate of candles to Father Gavin at Misty Pine Refuge.",st="There's a priest out in the mountains that belongs to an organization called the Argent Dawn. They're a holy group that is dedicated to finding and destroying the unholy and unnatural.\r\n\r\nFather Gavin though, he's mostly the type that seeks to help and heal everyone rather than grab a weapon. He's fixed up an old building to serve as a rest spot for travelers and called it Misty Pine Refuge. I've got a shipment of holy candles that I need to get him. Could you bring them to him if you're going that way?"},[99159]={t="Finding Warmth",lv=8,min=5,ot="Collect $1oa pieces of firewood.",st="My hearth is open to warm any soul, but I'd like to ask you to help me if you could.\r\n\r\nI simply need more firewood. It is something I would normally do myself, but I have been preoccupied by other tasks.",how={{"open",286339,{694934}}}},[99160]={t="Rime's Wrath",lv=8,min=5,pre1={99159},nx=99161,ot="Destroy $1oa minor ice elementals.",st="You may have noticed the elementals nearby. A shelf of rock and ice fell from the mountain peaks a few days ago and riled them up.\r\n\r\nThese frozen mountains are already treacherous for the average dwarf or human without the elements taking form. I am not one for fighting anymore--so any of the spirits you can kill would help make the road safer.",how={{"kill",276003}}},[99161]={t="Rime's Wrath",lv=8,min=5,pre1={99160},ot="Kill Avala and retrieve its core.",st="I noticed that the first elemental that appeared after the rockslide was larger than its peers. And from what I can tell, it has been the source of occasional weather changes and other minor slides.\r\n\r\nI've been calling it 'Avala', if you could kill it and retrieve the core as proof, I will reward you.",how={{"loot",286325,{276009}}}},[99162]={t="Treacherous Cold",lv=8,min=5,pre1={99159},ot="Collect the rifles of fallen mountaineers.",st="Even mountaineers from Ironforge have to keep their wits about them when traversing through the peaks of Dun Morogh. Falling snow and ice often spells the end of some more novice members' lives.\r\n\r\nAfter a slide, I usually try to find any sign of survivors or victims--while praying to the Light that there's nothing to be found. But with the elements acting up, I've held off wandering too far. If you could look for some lost mountaineers and bring me their rifles, I will return them to Ironforge.",how={{"open",286360,{695277}},{"open",286359,{695223}},{"open",286358,{695222}}}},[99260]={t="Fillion's Mission",lv=10,min=5,pre1={92850},nx=92840,ot="Speak with Elaadrin Evengale in Valanaar.",st="I was tasked to retrieve important data on the flow of elemental energy from the Overlook Standing Stones. That data is vital to our plans to safely travel between Skywall and Azeroth. Without that data to aid in our calculations, our attempts to steer our skycutter ships through the elemental plane will fail.\r\n\r\nThe data is likely lost at this point, and I'm in no state to attempt to gather it again. I told the Supreme Magister of your role in saving me, and he wishes to speak with you again."}},
